window.STUDY_DATA = {"version":1,"questions":[{"stem":"What a beautiful hat you are wearing today! ______. It's nice of you to say so.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"Oh, no."},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对赞美的回应，应先表达感谢。句意：“今天你戴的这顶帽子好漂亮啊！”“谢谢。你这样说真是太好了。”","point":"表达赞美。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":1,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-c9f3d55decbeda12"},{"stem":"How great you won the first prize in the English competition! ______. But I made several terrible mistakes.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I think so"},{"key":"B","text":"Thank you very much"},{"key":"C","text":"You are welcome"},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"回应夸奖和祝贺，一般先表示感谢，再说明自己也犯了一些错误。句意：“你赢得英语竞赛一等奖，真是太棒了！”“非常感谢。但我犯了几个糟糕的错误。”","point":"表达感谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":2,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-69288c5976767e2e"},{"stem":"You've given us a wonderful dinner, Mrs. Smith. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Oh, I'm afraid I didn't cook very well."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm glad you enjoyed it."},{"key":"C","text":"Come again when you are free."},{"key":"D","text":"It's not necessary for you to say so."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方表达感谢，主人回应认可和接受：“你为我们准备的晚餐太棒了。”“我很高兴你们能喜欢。”","point":"表达感谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":3,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-fc14b98e58f8bfc2"},{"stem":"Thank you for all your hard work! ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can say that."},{"key":"B","text":"Why do you say so?"},{"key":"C","text":"No, thanks."},{"key":"D","text":"You're welcome!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方感谢时，用 You're welcome 表示“不客气”。句意：“感谢你所有的努力！”“不客气。”","point":"回应感谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":4,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-d333608dfef63d27"},{"stem":"Thank you for the beautiful gift you have prepared for us. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's right."},{"key":"B","text":"All right."},{"key":"C","text":"Are you serious?"},{"key":"D","text":"My pleasure."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方感谢礼物，应回答 My pleasure 或 You're welcome，表示“不客气”。句意：“谢谢你为我们准备的漂亮礼物。”“不客气。”","point":"回应感谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":5,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-fdad54238300afd7"},{"stem":"You've won the football game. Congratulations! ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't say so."},{"key":"B","text":"We are really lucky."},{"key":"C","text":"No one else could do it."},{"key":"D","text":"Oh, not really."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方表示祝贺，可谦虚回应“我们真幸运”。句意：“你们赢得了足球比赛。祝贺！”“我们真幸运。”","point":"表达祝贺。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":6,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-816d95c3a3cf7759"},{"stem":"I was worried about my maths, but Mr. Brown gave me an A. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't worry about it."},{"key":"B","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"C","text":"Mr. Brown is very good."},{"key":"D","text":"Good luck to you."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"听到对方取得好成绩，应表示祝贺。句意：“我一直担心我的数学，但布朗老师给了我一个 A。”“祝贺！”","point":"表达祝贺。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":7,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-e024f25e1648530a"},{"stem":"I'm leaving for Shanghai tomorrow. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"See you later."},{"key":"B","text":"Have a pleasant trip!"},{"key":"C","text":"Let's go out for a drink."},{"key":"D","text":"Nice meeting you."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方说即将去上海，应祝其旅途愉快。句意：“明天我要去上海。”“旅途愉快！”","point":"表达祝愿。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":8,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-8fca85c775be1c07"},{"stem":"I'm going to Beijing on a business trip tomorrow. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's a great deal."},{"key":"B","text":"See you later."},{"key":"C","text":"It's none of your business."},{"key":"D","text":"Have a good trip."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方说明即将去北京出差，回应“祝你旅途愉快”。","point":"表达祝愿。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":9,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-940dc6683ba20af2"},{"stem":"I've started my own software company. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Could you tell me who is the owner?"},{"key":"B","text":"No kidding! Congratulations!"},{"key":"C","text":"If I had the money, I'd start one."},{"key":"D","text":"My company runs well."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方告知开办软件公司的好消息，应表示惊讶和祝贺。句意：“我开了自己的软件公司。”“不是开玩笑吧！祝贺你！”","point":"表达祝贺。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":10,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-cbdf68da8e0e5555"},{"stem":"You know what? I've passed the exam. Oh, ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"what for?"},{"key":"B","text":"why not?"},{"key":"C","text":"congratulations!"},{"key":"D","text":"too bad!"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方通过考试，应表示祝贺。句意：“你知道吗？我通过了考试。”“哦，祝贺你！”","point":"表达祝贺。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":11,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-436bdb635956fb30"},{"stem":"Which one of these do you want? ______. Maybe either will be OK.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can say it again."},{"key":"B","text":"I don't care."},{"key":"C","text":"Come on."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm not sure."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对选项不确定，可说 I'm not sure（我不确定），再补充“可能哪个都可以”。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":12,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-565e2627233f14b1"},{"stem":"What do you think of these new mobile phones? Do you want to buy one? ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why"},{"key":"B","text":"What"},{"key":"C","text":"How"},{"key":"D","text":"How about it"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"页面将 Why? 解释为口语中的进一步追问“为什么”，用于问对方是否想买手机的原因。题干中的两句对话衔接略显生硬，复习时以页面给出的 A 为本题标准答案。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":13,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-1077ade3470e1d9a"},{"stem":"______? The one who is slim and wears a blue dress.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What's the lady?"},{"key":"B","text":"What's your English teacher like?"},{"key":"C","text":"Which girl do you want to see?"},{"key":"D","text":"What does your girlfriend look like?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"回答中的 The one 指定了具体的一个人，前句应问“你想见哪个女孩？”而非询问女友的外貌。句意：“你想见哪个女孩？”“那个身材苗条、穿蓝色裙子的女孩。”","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":14,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-3c338e886b4b626e"},{"stem":"How about going to dinner at the Italian restaurant tonight? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sorry."},{"key":"B","text":"That's great."},{"key":"C","text":"Forget it."},{"key":"D","text":"Glad you like it."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方提出今晚去意大利饭店吃饭的建议，用“太好了”表示赞同。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":15,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-642958db600dc99a"},{"stem":"English is very important in our daily life. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I dislike English."},{"key":"B","text":"It is interesting."},{"key":"C","text":"I couldn't agree more!"},{"key":"D","text":"It is difficult."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"“I couldn't agree more”表示非常同意，正好回应英语在日常生活中很重要这一观点。","point":"表达赞同。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":16,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-ff07ac586d52690c"},{"stem":"How did you enjoy the performance? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a good question."},{"key":"B","text":"It's up to you."},{"key":"C","text":"Perfect. It is attractive."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, you did well."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方询问对表演的看法，应给出评价：“完美，很吸引人。”","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":17,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-a83d30d2264ab600"},{"stem":"Could you please tell me which skirt suits me? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'd love to go to the mall."},{"key":"B","text":"Why don't you wear the pink one?"},{"key":"C","text":"The blue dress is in the closet."},{"key":"D","text":"The black suit is good."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方请你建议哪条裙子适合她，可以用“Why don't you ...?”提出穿粉色那条的建议。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":18,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-2f3b31e6af51944c"},{"stem":"What do you think of the documentary A Bite of China? ______. It has aroused great interest in Chinese food culture.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Enjoy yourself."},{"key":"B","text":"Many thanks."},{"key":"C","text":"Pretty good."},{"key":"D","text":"It's hard to say."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句肯定纪录片激发了对中国饮食文化的兴趣，前面应给出“相当好”的肯定评价。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":19,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-410d0531a171afb5"},{"stem":"What about having a drink? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Help yourself."},{"key":"B","text":"Good idea."},{"key":"C","text":"Go ahead, please."},{"key":"D","text":"Me, too."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方建议喝点饮料，答“好主意”表示赞同。","point":"征询意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":20,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-f690c806cdcb260d"},{"stem":"I don't have any change on me. Would you please pay the fare for me? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's right."},{"key":"B","text":"Nothing serious."},{"key":"C","text":"Don't mind."},{"key":"D","text":"No problem."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方请求帮忙支付车费，“No problem.”表示愿意帮忙。","point":"回应求助。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":21,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-c1bd3818bce2846c"},{"stem":"I wonder if I could use your computer tonight? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sure, go ahead."},{"key":"B","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"C","text":"Who cares?"},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方请求今晚借用电脑，“Sure, go ahead.”表示同意并允许使用。","point":"回应请求。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":22,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-dee3204b51970b8f"},{"stem":"Would you mind my turning on the heating system? The temperature goes too low. ______. I feel a little bit cold as well.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I'd love to."},{"key":"B","text":"Of course."},{"key":"C","text":"No, I don't care."},{"key":"D","text":"Of course not."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"“Would you mind ...?”问对方是否介意。后句说自己也有点冷，故应礼貌地说“当然不介意”。“Of course”表示介意，与语境相反。","point":"情景交际（对“Would you mind ...?”的应答）。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":23,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-f953cf250c3898b1"},{"stem":"Can I have a look at your letter, please? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Excuse me, you can't."},{"key":"B","text":"I can't agree with you."},{"key":"C","text":"You can say that again."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm afraid you can't."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方请求看信件，若要拒绝，应以“恐怕不行”委婉表达。","point":"提出请求。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":24,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-70d961b67e21d7f6"},{"stem":"Would you mind if I smoke here? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, go ahead."},{"key":"B","text":"No, I wouldn't mind at all."},{"key":"C","text":"No, you cannot smoke here."},{"key":"D","text":"You are a smoker!"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方询问是否介意在这里抽烟，回答“不，我一点也不介意”表示许可。注意回答的是“介不介意”，不能用“Yes, go ahead”混淆肯否。","point":"请求许可。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":25,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-3c1bfe2111f32c69"},{"stem":"May I have some more chicken? It's really delicious. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course. Help yourself."},{"key":"B","text":"More food, please."},{"key":"C","text":"Absolutely not."},{"key":"D","text":"It's yummy."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"客人想再吃一些鸡肉，主人答“当然，请自便”表示同意并请对方取用。","point":"回应食物续添请求。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":26,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-60206e71c9f5bd15"},{"stem":"What are the work hours of the library? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's open from 10a.m.to4p.m."},{"key":"B","text":"It opens at eleven in the morning."},{"key":"C","text":"It closes at seventeen in the afternoon."},{"key":"D","text":"It is open at twelve."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"问图书馆的开放时段，应回答完整的起止时间：上午10点到下午4点。选项原文的时间书写缺少空格，此处照录页面。","point":"询问信息。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":27,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-3d3f3b82c7334da6"},{"stem":"What is the distance between the two places? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The distance is not important."},{"key":"B","text":"We should care about it."},{"key":"C","text":"It is about 15 kilometers."},{"key":"D","text":"It is not far away."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"问两地之间的距离，应给出具体距离数值：大约15公里。","point":"询问距离。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":28,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-48e7f8c55f8e7276"},{"stem":"______? I am so glad that there was no traffic jam.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How have you been recently?"},{"key":"B","text":"How did you come over here?"},{"key":"C","text":"How was the traffic coming over here?"},{"key":"D","text":"How was the position?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"答语谈到“没有堵车”，前句应询问过来的交通状况。","point":"询问交通状况。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":29,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-53718a024709d482"},{"stem":"Hello, I'm Bill Wang from East Sea International. ______. Nice to meet you.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Thanks a lot, Bill."},{"key":"B","text":"What a pleasure, Bill."},{"key":"C","text":"You are welcome."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm Lucas Bowen from London."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"初次见面，对方先介绍自己，答话者也应自我介绍，然后说很高兴认识你。","point":"自我介绍。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":30,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-efecaa552365751b"},{"stem":"This is Kathy Chen, our Financial Officer. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Finance Officer is an important position."},{"key":"B","text":"OK. Let's go to see her."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm pleased to meet you, Kathy."},{"key":"D","text":"Thank you, Kathy."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"被介绍给财务主管 Kathy 后，应礼貌地问候并表示很高兴见到她。","point":"介绍与问候。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":31,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-872ed400dce500be"},{"stem":"Hello, this is 83788. ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How are you?"},{"key":"B","text":"Is that Mike?"},{"key":"C","text":"Can I take a message?"},{"key":"D","text":"Will you come tonight?"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"电话中确认对方身份，用“Is that ...?”询问“是……吗”。","point":"电话用语。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":32,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-c39f9245e5ca58ce"},{"stem":"Hello, may I speak to Mike? ______. May I ask who is calling?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm Mike."},{"key":"B","text":"This is Mike myself."},{"key":"C","text":"This is Mike speaking."},{"key":"D","text":"You are speaking to myself."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"电话中介绍自己用“This is ... speaking”。句意：你好，请找迈克接电话。——我就是迈克。请问您是哪位？","point":"电话用语。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":33,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-4bb8ffee2e8610a4"},{"stem":"Sorry, I made a mistake again. ______. Practise more, and you'll succeed.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take it easy."},{"key":"B","text":"Certainly not."},{"key":"C","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"D","text":"Don't blame yourself."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方因再次犯错而道歉，回应“别着急，慢慢来”，再鼓励多练习。句意：“对不起，我又犯错了。”“别着急，慢慢来。多多练习，你就能成功。”","point":"回应道歉。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":34,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-85e93597b35b9028"},{"stem":"I'm so sorry for stepping on your toes. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"B","text":"No, it's my fault."},{"key":"C","text":"You didn't hurt me at all."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, don't worry about it."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"“That's all right”表示没关系。句意：“对不起，踩到你的脚了。”“没关系。”","point":"回应道歉。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":35,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-20a4ac55dd95e263"},{"stem":"It's a pity but I have to tell you that I can't finish the book this week. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take your time."},{"key":"B","text":"That's right."},{"key":"C","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"D","text":"You are welcome."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"“Take your time”表示谅解和安慰，即“慢慢来”。句意：“很遗憾，我得告诉你这周我完不成这本书。”“慢慢来。”","point":"道歉用语。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":36,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-397e15ff63081d94"},{"stem":"I will go to the countryside to see my friend tomorrow, so I can't go shopping with you. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's my pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"You are welcome."},{"key":"C","text":"That's a pity."},{"key":"D","text":"Sure, I am."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方不能参加活动，表示遗憾。句意：“我明天去乡村看望朋友，所以我不能和你一起逛街了。”“真遗憾。”","point":"表达遗憾。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":37,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-01526f8c1cbea720"},{"stem":"The visit to Italy is fairly good, though we did have quite a lot of rain. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's a wonderful journey."},{"key":"B","text":"You must get wet."},{"key":"C","text":"It's a hard journey."},{"key":"D","text":"What a pity!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"虽然意大利之行相当不错，但确实下了不少雨，因此表示遗憾。句意：“意大利之行相当不错，尽管确实下了不少雨。”“真可惜！”","point":"表达遗憾。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":38,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-d0c40f94426ff3dd"},{"stem":"Though everyone played well, we lost the game. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's what I expected."},{"key":"B","text":"Congratulations."},{"key":"C","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"D","text":"I'm sorry."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"听到对方输了比赛，应表示遗憾。句意：“虽然每个人都打得很好，但我们还是输了比赛。”“真可惜！”","point":"表达遗憾。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":39,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-32334e9a4c305c2d"},{"stem":"Stop, sir. Please show me your driving license. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You'll regret for it."},{"key":"B","text":"Certainly, here you are."},{"key":"C","text":"I'll remember to bring it."},{"key":"D","text":"I insist on taking this way."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"警察要求出示驾照，应礼貌配合：“当然，给您。”A过于强硬，C的时态与“现在出示”不符，D与话题无关。句意：“停车，先生。请出示您的驾照。”“当然，给您。”","point":"情景交际。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":40,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-eda62c486674e5b9"},{"stem":"I love the Internet. I've come to know many friends on the Net. ______. Few of them would become your real friends.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's for sure."},{"key":"B","text":"It's not the case."},{"key":"C","text":"I couldn't agree more."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm pleased to know that."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"“It's not the case”表示“事实并非如此”，用于否定前面的观点。句意：“我喜欢互联网，已在网上认识很多朋友。”“事实并非如此，其中很少有人会成为你真正的朋友。”","point":"表达相反观点。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":41,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-1a7bd3274565c769"},{"stem":"Are you ready to buy a car, Sir? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"B","text":"Please don't buy it."},{"key":"C","text":"No, don't mention it."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I'd like to have a Jeep."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"明确表达购买意向。句意：“先生，您准备买车吗？”“是的，我想买一辆吉普车。”","point":"回应购买意向。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":42,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-e61306120b940569"},{"stem":"What do you do on the Internet? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I like the Internet."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, I will buy clothes on the Internet."},{"key":"C","text":"I don't like the Internet."},{"key":"D","text":"I often buy something I need."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"问“你在网上做什么”，应回答具体行为：“我经常买我需要的东西。”","point":"回答日常活动。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":43,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-d115472e017da4b4"},{"stem":"How do you calculate the cost of moving? Well, ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"we are professional movers."},{"key":"B","text":"the cost depends on the floor you are moving to."},{"key":"C","text":"the cost has been cut by 30 to 50 percent."},{"key":"D","text":"the cost is still too high."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"问搬家费用如何计算，回答费用取决于搬到哪一层楼，解释了计费依据。句意：“你们搬家费用怎么计算？”“嗯，费用取决于你搬到哪一层楼。”","point":"解释计费方式。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":44,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-4f4fdc7f51cbbbbd"},{"stem":"Excuse me, would you please show me the way to the hospital? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Go forward, please."},{"key":"B","text":"Just go on and on."},{"key":"C","text":"Where shall we go?"},{"key":"D","text":"I know it."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方询问去医院的路，应给出明确的指路信息：“请往前走。”","point":"问路与指路。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":45,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-e9bc79aed2a45a04"},{"stem":"Sir, how do you like your steak cooked? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Wonderful."},{"key":"B","text":"Medium, please."},{"key":"C","text":"It's delicious."},{"key":"D","text":"Three, please."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"问牛排要几分熟，回答“Medium, please”（五分熟，谢谢）。","point":"餐厅点餐用语。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":46,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-35c7875120cbe2f9"},{"stem":"Er, can you show me the schedule? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sure, I'll give you a hand."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, a tight schedule as usual."},{"key":"C","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"D","text":"Hum, not too bad."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方请求看日程表，回应同意并提供帮助。句意：“呃，你能给我看一下日程表吗？”“当然，我来帮你。”","point":"回应请求。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":47,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-58dae084a27e17af"},{"stem":"Cheer up, and things will be much better. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"My pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"I won't believe your words."},{"key":"C","text":"It's OK."},{"key":"D","text":"Thank you very much."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方安慰、鼓励时，礼貌表示感谢。句意：“振作起来，事情会好起来的。”“非常感谢。”","point":"回应安慰与鼓励。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":48,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-578b8a5403eca32c"},{"stem":"Sorry to interrupt your phone call. This is a library, and you are talking too loudly. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm sorry."},{"key":"B","text":"Am I talking quietly?"},{"key":"C","text":"That's OK."},{"key":"D","text":"You are welcome."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"被提醒在图书馆说话太大声时，应表示歉意。句意：“抱歉打断你打电话。这里是图书馆，你说话太大声了。”“对不起。”","point":"回应提醒与道歉。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":49,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-3994df349e2da0d6"},{"stem":"Would you like to walk around with me? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's good for you."},{"key":"B","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"C","text":"So do"},{"key":"D","text":"That's a good idea."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对散步邀请表示肯定：“好主意。”句意：“你愿意和我一起散步吗？”“好主意。”","point":"回应邀请。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":50,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-268ed948f5ce33cc"},{"stem":"Please don't talk loudly in the library. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"So what?"},{"key":"B","text":"I'm sorry."},{"key":"C","text":"That's all."},{"key":"D","text":"Not at all."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"被提醒不要在图书馆大声说话，应表示歉意：“对不起。”","point":"回应提醒/道歉。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":51,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-88c6fa55801ddf89"},{"stem":"How is your essay going? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I see your point."},{"key":"B","text":"I really appreciate it."},{"key":"C","text":"Well, I am running a little behind."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm pretty busy this morning."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"问论文写作进展，应说明进度：“嗯，我有点落后了。”","point":"回应进展询问。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":52,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-5f20a601347d2bec"},{"stem":"Henry, I think Team Tiger will win the game. ______. I think Team Bull will.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I don't think so."},{"key":"B","text":"I hope so."},{"key":"C","text":"Neither do"},{"key":"D","text":"Me too."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"后句认为公牛队会赢，因此先表示不赞同前面的“老虎队会赢”。句意：“亨利，我认为老虎队会赢得比赛。”“我不这么认为。我认为公牛队会赢。”","point":"表达不同意见。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":53,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-5c88c8d6a304210f"},{"stem":"Excuse me, but could I ask you how to go to the train station? ______. Will you walk or take a bus?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I know."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"I am sure."},{"key":"D","text":"Let me see."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"回答指路前，先说“让我想想”，再询问对方步行还是乘公交。句意：“打扰一下，请问去火车站怎么走？”“让我想想。您步行还是坐公交？”","point":"指路前的回应。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":54,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-b44f7ced6d1e1b8c"},{"stem":"Well done! Your English writing is good. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's hard to say."},{"key":"B","text":"Thank you."},{"key":"C","text":"No, my English is poor."},{"key":"D","text":"Sorry, I don't think so."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方表扬英语写作好，应礼貌表示感谢。句意：“做得好！你的英语写作很好。”“谢谢。”","point":"回应表扬。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":55,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-f8ffa9fbdae6c3c0"},{"stem":"Welcome to Lens Magic. What can I do for you? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Let me alone, please."},{"key":"B","text":"I'd like to buy a digital camera."},{"key":"C","text":"I'll contact you if there is a digital camera."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm just looking for a digital camera online."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"店员询问需要什么帮助，顾客表达购买意向：“我想买一台数码相机。”","point":"购物用语。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":56,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-e1c186ae240bbdf3"},{"stem":"I haven't seen Billy for 10 years. ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Either have"},{"key":"B","text":"So have"},{"key":"C","text":"Haven't"},{"key":"D","text":"Neither have I"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"前句为否定句，表示“我也没有”用 Neither 引导倒装，助动词与前句一致：Neither have I。句意：“我已经十年没见过比利了。”“我也没有。”","point":"情景交际（So / Neither 引导的倒装结构）。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":57,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-29253880e6bd1615"},{"stem":"What would you like, tea or coffee? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I would."},{"key":"B","text":"Coffee, please."},{"key":"C","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"D","text":"It's very nice."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"茶或咖啡的选择疑问句，应明确选一项：“咖啡，谢谢。”","point":"选择疑问句。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":58,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-faf54415e7ce0975"},{"stem":"Do you know who telephoned me? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I heard it was Sally."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, I remember it now."},{"key":"C","text":"No, I didn't phone you."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I know you well."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"问谁打了电话，直接回答来电者：“我听说是萨莉。”","point":"宾语从句。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":59,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-3b53cd07b61f93e3"},{"stem":"Excuse me, how far is the airport from here? ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can take a taxi."},{"key":"B","text":"It is about thirty miles."},{"key":"C","text":"I'll fly to Sydney."},{"key":"D","text":"It is only six hundred dollars."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"问机场距离这里多远，应回答具体距离：“大概30英里。”","point":"询问距离。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":60,"group":"交际用语","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-66ce491a48d0dd42"},{"stem":"How long do you think ______ to finish this urgent task?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did it take you"},{"key":"B","text":"it will take you"},{"key":"C","text":"will it take you"},{"key":"D","text":"it to take you"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"“It takes + 人 + 时间 + to do”表示做某事花费多长时间。在 how long 引起的特殊疑问句中，do you think 后用陈述语序。句意：“你认为要花费多长时间完成这项紧急任务？”","point":"it takes 句式。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":1,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-3167c00d6d97caa2"},{"stem":"Wealth, education and occupation vary greatly ______ members of the middle class.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"among"},{"key":"B","text":"between"},{"key":"C","text":"from"},{"key":"D","text":"inside"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"among 表示在三者或以上“之间”；句中指中产阶级的众多成员，故用 among。句意：“中产阶级成员之间财富、教育和职业差异很大。”","point":"介词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":2,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-db6bd800cd2a56e0"},{"stem":"Let's buy our tickets while I still have ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a little money to save"},{"key":"B","text":"little money left"},{"key":"C","text":"a few dollars left"},{"key":"D","text":"few dollars to spend"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"“a few dollars left”表示“还剩一些美元”，符合题意。句意：“我们买票吧，我还剩下几美元。”","point":"词汇搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":3,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-296f7e29eddaa6ea"},{"stem":"______ was not the way the event happened.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Which the press reported"},{"key":"B","text":"That the press reported"},{"key":"C","text":"What did the press report"},{"key":"D","text":"What the press reported"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主语从句由 what 引导，使用陈述语序。句意：“媒体报道的内容与事件发生情况不一致。”","point":"主语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":4,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-0f0ee2da14b7dcc5"},{"stem":"People do not like those who are always ______ the way of others.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"by"},{"key":"C","text":"in"},{"key":"D","text":"behind"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"固定词组 in the way 表示“挡道、造成障碍”。句意：“人们不喜欢总是给别人造成障碍的人。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":5,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-ba1fa93c2234c1e3"},{"stem":"At first we were ______ amused by Don's words, but soon we were tired of them.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"great"},{"key":"B","text":"far"},{"key":"C","text":"much"},{"key":"D","text":"never"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"much 作副词，表示“非常”，可修饰形容词化的过去分词 amused。句意：“起初，我们觉得唐的话非常有趣，但很快就厌倦了。”","point":"副词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":6,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-c22674412ab6d8a3"},{"stem":"He talks as if he ______ everything in the world.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"knows"},{"key":"B","text":"knew"},{"key":"C","text":"had known"},{"key":"D","text":"would have known"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"as if 引导的从句与现在事实相反，用一般过去时。句意：“他侃侃而谈，好像他了解世界上的一切。”","point":"虚拟语气。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":7,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-3dd2281e55cd9608"},{"stem":"The doctor advised that Mr. Malan ______ an operation right away so as to save his life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had"},{"key":"B","text":"would have"},{"key":"C","text":"have"},{"key":"D","text":"was going to have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"advise 后的宾语从句使用虚拟语气，形式为 (should) + 动词原形，should 可省略。句意：“医生建议马兰先生立刻进行手术，以挽救他的生命。”","point":"虚拟语气。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":8,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-2fba6379a1faa462"},{"stem":"He forgot about ______ him to attend my wife's birthday party.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I asking"},{"key":"B","text":"my asking"},{"key":"C","text":"me to ask"},{"key":"D","text":"me ask"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"forget about 后接动名词；名词前可用物主代词修饰。句意：“他忘记了我请他参加我妻子的生日聚会这件事。”","point":"动名词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":9,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-c67348fc5776270e"},{"stem":"So little ______ about stock exchange that the lecture was completely beyond me.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did I know"},{"key":"B","text":"I had known"},{"key":"C","text":"I knew"},{"key":"D","text":"was I known"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"little 位于句首，句子使用部分倒装。句意：“我对股票交易了解太少，以至于我完全听不懂这个讲座。”","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":10,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-170eadb326635317"},{"stem":"The boy's laziness ______ his failure in the exams.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"occurred to"},{"key":"B","text":"brought in"},{"key":"C","text":"resulted in"},{"key":"D","text":"led into"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"result in 表示“导致”，符合因果关系。句意：“男孩的懒惰导致了他考试不及格。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":11,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-d24d0b80436658f7"},{"stem":"Only guests of the hotel enjoy the ______ of using the private beach.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"privilege"},{"key":"B","text":"possibility"},{"key":"C","text":"favor"},{"key":"D","text":"advantage"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"privilege 表示“特权”，符合句意。句意：“只有酒店的客人才享有使用私人海滩的特权。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":12,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-4e16f6ca3c0e9cb4"},{"stem":"Tom ______ more than twenty pounds for the dictionary.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"spent"},{"key":"B","text":"paid"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"took"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"paid 与 for 搭配，表示“为……付款”。句意：“汤姆花了二十多英镑购买这本词典。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":13,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-5e2daf1e10f67956"},{"stem":"The governor had to ______ all his appointments for the day and rush to the train accident.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"set off"},{"key":"B","text":"pay off"},{"key":"C","text":"see off"},{"key":"D","text":"call off"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"call off 表示“取消”。句意：“州长不得不取消当天的所有预约，并赶往火车事故现场。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":14,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-1abf77221dcefb0b"},{"stem":"One car went too fast and ______ missed hitting another car.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"completely"},{"key":"B","text":"greatly"},{"key":"C","text":"narrowly"},{"key":"D","text":"little"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"narrowly 表示“勉强地”，narrowly missed 即“险些撞上但最终避开”。句意：“一辆小轿车开得飞快，差一点儿就撞到了另一辆车。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":15,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-810ace735e9f11ed"},{"stem":"When you ______ this over with her, how did she react?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"talk"},{"key":"B","text":"talked"},{"key":"C","text":"will talk"},{"key":"D","text":"talking"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句 how did she react 使用一般过去时，从句描述此前的交谈，也用一般过去时。talk sth. over with sb. 表示“与某人讨论某事”。句意：“当你和她仔细讨论这件事时，她作何反应？”","point":"一般过去时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":16,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-f53a7acfe75e67b3"},{"stem":"The flowers were all that remained: ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"two yellow little"},{"key":"B","text":"little two yellow"},{"key":"C","text":"yellow two little"},{"key":"D","text":"two little yellow"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"形容词顺序为“数量、大小、颜色”。句意：“两朵小黄花是留存下来的一切。”原题的空格只有形容词短语，按页面原文记录。","point":"形容词的次序。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":17,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-497a461441699758"},{"stem":"The pain will go away ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"by and by"},{"key":"B","text":"by and chance"},{"key":"C","text":"all over"},{"key":"D","text":"at present"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"by and by 表示“不久”。句意：“痛苦不久后会消散的。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":18,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-11abc060f9b6f0ee"},{"stem":"I'm far from ______ with what you have done.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pleased"},{"key":"B","text":"pleasing"},{"key":"C","text":"pleasure"},{"key":"D","text":"pleasant"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"far from pleased 表示“非常不满意”。句意：“我对你所作所为非常不满意。”","point":"常见搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":19,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-ce109b2171edaa68"},{"stem":"The ability ______ is very important for any speaker.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to hear clearly"},{"key":"B","text":"to be clearly heard"},{"key":"C","text":"to hearing clearly"},{"key":"D","text":"to being clearly heard"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"不定式的被动结构 to be + 过去分词表示“被清楚地听到”。句意：“能够让别人清楚聆听的能力对任何演讲者来说都很重要。”","point":"非谓语动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":20,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-7ed93713b5a27044"},{"stem":"______ she finds out that you've lost her books?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As if"},{"key":"B","text":"Even if"},{"key":"C","text":"What if"},{"key":"D","text":"Suppose that"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"What if 表示“如果……怎么办”。句意：“如果她发现你弄丢了她的书怎么办？”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":21,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-0d696d8ce0e4cb3c"},{"stem":"Dr. Robert went to New York, gave a few lectures and ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"visiting his daughter"},{"key":"B","text":"to visit his daughter"},{"key":"C","text":"visit his daughter"},{"key":"D","text":"visited his daughter"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"and 连接的并列谓语应保持一致，went、gave、visited 都用过去式。句意：“罗伯特博士去了纽约，做了几个讲座，看望了他的女儿。”","point":"并列谓语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":22,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-a4cb89d23e5bfb19"},{"stem":"Are you serious in ______ such a view?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"putting on"},{"key":"B","text":"putting off"},{"key":"C","text":"putting up"},{"key":"D","text":"putting forward"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"put forward 表示“提出”。句意：“你是严肃地提出这样的观点吗？”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":23,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-51a881fc40618e10"},{"stem":"The plane crashed, its bombs ______ as it hit the ground.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"exploded"},{"key":"B","text":"were exploded"},{"key":"C","text":"exploding"},{"key":"D","text":"were exploding"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"独立主格结构中，名词 its bombs 后用现在分词表示主动。句意：“飞机坠毁了，在撞击地面时炸弹爆炸了。”","point":"独立主格结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":24,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-20b77e3dfa4d5294"},{"stem":"You should be content ______ what you have.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to"},{"key":"B","text":"about"},{"key":"C","text":"with"},{"key":"D","text":"for"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"be content with 表示“对……满意”。句意：“你应该对你拥有的一切感到满意。”","point":"常见搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":25,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-9f2779454fdfd225"},{"stem":"Do you like to ride on the old bus to school? Yes, I prefer it ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to walk"},{"key":"B","text":"to walking"},{"key":"C","text":"walking"},{"key":"D","text":"having walked"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"prefer sth. to sth. 表示“比起……更喜欢……”，这里的 to 是介词，后接动名词。句意：“你喜欢乘那辆旧公共汽车上学吗？是的，比起走路，我更喜欢乘公共汽车。”","point":"prefer 的用法。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":26,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-e69bcd30ae5c53a4"},{"stem":"My vacation begins next Tuesday, ______ I will leave for Florida.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"while"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"when 表示“在那时”，指代前面的 next Tuesday，引导定语从句。句意：“我的假期要在下周二开始，那时我将要出发去佛罗里达。”","point":"when 引导的定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":27,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-ed71cbeedff6f111"},{"stem":"This is the dictionary you're looking for, ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"isn't this"},{"key":"B","text":"isn't it"},{"key":"C","text":"isn't that"},{"key":"D","text":"isn't there"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"陈述句的主语为 this，反意疑问部分的主语用 it。句意：“这就是你一直在找的词典，是吗？”","point":"反意疑问句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":28,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-d3b683e1b228c461"},{"stem":"Though he is very intelligent, he is very modest, ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hence"},{"key":"B","text":"otherwise"},{"key":"C","text":"nevertheless"},{"key":"D","text":"therefore"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"nevertheless 表示“然而”，表达转折。句意：“他尽管很聪明，但是非常谦虚。”原题同时用了 though 和 nevertheless，按页面答案记录。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":29,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-af849032c0719ecc"},{"stem":"Lack of imagination is an obstacle ______ one's advancement.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to"},{"key":"B","text":"of"},{"key":"C","text":"for"},{"key":"D","text":"about"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"obstacle to 表示“……的障碍”。句意：“缺乏想象力是一个人进步的障碍。”","point":"介词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":30,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-5126148564eec54b"},{"stem":"About two thirds of the students ______ the meeting yesterday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attended"},{"key":"B","text":"attend"},{"key":"C","text":"attends"},{"key":"D","text":"was attending"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"yesterday 是一般过去时的标志，attend 的过去式是 attended。句意：“昨天大约有三分之二的学生参加了会议。”","point":"一般过去时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":31,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-c2768a62971affc5"},{"stem":"They got there an hour ______ than others.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"early"},{"key":"B","text":"much early"},{"key":"C","text":"more early"},{"key":"D","text":"earlier"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"than 标志比较级，early 的比较级是 earlier。句意：“他们比其他人早到了一个小时。”","point":"比较等级。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":32,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-9cbec1911730dd79"},{"stem":"Please ______ the names and numbers when you have got the list.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"check out"},{"key":"B","text":"check on"},{"key":"C","text":"check in"},{"key":"D","text":"check up"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"check out sth. 表示“查明、查实，核实是否正确”；check on 强调核查情况，check in 是签到，check up 常指体检。句意：“当收到名单时，请你查明姓名和号码。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":33,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-347b1d4682b10e61"},{"stem":"Hua Luogeng was a ______ mathematician.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"previous"},{"key":"B","text":"proper"},{"key":"C","text":"prevailing"},{"key":"D","text":"prominent"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"prominent 表示“杰出的”，修饰 mathematician；previous 是“以前的”，proper 是“合适的”，prevailing 是“流行的、占优势的”。句意：“华罗庚是一位杰出的数学家。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":34,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-ab2c874ae715e168"},{"stem":"You can go out, ______ you promise to be back before 12 o'clock.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so far as"},{"key":"B","text":"as far as"},{"key":"C","text":"as long as"},{"key":"D","text":"as soon as"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"as long as 表示“只要”，引导条件状语从句；as soon as 表示“一……就……”。句意：“只要你承诺 12 点之前回来，你就可以出去。”","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":35,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-347c897d8022b2bb"},{"stem":"Old and young people learn from each other and ______ each other.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"encourage"},{"key":"B","text":"enhance"},{"key":"C","text":"endeavor"},{"key":"D","text":"encounter"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"encourage 表示“鼓励”，与 each other 搭配表示“彼此鼓励”；enhance 是“提高”，endeavor 是“努力”，encounter 是“偶然遇见”。句意：“老年人和年轻人互相学习，彼此鼓励。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":36,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-4ce153188813461f"},{"stem":"The experiment ______ successfully.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has done"},{"key":"B","text":"has been done"},{"key":"C","text":"had been done"},{"key":"D","text":"had done"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"experiment 与 do 之间为被动关系，应用被动语态；题目没有明显的过去完成时标志，故选现在完成时的被动结构 has been done。句意：“实验已经成功完成了。”","point":"被动语态。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":37,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-13cdbdd7a8a573d0"},{"stem":"If the soldiers ______ the military orders, they would have taken over the city last week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"followed"},{"key":"B","text":"could follow"},{"key":"C","text":"had followed"},{"key":"D","text":"could have followed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"这是与过去事实相反的虚拟条件句。主句用 would have + 过去分词，if 从句用过去完成时 had followed。句意：“如果士兵们服从了军令，他们上周就能占领这座城市了。”","point":"虚拟语气。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":38,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-45b8b39894b5c4d7"},{"stem":"The capital city is growing quickly, but ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so is the city's crime rate"},{"key":"B","text":"so the city's crime rate is"},{"key":"C","text":"so does the city's crime rate"},{"key":"D","text":"so do the city's crime rates"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"so + 助动词 + 主语表示“也如此”；前句用现在进行时 is growing，后句用 is 与之呼应。句意：“首都发展迅速，但是城市的犯罪率也迅速增长了。”","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":39,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-a76a1bd53e3c8c87"},{"stem":"The boy thinks that he should play up his strong points and ______ his weaknesses.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"maximize"},{"key":"B","text":"strengthen"},{"key":"C","text":"minimize"},{"key":"D","text":"decrease"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"play up his strong points 表示突出自己的优势；与之相对，minimize his weaknesses 表示尽量弱化自己的弱点。句意：“男孩认为他应该扬长避短。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":40,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-578ff40d399474be"},{"stem":"Children tend to copy the behaviour of others whom they admire or ______ with.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"identify"},{"key":"B","text":"recognize"},{"key":"C","text":"emphasize"},{"key":"D","text":"justify"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"identify with 表示“认同”，与 admire 构成意义上的并列。句意：“孩子们倾向于模仿他们崇拜或认同的人的行为。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":41,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-dd80f79d14313e57"},{"stem":"Ryle explained the ______ for his sudden return to London.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cause"},{"key":"B","text":"excuse"},{"key":"C","text":"reason"},{"key":"D","text":"truth"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"表示“……的原因”时用 reason for。句意：“赖尔解释了他突然返回伦敦的原因。”","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":42,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-775b1e43a332cdd6"},{"stem":"When I was your age, attending on-campus concerts ______ part of the pleasure of college life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"are"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"was"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"when 从句用过去时，主句也用过去时；动名词短语 attending on-campus concerts 作主语视为单数，故用 was。句意：“我在你这个年纪的时候，参加校园音乐会是大学生活乐趣的一部分。”","point":"主谓一致与时态。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态","主谓一致","非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":43,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-5c54c9f83fb8b77a"},{"stem":"You must have lived here for a long time, ______ you?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"mustn't"},{"key":"B","text":"needn't"},{"key":"C","text":"hadn't"},{"key":"D","text":"haven't"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"must have done 在此表示对过去情况的推测，反意疑问部分按实际谓语 have lived 来确定；没有明确的过去时间状语，用 haven't you。句意：“你一定在这里生活了很长时间了，是吗？”","point":"反意疑问句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":44,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-f549552f9e5120b8"},{"stem":"The short break will give both of you time to think and really listen to each other, ______ is very important.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"what"},{"key":"B","text":"which"},{"key":"C","text":"who"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"非限制性定语从句用 which 指代前面整个事件：短暂休息让双方有时间思考并认真倾听彼此，这一点非常重要。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":45,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-767e5a79493ab978"},{"stem":"As a nurse, ______ important that you get to know the patients in your care, their daily habits, likes and dislikes, etc.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"who is"},{"key":"B","text":"what is"},{"key":"C","text":"it is"},{"key":"D","text":"that is"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"固定句式 It is + 形容词 + that 从句中，it 为形式主语，that 从句是真正主语。句意：作为护士，了解所照顾病人的日常习惯和喜恶很重要。","point":"形式主语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":46,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-5cb7d7e8e1bca6fc"},{"stem":"The customer service representatives often allow customers to exchange the item or return it for a full ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reform"},{"key":"B","text":"refund"},{"key":"C","text":"refusal"},{"key":"D","text":"refreshment"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"refund 是“退款”，a full refund 为“全额退款”。reform 是“改革”，refusal 是“拒绝”，refreshment 是“茶点”。句意：客服代表通常允许顾客换货或退货并获得全额退款。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":47,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-78a33e1e8c1788ba"},{"stem":"It ______ last night, or the ground wouldn't be so wet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rain"},{"key":"B","text":"being"},{"key":"C","text":"rained"},{"key":"D","text":"must have rained"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"根据地面现在很湿，推测昨晚肯定下过雨。must have done 表示对过去事情的肯定推测。句意：昨晚肯定下雨了，否则地面不会这么湿。","point":"情态动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":48,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-20d7be5d7aa44d90"},{"stem":"If you do not advertise more widely, your ______ will not get other potential employees.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"absence"},{"key":"B","text":"vacancy"},{"key":"C","text":"candidate"},{"key":"D","text":"comment"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"absence“缺席”；vacancy“空位、空缺职位”；candidate“候选人”；comment“评论”。本题谈论职场招聘，vacancy 符合句意。句意：如果你不更为广泛地宣传，你的空缺职位将招不到其他潜在雇员。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":49,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-74671e8454679ba8"},{"stem":"Unfortunately, ______ bad weather, this year's show has been canceled.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"due to"},{"key":"B","text":"despite"},{"key":"C","text":"because"},{"key":"D","text":"since"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"空后是名词短语 bad weather，表示原因，选介词短语 due to。because 和 since 作连词引导从句；despite 表“尽管”，语义不合。句意：由于天气恶劣，今年的展览已被取消。","point":"介词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":50,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-a4721a5c9611a92a"},{"stem":"Both sides should ______ their proposals before they get down to trading.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"put down"},{"key":"B","text":"put away"},{"key":"C","text":"put forward"},{"key":"D","text":"put off"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"put down 表示“写下、记录”，put away 表示“储存”，put forward 表示“提出”，put off 表示“推迟”。put forward 与 proposals 搭配，意为“提出建议”。句意：双方都应该在开始交易前提出他们的建议。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":51,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-1ceb9b1f9d260711"},{"stem":"The lack of management may ______ financial problems.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"relate to"},{"key":"B","text":"lead to"},{"key":"C","text":"result from"},{"key":"D","text":"react to"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"lead to 表示“导致、通向”；result from 表示“由……产生”，方向相反。主语“管理不力”是原因，后接结果“财务问题”，因此选择 lead to。句意：管理不力可能导致财务问题。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":52,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-497f3e3bd2137a42"},{"stem":"He ______ to work by bus, but now he drives.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"used to go"},{"key":"B","text":"is used to going"},{"key":"C","text":"is used to go"},{"key":"D","text":"used to going"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"used to + 动词原形表示“过去常常做某事”；be used to + 动名词表示“习惯于做某事”；be used to + 动词原形表示“被用来做某事”。but now 表示与过去相反。句意：他过去常坐公交车去上班，但现在开车。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":53,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-d4c1f24178aff123"},{"stem":"Communication plays an important role in a ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"negotiation"},{"key":"B","text":"irrigation"},{"key":"C","text":"immigration"},{"key":"D","text":"reputation"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"negotiation“谈判”；irrigation“灌溉”；immigration“移民”；reputation“声望”。沟通在谈判中发挥重要作用。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":54,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-244aa6dd4551f48b"},{"stem":"______ is always a good way to get relaxation and refreshment.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Taken a vacation"},{"key":"B","text":"Taking a vacation"},{"key":"C","text":"Took a vacation"},{"key":"D","text":"Take a vacation"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"本题考查非谓语动词中动名词的使用。动名词短语 taking a vacation 在句中作主语。句意：度假是放松和恢复活力的好方法。","point":"非谓语动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":55,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-bd42cac535fcff89"},{"stem":"You should be prepared ______ your customer turns down your proposals by having a second plan to fall back on.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in favor of"},{"key":"B","text":"in view of"},{"key":"C","text":"despite"},{"key":"D","text":"in case"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"in favor of 表示“赞同、支持”，in view of 表示“考虑到”，despite 表示“尽管”，in case 表示“万一”。空格后接“客户拒绝你的提议”，表示预防的情况，选择 in case，引导从句。句意：你应该准备好备用方案，以防客户拒绝你的提议。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":56,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-6d1bf9c12e95705f"},{"stem":"The newly-designed advertisement ______ a higher click-through rate by the end of next month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have brought about"},{"key":"B","text":"will have brought about"},{"key":"C","text":"brought about"},{"key":"D","text":"brings about"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"“by the end of next month”是将来的某个时间点，用将来完成时 will have done，表示到那时已经完成。句意：新设计的广告将在下月底前带来更高的点击量。","point":"将来完成时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":57,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-58d1c9b63ababd31"},{"stem":"If you ______ eye contact, the other person might think you are covering something or you are distrustful.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will avoid"},{"key":"B","text":"avoided"},{"key":"C","text":"avoid"},{"key":"D","text":"had avoided"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"if 引导真实条件状语从句，主句为 might think，从句用一般现在时表示条件。句意：如果你避开眼神交流，对方可能认为你在掩盖什么，或者你不诚实。","point":"条件状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句","交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":58,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-a4113d46452f17fb"},{"stem":"It ______ only 13 hours for sales on just two online sites, Taobao and Tmall, to fly past last year's overall total of 19.1 billion yuan.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cost"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"spent"},{"key":"D","text":"expanded"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It takes + 时间 + to do sth. 表示“做某事花费多长时间”。这里表达销售额超过去年的总额仅用13小时。cost 常以物为主语，表示花钱；spend 常以人为主语。句意：在淘宝和天猫这两个线上平台，销售额突破去年191亿元的总成绩，仅用了13个小时。","point":"词汇辨析（形近／近义动词）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":59,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-a747472a099318d3"},{"stem":"No matter ______, the little sisters managed to round the sheep up and drive them back home safely.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"how it was snowing hard"},{"key":"B","text":"how hard was it snowing"},{"key":"C","text":"how it was hard snowing"},{"key":"D","text":"how hard it was snowing"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"no matter how + 形容词／副词 + 句子的其他部分；hard 修饰 snowing，且从句用陈述语序，所以是 how hard it was snowing。句意：无论雪下得多么大，小姐妹们都努力把羊赶到一起，并安全赶回家。","point":"让步状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":60,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-9f0b8997040560d7"},{"stem":"The scientist spoke confidently, ______ impressed me most.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"which"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"how"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"逗号后为非限制性定语从句，which 作主语，指代前面“科学家讲话自信”这件事；that 不用于非限制性定语从句。句意：科学家讲话很自信，这给我留下深刻印象。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":61,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-30280b0463b83163"},{"stem":"Mary did not have time to go to the concert last night because she was busy ______ for her examination.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to prepare"},{"key":"B","text":"to be prepared"},{"key":"C","text":"preparing"},{"key":"D","text":"prepared"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"be busy doing sth. 表示“忙于做某事”，后面接动名词；be busy with sth. 后面接名词。句意：玛丽昨晚没有时间去音乐会，因为她忙于准备考试。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":62,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-85e3b14808d622a5"},{"stem":"I ______ to know how often the bus runs during rush hour.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"occur"},{"key":"B","text":"happen"},{"key":"C","text":"agree"},{"key":"D","text":"arise"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"happen to do sth. 表示“碰巧做某事”。occur 不接不定式（常用 occur to sb.）；agree 虽可接不定式，但意思不合；arise 也不接不定式。句意：我碰巧知道高峰时段公交车多久发一趟车。","point":"词汇辨析（动词词义及固定搭配）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":63,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-bc9fe7d8eb75d15c"},{"stem":"It is ______ an interesting story that I want to read it again.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"So"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"how"},{"key":"D","text":"such"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"such + a/an + 形容词 + 可数名词单数 + that 为固定结构。若用 so，须改为 so interesting a story；what 和 how 用于感叹句，不引导此类结果状语从句。句意：这是一个如此有趣的故事，以至于我想再读一遍。","point":"状语从句（such...that 与 so...that 的辨析）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句","词汇与搭配","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":64,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-c0354bab2cfefb18"},{"stem":"All things ______, the planned flight will have to be canceled.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be considered"},{"key":"B","text":"considered"},{"key":"C","text":"be considering"},{"key":"D","text":"considering"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"独立主格结构由“名词／代词＋非谓语动词”构成。all things 与 consider 之间是动宾关系，应用表示被动的过去分词。句意：综合各方面考虑，原计划航班将不得不取消。","point":"独立主格。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":65,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-76d0b8b03cf6f92f"},{"stem":"The BBC has just successfully demonstrated a ______ radio transmission system.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"direct"},{"key":"B","text":"diplomatic"},{"key":"C","text":"digital"},{"key":"D","text":"diligent"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"direct“直接的”；diplomatic“外交的”；digital“数字的”；diligent“勤奋的”。digital 与 radio transmission system 搭配，表示“数字无线电传输系统”。句意：BBC广播公司成功展示了一套数字无线电传输系统。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":66,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-8db6a9e13f1b637b"},{"stem":"You ______ Harry Potter, since I remember once you discussed its main plot with Cathy.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could have watched"},{"key":"B","text":"should have watched"},{"key":"C","text":"might have watched"},{"key":"D","text":"must have watched"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"must have done 表示对过去某个动作的肯定推测。后文“我记得你曾经和凯西讨论过它的主要情节”是推测依据。句意：你过去一定看过《哈利·波特》，因为我记得你曾经和凯西讨论过它的主要情节。","point":"情态动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":67,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-442b88ad1b28ede7"},{"stem":"We trust that this new product of ours will ______ to your market.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"appeal"},{"key":"B","text":"appear"},{"key":"C","text":"appease"},{"key":"D","text":"appreciate"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"appeal“吸引”，appeal to 表示“对……有吸引力”；appear“出现”；appease“安抚”；appreciate“感激、欣赏”。句意：我们相信我们的这款新产品将吸引你们的市场。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":68,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-794352a743be4fcc"},{"stem":"Under no circumstances ______ to tell lies to parents.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"children are allowed"},{"key":"B","text":"are children allowed"},{"key":"C","text":"will children allow"},{"key":"D","text":"children will allow"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Under no circumstances 表示否定意义，位于句首时，句子使用部分倒装，助动词前置。children 与 allow 是被动关系，故使用 are children allowed。句意：在任何情况下，孩子都不允许对家长撒谎。","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":69,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-5ec53ce67f332979"},{"stem":"This is a highly ______ new heating system.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"electrical"},{"key":"B","text":"efficient"},{"key":"C","text":"emotional"},{"key":"D","text":"effective"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"electrical意为“电的”；efficient意为“有效率的”；emotional意为“有感情的”；effective意为“有效果的”。highly修饰efficient，表示“高效能的”。句意：这是一个高效能的新型加热系统。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":70,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-bd85aba5a9a0fc31"},{"stem":"Let's discuss these problems at the meeting, ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will we"},{"key":"B","text":"will you"},{"key":"C","text":"shall we"},{"key":"D","text":"do we"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"一般祈使句的反意疑问句用will you；let's祈使句包含说话人和听话人，简短问句用shall we。句意：我们一起在会上讨论这些问题吧，好吗？","point":"反意疑问句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":71,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-6665caaf66477adc"},{"stem":"Community service is a great way to help people in their time of need. It is great to see the happiness that ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"comes out"},{"key":"B","text":"turns in"},{"key":"C","text":"results from"},{"key":"D","text":"takes place"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"come out意为“出来”；turn in意为“提交”；result from意为“由……产生”；take place意为“发生”。题中的幸福感由社区服务产生，因此选C。句意：社区服务是在人们有需要时帮助他们的良好方式，感受由此产生的幸福感是很棒的。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":["页面题干以 that results from. 结尾；result from 通常需要说明“由什么产生”（如 results from helping others），此处缺少宾语。A 的 comes out 也不够自然。此题按页面答案记 C，同时记住完整搭配 result from + 原因。"],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":72,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-894487b1cf83414b"},{"stem":"She suggested that the factory ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was extended"},{"key":"B","text":"will be extended"},{"key":"C","text":"would be extend"},{"key":"D","text":"be extended"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"suggest等动词后加宾语从句时，从句使用虚拟语气，形式为“should＋动词原形”，should可以省略；此处用被动形式be extended。句意：她建议应该扩建工厂。","point":"虚拟语气。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":73,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-bfe2e99a6e306ed4"},{"stem":"The program gives students the ______ to learn more about global warming.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"power"},{"key":"B","text":"ambition"},{"key":"C","text":"opportunity"},{"key":"D","text":"expectation"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"power表示“力量”；ambition表示“雄心、志向”；opportunity表示“机会”；expectation表示“期待”。根据题意应填“机会”。句意：该项目给学生们提供了更多了解全球变暖的机会。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":74,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-5fe04078251eaebe"},{"stem":"______, he knows a lot about computer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As he is a child"},{"key":"B","text":"Child as is he"},{"key":"C","text":"As a child he is"},{"key":"D","text":"Child as he is"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as作连词表示“尽管”，引导让步状语从句时，通常将表语部分前置以突出强调。四个选项中只有Child as he is形式正确。句意：尽管他还是个孩子，但他懂得很多计算机方面的知识。","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":75,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-ba17089edd2590a4"},{"stem":"No one had enough foresight to ______ the winner.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"predict"},{"key":"B","text":"prevent"},{"key":"C","text":"prepare"},{"key":"D","text":"prefer"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"predict意为“预测”；prevent意为“阻止”；prepare意为“准备”；prefer意为“喜欢”。predict与foresight（远见）在语义上搭配。句意：谁也没有足够的远见能预测出获胜者。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":76,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-6f77eb5ebd61bf07"},{"stem":"Involvement in community activities has ______ an integral and inescapable part of senior managers' jobs.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"regarded as"},{"key":"B","text":"been regarded for"},{"key":"C","text":"been seen as"},{"key":"D","text":"seen for"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"regard/see sth. as sth.意为“把……看作……”。本题需要被动语态，has提示现在完成时，因此用has been seen as。句意：参加社区活动被认为是资深经理人工作中必要且不可或缺的一部分。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":77,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-2c31e18b4bf1ffd8"},{"stem":"______ people are no longer worried about whether their food is safe or not, can they enjoy a better life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Only if"},{"key":"B","text":"If only"},{"key":"C","text":"What if"},{"key":"D","text":"If not"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"only if意为“只有……”，表示唯一条件，位于句首时主句使用部分倒装。本题主句can they enjoy已采用部分倒装，符合only if的用法。句意：只有人们不再为食物安全担忧，他们才能过上更好的生活。","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":78,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-e4825cc16a8fdc02"},{"stem":"I heard that you really ______ a wonderful time at John's birthday party, didn't you?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have"},{"key":"B","text":"had"},{"key":"C","text":"will have"},{"key":"D","text":"have had"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句I heard使用一般过去时，宾语从句时态与主句保持一致，使用过去时态。句意：我听说你在约翰的生日聚会上很开心，是吗？","point":"一般过去时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":79,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-787fe40b5ebd64f2"},{"stem":"You can go out, ______ you promise to be back before 12 o'clock.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so far as"},{"key":"B","text":"as well as"},{"key":"C","text":"as long as"},{"key":"D","text":"as soon as"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"so far as表示距离；as well as表示“除……之外，也”；as long as表示“只要”；as soon as表示“一……就……”。题意是以承诺12点前回来作为可以外出的条件。句意：只要你承诺12点之前回来，你就可以出去。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":80,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-552a605f5f60d74d"},{"stem":"Many factors both at home and abroad ______ the bankruptcy of the multinational corporation.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"based on"},{"key":"B","text":"contributed to"},{"key":"C","text":"devoted to"},{"key":"D","text":"put on"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"base on意为“基于……”；contribute to意为“有助于……、促成、促使”；devote to意为“献身于……”；put on意为“穿上”。factor意为“因素”，bankruptcy意为“破产”，选contributed to符合题意。句意：国内外的多种因素共同导致了跨国公司的破产。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":81,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-adebaedbcba5f6af"},{"stem":"Spaceships are stocked with a variety of ______ foods.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"instant"},{"key":"B","text":"initial"},{"key":"C","text":"instinct"},{"key":"D","text":"innocent"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"instant表示“瞬间的、方便的”；initial表示“最初的”；instinct是名词，意为“本能”；innocent表示“无辜的”。instant与food搭配表示“方便食品”。句意：宇宙飞船装载了各种方便食品。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":82,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-c771e412ccc86564"},{"stem":"This is the book ______ I have learned a lot.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"from which"},{"key":"D","text":"of which"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"关系代词在从句中作介词宾语时，用whom（指人）或which（指物）。本题表示“我从书中学习到很多”，使用from which，which作from的宾语。句意：这就是我学有所获的那本书。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":83,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-17f99d926cfeed17"},{"stem":"One of the main benefits of community service is that it ______ a person's character.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"takes"},{"key":"B","text":"builds"},{"key":"C","text":"makes"},{"key":"D","text":"establishes"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"take意为“带走”；build意为“建立、建设”，引申为“树立、塑造”；make意为“制造”；establish意为“建立、创办、确立”。build与character搭配表示“塑造品格”。句意：社区服务的一个主要好处就是它可以塑造一个人的品格。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":84,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-467796d704489aa9"},{"stem":"He gave up his study in college in ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disagreement"},{"key":"B","text":"despair"},{"key":"C","text":"destruction"},{"key":"D","text":"distance"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"disagreement意为“意见不一、不同意”；despair意为“绝望”，in despair表示“绝望地”；destruction意为“破坏”；distance意为“距离”。句意：他绝望地放弃了大学学业。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":85,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-9da78a170397832e"},{"stem":"Proper controls that should ______ developed as part of routine safety procedures were not in place.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be"},{"key":"B","text":"have"},{"key":"C","text":"has been"},{"key":"D","text":"have been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"should have been done表示“过去本应该做某事，但实际上没有做”。本题需要被动语态，并表达“本应……却没有”之意，因此选have been。句意：本应成为常规安全程序一部分的适当控制并不到位。","point":"情态动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":86,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-d08793b734a33646"},{"stem":"The director of the office will organize a spring outing if weather ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will permit"},{"key":"B","text":"is permitting"},{"key":"C","text":"permits"},{"key":"D","text":"permitted"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"条件状语从句中，主句用一般将来时，从句通常用一般现在时；此处表示天气状况，用permits。句意：如果天气允许，办公室主任将组织一次春游。","point":"条件状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":87,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-b53ae4e4f4ab7529"},{"stem":"By that moment he ______ longer and longer periods alone, but when she walked away, he still wanted to rush after her.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was used to spend"},{"key":"B","text":"used to spend"},{"key":"C","text":"used to spending"},{"key":"D","text":"was used to spending"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"used to do表示“过去常常做某事”；be used to doing表示“习惯于做某事”。根据题意，他习惯于越来越长时间的独处，因此选D。句意：在那个时候，他已经习惯于越来越长时间的独处，但当她离开的时候，他仍然想追上去。","point":"词组。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":88,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-414399e725d1e426"},{"stem":"The company is planning to ______ at least 100 million dollars for the fund.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rise"},{"key":"B","text":"carry"},{"key":"C","text":"design"},{"key":"D","text":"raise"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"rise为不及物动词，意为“升起”；carry为及物动词，意为“搬动”；design意为“设计”；raise为及物动词，意为“提高、升起”，也可表示“筹集款项”。句意：公司正在计划为该基金项目至少筹款1亿美元。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":89,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-4143b182fdaadc70"},{"stem":"Don't be afraid of making mistakes because it is simply ______ way of learning.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the other"},{"key":"B","text":"another"},{"key":"C","text":"other"},{"key":"D","text":"others"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"other一般不单独使用；others表示复数意义；the other表示两者中的另一个；another表示三者或三者以上中的另一个。句中没有强调两者关系，故用another。句意：不要害怕犯错，因为这是学习的另一种方式。","point":"词汇辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":90,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-da10fc2d2b22324a"},{"stem":"Sometimes punishment doesn't work and the boy ______ another bad habit instead of behaving better.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"carries out"},{"key":"B","text":"picks up"},{"key":"C","text":"carries on"},{"key":"D","text":"picks out"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"pick up a habit是固定搭配，表示“养成（坏）习惯”；carry out表示“执行”；carry on表示“继续”；pick out表示“挑出”。句意：有时惩罚不起作用，男孩反而养成了另一个坏习惯，而不是表现更好。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":91,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-18ba63aff19aa69e"},{"stem":"Charles Dickens ______ many wonderful characters in his novels.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"invented"},{"key":"B","text":"discovered"},{"key":"C","text":"uncovered"},{"key":"D","text":"created"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"create characters意为“创造人物角色”，用于文学创作；invent多指发明实物；discover表示发现已存在的事物；uncover表示“揭露”。句意：查尔斯·狄更斯在他的小说中创造了许多精彩的人物。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":92,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-a11cdac335d3f9d4"},{"stem":"To meet the publisher's deadline, I have to ______ late tonight finishing the last chapter of my autobiography.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"keep up"},{"key":"B","text":"stay up"},{"key":"C","text":"wake up"},{"key":"D","text":"jump up"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"stay up late意为“熬夜”，符合语境；keep up表示“保持”；wake up表示“醒来”；jump up表示“跳起来”。句意：为了赶上出版商的截止日期，我今晚必须熬夜完成自传的最后一章。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":93,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-499e1f550a68dda0"},{"stem":"We have to accept the fact ______ most of us have been raised with certain foods and we stick to them all our lives.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"that"},{"key":"D","text":"for that"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"fact后接同位语从句，用that引导，从句内容完整、不缺成分。句意：我们不得不接受这个事实：我们大多数人是吃着某些食物长大的，并且一生都离不开它们。","point":"同位语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":94,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-cf0a23e22040a7cd"},{"stem":"Running up big bills on credit cards means you'll have trouble ______ the full debt when the statement arrives.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to pay off"},{"key":"B","text":"paying off"},{"key":"C","text":"paid off"},{"key":"D","text":"being paid off"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"have trouble (in) doing sth.为固定搭配，意为“做某事有困难”。句意：刷信用卡欠下大笔账单意味着当账单寄到时，你将难以还清全部债务。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":95,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-2fe077c4d56c7b81"},{"stem":"______ in charge of the night club has bothered him for quite some time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Left"},{"key":"B","text":"Being left"},{"key":"C","text":"Having left"},{"key":"D","text":"To leave"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Being left in charge意为“被留下来负责”，动名词短语作主语，表示被动状态。bother为谓语，主语应是“被留下负责”这件事。句意：被留下来负责夜总会这件事困扰了他好一阵子。","point":"动名词短语作主语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":96,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-f2c0e781281fa63b"},{"stem":"Were it not for the bad weather, we ______ tennis at the moment.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be playing"},{"key":"B","text":"would have played"},{"key":"C","text":"were playing"},{"key":"D","text":"had played"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"Were it not for...是If it were not for...的倒装，表示与现在事实相反的假设，主句用would be doing表示此刻正在进行的动作。句意：要不是天气不好，我们现在正在打网球。","point":"虚拟语气（与现在事实相反）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":97,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-5c50734a71a917a2"},{"stem":"Since there isn't much time left, you can just tell us about it ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in detail"},{"key":"B","text":"at length"},{"key":"C","text":"in all"},{"key":"D","text":"in brief"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"in brief意为“简短地、扼要地”，符合时间不多的语境；in detail表示“详细地”；at length表示“详尽地、长时间地”；in all表示“总共”。句意：既然剩下的时间不多了，你就简要地告诉我们吧。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":98,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-c6b4f5f75934d47d"},{"stem":"The number of women who ______ a single child increased continuously from only 8% in 1981 to 13% in 2006.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gave life to"},{"key":"B","text":"gave consideration to"},{"key":"C","text":"gave birth to"},{"key":"D","text":"gave a hand to"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"give birth to意为“生育（孩子）”，符合语境；give life to表示“赋予生命”，较抽象；give consideration to表示“考虑”；give a hand to表示“帮助”。句意：只生育一个孩子的女性数量从1981年的仅8%持续增长到2006年的13%。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":99,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-d91b54e8746d4eb3"},{"stem":"When ______ to stress, our body reacts both chemically and physically.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"exposed"},{"key":"B","text":"imposed"},{"key":"C","text":"disposed"},{"key":"D","text":"proposed"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"be exposed to意为“暴露于……、受到……影响”，exposed to stress表示“面对压力”。句意：当面对压力时，我们的身体会产生化学和生理上的反应。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":100,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-72648fc42e6d71bf"},{"stem":"He has just finished a ______ jogging.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"twohours"},{"key":"B","text":"two hour"},{"key":"C","text":"twohour"},{"key":"D","text":"twohoured"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"本题考查复合形容词：“数词＋单数名词”用连字符连接，修饰后面的名词，名词必须用单数。A为复数且无连字符；B无连字符；D形式错误。句意：他刚完成了一次两小时的慢跑。页面选项原样显示为twohour；按页面解析所述，其规范形式为two-hour。","point":"复合形容词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":["页面的 a two-hour jogging 搭配不够自然；复习时宜写 a two-hour jog 或 two hours of jogging。"],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":101,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-f27d33f7a8a283e0"},{"stem":"We have to ______ the news before 5 o'clock tomorrow morning.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"realize"},{"key":"B","text":"release"},{"key":"C","text":"resolve"},{"key":"D","text":"relay"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"release the news意为“发布新闻”；realize表示“意识到”；resolve表示“解决”；relay表示“转播、传达”。句意：我们必须在明天早上5点之前发布这条新闻。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":102,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-8ad7e9eec1c9ac7e"},{"stem":"Perhaps the most unusual ______ in the room is an extraordinary pair of candles.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"characteristic"},{"key":"B","text":"specialty"},{"key":"C","text":"trait"},{"key":"D","text":"feature"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"feature指房间的“特征、特色”；characteristic表示较抽象的“特性”；specialty表示“特产、专长”；trait表示“品质、性格特征”。句意：房间里最不寻常的特色可能是一对奇特的蜡烛。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":103,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-d87385bf2f588a3c"},{"stem":"Our usual figure is around 5%, but that ______ the size of the order.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"depends on"},{"key":"B","text":"looks up"},{"key":"C","text":"holds up"},{"key":"D","text":"deals with"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"depend on意为“取决于”；look up表示“查阅”；hold up表示“举起、耽搁”；deal with表示“处理”。句意：我们通常的数字是5%左右，但那取决于订单的大小。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":104,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-ab124f579eaa62ae"},{"stem":"The two parties held the talk in a friendly ______ and reached an agreement.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"atmosphere"},{"key":"B","text":"state"},{"key":"C","text":"situation"},{"key":"D","text":"phenomenon"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"in a friendly atmosphere意为“在友好的气氛中”；state表示“状态”；situation表示“形势”；phenomenon表示“现象”。句意：双方在友好的气氛中进行了会谈并达成了协议。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":105,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-c945626f38aa0820"},{"stem":"The number of television programs ______ toward infants is growing.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to gear"},{"key":"B","text":"gearing"},{"key":"C","text":"geared"},{"key":"D","text":"gear"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"programs geared toward infants意为“针对婴幼儿的节目”。gear toward是固定短语，用过去分词作后置定语表示被动。句意：面向婴幼儿的电视节目数量正在增长。","point":"过去分词作定语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":106,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-74b6095cd82e9e21"},{"stem":"______ is known to the Americans, Mark Twain is a great American writer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That"},{"key":"B","text":"Which"},{"key":"C","text":"What"},{"key":"D","text":"As"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"As is known to...是固定结构，意为“正如……所知道的”，as指代后面整个主句。句意：正如美国人所知，马克·吐温是一位伟大的美国作家。","point":"定语从句（as引导）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":107,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-b01f6089b68ebc9c"},{"stem":"Although he is very old, ______ he is quite strong.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"yet"},{"key":"B","text":"but"},{"key":"C","text":"so"},{"key":"D","text":"if"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"although和but不能同时使用，但yet可以与although搭配，表示“虽然……但是……”。句意：虽然他年纪很大，但身体很强壮。","point":"连词搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":108,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-fac70ec027bc0499"},{"stem":"We have decided to have a party ______ the occasion.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in honor of"},{"key":"B","text":"in need of"},{"key":"C","text":"in spite of"},{"key":"D","text":"in quest of"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"in honor of意为“为庆祝……、为纪念……”；in need of表示“需要”；in spite of表示“尽管”；in quest of表示“寻求”。句意：我们决定为这一时刻举办一个派对。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":109,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-d19e57f4846101d9"},{"stem":"Only if people are no longer worried about whether their food is safe or not ______ enjoy a better life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"they will"},{"key":"B","text":"will they"},{"key":"C","text":"they would"},{"key":"D","text":"would they"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Only if置于句首时，主句需要部分倒装；此处为一般将来时，因此用will they。句意：只有当人们不再担心食物是否安全时，他们才能享受更好的生活。","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":110,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-f02dc6dd560f856f"},{"stem":"Although they lost their jobs, savings and unemployment benefits allow the couple to ______ their comfortable home.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"come in for"},{"key":"B","text":"catch up with"},{"key":"C","text":"look forward to"},{"key":"D","text":"hold on to"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"hold on to意为“保住、不失去”；come in for表示“受到”；catch up with表示“赶上”；look forward to表示“期待”。句意：虽然他们失业了，但积蓄和失业救济金使这对夫妇能够保住他们舒适的家。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":111,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-e2cd59800ef915a9"},{"stem":"The hardware inside your laptop is hopelessly ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"up to now"},{"key":"B","text":"out of necessity"},{"key":"C","text":"out of date"},{"key":"D","text":"up to date"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"out of date意为“过时的”；up to now表示“到目前为止”；out of necessity表示“出于必要”；up to date表示“最新的”。句意：你笔记本电脑里的硬件已经过时得无可救药了。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":112,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-3c11b9da66191ace"},{"stem":"This is the house ______ we had a business negotiation last month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to which"},{"key":"B","text":"in which"},{"key":"C","text":"for which"},{"key":"D","text":"which"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"从句中的had a business negotiation发生在房子里，使用in which引导，相当于where。句意：这就是上个月我们进行商务谈判的那所房子。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":113,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-eb4eaf7fddea7e20"},{"stem":"With the rapid economic growth in China, the logistics industry is ______ greatly.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"expanding"},{"key":"B","text":"exploring"},{"key":"C","text":"exploding"},{"key":"D","text":"expecting"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"expanding意为“扩张、发展”，符合物流行业伴随经济增长而发展的语境；exploring表示“探索”；exploding表示“爆炸”；expecting表示“期待”。句意：随着中国经济的快速增长，物流业正在大幅扩张。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":114,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-2ee2caca6310812e"},{"stem":"______ difficulties he may meet with, he will not be discouraged.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Whenever"},{"key":"B","text":"Wherever"},{"key":"C","text":"However"},{"key":"D","text":"Whatever"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"Whatever difficulties意为“无论什么困难”，whatever修饰名词difficulties；however后接形容词或副词。句意：无论他遇到什么困难，他都不会气馁。","point":"让步状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":115,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-ed779eaf0bf0548e"},{"stem":"A ______ in working in customer service is to ensure that you have focused your attention on the right key areas.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"choice"},{"key":"B","text":"challenge"},{"key":"C","text":"change"},{"key":"D","text":"channel"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"a challenge意为“一个挑战”，符合语境；choice表示“选择”；change表示“改变”；channel表示“渠道”。句意：从事客户服务工作的一个挑战是确保你把注意力集中在正确的关键领域。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":116,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-eba21a8fec0d18e0"},{"stem":"Sally as well as her brother ______ reading books.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"likes"},{"key":"B","text":"like"},{"key":"C","text":"have liked"},{"key":"D","text":"is liking"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"as well as连接主语时，谓语动词与前面的主语Sally保持一致，用第三人称单数likes。句意：莎莉和她的弟弟都喜欢读书。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":117,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-5242bb2e13cb35c6"},{"stem":"You should open a(n) ______ at an online bank first.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"accuracy"},{"key":"B","text":"discount"},{"key":"C","text":"account"},{"key":"D","text":"achievement"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"open an account意为“开账户”，是银行常用短语；accuracy表示“准确性”；discount表示“折扣”；achievement表示“成就”。句意：你应该首先在网上银行开一个账户。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":118,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-5db1e23034d6f58b"},{"stem":"We ______ for 13 hours by the time we get to New York.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will fly"},{"key":"B","text":"will have flown"},{"key":"C","text":"flew"},{"key":"D","text":"fly"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"by the time we get to New York表示将来某个时间点之前，谓语用将来完成时will have flown。句意：等我们到达纽约时，我们将已经飞了13个小时。","point":"将来完成时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":119,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-bb3808d04fbbf5cc"},{"stem":"Please tell me how I can use the computer, ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"can you"},{"key":"B","text":"could you"},{"key":"C","text":"will you"},{"key":"D","text":"would you"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"祈使句Please tell me...的反意疑问句通常用will you或won't you。句意：请告诉我怎么用这台电脑，好吗？","point":"反意疑问句（祈使句）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":120,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-30469a9ad08bc2aa"},{"stem":"James Watt ______ the steam engine in 1796.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was inventing"},{"key":"B","text":"invented"},{"key":"C","text":"had invented"},{"key":"D","text":"has invented"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"1796年是明确的过去时间，且“发明”是过去发生的动作，用一般过去时invented。句意：詹姆斯·瓦特于1796年发明了蒸汽机。","point":"一般过去时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":["本题按页面原句记录，重点是时态判断；句中的历史事实未核验。"],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":121,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-99c8134f2e6eee57"},{"stem":"______ important it is for kids to imagine freely!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What"},{"key":"B","text":"How"},{"key":"C","text":"So"},{"key":"D","text":"Much"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"“How + 形容词 + 主语 + 谓语”结构。句中有形容词important，故用How。句意：孩子们自由想象是多么重要啊！","point":"感叹句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":122,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-39b82c7d1347b4b1"},{"stem":"They are ______ cheap that the salesman can hardly have any more profits.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"much"},{"key":"B","text":"too"},{"key":"C","text":"so"},{"key":"D","text":"very"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"“so + 形容词 + that + 从句”表示“如此……以至于……”。句意：它们如此便宜，以至于销售人员几乎没有任何利润了。","point":"so...that结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":123,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-b1aa04d9b44f43c4"},{"stem":"Would you like ______ the window? It's somewhat hot.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"open"},{"key":"B","text":"opening"},{"key":"C","text":"opened"},{"key":"D","text":"to open"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"Would you like to do sth.是固定句型，表示“你想要做某事吗？”句意：你愿意打开窗户吗？有点热。","point":"would like to do sth.","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":124,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-e8bf0e3bf4889684"},{"stem":"I shall never forget ______ her singing that song.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hearing"},{"key":"B","text":"to hear"},{"key":"C","text":"heard"},{"key":"D","text":"have heard"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"forget doing表示“忘记做过某事”；forget to do表示“忘记去做某事”。此处是“永远不会忘记听过她唱那首歌”，用hearing。句意：我永远不会忘记听过她唱那首歌。","point":"forget doing vs. forget to do。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":125,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-ce47a86d13a095aa"},{"stem":"No matter ______ and what industry you are in, your company has assets.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"your business is how small"},{"key":"B","text":"your business how small is"},{"key":"C","text":"how your business is small"},{"key":"D","text":"how small your business is"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"no matter how后接“形容词 + 主语 + 谓语”，即how small your business is。句意：无论你的企业有多小，无论你身处什么行业，你的公司都有资产。","point":"no matter how引导让步状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":126,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-87fc61a64974a9fa"},{"stem":"If he ______ my advice, he wouldn't have lost his job.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"followed"},{"key":"B","text":"had followed"},{"key":"C","text":"should follow"},{"key":"D","text":"would follow"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句wouldn't have lost表示与过去事实相反，从句用“had + 过去分词”。句意：如果他听了我的建议，他就不会丢掉工作。","point":"虚拟语气（与过去事实相反）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":127,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-566613a0cdc1efe6"},{"stem":"I will have my hair ______ and the long hair will drive me crazy.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cut"},{"key":"B","text":"cutting"},{"key":"C","text":"to cut"},{"key":"D","text":"being cut"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"句意是“我要去剪头发”，即“让头发被剪”，my hair与cut之间是被动关系，因此需用过去分词cut作宾语补足语，构成have my hair cut（让某事被做）。句意：我要去剪头发，这头长发会让我发疯。","point":"have sth. done结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":["原句并列部分时态和逻辑略显别扭，重点记住 *have my hair cut*。"],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":128,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-d877779e45677abb"},{"stem":"The more time you spend with your kids, ______ you'll get in communicating with them.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the least"},{"key":"B","text":"the best"},{"key":"C","text":"the less"},{"key":"D","text":"the better"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"“越……，越……”结构，前句the more time，后句用the better。句意：你花在孩子们身上的时间越多，你和他们沟通就越好。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":129,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-f8cae5e184204e04"},{"stem":"It was not until nearly a month later ______ I received the manager's reply.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"that"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It was not until... that...是强调句型的固定结构。句意：直到近一个月后，我才收到经理的回复。","point":"强调句型。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":130,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-3e25b738d0853549"},{"stem":"The first book ______ for English teaching came out in the 16th century.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"written"},{"key":"B","text":"writing"},{"key":"C","text":"to write"},{"key":"D","text":"wrote"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"book与write是被动关系，用过去分词written作后置定语。句意：第一本为英语教学而写的书出版于16世纪。","point":"过去分词作定语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":131,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-110d1f69b9763b08"},{"stem":"For many students, university is the place ______ they are exposed to different cultures and different people.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"where"},{"key":"D","text":"which"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"先行词place表示地点，关系副词用where。句意：对许多学生来说，大学是他们接触不同文化和不同人群的地方。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":132,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-b79e58240a47a619"},{"stem":"Baidu says the device ______ to support image search.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"designs"},{"key":"B","text":"designed"},{"key":"C","text":"had been designed"},{"key":"D","text":"is designed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"设备是被设计用来支持图像搜索的，且陈述客观事实，用is designed。句意：百度表示，该设备被设计用来支持图像搜索。","point":"一般现在时被动语态。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":133,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-c27e47a7d6bc057d"},{"stem":"______ did he watch the football match ______ participate in the marathon last Sunday. He chose to play golf instead.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Neither...nor"},{"key":"B","text":"Either...or"},{"key":"C","text":"Not only...but also"},{"key":"D","text":"Both...and"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"根据后文He chose to play golf instead可知，他既没有看足球赛也没有参加马拉松，用Neither...nor。句意：上周日他既没有看足球赛，也没有参加马拉松。他选择去打高尔夫了。","point":"并列连词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":134,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-c1d18df65a539023"},{"stem":"The teacher, together with his students, ______ planting trees in the street now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"are"},{"key":"D","text":"is"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"together with连接主语时，谓语与前面的主语The teacher一致，用单数；且now表示现在进行时，用is planting。句意：老师和他的学生们现在正在街上植树。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":135,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-b6011f3824425c8c"},{"stem":"You're doing a great job. The division's ______ are in great shape.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fashions"},{"key":"B","text":"finances"},{"key":"C","text":"factors"},{"key":"D","text":"findings"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"finances意为“财务状况”，符合in great shape（状况良好）的语境。句意：你做得很好。这个部门的财务状况良好。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":136,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-65d61d22d860192b"},{"stem":"In our daily life, everyone fails every now and then. It is how you react that makes a ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"development"},{"key":"B","text":"difference"},{"key":"C","text":"progress"},{"key":"D","text":"point"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"make a difference意为“有影响，起作用”，是常用短语。句意：在日常生活中，每个人都会时不时失败。重要的是你的反应方式，这会产生不同的结果。","point":"固定短语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":137,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-27366891adc82f6a"},{"stem":"I have been very lucky to have had so many ______ managers during my career so far.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"terrific"},{"key":"B","text":"terrible"},{"key":"C","text":"terrifying"},{"key":"D","text":"troublesome"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"terrific意为“极好的，了不起的”，与lucky语境一致。其他选项均为贬义。句意：我很幸运，在我的职业生涯中到目前为止有这么多出色的经理。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":138,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-f58a0162c0cc2282"},{"stem":"If you are in a shopping mall and ______ a woman whose skirt looks really attractive, you can take a photo of her skirt using Baidu Eye.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"come across"},{"key":"B","text":"come out"},{"key":"C","text":"come in"},{"key":"D","text":"come up"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"come across意为“偶然遇到”，符合语境。句意：如果你在购物中心遇到一位裙子看起来很吸引人的女士，你可以用百度眼镜拍下她的裙子。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":139,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7d529f4865579d98"},{"stem":"Her determination to ______ her goal of life motivated her greater effort.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"retain"},{"key":"B","text":"attain"},{"key":"C","text":"contain"},{"key":"D","text":"entertain"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"本题考查形近动词辨析。attain a goal为固定搭配，意为“实现目标”，且attain强调“经过努力而达到”，与句中determination和greater effort呼应。retain意为“保留”，contain意为“包含”，entertain意为“娱乐”，均不能与goal搭配。句意：她实现人生目标的决心激励她更加努力。","point":"动词辨析（形近词）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":140,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-da2db71f6bc9ec4c"},{"stem":"Team spirit means you are willing to ______ personal considerations for the welfare of all.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"scare"},{"key":"B","text":"sacrifice"},{"key":"C","text":"salute"},{"key":"D","text":"satisfy"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"sacrifice意为“牺牲”，符合团队精神中为集体利益牺牲个人考虑的含义。句意：团队精神意味着你愿意为了大家的福祉牺牲个人考虑。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":141,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-22c4f05e9ca1982d"},{"stem":"I'm going to have a ______ with Mark about this issue tomorrow.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"speech"},{"key":"B","text":"sentence"},{"key":"C","text":"word"},{"key":"D","text":"lecture"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"have a word with sb.意为“和某人谈一谈”。句意：我明天要和马克谈谈这个问题。","point":"固定短语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":142,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-d2809774f5e1e9a3"},{"stem":"I would ______ E-accounting to my colleagues.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recognize"},{"key":"B","text":"recommend"},{"key":"C","text":"reward"},{"key":"D","text":"reduce"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"recommend...to...意为“向……推荐……”。句意：我会向同事们推荐电子会计。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":143,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-68bec093d5fe9cc4"},{"stem":"How much time should I ______ to preparing the annual sales presentation?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"spend"},{"key":"B","text":"spare"},{"key":"C","text":"dedicate"},{"key":"D","text":"devise"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"dedicate time to doing sth.意为“把时间奉献给做某事”。spend通常说spend time (in) doing，但后面接to preparing不搭配；spare抽出时间，但不如dedicate正式。根据常见考题，此处选C。句意：我应该花多少时间来准备年度销售演示？","point":"动词辨析与搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":144,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-54d797dfd8b4586a"},{"stem":"Since she ______ herself in the survey, she has spent one month collecting the questionnaires.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"devoted"},{"key":"B","text":"engaged"},{"key":"C","text":"focused"},{"key":"D","text":"managed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"engage oneself in意为“忙于，从事于”。也可说devote oneself to，但后面是in，所以用engaged。句意：自从她忙于这项调查以来，她已经花了一个月时间收集问卷。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":145,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-737a52ef104e4ac3"},{"stem":"Official figures show a sharp ______ in the number of foreign companies.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"incline"},{"key":"B","text":"indication"},{"key":"C","text":"decline"},{"key":"D","text":"declaration"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"a sharp decline意为“急剧下降”。根据常识，此处应为外企数量的下降趋势。句意：官方数据显示外企数量急剧下降。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":146,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-8351237b9ad2fecf"},{"stem":"We all believe that it'd be hard for him to ______ extra responsibilities now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take away"},{"key":"B","text":"take off"},{"key":"C","text":"take on"},{"key":"D","text":"take down"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"take on responsibilities意为“承担职责”。句意：我们都认为他现在很难承担额外的责任。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":147,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-87cb54dacc595ae9"},{"stem":"Herbs have been used for centuries to make ______ drinks.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"relaxed"},{"key":"B","text":"renewable"},{"key":"C","text":"refreshing"},{"key":"D","text":"restless"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"refreshing drinks意为“提神饮料”。句意：几个世纪以来，草药一直被用来制作提神饮料。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":148,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-4fc9013d496fb0a8"},{"stem":"The child is ______ a difficult phase.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"going over"},{"key":"B","text":"going through"},{"key":"C","text":"going ahead"},{"key":"D","text":"going off"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"go through a phase意为“经历一个阶段”。句意：这个孩子正在经历一个困难的阶段。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":149,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-135f854a17344992"},{"stem":"Everyone's fingerprints are ______, therefore, the policeman can track the criminals with them.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"unusual"},{"key":"B","text":"unique"},{"key":"C","text":"special"},{"key":"D","text":"distinct"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"unique意为“独一无二的”，强调唯一性，符合指纹特性。句意：每个人的指纹都是独一无二的，因此警察可以用它们追踪罪犯。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":150,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-bf5dd05be4391dec"},{"stem":"He failed to pass his exam as everyone expected, ______ proves that he wasn't working hard enough.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"which"},{"key":"C","text":"who"},{"key":"D","text":"what"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"which指代前面整个主句的内容，引导非限制性定语从句。句意：他没有通过考试，正如大家所料，这证明他不够努力。","point":"非限制性定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":151,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-698b279ab2235549"},{"stem":"Not all restaurants ______ mobile payment, so you may have to pay cash or by card.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gather"},{"key":"B","text":"accept"},{"key":"C","text":"admit"},{"key":"D","text":"get"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"accept mobile payment意为“接受移动支付”。句意：并不是所有餐厅都接受移动支付，所以你可能需要用现金或刷卡支付。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":152,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-04d058bab335089d"},{"stem":"Managers must understand how information ______ gathered and analyzed.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"are"},{"key":"C","text":"be"},{"key":"D","text":"being"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"information是不可数名词，谓语用单数is，且为被动is gathered。句意：管理者必须了解信息是如何收集和分析的。","point":"主谓一致与被动语态。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态","主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":153,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-3501201553b0a41e"},{"stem":"Importing and exporting is transferring goods from one country to ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"other"},{"key":"B","text":"others"},{"key":"C","text":"another"},{"key":"D","text":"the other"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"one...another表示“一个……另一个”，不特指。句意：进出口是将货物从一个国家转移到另一个国家。","point":"不定代词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配","代词与限定词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":154,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-95610f33618ef9fa"},{"stem":"It was because we booked the ticket in advance ______ we could enjoy the concert.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"where"},{"key":"C","text":"why"},{"key":"D","text":"which"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It was...that...是强调句型，强调原因状语。句意：正是因为我们提前订了票，才能欣赏到音乐会。","point":"强调句型。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":155,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-f73085bc4bba366c"},{"stem":"You'd better spend your time finding the best solution ______ complaining.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"other than"},{"key":"B","text":"rather than"},{"key":"C","text":"except for"},{"key":"D","text":"but for"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"rather than意为“而不是”，连接并列结构。句意：你最好把时间花在寻找最佳解决方案上，而不是抱怨。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":156,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-1a12af0ef135c308"},{"stem":"My teacher is very patient. I ______ anyone else as helpful as she is.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"never meet"},{"key":"B","text":"had never met"},{"key":"C","text":"will never meet"},{"key":"D","text":"have never met"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"表示从过去到现在从未遇到过，用现在完成时。句意：我的老师很有耐心。我从未遇到过像她这样乐于助人的人。","point":"现在完成时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":157,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-4db4c09edc4b5f50"},{"stem":"Her father's illness may ______ her hot temper these days.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"account for"},{"key":"B","text":"agree with"},{"key":"C","text":"call for"},{"key":"D","text":"look into"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"account for意为“解释，是……的原因”。句意：她父亲的病可能是她这些天脾气暴躁的原因。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":158,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-b98ffaf3fc6ce872"},{"stem":"Ms. Green never told you what a hard life she had ever lived, ______?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did she"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't she"},{"key":"C","text":"had she"},{"key":"D","text":"hadn't she"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句never told为否定，故反问部分用肯定did she。句意：格林女士从未告诉过你她曾经过着多么艰苦的生活，是吗？","point":"反意疑问句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":159,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-cf5be23f8ad0c8d6"},{"stem":"Many car accidents were ______ to drunk driving.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attributed"},{"key":"B","text":"attained"},{"key":"C","text":"attached"},{"key":"D","text":"attracted"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"attribute...to...意为“把……归因于……”。句意：许多车祸归因于酒驾。","point":"短语搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":160,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"}],"id":"q-382cf57b544e912c"},{"stem":"If we ______ a reputation for being unreliable, our sales volumes will drop.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"get"},{"key":"B","text":"will get"},{"key":"C","text":"had got"},{"key":"D","text":"got"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"真实条件句中，主句用将来时，从句用一般现在时。句意：如果我们落下了不可靠的名声，我们的销量就会下降。","point":"条件状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":161,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-a5c9a896691010d5"},{"stem":"The government is spending more and more money to make better medical service ______ to the farmers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reasonable"},{"key":"B","text":"accessible"},{"key":"C","text":"acceptable"},{"key":"D","text":"sensible"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"accessible to意为“可获得的，可享用的”。句意：政府正在投入越来越多的资金，使更好的医疗服务惠及农民。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":162,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-c031c4e6f07bfbad"},{"stem":"Several months ago, a teacher as well as many of his students ______ helped by the police to get out of a dangerous mountain.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are"},{"key":"B","text":"is"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"were"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"as well as连接主语时，谓语与前面的主语（a teacher）一致，用单数；且时间为several months ago，用过去时was。句意：几个月前，一位老师和他的许多学生在警察的帮助下脱离了危险的山。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":163,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-cad15747f30054ac"},{"stem":"Defining concepts will ______ nearly half the total time spent on research.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"come up"},{"key":"B","text":"take off"},{"key":"C","text":"come on"},{"key":"D","text":"take up"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"take up意为“占据（时间、空间）”。句意：定义概念将占据研究总时间近一半。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":164,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-82fcaae0be946d03"},{"stem":"They still decided to set out for the mountain village ______ the heavy rain.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in place of"},{"key":"B","text":"instead of"},{"key":"C","text":"in spite of"},{"key":"D","text":"in case of"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"in spite of意为“尽管”，表示让步。句意：尽管下着大雨，他们仍然决定出发去那个山村。","point":"短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":165,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-ebfdb16a6bcf15bc"},{"stem":"We know that the word \"infosphere\" has been used, ______ the sense of \"information\" and \"atmosphere\".","options":[{"key":"A","text":"combine"},{"key":"B","text":"combining"},{"key":"C","text":"combined"},{"key":"D","text":"being combined"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"combining...为现在分词短语作状语，表示伴随或补充说明。句意：我们知道“信息圈”这个词已经被使用，它结合了“信息”和“氛围”的意思。","point":"非谓语动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":166,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0e71ce2333e77ab5"},{"stem":"You don't mind ______ you Jenny, do you?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I called"},{"key":"B","text":"to call"},{"key":"C","text":"to be called"},{"key":"D","text":"my calling"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"mind sb's doing sth.意为“介意某人做某事”。句意：你不介意我叫你珍妮吧？","point":"动名词复合结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":167,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-68f1db8dff8d082c"},{"stem":"The new marketing assistants are all ______ and helping each other out with problems.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"getting along"},{"key":"B","text":"getting about"},{"key":"C","text":"getting over"},{"key":"D","text":"getting out"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"get along意为“相处融洽”。句意：新来的市场助理们都相处得很好，互相帮助解决问题。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":168,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-567ff61770f2a566"},{"stem":"The moment of a kid helping a disabled man was ______ by a young photographer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"calculated"},{"key":"B","text":"captured"},{"key":"C","text":"carved"},{"key":"D","text":"crashed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"capture a moment意为“捕捉瞬间”。句意：一个孩子帮助残疾人的瞬间被一位年轻的摄影师捕捉到了。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":169,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-70d249f33e734fe7"},{"stem":"They have been looking forward to ______ your reply.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"receive"},{"key":"B","text":"receiving"},{"key":"C","text":"being received"},{"key":"D","text":"be received"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"look forward to doing sth.，其中to是介词，后接动名词。句意：他们一直期待着收到你的回复。","point":"动名词作宾语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":170,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-aa169e4014813e31"},{"stem":"The university plans to invite ______ people from various academic fields to give lectures.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"practical"},{"key":"B","text":"proud"},{"key":"C","text":"prominent"},{"key":"D","text":"prolonged"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"prominent意为“杰出的，著名的”。句意：大学计划邀请来自各个学术领域的杰出人士来做讲座。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":171,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-a3061a898584b632"},{"stem":"______ we expected, the supplier delivered the goods on time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As"},{"key":"B","text":"That"},{"key":"C","text":"Which"},{"key":"D","text":"When"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"As we expected意为“正如我们所料”，as指代后面主句的内容。句意：正如我们所料，供应商按时交付了货物。","point":"定语从句（as引导）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":172,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-68b57949194ecfd5"},{"stem":"Thank you very much for sharing this valuable ______ with us.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"exposure"},{"key":"B","text":"explanation"},{"key":"C","text":"experience"},{"key":"D","text":"expectation"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"valuable experience意为“宝贵的经验”。句意：非常感谢你与我们分享这个宝贵的经验。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":173,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-96b357912a654191"},{"stem":"Had he recited this text, he ______ the final examination.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could pass"},{"key":"B","text":"should pass"},{"key":"C","text":"had passed"},{"key":"D","text":"would have passed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"Had he recited是If he had recited的倒装，主句用would have done。句意：如果他背诵了这篇课文，他就能通过期末考试了。","point":"虚拟语气（与过去事实相反）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":174,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-1bb171d82a84d745"},{"stem":"The company drew up a thorough plan about the advertising campaign in order to ______ sales.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"achieve"},{"key":"B","text":"boost"},{"key":"C","text":"produce"},{"key":"D","text":"yield"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"boost sales意为“提高销量”。句意：公司制定了关于广告活动的详尽计划，以提高销量。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":175,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-522b9155ac0dd43e"},{"stem":"______, he can speak several languages.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As he is young"},{"key":"B","text":"Young as he is"},{"key":"C","text":"Young that he is"},{"key":"D","text":"For he is young"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"“形容词/名词 + as + 主语 + 谓语”表示“尽管……”。句意：尽管他年轻，他能说好几种语言。","point":"让步状语从句（倒装）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":176,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-5bdcff019211e569"},{"stem":"Chinese tech giant Huawei officially announced the ______ of its new operating system called Harmony.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"management"},{"key":"B","text":"publishing"},{"key":"C","text":"devotion"},{"key":"D","text":"launch"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"launch意为“发布，推出”。句意：中国科技巨头华为正式宣布推出名为“鸿蒙”的新操作系统。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":177,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-0ebe967e045e98ac"},{"stem":"The main concern is not who gave these answers, ______ they are right or not.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"and whether"},{"key":"B","text":"but whether"},{"key":"C","text":"but how"},{"key":"D","text":"and how"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"not...but...意为“不是……而是……”。句意：主要问题不是谁给出了这些答案，而是它们是否正确。","point":"固定结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":178,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-ec4a33bfd04db3d9"},{"stem":"We are professional movers and we have ______ special protective measures.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"addressed"},{"key":"B","text":"addicted"},{"key":"C","text":"adapted"},{"key":"D","text":"adopted"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"adopt measures意为“采取措施”。句意：我们是专业的搬家公司，并且我们已经采取了特殊的保护措施。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":179,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-d8e9ab8d4e1847d1"},{"stem":"The police reported that the ______ has been caught.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"respect"},{"key":"B","text":"suspect"},{"key":"C","text":"aspect"},{"key":"D","text":"prospect"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"suspect意为“嫌疑犯”。句意：警方报告说嫌疑犯已被抓获。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":180,"group":"词语用法与语法结构","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-dab5e82aa5b89503"},{"stem":"如果你愿意，我就把这辆车送给你。","options":[],"answer":"If you like, I will give this car to you.","explanation":"主句用一般将来时，从句用一般现在时。","point":"if引导的条件状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":1,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-05ce249d72646f73"},{"stem":"他的包里装满了英语考试方面的书。","options":[],"answer":"His bag is filled with books about English exams.","explanation":"“装满”译为be filled with。","point":"被动语态。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":2,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-35ade797500217f9"},{"stem":"这个问题不像我想象得那么难。","options":[],"answer":"This question is not as difficult as I imagined.","explanation":"“不像……那么……”译为not as...as...。","point":"主系表结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":3,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-00c2496c09e4746a"},{"stem":"正是那本书的作者获得了茅盾文学奖。","options":[],"answer":"It was the writer of that book who won the Mao Dun Literature Prize.","explanation":"强调句结构it is/was...that/who...。","point":"强调句型。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":4,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-5715b775e53d3ae1"},{"stem":"我们发现在今晚不可能完成这项工作。","options":[],"answer":"We found it impossible to finish the job tonight.","explanation":"find it + adj. + to do结构。","point":"it作形式宾语。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":5,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-f1eb0089ee3a050d"},{"stem":"他比我们想象的成功。","options":[],"answer":"He's more successful than we thought.","explanation":"翻译时注意形容词比较级be + adj.（比较级）+ than，这里的than之后接“我们想象的”，是将现在与过去所想象的进行对比，动词用过去式，翻译为we thought。","point":"形容词比较级。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配","比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":6,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-f8f53fe1d05eacf7"},{"stem":"这个故事使我想起了我的母亲。","options":[],"answer":"This story reminds me of my mother.","explanation":"remind somebody of somebody意为“使某人想起某人”。“这个故事”作主语，谓语动词应用第三人称单数形式。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"汉译英","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":7,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-3219b3f4c7489514"},{"stem":"我向你保证我有能力解决这个问题。","options":[],"answer":"I assure you that I have the ability to solve the problem.","explanation":"“向某人保证……”译为assure somebody that...。“有能力做某事”译为have the ability to do something。","point":"宾语从句和双宾语。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":8,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-74f502cc0b72c0b5"},{"stem":"等我们赶到那里时，天渐渐黑下来了。","options":[],"answer":"By the time we got there, it was already getting dark.","explanation":"首先，翻译时间状语时用by the time引导。其次，由主句“天渐渐黑下来了”可以推断出应选用过去进行时。","point":"过去进行时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":9,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-e55cc7ccbe2a0ff3"},{"stem":"英国人和美国人不但说同一种语言，而且有很多相同的风俗习惯。","options":[],"answer":"The British and the Americans not only speak the same language but also share many customs.","explanation":"本题考查not only...but also...固定句型，连接两个并列谓语speak和share。“the + 形容词”表示一类人（the British英国人，the Americans美国人），谓语用复数。“很多”修饰可数名词customs，可用many或a large number of。“风俗习惯”译为customs即可，不必重复habits。若将not only置于句首，需倒装：Not only do the British...but also...。","point":"固定句型（not only...but also...）+ 名词复数及主谓一致。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配","主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":10,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-460ae4a920fb430f"},{"stem":"他昨天写了一封信。","options":[],"answer":"He wrote a letter yesterday.","explanation":"找出该简单句的主谓宾“他写信”，确定时态为一般过去时，时间状语yesterday置于句末。","point":"一般过去时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":11,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-892a013adff155ba"},{"stem":"我不记得在哪儿见过他了。","options":[],"answer":"I can't remember where I have seen him.","explanation":"根据汉语意思确定使用“where”引导的宾语从句，“我曾经见过他”这一宾语从句的时态为现在完成时，翻译为“I have seen him”。","point":"where引导的宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":12,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-2473360a6a31aaa9"},{"stem":"这音乐让每个人都想跳舞。","options":[],"answer":"This music makes everyone want to dance.","explanation":"“让某人做某事”翻译时可用make/let somebody do something。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"汉译英","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":13,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-13916055aebc6eb1"},{"stem":"她花了很长时间读这本书。","options":[],"answer":"It took her a long time to read this book.","explanation":"“某人花费时间做某事”用结构“it takes somebody some time to do something”，根据“花了”可确定谓语动词用一般过去时。","point":"固定句型。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":14,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-e6b338e7af6bfc31"},{"stem":"我们需要的是自由。","options":[],"answer":"What we need is freedom.","explanation":"根据中文“我们需要的”可选用“what we need”作为主语从句，整个句子采用主系表结构，谓语动词用单数“is”。","point":"主语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":15,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-9de995052f87ed8e"},{"stem":"这部电影值得一看。","options":[],"answer":"The film is worth seeing.","explanation":"“值得做某事”用“be worth doing”，主动形式表示被动意义。","point":"“be worth doing”结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":16,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-019530176d4d57c4"},{"stem":"正是他们昨天清扫的教室。","options":[],"answer":"It was they that (who) cleaned the classroom yesterday.","explanation":"本题考查强调句型“It is/was + 被强调部分 + that/who + 其他”。被强调部分为主语they（人），引导词可用that或who。注意被强调部分在句中作主语时，代词需用主格they（而非宾格them）。将强调结构去掉后，句子还原为They cleaned the classroom yesterday.，结构完整，符合强调句的特征。","point":"强调句型（It is/was... that/who...）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":17,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-75e9fcac7e641541"},{"stem":"该公司承认，前方的道路困难重重。","options":[],"answer":"The company admits that the road ahead is full of difficulties.","explanation":"“承认……”用“admit that...”；“困难重重”译为“is full of difficulties”。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":18,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-8919ab95868c71a3"},{"stem":"我们期待和你一起工作。","options":[],"answer":"We are looking forward to working with you.","explanation":"“期待做某事”用“look forward to doing sth.”，其中“to”是介词。","point":"“look forward to”短语。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":19,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-d2a65227e26b083e"},{"stem":"无论经济形势有多糟糕，这家公司都能盈利。","options":[],"answer":"The company makes a profit no matter how bad the economic situation is.","explanation":"“无论多……”用“no matter how + 形容词 + 主语 + 谓语”；“盈利”译为“make a profit”。","point":"“no matter how”让步状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":20,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-e7ba02e7487a0a82"},{"stem":"我们的友谊将地久天长。","options":[],"answer":"Our friendship will last forever.","explanation":"“地久天长”译为“last forever”。","point":"一般将来时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":21,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-434a08de0337fb22"},{"stem":"他儿子太小不能上学。","options":[],"answer":"His son is too young to go to school.","explanation":"“太小不能……”译为“too young to...”。","point":"“too...to”结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":22,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-f6c40ebcae986ec9"},{"stem":"你越用功，进步就越大。","options":[],"answer":"The harder you work, the greater progress you will make.","explanation":"“越……越……”结构。","point":"“the + 比较级，the + 比较级”。","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":23,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-3f09e5b1396293f5"},{"stem":"昨天我读过的那本书在哪里？","options":[],"answer":"Where is the book (that) I read yesterday?","explanation":"关系代词“that”可省略。","point":"定语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":24,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-9d2368c00eb4d834"},{"stem":"当春天到来的时候，我们去公园吧。","options":[],"answer":"When spring comes, let's go to the park.","explanation":"主句用“let's”，从句用一般现在时。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":25,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-999c324cdeaf6d4c"},{"stem":"我一到那里，就打电话给你。","options":[],"answer":"I will telephone you as soon as I get there.","explanation":"主句用一般将来时，从句用一般现在时表示将来。","point":"“as soon as”引导时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":26,"group":"汉译英","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-92e40e3d53f05f1b"},{"stem":"The Dutch company Nerdalize thinks paying for electricity to operate the servers and then paying again to cool them is a waste of energy.","options":[],"answer":"一家名为Nerdalize的荷兰公司认为，维持这些服务器运转得付电费，随后冷却还得付费，这是一种能源浪费。","explanation":"宾语从句顺译；“a waste of”译为“……的浪费”。","point":"宾语从句和短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":1,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-0059e699679cb9b3"},{"stem":"He says it cannot be used as the primary source of heat.","options":[],"answer":"他指出，这种热量还不能用作供热的主要来源。","explanation":"“be used as”译为“用作”；“primary source of heat”译为“供热的主要来源”。","point":"宾语从句和短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":2,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-0fcddb740bb2540f"},{"stem":"Google also makes its employees want to work because managers provide tasks that are inspiring and challenging.","options":[],"answer":"谷歌还可以使员工拥有工作热情，因为管理人员提供了令人振奋和充满挑战的任务。","explanation":"将形容词“inspiring and challenging”放到“任务”之前翻译。","point":"定语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":3,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-637f413eff2cb742"},{"stem":"\"If you value people, and care about them as whole people, one thing you do is giving them a voice, and you really listen.\"","options":[],"answer":"如果你重视人才，把他们当作一个全方位的个体来关心，你所要做的事就是提供给他们一个发声的机会，而你要认真地倾听。","explanation":"“give them a voice”译为“提供给他们一个发声的机会”。","point":"并列句和短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":4,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-5480a20da0c717d4"},{"stem":"Let children learn to judge their own work.","options":[],"answer":"让孩子们学习对自己所做的事情做出判断。","explanation":"“learn to do”译为“学会做”；“judge one's own work”译为“对自己……的事情做出判断”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":5,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-a43b646b786ec2cd"},{"stem":"What other people see as garbage, I see as potential art.","options":[],"answer":"别人视为垃圾的东西，在我看来却是潜在的艺术品。","explanation":"本题考查what引导的名词性从句及宾语前置的翻译。 - what other people see as garbage是what引导的宾语从句（相当于the thing that...），在句中作see的宾语，为了强调而置于句首； - see A as B意为“把A看作B”； - 前后分句存在隐形的转折关系，翻译时补充“却”字，使逻辑更通顺。","point":"名词性从句（宾语从句）及宾语前置的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":6,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-c19b854487603307"},{"stem":"I also create more practical, useable art out of the trash I find.","options":[],"answer":"我还从找到的废旧物品中创造了更实用、更有用的艺术品。","explanation":"本题考查短语的翻译。“create art”翻译为“创造艺术作品”，“out of the trash I find”翻译为“从找到的废旧物品中”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":7,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-37587c0c0fc67ad0"},{"stem":"Some styles, for instance, are more people-oriented, while others tend to focus on a project or product.","options":[],"answer":"例如，一些风格更加以人为本，有些则专注于项目或产品本身。","explanation":"“while”在本题中表示对比转折，所以该句的主体是“一些……，另一些则……”。“focus on”翻译为“专注于……”，“people-oriented”翻译为“以人为本”。","point":"while对比句型的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":8,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-2345643a95a92773"},{"stem":"When you motivate people to pool their knowledge, the results may exceed your expectations.","options":[],"answer":"当你激发员工集思广益时，结果可能超出你的预期。","explanation":"“when”引导的状语从句往往翻译为“当……时，……”。“pool their knowledge”翻译为“集思广益”，“exceed your expectations”翻译为“超出你的预期”。","point":"when引导的状语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":9,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-1bbe0b0f4ed25cac"},{"stem":"The sooner the world comes together to help West Africa, the safer we all will be.","options":[],"answer":"世界越早团结一致帮助西非，我们就越安全。","explanation":"“the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...”句型翻译为“越……，越……”。“come together”翻译为“团结一致”。","point":"“the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...”句型的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":10,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-ccd709965d7afd3f"},{"stem":"One of your biggest struggles is to remind yourself of appropriate expectations.","options":[],"answer":"你最需要费力克服的事就是提醒自己要有适度的期望。","explanation":"“one's biggest struggles”译为“最需要费力克服的事”；“remind yourself of appropriate expectations”译为“提醒自己要有适度的期望”。","point":"短语翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":11,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-0c5d7a376c118904"},{"stem":"Besides, the more time you spend with your kids, the better you'll get at communicating with them.","options":[],"answer":"除此之外，你陪伴孩子的时间越长，你就越能更好地和他们沟通。","explanation":"该句型译为“越……，越……”。“get better at doing sth.”译为“更擅长做某事”。","point":"“the+比较级，the+比较级”结构。","category":"英译汉","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":12,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-7819cd2b9591459e"},{"stem":"Kelvin Macharia has invented a tracking device that uses computers and wireless technology to help owners know where their cars are.","options":[],"answer":"开尔文·马查里亚发明了一种追踪装置，它利用电脑和无线技术让车主知道车的位置。","explanation":"本题考查定语从句及动词不定式的翻译。 - that uses computers and wireless technology是that引导的限制性定语从句，修饰先行词tracking device； - 翻译时，由于定语从句较短，采用了前置法，将其译为“……的”结构，即“利用电脑和无线技术的”； - to help owners know...是不定式短语作目的状语，译为“让/帮助车主知道……”。","point":"定语从句的翻译及非谓语动词。","category":"英译汉","topics":["非谓语动词","定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":13,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-74d156e1a9a20478"},{"stem":"He says his company is now worth more than $100,000 and has more than 100 companies as clients.","options":[],"answer":"他说他的公司现在价值超过10万美元，拥有100余家公司客户。","explanation":"“is worth”译为“价值”；“has...as clients”译为“拥有……作为客户”。","point":"宾语从句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":14,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-6c024dbb30b784e2"},{"stem":"Information technology serves as the eyes and ears of management in a supply chain.","options":[],"answer":"信息技术在供应链上充当管理的眼睛和耳朵。","explanation":"“serves as”译为“充当”；“the eyes and ears”保留比喻，译为“眼睛和耳朵”。","point":"比喻句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":15,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-eecc205357048051"},{"stem":"It was divided into several departments at that time, such as the sales department, marketing department, and production department.","options":[],"answer":"当时，公司被划分为几个部门，例如销售部、营销部和生产部。","explanation":"本题考查代词补译、被动语态及专有名词的翻译。 - 英文原句使用了代词It作主语，在翻译成中文时，需结合上下文逻辑，将其具体化补译为“公司”； - was divided into为被动语态，译为“被分为……”； - such as引导举例，译为“例如”； - 掌握常见企业部门名称的翻译：sales department（销售部）、marketing department（营销部/市场部）、production department（生产部）。","point":"主语的补译和被动句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":16,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-1faa55a0d04569e5"},{"stem":"The structure today is that we form teams within teams to place people who can manufacture a product.","options":[],"answer":"如今的组织架构是，我们在大团队内部组建小团队，调配能够生产产品的人员。","explanation":"本句含有that引导的表语从句，采取顺译；句中包含定语从句“who can manufacture a product”，中文拆分为分句处理。“form teams within teams”译为“在大团队内部组建小团队”；“place people”译为“调配人员”。","point":"表语从句和定语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":17,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-6494d2c6a07d3ad0"},{"stem":"With the recent focus on customer privacy, door-knocking seems like an intrusion into other people's lives.","options":[],"answer":"随着近来对客户隐私的重视，上门探访似乎是对他人生活的侵扰。","explanation":"“with...”结构放句首通常翻译为“随着……”；“door-knocking”的意思是“敲门”，翻译为“上门探访”；“an intrusion into other people's lives”翻译为“对他人生活的侵扰”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":18,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-85755925f6f1de51"},{"stem":"Being a neighbor creates an immediate connection with the person answering the door; after that, everything else is easy.","options":[],"answer":"作为邻居能即刻与开门的人产生联结感，之后其他事情就都好办了。","explanation":"“being a neighbor”是现在分词短语作主语，翻译为“作为邻居”，更符合中文表达习惯。“connection”是“联结”的意思，“creates an immediate connection with”译为“即刻与……产生联结感”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":19,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-089d68645eae0bc6"},{"stem":"The Independent Television Act created an Independent Television Authority, which exercises general supervision.","options":[],"answer":"独立电视法案促成独立电视管理局的设立，由其行使监管权。","explanation":"翻译非限制性定语从句时，判断先行词充当的成分，以合理的逻辑关系使之成句。本句“which”代指“独立电视管理局”充当从句主语，直接承接主句加连接词“由其……”即可。","point":"非限制性定语从句和短语的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":20,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-54046499e88478f9"},{"stem":"You cannot live in the past, so denying that change could occur only makes things more complicated for you.","options":[],"answer":"你不能活在过去，所以否认变化可能发生只会让事情对你来说更加复杂。","explanation":"本题考查非谓语动词及宾语从句。 - denying that change could occur 是动名词短语作主语，其中 that change could occur 是 denying 的宾语从句，译为“否认变化可能发生”； - makes things more complicated 是“动词＋宾语＋宾语补足语”结构，译为“让事情更复杂”。 - 全句逻辑为：不能活在过去 → 否认变化 → 事情变复杂。","point":"宾语从句、动名词短语作主语。","category":"英译汉","topics":["非谓语动词","名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":21,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-22eb2576448057f6"},{"stem":"Some universities offer free, noncredit MOOCs available to anyone in the world.","options":[],"answer":"一些大学提供免费的、无学分的MOOC（大规模开放在线课程），面向世界上的任何人开放。","explanation":"“available to anyone in the world”修饰“MOOCs”，译为“面向世界上的任何人开放的”。","point":"形容词短语作定语。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":22,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-b153d85e9e164d44"},{"stem":"We can certainly deliver high-quality education to many students at a much lower cost.","options":[],"answer":"我们当然可以以低得多的成本向许多学生提供高质量的教育。","explanation":"“deliver...to...”译为“向……提供……”；“at a much lower cost”译为“以低得多的成本”。","point":"短语翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":23,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-a87432b1345f712b"},{"stem":"The first factor in team effectiveness is the diversity of skills and personalities.","options":[],"answer":"团队效率的第一个因素是技能和个性的多样性。","explanation":"“team effectiveness”译为“团队效率”；“diversity of skills and personalities”译为“技能和个性的多样性”。","point":"名词短语翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":24,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-3ccef3906bf82e91"},{"stem":"In real life, team work success rarely happens by itself if there are no focused team building efforts or activities.","options":[],"answer":"在现实生活中，如果没有有针对性的团队建设努力或活动，团队合作的成功很少会自动发生。","explanation":"“by itself”译为“自动地、自行地”；“focused team building efforts”译为“有针对性的团队建设努力”。","point":"条件状语从句。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":25,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-11982aadb5163ad0"},{"stem":"They will help to improve the lives of people with vision loss and vision difficulties.","options":[],"answer":"它们将有助于改善视力受损人群的生活。","explanation":"1. help to do 表示“有助于做某事”，help 后可接不定式（带 to 或不带 to）； 2. with vision loss and vision difficulties 是介词短语作后置定语，修饰 people，意为“有视力损失和视力困难的人”，在中文中可合并意译为“视力受损人群”； 3. vision loss 泛指视力下降/丧失，不等同于全盲（blindness），翻译时需注意程度区分。","point":"介词短语作定语及 help to do 句式的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":26,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-860af675adf43b2b"},{"stem":"However, breeding alone will not be enough to turn these young dogs into guide dogs.","options":[],"answer":"然而，仅靠饲养尚不足以将这些幼犬变成导盲犬。","explanation":"“turn...into...”译为“将……变成……”。","point":"转折关系翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":27,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-10bf063d41637213"},{"stem":"Television has become such a major part of life that many American parents use it as a babysitter.","options":[],"answer":"电视已经成为生活中如此重要的一部分，以至于许多美国父母把它当作保姆。","explanation":"“use...as a babysitter”译为“把……当作保姆”。","point":"“such...that”结构。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":28,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-bb3b5ee57e5922ee"},{"stem":"One's health should never be sacrificed for a need to work hard.","options":[],"answer":"永远不要为了迎合高强度的工作而牺牲个人健康。","explanation":"本题考查被动语态及介词短语的翻译。 - should never be sacrificed 为情态动词的被动语态，译为“永远不应该被牺牲/永远不要牺牲”； - be sacrificed for... 意为“为了……而牺牲……”； - a need to work hard 中，to work hard 是不定式作后置定语修饰 need，结合语境可意译为“迎合高强度的工作”或“拼命工作的需求”。","point":"被动语态翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":29,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-c9523f8e608127c7"},{"stem":"Traveling at home and abroad has now become convenient and affordable.","options":[],"answer":"如今，国内外旅游变得既便捷又经济实惠。","explanation":"本题考查形容词及动名词作主语的翻译。 - Traveling at home and abroad 是动名词短语作主语，译为“国内外旅游”； - convenient 译为“便捷的，方便的”； - affordable 意为“买得起的，价格合理的”，在旅游语境下常译为“经济实惠的”或“可负担的”。","point":"动名词作主语及形容词翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":30,"group":"英译汉","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-73a6aaf8f8f50d78"},{"stem":"I enjoyed the movie very much. I wish I ____ the book from which it was made.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have read"},{"key":"B","text":"had read"},{"key":"C","text":"should have read"},{"key":"D","text":"are reading"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"wish后接宾语从句，表达与过去事实相反的愿望，谓语动词使用过去完成时had done。\n句意：我非常喜欢这部电影。我真希望我读过改编成这部电影的那本书。","point":"虚拟语气-wish从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":1,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-9d7a2dd1c3be76b8"},{"stem":"You are late. If you ____ a few minutes earlier, you ____ him.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"come; would meet"},{"key":"B","text":"had come; would have met"},{"key":"C","text":"come; will meet"},{"key":"D","text":"had come; would meet"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"与过去事实相反的if虚拟条件句，从句用had done，主句用would have done。\n句意：你迟到了。如果你早几分钟来，你就会见到他了。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反的if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":2,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-5e77726e4172c97e"},{"stem":"The two students talked as if they ____ friends for years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should be"},{"key":"B","text":"would be"},{"key":"C","text":"have been"},{"key":"D","text":"had been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as if引导从句，描述与过去事实不符的假象，从句使用过去完成时had done。\n句意：这两个学生交谈着，仿佛他们是多年的朋友。","point":"虚拟语气-as if引导对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":3,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-3302c55e946b7f37"},{"stem":"It is important that I ____ with Mr. Williams immediately.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"speak"},{"key":"B","text":"spoke"},{"key":"C","text":"will speak"},{"key":"D","text":"to speak"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is important that...主语从句虚拟，从句用(should)＋动词原形，should可以省略。\n句意：我必须立刻和威廉姆斯先生谈话，这件事很重要。","point":"虚拟语气-It is important that句型 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":4,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-7cbc8b78dfa8c9b1"},{"stem":"He looked as if he ____ ill for a long time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was"},{"key":"B","text":"were"},{"key":"C","text":"has been"},{"key":"D","text":"had been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主句looked为过去时，as if表示与过去事实相反，从句用had done。\n句意：他看上去好像已经病了很久。","point":"虚拟语气-as if对过去事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":5,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-b7da8d0980845282"},{"stem":"If the doctor had come earlier, the poor child would not ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have laid there for two hours"},{"key":"B","text":"have been lied there for two hours"},{"key":"C","text":"have lied there for two hours"},{"key":"D","text":"have lain there for two hours"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"lie（躺）的过去分词为lain；本句是对过去虚拟，主句would have done。\n句意：如果医生早点来，这个可怜的孩子就不会在那儿躺两个小时了。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反；lie形近词辨析。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":6,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-23f5f708d471af6d"},{"stem":"I wish that I ____ with you last night.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"went"},{"key":"B","text":"could go"},{"key":"C","text":"have gone"},{"key":"D","text":"could have gone"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"last night为过去时间，wish从句表达过去本能够做却未能实现的愿望，用could have done。\n句意：我真希望昨晚我能跟你一起去。","point":"虚拟语气-wish从句对过去虚拟 could have done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":7,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":57,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-26bc662c5bf43b64"},{"stem":"Let’s say you could go there again, how ____ feel?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will you"},{"key":"B","text":"should you"},{"key":"C","text":"would you"},{"key":"D","text":"do you"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"本句为对将来情况的虚拟，主句谓语使用would＋动词原形。\n句意：假设你可以再去那里，你会有什么感受？","point":"虚拟语气-对将来虚拟主句结构。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":8,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-fe85af0b0c359fc3"},{"stem":"I can’t stand him. He always talks as though he ____ everything.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"knew"},{"key":"B","text":"knows"},{"key":"C","text":"has known"},{"key":"D","text":"had known"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"as though引导与现在事实相反的虚拟，从句谓语用一般过去式。\n句意：我受不了他。他说起话来好像什么都知道。","point":"虚拟语气-as though对现在事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":9,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-7b87370496269ff4"},{"stem":"____ the fog, we should have reached our school.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Because of"},{"key":"B","text":"In spite of"},{"key":"C","text":"In case of"},{"key":"D","text":"But for"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"but for意为“要不是”，引导含蓄虚拟条件，主句should have done表示对过去虚拟。\n句意：要不是这场大雾，我们本应该早就到学校了。","point":"虚拟语气-but for含蓄虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":10,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-bbe70bff611c94e8"},{"stem":"If you had told me in advance, I ____ him at the airport.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would meet"},{"key":"B","text":"would had met"},{"key":"C","text":"would have met"},{"key":"D","text":"would have meet"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"从句had told是对过去虚拟，主句用would have done。\n句意：如果你事先告诉我，我就会去机场接他。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":11,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-cfc22928ea360d1d"},{"stem":"Mike can take his car apart and put it back together again. I certainly wish he ____ me how.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"teaches"},{"key":"B","text":"will teach"},{"key":"C","text":"has taught"},{"key":"D","text":"would teach"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"wish从句表示对将来的愿望，希望对方做某事，用would＋动词原形。\n句意：迈克能把汽车拆开再组装好。我真希望他教教我怎么做。","point":"虚拟语气-wish从句表将来愿望 would do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":12,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-67a32d476c3c95d0"},{"stem":"I would have told him the answer had it been possible, but I ____ so busy then.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been"},{"key":"B","text":"were"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"but之后陈述真实过去事实，不是虚拟；then提示用一般过去时was。\n句意：如果有可能，我本来会告诉他答案的，但我那时候太忙了。","point":"虚拟语气与真实陈述区分-but转折用真实时态。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":13,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-5b8d387a189ef651"},{"stem":"He’s working hard for fear that he ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should fall behind"},{"key":"B","text":"fell behind"},{"key":"C","text":"may fall behind"},{"key":"D","text":"would fallen behind"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"for fear that（生怕，唯恐）引导虚拟从句，谓语用should＋动词原形。\n句意：他努力学习，生怕自己落后。","point":"虚拟语气-for fear that从句 should do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":14,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-064577bf3e8fbcac"},{"stem":"If it ____ another ten minutes, the game would have been called off.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had rained"},{"key":"B","text":"would have rained"},{"key":"C","text":"would rain"},{"key":"D","text":"rained"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句would have been called off，对过去虚拟，if从句使用had done。\n句意：如果当时雨再下十分钟，比赛就会被取消。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":15,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-891204195f55245f"},{"stem":"He suggested that they ____ use a trick instead of fighting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should"},{"key":"B","text":"would"},{"key":"C","text":"do"},{"key":"D","text":"had"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"suggest表示建议，宾语从句虚拟，(should)＋动词原形，空格处即should，故不可省略。\n句意：他建议他们耍个计谋，而不是动手打架。","point":"虚拟语气-suggest表建议后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":16,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-a4f4ea82b12a651d"},{"stem":"My father did not go to New York; the doctor suggested that he ____ there.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"not went"},{"key":"B","text":"won’t go"},{"key":"C","text":"not go"},{"key":"D","text":"not to go"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"suggest表建议，从句虚拟(should)＋动词原形；否定形式(should) not do，should省略直接not go。\n句意：我父亲没有去纽约；医生建议他不要去那里。","point":"虚拟语气-suggest后从句否定式虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":17,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-f38e14b30742c1ed"},{"stem":"I would have gone to the meeting if I ____ time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had had"},{"key":"B","text":"have had"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"would have had"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对过去事实相反的虚拟，if从句用had done。\n句意：如果我当时有时间，我就去参加会议了。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":18,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-010fb57ebb9f32bc"},{"stem":"Would you rather I ____ buying a new bike?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"decided against"},{"key":"B","text":"will decide against"},{"key":"C","text":"have decided"},{"key":"D","text":"shall decide against"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"would rather后接从句，对现在/将来虚拟，谓语动词用一般过去式。\n句意：你宁愿我打消买新自行车的念头吗？","point":"虚拟语气-would rather后接从句用过去式。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":19,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-dde500933fd825e7"},{"stem":"You look so tired tonight. It is time you ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"go to sleep"},{"key":"B","text":"went to sleep"},{"key":"C","text":"go to bed"},{"key":"D","text":"went to bed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It is time that句型，从句谓语必须用动词过去式；go to bed表示上床睡觉。\n句意：你今晚看上去很累。你该上床睡觉了。","point":"虚拟语气-It is time that句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":20,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-822b8f9c9316eccd"},{"stem":"—Why didn’t you buy a new car? —I would have bought one if I ____ enough money.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had"},{"key":"B","text":"have had"},{"key":"C","text":"would have"},{"key":"D","text":"had had"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"与过去事实相反，if从句用had done。\n句意：——你为什么没有买新车？——如果当时我有足够的钱，我就买一辆了。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":21,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-38bb62378f42c9fb"},{"stem":"If she could sew, ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"she make a dress"},{"key":"B","text":"she would make a dress"},{"key":"C","text":"she will make a shirt"},{"key":"D","text":"she would had made a coat"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"If she could sew 是对现在能力的虚拟，主句应使用would＋动词原形来表示对现在或将来的虚拟结果。\n句意：如果她会做针线活，她就会做一件连衣裙。","point":"虚拟语气—与现在事实相反的if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":22,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-46c78e789a50aa7e"},{"stem":"____ today, he would get there by Friday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Would he leave"},{"key":"B","text":"Was he leaving"},{"key":"C","text":"Were he to leave"},{"key":"D","text":"If he leaves"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对将来虚拟，if从句were to do；省略if，把were提前倒装Were he to leave。\n句意：假如他今天动身，星期五前就能到那儿。","point":"虚拟语气-将来虚拟、if省略倒装 were to do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":23,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":44,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-9deba2174ad2375a"},{"stem":"His doctor suggested that he ____ a short trip abroad.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will take"},{"key":"B","text":"would take"},{"key":"C","text":"take"},{"key":"D","text":"took"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"本题考查suggest表示“建议”时，其后that宾语从句中的虚拟语气。此时从句谓语应用（should）＋动词原形（should可省略）。本题选项中没有should take，因此选用省略should后的动词原形take。will take / would take / took均为陈述语气，不符合suggest表“建议”的虚拟要求。\n句意：他的医生建议他去国外进行一次短途旅行。","point":"虚拟语气（suggest表示“建议”后接（should）do）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":24,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-019e0f795ee6daff"},{"stem":"The Bakers arrived last night. If they’d only let us know earlier, ____ at the station.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"we’d meet them"},{"key":"B","text":"we’ll meet them"},{"key":"C","text":"we’d have met them"},{"key":"D","text":"we’ve met them"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"从句had let是对过去虚拟，主句用would have done。\n句意：贝克一家昨晚到了。要是他们早点告诉我们，我们就会去车站接他们。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":25,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-9e6edca6be32cb7c"},{"stem":"If I ____ you, I ____ more attention to English idioms and phrases.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was; shall pay"},{"key":"B","text":"am; will pay"},{"key":"C","text":"would be; would pay"},{"key":"D","text":"were; would pay"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"If I were you对现在事实虚拟；be动词虚拟一律用were，主句would+动词原形。\n句意：如果我是你，我会更加注意英语习语和短语。","point":"虚拟语气-与现在事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":26,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-c569de069c159679"},{"stem":"We might have failed if you ____ us a helping hand.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have not given"},{"key":"B","text":"would not give"},{"key":"C","text":"had not given"},{"key":"D","text":"did not give"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"主句might have done对过去虚拟，if从句用had not done。\n句意：如果当初你没有帮我们一把，我们可能就失败了。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":27,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-38b94268ed2da03b"},{"stem":"The law requires that everyone ____ his car checked at least once a year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"had"},{"key":"C","text":"have"},{"key":"D","text":"will have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"require that...从句虚拟，(should)+动词原形，should省略直接用have。\n句意：法律要求每个人每年至少把汽车检修一次。","point":"虚拟语气-require后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":28,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-8f7a1899382b898c"},{"stem":"It is strange that he ____ so.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would say"},{"key":"B","text":"would speak"},{"key":"C","text":"should say"},{"key":"D","text":"will speak"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It is strange that...主语从句虚拟，从句使用should+动词原形。\n句意：真奇怪，他竟然这么说。","point":"虚拟语气-It is strange that句型 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":29,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-45251a7a945ef0cb"},{"stem":"Had I known her name, ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"or does she know mine?"},{"key":"B","text":"and where does she live?"},{"key":"C","text":"she would be beautiful."},{"key":"D","text":"I would have invited her to lunch."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"Had I known=If I had known，省略if的过去虚拟倒装，主句用would have done。\n句意：要是我当时知道她的名字，我就会邀请她吃午饭。","point":"虚拟语气-if省略，had提前倒装（对过去虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":30,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-755561d4ec32ab0e"},{"stem":"He has just arrived, but he talks as if he ____ all about that.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"know"},{"key":"B","text":"knows"},{"key":"C","text":"known"},{"key":"D","text":"knew"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as if引导与现在事实相反的虚拟，从句谓语用一般过去式。\n句意：他刚刚到，但是他说起话来好像对那件事了如指掌。","point":"虚拟语气-as if对现在事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":31,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-3d3f363c123e6cd1"},{"stem":"If I ____ the money, I would have bought a much bigger car.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"possessed"},{"key":"B","text":"owned"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"had had"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主句would have done对过去虚拟，if从句用had done。\n句意：如果我当时有这笔钱，我就会买一辆大得多的汽车。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":32,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-7389cdb2a7cd70f1"},{"stem":"He was very busy yesterday; otherwise, he ____ to the meeting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would come"},{"key":"B","text":"came"},{"key":"C","text":"would have come"},{"key":"D","text":"will come"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"otherwise含蓄虚拟，yesterday提示对过去虚拟，主句would have done。\n句意：他昨天很忙，不然他本来会参加会议的。","point":"虚拟语气-otherwise引导含蓄虚拟条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":33,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-f7e8ba55e131be10"},{"stem":"The librarian insists that John ____ no more books from the library before he returns all the books he has borrowed.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will take"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"take"},{"key":"D","text":"takes"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"insist表示“坚持要求”，宾语从句虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略用take。\n句意：图书管理员坚持要求约翰归还所有借的书之后，才能再从图书馆借书。","point":"虚拟语气-insist表坚持要求后从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":34,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-26e3dba88e93d7c3"},{"stem":"I left very early last night, but I wish I ____ so early.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"didn’t leave"},{"key":"B","text":"hadn’t left"},{"key":"C","text":"haven’t left"},{"key":"D","text":"couldn’t leave"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"last night过去时间，wish从句表达与过去事实相反的愿望，否定用hadn’t done。\n句意：我昨晚走得很早，但是我真希望我没有那么早离开。","point":"虚拟语气-wish从句对过去虚拟否定。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":35,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-2589edbf9aa9eb1d"},{"stem":"I do not have a job. I would find one but I ____ no time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had"},{"key":"B","text":"didn’t have"},{"key":"C","text":"had had"},{"key":"D","text":"have"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"but后面为真实现在事实，不用虚拟，用一般现在时have。\n句意：我没有工作。我本想找一份，但是我没有时间。","point":"虚拟语气与真实陈述区分-but后用真实时态。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":36,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-f6a3b39828ff7660"},{"stem":"I wish that you ____ such a bad headache because I’m sure that you would have enjoyed the concert.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hadn’t"},{"key":"B","text":"didn’t have had"},{"key":"C","text":"hadn’t had"},{"key":"D","text":"hadn’t have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"wish从句对过去已经发生的事情虚拟，用hadn’t had。\n句意：我真希望你当时头没有疼得这么厉害，我确信你本可以好好欣赏这场音乐会。","point":"虚拟语气-wish从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":37,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-108e2c9a1ad616fe"},{"stem":"He insisted that we all ____ in his office at one o’clock.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be"},{"key":"B","text":"to be"},{"key":"C","text":"would be"},{"key":"D","text":"shall be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"insist表坚持要求，that从句虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略直接be。\n句意：他坚持要求我们所有人一点钟到他的办公室。","point":"虚拟语气-insist后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":38,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-aac121b92c3d5e2c"},{"stem":"Helen couldn’t go to France after all. That’s too bad. I’m sure she would have enjoyed it if ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"she’s gone"},{"key":"B","text":"she’ll go"},{"key":"C","text":"she’d gone"},{"key":"D","text":"she’d go"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"主句would have enjoyed对过去虚拟，if从句用had done，she’d gone = she had gone。\n句意：海伦终究没能去法国。太可惜了。我敢肯定，如果她去了，她会玩得很开心。","point":"虚拟语气-与过去事实相反if条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":39,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-375968f49a2191b9"},{"stem":"Were it not for the snowy weather, we ____ all right.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be"},{"key":"B","text":"would have been"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"may be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"Were it not for...为if it were not for的倒装省略if结构，是对现在事实相反的虚拟，主句使用would+动词原形。\n句意：要不是下雪天气，我们一切都会顺利。","point":"虚拟语气 与现在事实相反的虚拟条件句、if省略倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":40,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-413ff6fe4921316c"},{"stem":"____ more careful, his ship would not have sunk.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If the captain were"},{"key":"B","text":"Had the captain been"},{"key":"C","text":"Should the captain be"},{"key":"D","text":"If the captain would have been"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句would not have sunk说明是对过去事实相反的虚拟；if从句用had done，省略if时把had提前构成倒装。\n句意：如果船长当时更加小心，他的船就不会沉没了。","point":"虚拟语气 与过去事实相反、if省略的倒装结构。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":41,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-e38cdc01abe56545"},{"stem":"If he ____ me tomorrow, I would let him know.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should call"},{"key":"B","text":"should not have been able"},{"key":"C","text":"were not able"},{"key":"D","text":"are not able"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"tomorrow提示是对将来的虚拟，if从句可用should do / were to do / 过去式。should call表示将来万一。\n句意：如果他明天打电话给我，我会通知他。","point":"虚拟语气 对将来事实的虚拟条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":42,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-0227ec26767ae243"},{"stem":"If you asked your father, you ____ permission.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"may get"},{"key":"B","text":"might get"},{"key":"C","text":"should have called"},{"key":"D","text":"maybe get"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"从句asked是对现在/将来虚拟（与事实相反），主句用might/would/could+动词原形；maybe是副词不能作谓语。\n句意：如果你问问你的父亲，你或许可以得到许可。","point":"虚拟语气 与现在/将来相反的条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":43,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-bf14ea0a9bda8164"},{"stem":"____ I you, I would go with him to the party.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Was"},{"key":"B","text":"Had been"},{"key":"C","text":"Will be"},{"key":"D","text":"Were"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"If I were you对现在虚拟，if省略时把were提前，写成Were I you。虚拟中be动词一律用were。\n句意：如果我是你，我就会和他一起去参加派对。","point":"虚拟语气 与现在事实相反、if省略倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":45,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-9f281d2516bae3f2"},{"stem":"The millions of calculations involved, had they been done by hand, ____ all practical value by the time they were finished.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could lose"},{"key":"B","text":"would have lost"},{"key":"C","text":"might lose"},{"key":"D","text":"ought to have lost"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"had they been done是if省略倒装，对过去虚拟；by the time they were finished表示过去时间，主句用would have done。\n句意：相关的数百万次运算，如果靠手工完成，等到算完时就已经失去全部实用价值。","point":"虚拟语气 过去虚拟、插入式倒装条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":46,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-b92a54bb767c848b"},{"stem":"Had Paul received six more votes in the last election, he ____ our chairman now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"must have been"},{"key":"B","text":"would have been"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"混合虚拟：从句had received是对过去虚拟；主句有now，是对现在虚拟，用would+动词原形。\n句意：要是保罗在上次选举多拿到六票，他现在就是我们的主席了。","point":"虚拟语气 混合（错综时间）虚拟语气。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":47,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":1,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md"}],"id":"q-4611935e87f0bc4e"},{"stem":"If you ____ Jerry Brown until recently, you'd think the photograph on the right was strange.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shouldn't contact"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't contact"},{"key":"C","text":"weren't to contact"},{"key":"D","text":"hadn't contacted"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"until recently，从句是对过去事实虚拟用had done；主句you’d think是对现在虚拟，属于错综时间虚拟句。\n句意：如果你直到最近才接触杰里·布朗，你就会觉得右边那张照片很怪异。","point":"虚拟语气 错综时间混合虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":48,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-f379a09915bbe2b8"},{"stem":"Look at the terrible situation I am in! If only I ____ your advice!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"follow"},{"key":"B","text":"would follow"},{"key":"C","text":"had followed"},{"key":"D","text":"have followed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"If only“要是……就好了”，本句表达后悔，事实是当初没听从建议，对过去虚拟用had done。\n句意：看我现在糟糕处境！我要是当初听了你的建议就好了。","point":"虚拟语气 If only从句（对过去虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":49,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-4e91181ecc1b0928"},{"stem":"If the horse won today, it ____ thirty races in five years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would have won"},{"key":"B","text":"won"},{"key":"C","text":"must have won"},{"key":"D","text":"did have won"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"本题考查错综时间条件句（混合虚拟语气）。if从句用won（一般过去时）表示与现在事实相反（今天没赢），主句用would have done表示与过去事实相反（五年内本该赢下30场但实际没有）。时态不一致是合理的，因为从句虚拟的时间是“今天”，主句虚拟的结果是“到今天为止的五年内”。B非虚拟，C表推测，D结构错误。\n句意：倘若这匹马今天获胜，那它在五年内就已赢下三十场比赛。","point":"虚拟语气（错综时间条件句 / 混合虚拟语气）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":50,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-eec851ce3b413dea"},{"stem":"There is a real possibility that these animals could be frightened, ____ a sudden loud noise.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"being there"},{"key":"B","text":"should there be"},{"key":"C","text":"there was"},{"key":"D","text":"there having been"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"should there be =if there should be，对将来虚拟，if省略should提前倒装。\n句意：一旦有突然巨大声响，这些动物真的有可能被惊吓。","point":"虚拟语气 将来虚拟、should倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":51,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-37c8a0b8074427cc"},{"stem":"Jean Wagner's most enduring contribution to the study of Afro American poetry is his insistence that it ____ in a religious, as well as worldly, frame of reference.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is to be analyzed"},{"key":"B","text":"has been analyzed"},{"key":"C","text":"be analyzed"},{"key":"D","text":"should have been analyzed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"insistence表示坚持主张，同位语从句虚拟：(should)+动词原形；it和analyze被动，(should) be analyzed，should省略。\n句意：吉恩·瓦格纳对非裔美国诗歌研究最持久的贡献就是，他坚持该诗歌应当从宗教以及世俗双重参照体系下进行分析。","point":"虚拟语气 表示建议/坚持名词后的同位语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":52,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-eec8a4a4ea935ed6"},{"stem":"I would have gone to visit him in the hospital had it been at all possible, but I ____ fully occupied the whole of last week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"have been"},{"key":"D","text":"was"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"but后面陈述真实发生的过去事实，不是虚拟；last week用一般过去时was。\n句意：要是有可能我本会去医院看望他，但我上周一整周都很忙。","point":"虚拟语气与真实陈述区分：but转折真实时态。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":53,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-c8fcf13793363250"},{"stem":"I apologize if I ____ you, but I assure you it was unintentional.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"offend"},{"key":"B","text":"had offended"},{"key":"C","text":"should have offended"},{"key":"D","text":"might have offended"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"本题考查if从句中的虚拟语气。“冒犯”发生在过去（由后文was unintentional可知），if从句假设的是与过去事实相反的情况，因此用had + 过去分词。A项表与现在相反，时态错误；C项表示“本应该冒犯”，语义矛盾；D项表推测而非虚拟，语气不符。\n句意：如果我当时冒犯了你，我很抱歉，但我向你保证那不是故意的。","point":"虚拟语气（if从句与过去事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":54,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-0852438d906d77ad"},{"stem":"If you hadn't taken such a long time to get dressed, we'd ____ there by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be"},{"key":"B","text":"been"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"have been"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"从句hadn’t taken对过去虚拟；by now主句描述现在结果，对现在虚拟用would +动词原形be。\n句意：如果你刚才没有花那么久穿衣打扮，我们现在就已经到那里了。","point":"虚拟语气 错综（混合时间）虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":55,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":2,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md"}],"id":"q-aa7a1e4bfc12a7a7"},{"stem":"The sun rises in the east and sets in the west, so it seems as if the sun ____ round the earth.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were circling"},{"key":"B","text":"circles"},{"key":"C","text":"is circling"},{"key":"D","text":"be circling"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"as if引导与现在事实相反虚拟，be动词用were，进行式were circling表示仿佛正在发生。\n句意：太阳东升西落，所以看上去好像太阳在绕地球转。","point":"虚拟语气 as if引导与现在事实相反。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":56,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-6919e3844c4f33a6"},{"stem":"I wish I ____ with her now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be"},{"key":"B","text":"am"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"were"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"now表示对现在愿望，wish从句虚拟，be动词统一使用were。\n句意：我真希望我现在和他在一起。","point":"虚拟语气 wish对现在虚拟（be动词用were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":58,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-f73b06d36f701279"},{"stem":"I wish that I ____ the concert last night.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could"},{"key":"B","text":"have attended"},{"key":"C","text":"had attended"},{"key":"D","text":"attended"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"last night，wish对过去虚拟，从句用had done。\n句意：我多希望我昨晚听了那场音乐会。","point":"虚拟语气 wish从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":59,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-41bad4d1d2a5509f"},{"stem":"The picture exhibition bored me to death. I wish I ____ to it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had not gone"},{"key":"B","text":"have not gone"},{"key":"C","text":"did not go"},{"key":"D","text":"can not have gone"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"事实已经去了展览感到厌烦；wish对过去虚拟，否定用had not done。\n句意：这个画展把我无聊透顶。我真希望我当初没有去。","point":"虚拟语气 wish从句对过去虚拟否定。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":60,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-0a2a1d90e666ac0d"},{"stem":"\"I wish you ____ me to put these things away,\" he said.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will help"},{"key":"B","text":"help"},{"key":"C","text":"are helping"},{"key":"D","text":"would help"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"wish后对将来愿望，希望对方愿意做某事，用would do。\n句意：“我真希望你能帮我把这些东西收好。”他说道。","point":"虚拟语气 wish从句希望某人将来做某事 would do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":61,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-1b5d385b5fc3e8eb"},{"stem":"The teacher suggested that her students ____ experiences with ESP.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"write a composition on their"},{"key":"B","text":"to write composition about the"},{"key":"C","text":"wrote some compositions of his or her"},{"key":"D","text":"had written any compositions for his"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"suggest表示建议，宾语从句虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略直接用write。\n句意：老师建议学生写一篇关于自己超感官体验的作文。","point":"虚拟语气 suggest表建议后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":62,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-d3eec4c7a23864ea"},{"stem":"He speaks Chinese as fluently as if he ____ a Chinese.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"has been"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"as if，与现在事实相反，他并不是中国人，be动词虚拟用were。\n句意：他中文说得十分流利，仿佛他就是中国人。","point":"虚拟语气 as if与现在事实相反。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":63,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":3,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md"}],"id":"q-d6a259d8fa3066fb"},{"stem":"As usual, he put on a show as though his trip ____ a great success.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been"},{"key":"B","text":"has been"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"was"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"put on show是过去动作；as though表示仿佛过去已经取得成功，与事实相反，用had done。\n句意：像往常一样，他大肆宣扬，仿佛他这次旅行取得巨大成功。","point":"虚拟语气 as though对过去事实虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":64,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-8d33c05196bfea2f"},{"stem":"Looking round the town, he felt as though he ____ away for ages.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has been"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"had been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"felt为过去时；as though从句表达仿佛很久之前就离开此地，对过去虚拟用had done。\n句意：环顾这座小镇，他感觉自己仿佛已经离开这里很久很久。","point":"虚拟语气 as though对过去虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":65,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-05348cc02a8a72d2"},{"stem":"John is so strongly built that he looks as if he ____ an elephant.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lifts"},{"key":"B","text":"is lifting"},{"key":"C","text":"lifted"},{"key":"D","text":"could lift"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as if与现在事实相反，表示仿佛有能力举起大象，用could+动词原形。\n句意：约翰体格如此健壮，看上去仿佛能举起一头大象。","point":"虚拟语气 as if 虚拟中情态动词could用法","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":66,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-5978e01b73feec9a"},{"stem":"He described the town as if he ____ it himself.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had seen"},{"key":"B","text":"has seen"},{"key":"C","text":"saw"},{"key":"D","text":"sees"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"described过去时；事实他并未亲眼见过，as if对过去虚拟用had done。\n句意：他描述这座小镇，仿佛他亲眼见过。","point":"虚拟语气 as if对过去事实虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":67,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-35fd5cd51a4dbe37"},{"stem":"At that thought he shook himself, as though he ____ from an evil dream.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"woke"},{"key":"B","text":"wakes"},{"key":"C","text":"would wake"},{"key":"D","text":"had woken"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as though 引导的从句表示与过去事实相反的虚拟语气，应使用过去完成时（had + 过去分词）。wake 的过去分词是 woken。\n句意：一想到这儿，他浑身一抖，仿佛（刚才）刚从一场噩梦中惊醒过来。","point":"虚拟语气–as though对过去事实虚拟（had done）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":68,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-2c3e1ebc75bcadc8"},{"stem":"Most insurance agents would rather you ____ anything about collecting claims until they investigate the situation.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"do"},{"key":"B","text":"don't"},{"key":"C","text":"didn't"},{"key":"D","text":"didn't do"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"would rather +从句，对现在/将来虚拟，谓语动词用一般过去式；否定用didn’t do。\n句意：大多数保险代理人宁愿你在他们调查清楚情况之前不要做任何有关理赔的操作。","point":"虚拟语气 would rather后接从句用过去式","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":69,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-86fa06a7dbc107c4"},{"stem":"Although most adopted persons want the right to know who their natural parents are, some who have found them wish that they ____ the experience of meeting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hadn't"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't have had"},{"key":"C","text":"hadn't had"},{"key":"D","text":"hadn't have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"已经见过亲生父母（过去发生），wish对过去已发生事情虚拟，希望当初没有经历，用hadn’t had。\n句意：尽管大多数被收养的人希望有权知道自己的亲生父母是谁，但部分找到亲生父母的人却希望自己不曾有过这次相见的经历。","point":"虚拟语气 wish从句对过去已发生事情虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":70,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-bd75ba6aa3f9be76"},{"stem":"It is important that the TOEFL office ____ your registration.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will confirm"},{"key":"B","text":"confirm"},{"key":"C","text":"confirms"},{"key":"D","text":"must confirm"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is important that…主语从句虚拟，从句(should)+动词原形，should省略，直接用confirm。\n句意：托福办公室确认你的注册信息这件事很重要。","point":"虚拟语气 It is important that 句型 (should) do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":71,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":4,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md"}],"id":"q-ea4500f60abd1b7e"},{"stem":"Without electronic computers, much of today's advanced technology ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will not have been achieved"},{"key":"B","text":"have not been achieved"},{"key":"C","text":"would not have been achieved"},{"key":"D","text":"had not been achieved"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"without引导含蓄虚拟，事实已经有计算机，对过去虚拟；technology和achieve被动，主句would not have been done。\n句意：倘若没有电子计算机，如今很多先进技术就无法实现。","point":"虚拟语气 without引导含蓄虚拟条件句","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":72,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-cb8a15a0a6c5fbd0"},{"stem":"He told her to return the book in time so that others ____ a chance to read it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"may have"},{"key":"B","text":"will have"},{"key":"C","text":"would have"},{"key":"D","text":"might have"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"本题考查 so that 引导的目的状语从句中的时态一致。主句 told 为一般过去时，目的状语从句中应使用过去式情态动词 might（may 的过去式），表示“（当时）以便其他人能够有机会”。may have 为现在时形式，时态不一致；will have 和 would have 均不符合目的状语从句中常用 may/might 的习惯。\n句意：他让她按时还书，以便其他人有机会阅读。","point":"目的状语从句（so that 的时态呼应）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","状语从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":73,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-e734808cc6b62e32"},{"stem":"It is time that the government ____ measures to protect the rare birds and animals.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"takes"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"has taken"},{"key":"D","text":"taking"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is time that…句型，从句虚拟，谓语动词必须用过去式。\n句意：政府是时候采取措施保护珍稀鸟兽了。","point":"虚拟语气 It is time that 从句用动词过去式","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":74,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-8597047b58a5d688"},{"stem":"Some people are too particular about school records, insisting that every applicant ____ all diplomas from elementary school to university.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"will have"},{"key":"C","text":"should have"},{"key":"D","text":"must have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"本题考查 insist 表示“坚持要求”时，其后 that 宾语从句的虚拟语气。此时从句谓语应用（should）+ 动词原形（should 可省略）。本题选项中没有省略 should 的 have 形式，故选用完整形式 should have。has 和 will have 为陈述语气，与“要求”语义不符；must have 虽表“必须”，但不能用于 insist 后的虚拟结构。\n句意：有些人对学业记录过分苛求，坚持要求每位申请者都应持有从小学到大学的所有文凭。","point":"虚拟语气（insist 表示“坚持要求”后接（should）do）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":75,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-feeea5f9f30781c5"},{"stem":"He was very busy yesterday, otherwise he ____ to the meeting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would come"},{"key":"B","text":"came"},{"key":"C","text":"would have come"},{"key":"D","text":"had come"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"otherwise含蓄虚拟；yesterday说明是对过去虚拟，主句would have done。\n句意：他昨天很忙，不然他本会参加会议。","point":"虚拟语气 otherwise引导含蓄虚拟条件句","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":76,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-5d4188ec112828ba"},{"stem":"I must say he reads very well, and I shouldn't be surprised if he ____ acting for a living one day.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had taken up"},{"key":"B","text":"takes up"},{"key":"C","text":"have taken up"},{"key":"D","text":"would have taken up"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"本句if引导真实条件句，不是虚拟；主将从现，从句用一般现在时表将来。\n句意：不得不说他读得非常好，如果有一天他以表演谋生，我不会感到惊讶。","point":"真实条件句与虚拟语气区分","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":77,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-50f844ed151ae1ac"},{"stem":"If I had seen the movie, I ____ you all about it now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would tell"},{"key":"B","text":"will tell"},{"key":"C","text":"have told"},{"key":"D","text":"would have told"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"从句had seen对过去虚拟；主句now是对现在虚拟，用would+动词原形。\n句意：如果我当初看过这部电影，我现在就会把全部内容告诉你。","point":"虚拟语气 错综（混合时间）虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":78,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-47a86d07c203635b"},{"stem":"I hadn't expected Henry to apologize but I had hoped ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"him to call me up"},{"key":"B","text":"him calling me up"},{"key":"C","text":"that he would call me up"},{"key":"D","text":"that he will call me"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"had hoped表示过去本希望（未实现），后接that从句，用would do；hope不接hope sb to do；时态保持过去用would。\n句意：我没指望亨利道歉，但我原本希望他会打电话给我。","point":"虚拟语气 had hoped + that从句 would do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":79,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":5,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md"}],"id":"q-a41a701d5a99e1a6"},{"stem":"I had hoped that John ____ a year in Africa, but he stayed there only for three months.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"spends"},{"key":"B","text":"spent"},{"key":"C","text":"would spend"},{"key":"D","text":"will spend"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"had hoped表示过去原本期望，实际未达成，宾语从句用would+动词原形。\n句意：我原本希望约翰能在非洲待一年，但他只待了三个月。","point":"虚拟语气 had hoped后宾语从句 would do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":80,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-2a8a70a2221bb754"},{"stem":"I had hoped that Jennifer ____ a doctor, but she wasn't good enough at science.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will become"},{"key":"B","text":"became"},{"key":"C","text":"would become"},{"key":"D","text":"becomes"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"had hoped，过去本希望但未实现，从句用would do。\n句意：我原本希望詹妮弗成为一名医生，但她理科成绩不够好。","point":"虚拟语气 had hoped + that从句 would do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":81,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-0e1747cded30f4de"},{"stem":"I'd rather you ____ anything about it for the time being.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"do"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't do"},{"key":"C","text":"don't"},{"key":"D","text":"didn't"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"would rather +从句，对现在/将来虚拟，否定用didn’t do。\n句意：我宁愿你暂时不要对此事做任何处理。","point":"虚拟语气 would rather 从句虚拟过去式","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":82,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-f565792006959147"},{"stem":"I'd just as soon ____ rudely to her.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that you won't speak"},{"key":"B","text":"you not speaking"},{"key":"C","text":"you not speak"},{"key":"D","text":"you didn't speak"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"would just as soon=would rather，后接从句虚拟，谓语动词用过去式。\n句意：我宁愿你不要粗鲁地对她说话。","point":"虚拟语气 would just as soon后从句虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":83,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-899b7d38b7eae31d"},{"stem":"It's high time they ____ this road.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"mend"},{"key":"B","text":"mended"},{"key":"C","text":"must have mended"},{"key":"D","text":"will mend"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It’s high time that…，从句虚拟，谓语动词用过去式。\n句意：他们早该修补这条道路了。","point":"虚拟语气 It’s high time that句型","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":84,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-d2c3b4ed6966e6e7"},{"stem":"It's about time people ____ notice of what women did during the war.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"have taken"},{"key":"D","text":"will take"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It’s about time that…，从句谓语动词用过去式表虚拟。\n句意：是时候人们该重视女性在战争期间所做的贡献。","point":"虚拟语气 It’s about time that句型","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":85,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-d79c1e0de0c9385b"},{"stem":"Everybody has arrived. It's time we ____ the class.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shall start"},{"key":"B","text":"started"},{"key":"C","text":"had started"},{"key":"D","text":"start"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It's time that... 句型中，从句谓语动词应用一般过去式（如 started）或 should + 动词原形，表示“该做某事了”。本题选 started。\n句意：所有人都到齐了，我们该上课了。","point":"虚拟语气——It’s time that句型","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":86,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-2a97a9059b6a3eb1"},{"stem":"____ the English examination I would have gone to the concert last Sunday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In spite of"},{"key":"B","text":"But for"},{"key":"C","text":"Because of"},{"key":"D","text":"As for"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"but for +名词，含蓄虚拟“要不是”，主句would have done对过去虚拟。\n句意：要不是英语考试，上周日我就去听音乐会了。","point":"虚拟语气 but for引导含蓄虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":87,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":6,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md"}],"id":"q-a4c3805992e64efd"},{"stem":"Mary ____ my letter; otherwise she would have replied before now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has received"},{"key":"B","text":"ought to have received"},{"key":"C","text":"couldn't have received"},{"key":"D","text":"shouldn't have received"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"本题考查 otherwise 暗示的虚拟语气 + 情态动词对过去的否定推测。otherwise 表示“否则”，暗含一个与过去相反的虚拟条件：如果 Mary 收到了信，她就会回信（would have replied）。但事实上她到现在都没回，因此说话人推测她过去不可能收到信，应用 couldn't have received。A 表已收到，与事实矛盾；B 表“本应收到”，逻辑不通；D 表“本不该收到”，语义不符。\n句意：玛丽不可能收到我的信，否则她早就回信了。","point":"虚拟语气 + 情态动词对过去的推测","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":88,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-13a3dc11fa49a135"},{"stem":"John did not feel well yesterday; otherwise he ____ to see his classmates off.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"came"},{"key":"B","text":"would come"},{"key":"C","text":"would have come"},{"key":"D","text":"should be coming"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"otherwise含蓄虚拟，yesterday提示对过去虚拟，主句would have done。\n句意：约翰昨天身体不舒服，不然他本会去为同学送行。","point":"虚拟语气 otherwise含蓄虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":89,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-984500d62c2db831"},{"stem":"He's working hard for fear that he ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should fall behind"},{"key":"B","text":"fell behind"},{"key":"C","text":"may fall behind"},{"key":"D","text":"would fall behind"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"for fear that“生怕，唯恐”引导从句，虚拟结构用should+动词原形。\n句意：他努力学习，生怕自己落后。","point":"虚拟语气 for fear that从句 should do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":90,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-8474757684add93f"},{"stem":"Without the dreams of the youth, this invention might ____ for a century.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have been postponed"},{"key":"B","text":"has been postponed"},{"key":"C","text":"postpone"},{"key":"D","text":"be postponed"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"without含蓄虚拟，对过去事实虚拟；invention与postpone被动，主句might have been done。\n句意：如果没有年轻人的梦想，这项发明或许会被推迟整整一个世纪。","point":"虚拟语气 without含蓄虚拟条件句","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":91,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-eda39fd6132b7d58"},{"stem":"In the past men generally preferred that their wives ____ in the home.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"worked"},{"key":"B","text":"would work"},{"key":"C","text":"work"},{"key":"D","text":"were working"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"prefer表示宁愿、主张，宾语从句虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略用work。\n句意：过去，男人普遍更希望妻子在家操持家务。","point":"虚拟语气 prefer后that从句 (should) do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":92,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-5cb82cbb534ef8f5"},{"stem":"For a child to give up his less mature idea for a more mature one, it requires that the child ____ psychologically ready for the new idea.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"were"},{"key":"C","text":"be"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"require that…从句虚拟，(should)+动词原形；should省略直接用be。\n句意：孩子要放弃不成熟想法去接受更成熟的观点，就要求孩子心理上做好接纳新观点的准备。","point":"虚拟语气 require后宾语从句 (should) do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":93,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-56f9d6618cddcad2"},{"stem":"Tom's father, as well as his mother, ____ in New York for a few days more.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ask him to stay"},{"key":"B","text":"ask he to stay"},{"key":"C","text":"asks he stays"},{"key":"D","text":"asks he stay"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主语Tom’s father，as well as就远原则谓语asks；ask表示要求，宾语从句虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略用stay。\n句意：汤姆的父亲，还有他母亲，要求他在纽约再多待几天。","point":"虚拟语气 ask表示要求后从句(should) do；主谓一致就远原则","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":94,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-99429a013317859f"},{"stem":"Your advice that ____ till next week is reasonable.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"she waits"},{"key":"B","text":"she wait"},{"key":"C","text":"wait she"},{"key":"D","text":"she waited"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"advice表示建议，that引导同位语从句，虚拟(should)+动词原形，should省略用she wait。\n句意：你提出让她等到下周的建议是合理的。","point":"虚拟语气 advice后同位语从句 (should) do","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":95,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-0fa04cecbcdb9621"},{"stem":"The board deemed it urgent that these files ____ right away.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had to be printed"},{"key":"B","text":"should have been printed"},{"key":"C","text":"must be printed"},{"key":"D","text":"should be printed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"deem it urgent that，it形式宾语；that从句虚拟(should)+动词原形；files和print被动，should be printed。\n句意：董事会认为，这些文件必须立刻打印出来，这件事十分紧急。","point":"虚拟语气 it urgent that 结构 (should) be done","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":96,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-6a17146a79264a58"},{"stem":"It was essential that we ____ the lease before the end of the month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sign"},{"key":"B","text":"signed"},{"key":"C","text":"had signed"},{"key":"D","text":"were signing"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"本题考查 It is/was essential that... 句型中的虚拟语气。在“It is/was + essential/important/necessary + that 从句”结构中，从句谓语应用（should）+ 动词原形（should 可省略），表示“必要/重要”。主句虽为过去时（was），但虚拟语气不随之变化，仍用 sign。B、C、D 均为陈述语气或错误时态，不符合该句型要求。\n句意：我们必须在月底前签署租约。","point":"虚拟语气（It is/was essential that 句型 + (should) do）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":97,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-cfa48c28cd956db4"},{"stem":"It is appropriate that some time ____ thorough study of the results of the Apollo mission.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"devotes to"},{"key":"B","text":"devoted to"},{"key":"C","text":"is devoted to"},{"key":"D","text":"be devoted to"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It is appropriate that…主语从句虚拟(should)+动词原形；time和devote被动，(should) be devoted to。\n句意：应当投入一定时间对阿波罗计划的成果做全面研究。","point":"虚拟语气 It is appropriate that句型 (should) be done","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"essential","day":null,"number":98,"group":"虚拟语气","file":"英语必刷题复习整理.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":8,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md"}],"id":"q-5f7dbfff67bb56a0"},{"stem":"Stop, sir. Please show me your driving license. _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You'll regret it."},{"key":"B","text":"Certainly, here you are."},{"key":"C","text":"I'll remember to bring it."},{"key":"D","text":"I insist on taking this way."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方要求出示驾照，合理应答是“当然，给您”。其他选项与当下要求不符。","point":"情景交际。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":7,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md"}],"id":"q-1afa286a7da84229"},{"stem":"我希望你们明天都能准时到达会场。","options":[],"answer":"I hope that you can all arrive at the meeting hall on time tomorrow.","explanation":"hope (that) ... 引导宾语从句；arrive at 表示到达较小地点，on time 表示准时。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":9,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md"}],"id":"q-292b37acca0a3b73"},{"stem":"我发现学好一门外语需要花很多时间。","options":[],"answer":"I found that it takes a long time to learn a foreign language well.","explanation":"find 后接 that 宾语从句；从句用形式主语 it，句型为 It takes sb time to do。我的译文表达了相同意思，但页面参考答案的 found 使用过去时。","point":"宾语从句；It takes sb time to do 句型。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-229662654764e3ec"},{"stem":"老师解释说太阳比地球大得多。","options":[],"answer":"The teacher explained that the sun is much bigger than the earth.","explanation":"explained 后接 that 宾语从句；客观真理“太阳比地球大”仍用一般现在时，即使主句为过去时。","point":"宾语从句的时态。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-c57c20afe95f3308"},{"stem":"I haven't seen Billy for 10 years. _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Either have"},{"key":"B","text":"So have"},{"key":"C","text":"Haven't"},{"key":"D","text":"Neither have"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"前句为否定句，表示“我也没有”应使用 Neither + 助动词 + 主语 的倒装结构。页面解析给出的完整回答是 Neither have I.。","point":"So / Neither 引导的倒装结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":["页面选项 D 只有 Neither have，缺少主语 I；按标准英语应写为 Neither have I.。"],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-8ba7fb7f3c7e6df2"},{"stem":"他问我是否知道那家书店在哪里。","options":[],"answer":"He asked me whether I knew where the bookstore was.","explanation":"if/whether 引导“是否”的宾语从句，where 引导嵌套宾语从句；从句用陈述语序。主句为过去时，从句作相应的时态变化。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":10,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md"}],"id":"q-584a124648a27739"},{"stem":"He explained that the experiment had been delayed because the equipment failed to function properly.","options":[],"answer":"他解释说，实验被推迟了，因为设备未能正常运行。","explanation":"主句用一般过去时，that 从句中的 *had been delayed* 为过去完成时的被动形式，表示“此前已被推迟”；*failed to function properly* 表示“未能正常运转”。","point":"宾语从句翻译；时态呼应。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-0c8d713553561af5"},{"stem":"The scientist believes that success comes from repeated failure, not sudden inspiration.","options":[],"answer":"这位科学家相信，成功源于反复的失败，而不是突如其来的灵感。","explanation":"*that* 引导 *believes* 的宾语从句；*repeated* 意为“反复的”，*sudden* 意为“突然的”。按原句顺序翻译。","point":"宾语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-3017277c131e0452"},{"stem":"我相信他一定会信守承诺。","options":[],"answer":"I am sure that he will keep his promise.","explanation":"*be sure + that* 从句表示确信将来的动作，从句用 *will + 动词原形*；*keep one's promise* 表示“信守承诺”。我的译文用 *believe* 表达“相信”，意思相近，但语气较“确信”稍弱。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-72acc94934d0ee0c"},{"stem":"You've read the novel too. What do you think of it? _____. The ending really surprised me.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I've never heard of it."},{"key":"B","text":"I quite enjoyed it."},{"key":"C","text":"Yes, I do."},{"key":"D","text":"Not at all."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"*What do you think of it?* 询问对小说的评价，应直接说出看法。后句提到结尾令人意外，说明说话人已读过且愿意评价，*I quite enjoyed it* 最贴切。A、C、D 均不合语境。","point":"征询意见；评价一本书。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-978ef981abfe64f0"},{"stem":"The weather forecast says it'll be sunny this weekend. _____? A picnic in the park sounds perfect!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Do you mind my opening the window?"},{"key":"B","text":"What time is it now?"},{"key":"C","text":"How about having a picnic in the park?"},{"key":"D","text":"Are you leaving for the airport?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"前句说周末天气晴朗，后句肯定“在公园野餐”这个建议，空处应提出该活动。*How about doing...?* 是地道的建议句型，其余选项与语境不符。","point":"建议与邀请；提出活动建议。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-3bc68121ff88312a"},{"stem":"Would you rather watch a movie or see a play this weekend? _____. I heard the new play at the City Theatre is wonderful.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"B","text":"That's right."},{"key":"C","text":"I'd rather see the play."},{"key":"D","text":"I don't know the way."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"*Would you rather A or B?* 询问两者偏好，回答可用 *I'd rather...*。后句说新话剧很精彩，因此应选“我更想看话剧”。","point":"征询意见；表达二选一偏好。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-fe7ff894ad008d8a"},{"stem":"Do you know any good coffee shop near our office? _____. Their lattes are really nice and it's quiet enough to work in.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm afraid not."},{"key":"C","text":"There's one around the corner."},{"key":"D","text":"Congratulations!"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方询问附近有没有好的咖啡店，应推荐具体地点并给出理由。*There's one around the corner* 意为“拐角处有一家”，与后句介绍拿铁和安静环境相接。","point":"征询意见；推荐具体地点。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-a7d23b0d48e62589"},{"stem":"The manager mentioned that the meeting would be rescheduled to next Tuesday afternoon.","options":[],"answer":"经理提到，会议将被改到下周二下午举行。","explanation":"*that* 引导宾语从句；*would be rescheduled* 是过去将来时的被动语态，*reschedule* 意为“重新安排、改期”。","point":"宾语从句翻译；过去将来时。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-44156684bb739eca"},{"stem":"我听说她上个月去了美国。","options":[],"answer":"I heard that she went to America last month.","explanation":"*hear* 后接 that 宾语从句；主句和从句均为过去时，*last month* 明确过去时间。*the United States* 与 *America* 在此语境中都可表达“美国”。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-6c2f23b01ee1ce9d"},{"stem":"I can't decide which jacket to buy. Do you prefer the red one or the blue one? _____. Red goes well with your skin tone.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I do."},{"key":"B","text":"It doesn't matter to me either."},{"key":"C","text":"I'd say the red one."},{"key":"D","text":"No, thanks."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方征求红色与蓝色外套的偏好，应明确给出选择。后句说红色很衬肤色，故选 *I'd say the red one*。","point":"征询意见；给出偏好选择。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-12ff1d70ae400089"},{"stem":"他想知道这本书为什么这么贵。","options":[],"answer":"He wants to know why the book is so expensive.","explanation":"*why* 引导宾语从句，从句使用陈述语序 *why the book is...*；主句为一般现在时，从句时态依句意也用一般现在时。我的译文 *this book* 与题目“这本书”对应。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-7a3ed22be9136ec1"},{"stem":"Which photo should I put on my resume? _____. The one with the blue background makes you look professional.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm not sure either."},{"key":"B","text":"I'd go with the second one."},{"key":"C","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"D","text":"Go ahead."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方在两张照片间犹豫，应给出明确建议并说明理由。*I'd go with the second one* 表示“我会选第二张”，与后句称赞蓝底照片相呼应。","point":"征询意见；给出选择建议。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":11,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md"}],"id":"q-054a35f6ccc93f11"},{"stem":"The traffic is terrible. I'm afraid we'll be late for the meeting. _____. It's usually faster than the main road.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I can't agree more."},{"key":"B","text":"Let's try the side street."},{"key":"C","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"D","text":"Help yourself."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"面对堵车可能迟到的问题，应提出可行方案。后句说小路通常比主路快，因此选 *Let's try the side street*。","point":"提建议；给出行车方案。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-c040ae9198b71e0f"},{"stem":"The doctor confirmed that the patient had fully recovered after the second surgery.","options":[],"answer":"医生确认，在第二次手术后，病人已完全康复。","explanation":"*that* 引导宾语从句；*had fully recovered* 为过去完成时，表示在“医生确认”之前已康复；*after the second surgery* 意为“第二次手术后”。","point":"宾语从句翻译；过去完成时。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-cd134c7ec8ab0c1e"},{"stem":"当他到达车站时，火车已经开走了。","options":[],"answer":"When he arrived at the station, the train had already left.","explanation":"到达车站用一般过去时 *arrived*；火车开走发生在到达之前，用过去完成时 *had already left*。*By the time* 与 *When* 均可表达时间关系。","point":"时间状语从句；过去完成时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-7172102b58647361"},{"stem":"每当我遇到困难时，她总是鼓励我不要放弃。","options":[],"answer":"Whenever I run into difficulties, she always encourages me not to give up.","explanation":"*Whenever* 表示“每当”，引导时间状语从句；表示经常发生的情况，主从句都用一般现在时。*run into difficulties* 或 *face difficulties* 都可表达“遇到困难”。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-b37e481aba0fa1cc"},{"stem":"How do you like the English course you're taking? _____. The teacher explains everything clearly.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm glad to hear that."},{"key":"B","text":"I like it very much."},{"key":"C","text":"It doesn't work."},{"key":"D","text":"Not yet."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"*How do you like...?* 询问对课程的感受，应直接表达评价。后句称赞老师讲解清楚，选 *I like it very much*。","point":"征询意见；表达课程感受。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-92ab95f6e1be66c6"},{"stem":"We're painting the living room. Do you think cream or light grey is better? _____ . Cream makes the room feel warmer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, of course."},{"key":"C","text":"I'd go for cream."},{"key":"D","text":"Neither."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方请你在两种颜色中表态，应答应明确选择并给出理由。*I'd go for cream*（我选米色）与后接的理由“米色让房间显得更温暖”逻辑一致；其余选项不符合语境。句意：——我们要粉刷客厅，你觉得米色和浅灰色哪个更好？——我选米色，米色让房间显得更温暖。","point":"征询意见——装修二选一表态。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-149ad26f41f5b5eb"},{"stem":"I've got a terrible sore throat. _____. And try to drink plenty of warm water.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's my pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"Well done!"},{"key":"D","text":"You'd better have a rest."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方身体不适，应给出关心式建议：*You'd better have a rest*（你最好休息一下）；后接多喝温水的建议，语意连贯。其他选项分别用于回应感谢、回应道歉和夸奖成绩，不合语境。句意：——我嗓子疼得厉害。——你最好休息一下，再尽量多喝温水。","point":"提建议——健康关怀。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-4afdd7dce256f7cb"},{"stem":"Our supervisor insisted that all reports must be submitted before the department meeting.","options":[],"answer":"我们的主管坚持，所有报告必须在部门会议前提交。","explanation":"宾语从句顺译；*insisted* 后接 *that* 从句，*must be submitted* 为被动语态，*before the meeting* 译为“在会议前”。","point":"宾语从句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-a1ac05e880ef4206"},{"stem":"She wonders whether her proposal will receive approval from the committee by next Friday.","options":[],"answer":"她想知道，她的提案能否在下周五之前获得委员会的批准。","explanation":"*whether* 引导表示“是否”的宾语从句，译为“能否”；主句 *wonders* 为现在时，从句 *will* 表示将来可能；*by next Friday* 意为“在下周五之前”。","point":"宾语从句翻译 + whether 用法。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-99a9e14ec3113f96"},{"stem":"My spoken English is still poor. Any suggestions? _____. Practice speaking with native speakers if possible.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why not find a language partner?"},{"key":"B","text":"Good luck to you."},{"key":"C","text":"I'd love to."},{"key":"D","text":"Not at all."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方请求提高英语口语的方法，应给出可行建议。*Why not ...?* 提建议语气自然委婉；后接与母语者练习形成递进。其余选项分别表示祝愿、接受邀请和回应感谢，不合语境。句意：——我的英语口语还是很差，有什么建议吗？——为什么不找个语伴呢？有机会就多和母语者练习。","point":"提建议——学习方法。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-bd7af46bbad150f9"},{"stem":"我一完成作业就会给你打电话。","options":[],"answer":"I will call you as soon as I finish my homework.","explanation":"*as soon as* 引导时间状语从句，主句用 *will + 动词原形* 表将来，从句用一般现在时表示将来，即“主将从现”。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-744bbb41b6a1cde7"},{"stem":"My computer just froze again. What should I do? _____. If that doesn't work, call the IT department.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"B","text":"It's up to you."},{"key":"C","text":"Same to you."},{"key":"D","text":"Try restarting it first."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方因电脑死机求助，应给出具体解决步骤。*Try restarting it first*（先试着重启）后接“如果不行再找 IT 部门”形成步骤逻辑；其余选项不合语境。句意：——我电脑又死机了，该怎么办？——先重启试试，不行的话就给 IT 部门打电话。","point":"提建议——故障处理。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":12,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md"}],"id":"q-bc527d6970e166f9"},{"stem":"_____ the rail strike, the commuters would have reached downtown two hours earlier.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"All of the above"},{"key":"B","text":"If not for"},{"key":"C","text":"But for"},{"key":"D","text":"Without"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 *would have reached* 表示与过去事实相反的虚拟语气。*But for*、*Without*、*If not for* 均可引导“要不是铁路罢工”这一含蓄虚拟条件，所以页面选 A。句意：要不是铁路罢工，通勤者本应早两小时抵达市中心。","point":"虚拟语气——含蓄虚拟条件（but for / without / if not for）三种表达等价。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-43a0c4ce52eae98c"},{"stem":"We're having a barbecue this Saturday. Would you like to join us? _____. What can I bring?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'd love to."},{"key":"B","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"C","text":"It's very kind of you, but I'm busy."},{"key":"D","text":"Never mind."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"受邀参加烧烤，后文询问能带什么，表明已接受邀请。*I'd love to* 是接受邀请的标准说法；拒绝邀请的 C 与后文冲突，其余选项也不合适。句意：——这周六我们要办烧烤，你想一起来吗？——我很乐意！我带点什么好呢？","point":"邀请回应——欣然接受并询问细节。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-744100494e15530f"},{"stem":"他一到家就下起了大雨。","options":[],"answer":"No sooner had he arrived home than it began to rain heavily.","explanation":"我的译文表达了原意，但本次交卷结果将此题计入错题；页面重点使用 *no sooner ... than ...* 表“一……就……”，句首的 *No sooner* 触发部分倒装，前句用过去完成时 *had arrived*，*than* 后用一般过去时。复习时应重点掌握此结构。","point":"时间状语从句 + 倒装句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-358e4f5625248146"},{"stem":"If it _____ for the timely first aid, the swimmer would not have survived.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had not been"},{"key":"B","text":"were not"},{"key":"C","text":"should not be"},{"key":"D","text":"has not been"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 *would not have survived* 表示对过去事实虚拟，从句用过去完成时 *had not been*。句意：要不是及时的急救，那名游泳者就活不下来了。","point":"虚拟语气——与过去事实相反的 if 条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a725fc097649f812"},{"stem":"If the explorers _____ enough supplies before the storm, they would be reaching the base camp by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"brought"},{"key":"B","text":"had brought"},{"key":"C","text":"should bring"},{"key":"D","text":"would bring"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"*would be reaching ... by now* 暗示现在的虚拟结果；从句说的是暴风雨前的过去情况，用过去完成时 *had brought*。句意：如果探险队在暴风雨前带了足够的补给，现在本该正抵达大本营。","point":"虚拟语气——错综时间虚拟条件句（从句对过去，主句对现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-5111bfbf33ee57ec"},{"stem":"Researchers who study sleep patterns have found that deep sleep enhances problem-solving abilities.","options":[],"answer":"研究睡眠模式的研究人员发现，深度睡眠能增强解决问题的能力。","explanation":"定语从句 *who study sleep patterns* 前置，译为“研究睡眠模式的”，修饰 *researchers*；*enhances* 译为“增强”，*problem-solving* 译为“解决问题的”。","point":"定语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-f1581911c9821f02"},{"stem":"The guidebook suggests that travelers should reserve their hotel rooms at least one month in advance.","options":[],"answer":"这本指南建议，旅行者应至少提前一个月预订酒店客房。","explanation":"宾语从句顺译；*suggest* 后接 *that* 从句用 *should + 动词原形*，*should* 可省略；*in advance* 译为“提前”。","point":"宾语从句翻译 + 虚拟语气建议。","category":"英译汉","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-e99da2ad2362eabb"},{"stem":"The deadline having passed, the editor demanded the revised draft immediately; otherwise, the entire issue _____ behind schedule.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would have fallen"},{"key":"B","text":"would fall"},{"key":"C","text":"fell"},{"key":"D","text":"has fallen"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"*otherwise* 引导含蓄虚拟条件，相当于“如果当时没有立即交出修订稿”。前文有 *having passed* 和 *demanded* 等过去背景，表示与过去事实相反，应用 *would have + 过去分词*。句意：截止日期已过，编辑要求立即交出修订稿；否则整期杂志当时就会延期出版。","point":"含蓄虚拟语气（otherwise + 与过去事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-29242998470ea310"},{"stem":"每次我去看她，她都在图书馆学习。","options":[],"answer":"Every time I go to see her, she is studying in the library.","explanation":"*every time* 引导时间状语从句，主句从现；主句用 *is studying* 表示每次到访时她正在学习。*visit her* 与 *go to see her* 均可表达“去看她”。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-2c6b22e73da77351"},{"stem":"I always feel so nervous before exams. _____. You've prepared well, and you'll do fine.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take it easy."},{"key":"B","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"C","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"D","text":"What a pity!"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方倾诉考前紧张，应安慰并鼓励。*Take it easy* 意为“放轻松”，与后文“你准备得很充分，会考好的”衔接自然；其余选项不合语境。句意：——考前我总是特别紧张。——放轻松，你准备得很充分，会考好的。","point":"宽慰鼓励——缓解考前紧张。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-4780cd5f84ab3e55"},{"stem":"在我做完作业之前，请不要打扰我。","options":[],"answer":"Please don't disturb me before I finish my homework.","explanation":"*before* 引导时间状语从句；主句用祈使句，从句主语是 *I*，所以动词用 *finish*。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a5d2542c2425c311"},{"stem":"If you _____ in my position, you would understand why I made that choice.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"are"},{"key":"C","text":"had been"},{"key":"D","text":"should be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"此处表示与现在事实相反的虚拟条件，if 从句中的 *be* 通常用 *were*；主句用 *would + 动词原形*。句意：如果你处于我的位置，你就会理解我为什么做出那个选择。","point":"虚拟语气——与现在事实相反的条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-5774cf46a73764b5"},{"stem":"We've just moved into our new flat. Can you come over for dinner on Friday? _____. I'd love to see your new place.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I do."},{"key":"B","text":"What a shame!"},{"key":"C","text":"I have no idea."},{"key":"D","text":"Sure, I'd be glad to."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"受邀到新居吃晚饭，应答应并表达期待。*Sure, I'd be glad to* 表示爽快接受；*Yes, I do* 不适用于对 *Can you ...?* 的回答，其他选项也不合语境。句意：——我们刚搬进新公寓，周五能来吃晚饭吗？——当然，我很乐意！我也想看看你们的新家。","point":"邀请回应——高兴地接受。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-4697f2cfee8f3c03"},{"stem":"_____ he take the early train, he would still miss the opening ceremony.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Even if"},{"key":"B","text":"Were"},{"key":"C","text":"Should"},{"key":"D","text":"Had"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对将来的虚拟条件可用 *should do* 代替 *if ... should do*；省略 *if* 后将 *should* 提前形成倒装：*Should he take ...*。句意：即使他坐早班火车，也仍然会错过开幕式。","point":"虚拟语气——对将来虚拟，if 省略 should 倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-dc6c10f285e0e5d9"},{"stem":"Recent evidence indicates that chronic stress may significantly impair both memory and concentration.","options":[],"answer":"最新证据表明，长期压力可能会显著损害记忆力和注意力。","explanation":"宾语从句顺译；*indicates* 后接 *that* 从句，*may* 表示可能性；*impair* 译为“损害”，*chronic* 译为“长期的”。","point":"宾语从句翻译 + 词义选择。","category":"英译汉","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a0878c30847579ea"},{"stem":"I really want to lose some weight, but I can't stop eating snacks. _____. Snacks are the biggest problem.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's a piece of cake."},{"key":"B","text":"With pleasure."},{"key":"C","text":"You should cut down on them gradually."},{"key":"D","text":"Same again, please."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方想减肥却停不下零食，应针对饮食习惯提建议。*cut down on them gradually* 意为“逐渐减少（零食摄入）”，与后文“零食是最大的问题”衔接。其余选项分别表示“轻而易举”、接受请求、餐厅续点，不合语境。","point":"交际用语（针对健康困扰提建议）。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-7c07425118a5e272"},{"stem":"I've got an extra ticket for the concert tonight. Will you go with me? _____. I have to finish a report by midnight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I wish I could, but"},{"key":"B","text":"I can't agree more."},{"key":"C","text":"That sounds like a good idea."},{"key":"D","text":"It's very nice of you to say so."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方邀请看演唱会，而答者需要在午夜前完成报告，故应委婉拒绝并说明原因。I wish I could, but... 表示“我很想去，但是……”。","point":"邀请回应——委婉谢绝并说明原因。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-17d9f8f77aeff2b4"},{"stem":"How about grabbing a coffee together after work today? _____. Can we make it tomorrow instead?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"My pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"C","text":"I'm afraid I can't today."},{"key":"D","text":"Of course not."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句提出改到明天，说明今天不能赴约。I'm afraid I can't today 是礼貌拒绝，并与后文衔接。","point":"邀请回应——婉拒并主动改期。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":13,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md"}],"id":"q-538fa2848c121f18"},{"stem":"How about selling our old car and buying a new one? _____. Let me think about it and talk to my wife first.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's a deal."},{"key":"B","text":"I agree completely."},{"key":"C","text":"That's worth considering."},{"key":"D","text":"Congratulations!"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句表明还需考虑并与妻子商量，因此用 That's worth considering.（值得考虑）；A、B 表示已决定，D 与语境无关。","point":"回应建议——保留态度，再作考虑。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-771fc6e3d8eedcaa"},{"stem":"I think we should start the project as early as possible. _____. The earlier, the better.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I couldn't agree more."},{"key":"B","text":"I don't think so."},{"key":"C","text":"It's up to you."},{"key":"D","text":"That's all right."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"后句“越早越好”表示完全赞成，因此用 I couldn't agree more.（我再同意不过了）。","point":"表达赞同——完全同意对方主张。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-d70599e64efe27d5"},{"stem":"The company has launched a new product line that targets young professionals in metropolitan areas.","options":[],"answer":"该公司推出了一条新产品线，主要面向大都市地区的年轻职场人士。","explanation":"*that targets...* 是修饰 *a new product line* 的定语从句，翻译时可前置为“面向……的新产品线”，也可独立成分句。*target* 为“面向、针对”，*metropolitan* 为“大都市的”。","point":"定语从句的翻译＋后置分句。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-a027f1a0a9ed07fb"},{"stem":"Had you informed me in advance, I _____ at the airport waiting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would not have been"},{"key":"B","text":"would not be"},{"key":"C","text":"won't be"},{"key":"D","text":"had not been"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"*Had you informed me* = *If you had informed me*，从句虚拟过去的情况；主句说“现在就不会在机场等着”，是对现在情况的虚拟，故用 *would not be*。我选的 *would not have been* 表示过去不会等，与页面强调的现在等待不一致。","point":"虚拟语气——错综时间虚拟条件句（从句过去，主句现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-776cd6e8f99db962"},{"stem":"The building that houses the library was constructed in the early twentieth century.","options":[],"answer":"那座用作图书馆的建筑建于 20 世纪初期。","explanation":"*that houses the library* 是修饰 *building* 的定语从句，可前置为“用作图书馆的建筑”。*in the early twentieth century* 指“20 世纪初期”。","point":"定语从句的翻译＋前置法。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-ffe4bbf5c2bebadd"},{"stem":"Our mentor, who has guided us for more than a decade, finally decided to retire this spring.","options":[],"answer":"我们的导师指导我们已有十多年，今年春天终于决定退休。","explanation":"*who has guided us...* 为非限制性定语从句，可译为并列分句，也可将其前置修饰“导师”；*for more than a decade* 为“十多年”。","point":"非限制性定语从句的翻译（拆译法）。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-b10400f27f9768e6"},{"stem":"无论天多冷，他每天都坚持早起跑步。","options":[],"answer":"However cold it is, he keeps running early every morning.","explanation":"*however + 形容词/副词* 与 *no matter how + 形容词/副词* 都可表示“无论多么……”，引导让步状语从句；*keep doing* 或 *insist on doing* 可表示坚持做某事。","point":"让步状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-3488cefbaa85e854"},{"stem":"The rescue helicopter would have located the stranded hikers sooner _____ the sudden fog.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had it not been for"},{"key":"B","text":"had there not been"},{"key":"C","text":"without"},{"key":"D","text":"A and B"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主句 *would have located* 表示对过去事实相反的虚拟语气。A 是 *If it had not been for* 的倒装形式；B 是 *If there had not been* 的倒装形式，都表达“若不是突然起雾”。页面说明 C *without* 在语法上也通顺，但题目将 A、B 两种倒装结构归为 D。","point":"虚拟语气——倒装结构（*had it not been for* 与 *had there not been*）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-ccb0154015a16a2b"},{"stem":"If she _____ the prescription carefully yesterday, she would not be suffering from dizziness now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"followed"},{"key":"B","text":"had followed"},{"key":"C","text":"should follow"},{"key":"D","text":"has followed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"*yesterday* 指过去的虚拟条件，if 从句用过去完成时 *had followed*；*now* 指现在的虚拟结果，主句用 *would not be suffering*。","point":"虚拟语气——错综时间条件句（主句对现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-c86b3591f3be8402"},{"stem":"If tomorrow _____ a public holiday, we _____ a three-day excursion to the lake.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were / would take"},{"key":"B","text":"should be / would take"},{"key":"C","text":"had been / would have taken"},{"key":"D","text":"were / would have taken"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"页面以 *If tomorrow were a public holiday, we would take...* 为标准，表示对将来的虚拟假设。页面解析同时承认 B 的 *should be / would take* 也可用于将来虚拟，只是说 A“更简洁”。因此此题不宜当作单一语法错误来记忆。","point":"虚拟语气——对将来事实的假设（*if ... were / should be, ... would do*）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-787a8574b13d94ca"},{"stem":"If you _____ so stubborn, you would accept their apology gracefully.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hadn't been"},{"key":"B","text":"shouldn't be"},{"key":"C","text":"weren't"},{"key":"D","text":"won't be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"主句 *would accept* 表示与现在事实相反的虚拟结果，if 从句用一般过去时；be 动词用 *were*，否定为 *weren't*。","point":"虚拟语气——与现在事实相反的条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-406b481b3f8b3156"},{"stem":"If we _____ off the coast at that moment, we could have dived into the water safely.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"should be"},{"key":"C","text":"are"},{"key":"D","text":"had been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主句 *could have dived* 表示对过去事实相反的结果；*at that moment* 也指过去，if 从句用过去完成时 *had been*。","point":"虚拟语气——与过去事实相反的 if 条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-a1673272b1c85d49"},{"stem":"Why don't we book the meeting room on the fifth floor? _____. It's always too noisy there.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Good idea."},{"key":"B","text":"No problem."},{"key":"C","text":"That's exactly what I was thinking."},{"key":"D","text":"I'd rather not, to be honest."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"后句说五楼一直太吵，说明不赞成预订那里，故用 *I'd rather not, to be honest* 委婉表达异议。","point":"表达异议——委婉否决他人提议。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-32d76e3212fad2d6"},{"stem":"如果你明天有空，我们一起去公园。","options":[],"answer":"If you are free tomorrow, we will go to the park together.","explanation":"真实条件句遵循“主将从现”：主句用 *will go*，if 从句用一般现在时 *are*；*be free* 表示“有空”。","point":"if 条件状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7f74e22dfc637a54"},{"stem":"The local economy would have been revitalized, _____ the proposed tax cut.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had the government approved"},{"key":"B","text":"if the government should approve"},{"key":"C","text":"were the government to approve"},{"key":"D","text":"should the government approve"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 *would have been revitalized* 是对过去事实的虚拟；从句省略 *if* 后将 *had* 提前，形成 *had the government approved...*。","point":"虚拟语气——过去虚拟从句省略 *if* 后倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-4ea7cb36232cc624"},{"stem":"Our English club is recruiting new members. Are you interested? _____. Could you tell me more about the activities first?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"That sounds interesting."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm afraid I can't."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句继续询问活动内容，说明答者感兴趣，但尚需了解详情；用 *That sounds interesting* 衔接最自然。","point":"邀请回应——感兴趣并进一步咨询。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-d76fed9e8ff42a69"},{"stem":"无论你说什么，我都不会改变我的决定。","options":[],"answer":"No matter what you say, I will not change my mind.","explanation":"*no matter what* 引导让步状语从句，*what* 在从句中作 *say* 的宾语；主句表达将来时。","point":"让步状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-f45556481cb7673e"},{"stem":"Let's work out at the gym after work, shall we? _____. My knee has been hurting lately.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'd be glad to."},{"key":"B","text":"What a good idea!"},{"key":"C","text":"The same to you."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm afraid I can't."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"答者膝盖最近疼，不能去健身房，因此用 *I'm afraid I can't* 礼貌拒绝。","point":"邀请回应——因身体原因婉拒。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-e3e985f0a3fbc12d"},{"stem":"I think we should have a welcome party for the new manager. _____. We can book the function room for Friday evening.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm sorry to hear that."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"Help yourself."},{"key":"D","text":"That's a good idea."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"后句主动提出预订周五晚上的多功能厅，说明赞成欢迎会提议，用 *That's a good idea*。","point":"表达赞同——赞同并补充具体方案。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-06e0a7ebc9322277"},{"stem":"If the museum _____ earlier than usual today, we could actually finish the guided tour.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had opened"},{"key":"B","text":"opens"},{"key":"C","text":"should open"},{"key":"D","text":"were to open"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"句子假设博物馆今天稍早开门，主句用 *could finish* 表示推测结果；页面以 *were to open* 表示对将来的假设。","point":"虚拟语气——与将来事实相反（*were to do*）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":14,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md"}],"id":"q-fd31339e078e36a3"},{"stem":"If the policy _____, our company would have benefited from the tax break.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been approved"},{"key":"B","text":"were approved"},{"key":"C","text":"should approve"},{"key":"D","text":"has been approved"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 *would have benefited* 表示与过去事实相反的结果，if 从句用过去完成时；政策是“被批准”，所以用 *had been approved*。","point":"虚拟语气——与过去事实相反的被动条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-5a4d2b235b83d194"},{"stem":"我永远不会忘记我第一次见到你的那一天。","options":[],"answer":"I will never forget the day when I first met you.","explanation":"*when I first met you* 是修饰 *the day* 的定语从句，*when* 在从句中作时间状语；*first* 表“第一次”。","point":"定语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-b59aac45bcbefe70"},{"stem":"If you _____ any difficulty with the software, feel free to contact our support desk.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"encountered"},{"key":"B","text":"had encountered"},{"key":"C","text":"would encounter"},{"key":"D","text":"should encounter"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"if 从句中 should encounter 表示“万一遇到”，对将来可能情况作委婉假设；主句用祈使句 feel free to contact。句意：要是使用软件时遇到任何困难，请随时联系我们的技术支持。","point":"对将来的虚拟条件句，if + should do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-844210ed48f3d928"},{"stem":"That's a beautiful necklace you're wearing! _____. It was a gift from my mother.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Thank you."},{"key":"B","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"C","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"D","text":"I don't think so."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"别人称赞佩戴的项链，应先表示感谢，再补充说明礼物来源。You're welcome 用来回应道谢，Not at all 和 I don't think so 不适合此处。","point":"交际用语；回应赞美并作补充说明。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-dad093ca53e1c65d"},{"stem":"I would _____ Eaccounting to my colleagues.（页面原文如此；Eaccounting 指电子会计）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recognize"},{"key":"B","text":"recommend"},{"key":"C","text":"reward"},{"key":"D","text":"reduce"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"recommend ... to ... 表示“向……推荐……”。句意：我会向同事们推荐电子会计。","point":"动词辨析；recommend sth. to sb.。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-18682d1fcf650046"},{"stem":"We admire people who maintain optimism even in the face of severe difficulties.","options":[],"answer":"我们钦佩那些即使面临严重困难也保持乐观的人。","explanation":"who maintain optimism 是修饰 people 的定语从句；in the face of 译作“面对”。","point":"定语从句的翻译；前置法。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-be2bbed3113bf96a"},{"stem":"Were it not for Professor Li's guidance, the graduate students _____ their thesis last term.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"couldn't complete"},{"key":"B","text":"can't complete"},{"key":"C","text":"couldn't have completed"},{"key":"D","text":"haven't completed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"Were it not for ... 是省略 if 的倒装虚拟条件句；last term 表明结果针对过去，主句用 could not have done。句意：若不是李教授指导，研究生们上学期就无法完成论文。","point":"错综时间虚拟语气；条件针对现在或普遍情况，结果针对过去。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-e47ef42a49013f17"},{"stem":"You look really smart in that new suit. _____. It was on sale last weekend.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's your business."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't make fun of me."},{"key":"C","text":"Really? I hate it."},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks. I'm glad you like it."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"面对对方称赞新西装，应礼貌致谢；随后补充“上周末打折买的”符合对话语境。","point":"交际用语；得体回应赞美。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-44982adc85168372"},{"stem":"The new policy, which came into effect last January, has significantly reduced workplace injuries.","options":[],"answer":"这项新政策于去年一月份生效，已显著减少了工伤事故。","explanation":"which came into effect last January 是修饰 policy 的非限制性定语从句，可译为定语或独立分句；come into effect 为“生效”，workplace injuries 为“工伤事故”。","point":"非限制性定语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-2eb90315b35d40e3"},{"stem":"Your daughter's drawing won the first prize. She's so talented! _____. She spends hours on it every day.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's not true at all."},{"key":"B","text":"It's none of my business."},{"key":"C","text":"What did you say?"},{"key":"D","text":"Thank you. She really loves painting."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"别人称赞自己的孩子，家长应礼貌致谢，再补充她热爱绘画、每天练习的信息。","point":"交际用语；替孩子接受赞美时表示感谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-7bef3ba3ba951f91"},{"stem":"If it _____ to rain tomorrow, the outdoor concert would be cancelled without question.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"should be"},{"key":"D","text":"is"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 would be cancelled 与 tomorrow 提示对将来的虚拟假设，条件句可用 If it were to rain tomorrow。句意：如果明天下雨，户外音乐会无疑会取消。","point":"对将来虚拟的 if + were to do 结构。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-67b7498ccae43ca5"},{"stem":"The patient _____ alive now if the surgeon had performed the operation in time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would have been"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"should be"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"if 从句 had performed 是对过去的虚拟；主句 now 指现在的结果，故用 would be。句意：若外科医生当时及时手术，病人现在本该还活着。","point":"错综时间虚拟条件句（条件过去，结果现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-0754554ac1bf24a2"},{"stem":"If he _____ the alarm clock last night, he would not be late for the meeting now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"set"},{"key":"B","text":"should set"},{"key":"C","text":"had set"},{"key":"D","text":"has set"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"last night 指过去的条件，用 had set；now 指现在的结果，用 would not be。句意：若他昨晚设了闹钟，现在就不会开会迟到。","point":"错综时间虚拟条件句（过去条件影响现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-5a79f0b3965e5b5e"},{"stem":"Your speech at the meeting was really excellent. _____. I was quite nervous on stage.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No problem."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"D","text":"Thank you for saying so."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方称赞演讲，应致谢；随后说“我在台上其实很紧张”是自然的谦逊回应。","point":"交际用语；回应赞美时谦虚致谢。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-ce542f2e81a054b7"},{"stem":"假如我是你，我会抓住这个难得的机会。","options":[],"answer":"If I were you, I would seize this rare opportunity.","explanation":"与现在事实相反的假设用 If I were you，主句用 would + 动词原形；seize 表示“抓住”。","point":"与现在相反的虚拟条件句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-a90655a0a5a20a37"},{"stem":"If only he _____ the road rules ten years ago, he would not be in prison now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"observed"},{"key":"B","text":"had observed"},{"key":"C","text":"should observe"},{"key":"D","text":"has observed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"if only 表“要是……就好了”；ten years ago 指过去未发生的情况，故用 had observed；现在不在监狱则为现在的虚拟结果。","point":"if only 引导的愿望与错综时间虚拟语气。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-58b4fb0594c4e037"},{"stem":"What a sweet voice! You sing really well. _____. I've been taking singing lessons for years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, no, my voice is terrible."},{"key":"B","text":"It's nothing to me."},{"key":"C","text":"Oh, thank you."},{"key":"D","text":"Who told you that?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"受到歌声好听的称赞，应先致谢，再补充多年上声乐课的经历。","point":"交际用语；回应赞美并分享努力。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-3da5ff00202d49a1"},{"stem":"_____ I in your shoes, I would definitely apologize to her in person.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Had"},{"key":"B","text":"Were"},{"key":"C","text":"Should"},{"key":"D","text":"If"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Were I in your shoes 等于 If I were in your shoes，表示“如果我处在你的位置”；主句用 would do。","point":"与现在事实相反的虚拟条件句；省略 if 后 were 提前倒装。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-9224f41f6375819c"},{"stem":"这是我昨天在书店买的那本书。","options":[],"answer":"This is the book which I bought in the bookstore yesterday.","explanation":"book 为先行词，在定语从句中作 bought 的宾语；可用 that 或 which，也可省略关系代词。yesterday 要求一般过去时 bought。at the bookstore 与 in the bookstore 在此处均能表达在书店购买。","point":"限制性定语从句；关系代词作宾语时的省略规则。","category":"汉译英","topics":["定语从句","代词与限定词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-9c1898dbac9acc8c"},{"stem":"Any student who fails to submit the assignment by Friday will be required to attend remediation classes.","options":[],"answer":"任何未能在周五前提交作业的学生都必须参加补习课。","explanation":"who fails to submit the assignment by Friday 是修饰 student 的定语从句；be required to do 表“被要求做／必须做”，remediation classes 为“补习课”。","point":"定语从句的翻译与主谓复合。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-2bb1118dcdd742ae"},{"stem":"You've given us such a delicious meal tonight. _____. I'm glad everyone likes it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's very kind of you to say so, but I cooked nothing."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm glad you enjoyed it."},{"key":"C","text":"Don't say so."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm afraid I didn't cook well."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主人面对客人称赞饭菜，应接受并表示高兴：“很高兴你喜欢。”与后句 I'm glad everyone likes it 一致。","point":"交际用语；主人回应赞美。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":15,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十五天.md"}],"id":"q-c9558b20b419f451"},{"stem":"Without the sun's energy, life on Earth _____ in any form.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could not exist"},{"key":"B","text":"could not have existed"},{"key":"C","text":"would not have existed"},{"key":"D","text":"won't exist"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"without 引出与现在事实相反的隐含条件；生命存在是持续状态，主句用 could not exist。句意：没有太阳能，地球上不可能存在任何形式的生命。","point":"without 含蓄虚拟语气（与现在事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-6a25dbd863c7d0a0"},{"stem":"The outdoor concert was cancelled because of the heavy rain. _____. I had been looking forward to it for weeks.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"B","text":"What fun!"},{"key":"C","text":"How wonderful!"},{"key":"D","text":"Congratulations!"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"期待已久的音乐会因雨取消，应表达遗憾。What a pity! 意为“真遗憾”。","point":"交际用语；对活动取消表达遗憾。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语","其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-3bd491ffcc85e880"},{"stem":"The witness gave clear testimony; otherwise the jury _____ a different verdict.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will have reached"},{"key":"B","text":"would reach"},{"key":"C","text":"would have reached"},{"key":"D","text":"reached"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"otherwise 相当于 if not，隐含对过去事实相反的条件：若证人没有作清楚证词，陪审团本会得出不同裁决。过去的虚拟结果用 would have done。","point":"otherwise 引导的含蓄虚拟条件（过去）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-e2a68c2b826687d1"},{"stem":"I missed the last bus and had to walk all the way home. _____. What an unlucky day for you!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's too bad."},{"key":"B","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"C","text":"Good luck!"},{"key":"D","text":"Never mind."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方错过末班车并走路回家，应表示同情。That's too bad! 表示“太糟糕了”。","point":"交际用语；对倒霉遭遇表示同情。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-cce38c72dbf75f0b"},{"stem":"Without their cooperation, the research project _____ suspended by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be"},{"key":"B","text":"should be"},{"key":"C","text":"would have been"},{"key":"D","text":"would have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"without their cooperation 为隐含虚拟条件；by now 表示“到现在为止已经”，强调已经发生的假设结果，需用 would have been suspended。","point":"without 引出的含蓄虚拟语气；by now 对过去至今的假设结果。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-fe863cb8b10d586a"},{"stem":"Our team lost the match; but for the referee's controversial decision, we _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would win"},{"key":"B","text":"would have won"},{"key":"C","text":"won / will win"},{"key":"D","text":"should have won"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"but for 表“若不是”，引出与已发生的过去事实相反的条件；比赛已经输了，假设结果用 would have won。","point":"but for 含蓄虚拟语气（与过去事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-2b0543c52f624760"},{"stem":"When making the plan, we must _____ the cost _____, or we will run out of money halfway.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bring...into effect"},{"key":"B","text":"put...into practice"},{"key":"C","text":"take...into account"},{"key":"D","text":"get...into trouble"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"take the cost into account 表示“把成本考虑在内”；否则可能中途耗尽资金。","point":"动词短语辨析；take sth. into account。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-9b26a41cf82db709"},{"stem":"The film about the brave little girl was so _____ that many people in the cinema wiped their tears.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moved"},{"key":"B","text":"move"},{"key":"C","text":"moves"},{"key":"D","text":"moving"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"电影使人感动，修饰“事物”用 moving；moved 通常描述“人感到感动”。","point":"-ing / -ed 形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-dbecccf3b39a7055"},{"stem":"这个问题据说已经解决了。","options":[],"answer":"The problem is said to have been solved.","explanation":"is said 是“据说”的被动结构；问题的解决先于“据说”，用不定式完成式被动语态 to have been solved。","point":"被动语态；be said to have been done。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-7ec8e71e9511a6a5"},{"stem":"这座桥是三年前建成的。","options":[],"answer":"This bridge was built three years ago.","explanation":"桥是建造动作的承受者，用一般过去时被动语态 was built；three years ago 是明确的过去时间。","point":"一般过去时的被动语态。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-a1d95551479e5dc5"},{"stem":"It is a great _____ for our school to host the national English competition this year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"honor"},{"key":"B","text":"favor"},{"key":"C","text":"prize"},{"key":"D","text":"reward"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"承办全国英语竞赛是一种“荣幸／荣誉”，用 honor。favor 为恩惠，prize 为奖品，reward 为报酬或奖赏。","point":"名词辨析；honor。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-41c4957e17bb26a8"},{"stem":"Tom is very _____ and makes friends easily wherever he goes.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"social"},{"key":"B","text":"sociable"},{"key":"C","text":"society"},{"key":"D","text":"socialist"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"sociable 形容人“好交际的、合群的”，符合到哪里都容易交朋友的语境。social 多指“社会的／社交的”，society 是名词。","point":"近形词辨析；sociable。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-bc05246e854d7df3"},{"stem":"火车再过五分钟就要开了。","options":[],"answer":"The train is leaving in five minutes.","explanation":"“in + 时间段”表示将来、倒计时；现在进行时 is leaving 表示即将发生的动作，尤其是位移动词。","point":"一般将来时（现在进行表将来）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-9890d402bc144a4e"},{"stem":"The weather was terrible. But for the fog, the climbers _____ the summit by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would reach"},{"key":"B","text":"will have reached"},{"key":"C","text":"would have reach"},{"key":"D","text":"would have reached"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"But for the fog 是含蓄虚拟语气条件，表示与过去事实相反；by now 表示到现在为止的结果，需用 would have + 过去分词。A 时态不符；B 非虚拟；C 的 reach 应为 reached。","point":"虚拟语气；含蓄条件（But for）＋瞬间动词＋by now（对过去动作虚拟，结果延续）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-30bc56ddf6691631"},{"stem":"The harder you practice, the more confident you will become when delivering a speech.","options":[],"answer":"练习得越多，你在演讲时就会越自信。","explanation":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级表示“越……就越……”。delivering a speech 意为发表演讲或进行演讲。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级结构。","category":"英译汉","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-8ec76be254e60f5b"},{"stem":"Her calmness under immense pressure reveals remarkable maturity and emotional resilience.","options":[],"answer":"她在巨大压力下的冷静表现出非凡的成熟与情绪韧性。","explanation":"under immense pressure 译为“在巨大压力下”；reveals 译为“表现出”；emotional resilience 译为“情绪韧性”。","point":"名词短语翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-e7a0b4b4dc142164"},{"stem":"I didn't get the position I applied for. _____. There will be more chances later.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Good for you!"},{"key":"B","text":"That's a shame."},{"key":"C","text":"No problem."},{"key":"D","text":"I think so."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"求职失利时应先表达遗憾，再给予希望；That's a shame 表示“真遗憾”。其余选项分别用于祝贺、回应求助或谢意、表示认同，均不合语境。","point":"遗憾——求职受挫。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-87f2d58c3400806c"},{"stem":"Our team lost the final game by one point last night. _____. You played so well all season.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How interesting!"},{"key":"B","text":"That's great news."},{"key":"C","text":"Enjoy yourself!"},{"key":"D","text":"What a shame!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"球队以一分惜败，应表达遗憾并肯定表现。What a shame 意为“真可惜”。其他选项表达兴趣、喜讯或祝玩得开心，均不切题。","point":"遗憾——惜败。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点","交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-340a6cba7e9a6770"},{"stem":"The speech was extended; otherwise, the minister _____ more time for the Q&A session.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would have"},{"key":"B","text":"would have had"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"would"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"演讲延长是过去事实；otherwise 表示“如果演讲不长”，对过去结果作相反假设，主句用 would have had。","point":"虚拟语气；otherwise 引导含蓄虚拟条件（过去完成）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-2e0e8f2a65e52014"},{"stem":"The teacher was quite _____ with the progress the students had made this term.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"satisfied"},{"key":"B","text":"satisfying"},{"key":"C","text":"satisfactory"},{"key":"D","text":"satisfaction"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"sb. be satisfied with sth. 表示“某人对某事感到满意”。satisfying / satisfactory 多指令人满意的事物；satisfaction 是名词。","point":"形容词辨析（satisfied with）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-ea3854130695de84"},{"stem":"The new traffic rules will come into _____ next month, and all drivers must obey them.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"affect"},{"key":"B","text":"effect"},{"key":"C","text":"effort"},{"key":"D","text":"afford"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"固定搭配 come into effect 意为“生效”。effect 是名词“效果”；affect 是动词“影响”；effort 意为“努力”；afford 意为“负担得起”。","point":"名词辨析（come into effect）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-bac7f08b4b5fee54"},{"stem":"A large _____ of wild birds flew over the lake and landed in the woods.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"herd"},{"key":"B","text":"swarm"},{"key":"C","text":"flock"},{"key":"D","text":"pack"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"a flock of birds 意为“一群鸟”。herd 常搭配牛、象；swarm 常搭配蜜蜂、昆虫；pack 常搭配狼。","point":"名词辨析（量词 flock）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-b5269c77f3e02cd3"},{"stem":"The more time you devote to reading, the broader your perspective will grow.","options":[],"answer":"你花在阅读上的时间越多，你的视野就会越宽广。","explanation":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级表示“越……就越……”。devote ... to 译为“将……奉献给或花……在”；broader 译为“更宽广的”。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级结构。","category":"英译汉","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"}],"id":"q-0b164625e248d6de"},{"stem":"The _____ of the new planet excited scientists all over the world.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"discovery"},{"key":"B","text":"invention"},{"key":"C","text":"creation"},{"key":"D","text":"production"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"新行星本已存在，是“被发现”，故用 discovery；invention 是发明原本不存在之物；creation 是创造；production 是生产。","point":"名词辨析（discovery / invention）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-1201a97a1559ce4e"},{"stem":"The two brothers had a heated _____ about which team would win the final match.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"agreement"},{"key":"B","text":"argument"},{"key":"C","text":"appointment"},{"key":"D","text":"apartment"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"heated argument 意为“激烈争论”。agreement 是同意；appointment 是约会或任命；apartment 是公寓。","point":"名词辨析（argument 及形近词）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-7f2f71d80d8bc0e1"},{"stem":"Once you have made up your mind, you should _____ your decision and never hesitate.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stick out"},{"key":"B","text":"point out"},{"key":"C","text":"stick to"},{"key":"D","text":"figure out"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"stick to 意为“坚持、遵守”，与 decision 搭配；stick out 是伸出或显眼，point out 是指出，figure out 是弄清楚。","point":"动词短语辨析（stick to）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-e934e5fb4e36992c"},{"stem":"My grandfather is in hospital. He fell and broke his leg. _____. I hope he recovers soon.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's good."},{"key":"B","text":"Well done."},{"key":"C","text":"How exciting!"},{"key":"D","text":"I'm sorry to hear that."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"听到坏消息应先表达难过并送上祝愿。I'm sorry to hear that 意为“听到这个消息我很难过”；其他选项均为积极或兴奋的回应，不合语境。","point":"遗憾——听闻不幸。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-dcdc0d2a58a28eec"},{"stem":"I lost my wallet on the subway this morning. _____. Did you report it to the police?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What a nice surprise!"},{"key":"B","text":"That's really unfortunate."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm glad to hear that."},{"key":"D","text":"Good news!"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方丢失钱包，应先表示遗憾，再询问是否报警。That's really unfortunate 意为“真不幸”；其他选项表达正面、欣喜的情绪，不符语境。","point":"遗憾——财物损失。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-bd8facd8c0be5b7d"},{"stem":"But for the early warning system, countless coastal residents _____ by last week's tsunami.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be killed"},{"key":"B","text":"will have been killed"},{"key":"C","text":"should be killed"},{"key":"D","text":"would have been killed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"but for 相当于 if it were not for / had it not been for，表示与过去事实相反的假设；居民与 kill 为被动关系，故用 would have been killed。","point":"虚拟语气；but for 引导含蓄虚拟条件（过去、被动）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-0651a8018696cc70"},{"stem":"But for the timely donation, the hospital _____ forced to cut back its services.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"should be"},{"key":"D","text":"would have been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"捐赠已发生在过去；but for 意为“如果没有它”，对过去结果作相反假设，主句用 would have been + 过去分词。","point":"虚拟语气；but for 含蓄虚拟条件（过去、被动）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":16,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十六天.md"},{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-818b86c23a1e0cfc"},{"stem":"She wishes her brother _____ such a reckless decision last Friday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hadn't made"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't make"},{"key":"C","text":"wouldn't make"},{"key":"D","text":"hasn't made"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"last Friday 已过去，wish 后对过去事实的虚拟用 had + 过去分词；否定形式为 hadn't made。","point":"虚拟语气；wish 从句对过去虚拟否定。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-5de395ee0dbd7328"},{"stem":"If we _____ to the original plan, we would now be relaxing at the seaside resort.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had stuck"},{"key":"B","text":"stuck"},{"key":"C","text":"should stick"},{"key":"D","text":"have stuck"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句 would now be 表示现在与事实相反；从句描述过去未坚持原计划，使用 had stuck。这是过去条件、现在结果的错综时间虚拟条件句。","point":"虚拟语气；错综时间条件句（主句对现在虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-d8467bad79b03ad4"},{"stem":"It's very kind of you to drive me to the airport so early. _____. I was heading that way anyway.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No trouble at all."},{"key":"B","text":"It's your duty."},{"key":"C","text":"Don't bother me again."},{"key":"D","text":"That's impossible."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方感谢清早送机，应客气地回应“不麻烦”；No trouble at all 与后句“我正好顺路”相符。","point":"回应感谢——顺路不麻烦。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-889910f1cba266f8"},{"stem":"Thank you so much for polishing my resume. _____. Feel free to ask if you need more help.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"My pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"That's too bad."},{"key":"D","text":"I don't care."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方感谢自己润色简历，My pleasure 是回应感谢的礼貌说法，表示“乐意效劳”；后句主动表示还可帮忙，也与此一致。","point":"回应感谢——乐意效劳。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-334e68e6454479f9"},{"stem":"Whenever I feel overwhelmed by deadlines, I take a short walk to clear my mind.","options":[],"answer":"每当我觉得被截止日期压得喘不过气时，我就会短暂地散个步，让头脑清醒一下。","explanation":"whenever 译为“每当”，引导时间状语从句；overwhelmed 译为“压垮或使应接不暇”；clear one's mind 译为“让头脑清醒”。","point":"whenever 状语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-17cc96572010df72"},{"stem":"If only I _____ taller, I would be able to reach the top shelf without a stool.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"had been"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"If only 对现状表达遗憾，be 动词在虚拟语气中一律用 were；主句 would be able to 也表明与现在事实相反。","point":"虚拟语气；If only 从句对现在虚拟，be 用 were。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-f95b5d64c9efb67c"},{"stem":"The detective said if the witness _____ the suspect's face at the lineup, the case _____ solved by Thursday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"identified / would be"},{"key":"B","text":"had identified / would be"},{"key":"C","text":"should identify / would have been"},{"key":"D","text":"had identified / would have been"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"by Thursday 强调过去某时点之前完成，主句用 would have been；从句对过去身份指认作相反假设，用 had identified；主句为被动语态。","point":"虚拟语气；错综时间虚拟（主句过去完成、从句过去）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-925e7a4be8ec944c"},{"stem":"I heard your baby was born yesterday. Congratulations to you both! _____. Mother and baby are both doing well.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's enough."},{"key":"B","text":"Thank you. We're over the moon."},{"key":"C","text":"It's not my baby."},{"key":"D","text":"Leave me alone."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"受到生子祝贺，应先感谢并报告平安；We're over the moon 意为“我们欣喜若狂”。其余选项均不合喜事情境。","point":"回应祝贺——致谢报平安。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-e5591ef53c1503e5"},{"stem":"正是这本书改变了我的人生。","options":[],"answer":"It is this book that has changed my life.","explanation":"强调句型是 It is/was + 被强调部分 + that/who ...。强调物用 that；页面用现在完成时 has changed 表示影响延续到现在。我的答案用一般过去时表达过去的改变，时态侧重点不同。","point":"强调句型。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-646d0ee35d08681d"},{"stem":"If the proposal is approved by the board, the construction will begin next spring.","options":[],"answer":"如果该提案获得董事会批准，建设工作将于明年春天启动。","explanation":"if 引导条件状语从句；主将从现，主句用 will，从句用一般现在时 is approved；begin 可译为“启动或开始”。","point":"if 条件状语从句 + 主将从现。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-b3c1837790d13ef2"},{"stem":"是他在昨天会议上提出了这个建议。","options":[],"answer":"It was he who put forward this suggestion at yesterday's meeting.","explanation":"强调句型为 It is/was + 被强调部分 + who/that ...。本题“是他”强调人，应把 he 放在被强调位置；yesterday 指过去，故用 was。put forward 保持原形。我的答案强调的是“在昨天会议上”，焦点与原句不同，应按参考答案复习。","point":"强调句型（It is/was ... who/that ...）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0f6fae3688ca83e8"},{"stem":"If only we _____ a larger apartment before the baby arrived!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bought"},{"key":"B","text":"should buy"},{"key":"C","text":"had bought"},{"key":"D","text":"would buy"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"before the baby arrived 表达过去的过去；If only 对过去事实表示遗憾，从句用 had bought。","point":"虚拟语气；If only 从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-bcf8a59272ceaaa7"},{"stem":"Thank you for lending me your umbrella. I'd have got soaked without it. _____. I'm glad it helped.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Give it back at once."},{"key":"B","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"C","text":"You owe me a lot."},{"key":"D","text":"What a shame!"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方感谢借伞，应答 You're welcome（不客气）；后句“很高兴它帮了你”表达友好。其他选项不合时宜。","point":"回应感谢——不客气。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-bd4199615e6b86f1"},{"stem":"He wishes he _____ a millionaire right now so that he could buy his parents a house.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"right now 表示对现在的愿望；wish 从句对现在虚拟时，be 动词一律用 were。","point":"虚拟语气；wish 对现在虚拟（be 用 were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-514044947a272820"},{"stem":"Congratulations on opening your own restaurant! _____. Please come by and try our food sometime.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's not a big deal."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't come near me."},{"key":"C","text":"Thank you. I'm a little nervous too."},{"key":"D","text":"That's what you think."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"受到餐馆开业祝贺，应感谢并可坦诚表达心情，随后邀请对方品尝；C 符合语境，其余选项均失礼。","point":"回应祝贺——致谢并邀客。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-5591592971912100"},{"stem":"老师建议我们下周去参观博物馆。","options":[],"answer":"The teacher advised us to visit the museum next week.","explanation":"页面讲解 advise + sb. + to do，注意不带 to 不可；advise + doing 也可。我的答案使用 suggest that + 主语 + 动词原形，也符合“建议”的表达。","point":"复杂宾语（advise + sb. + to do）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-494e2cc599f886ba"},{"stem":"I do wish the rain _____ right now so that we could finish the picnic outdoors.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would stop"},{"key":"B","text":"stopped"},{"key":"C","text":"stops"},{"key":"D","text":"had stopped"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"表达对将来“愿雨停”的请求或期望，wish 从句用 would do。stopped、stops 不符合这里的虚拟语气时态。句意：我真希望雨现在停下，这样我们就能在户外完成野餐。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 从句表示对将来的愿望时用 would do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0e82d1c9eaec7bc8"},{"stem":"I wish I _____ the chance to study abroad when I was younger.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had"},{"key":"B","text":"have"},{"key":"C","text":"had had"},{"key":"D","text":"would have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"when I was younger 表示过去已经错失的机会，wish 后用 had done；“本该拥有”的表达需 had had 复合。句意：我真希望我年轻时有出国学习的机会。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 从句对过去虚拟（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-5efb683f2c384dc2"},{"stem":"Thanks a lot for helping me move into the new apartment. _____. That's what friends are for.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"B","text":"It's all your fault."},{"key":"C","text":"I was forced to do it."},{"key":"D","text":"Mind your own business."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"朋友感谢搬家帮忙，应答“Don't mention it”（不用客气），后接 That's what friends are for（朋友就该这样）自然。其余选项抱怨或指责，不符合语境。句意：太感谢你帮我搬进新公寓了。——不用客气，朋友之间本该如此。","point":"回应感谢：朋友义气。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-8a356089185939e6"},{"stem":"When children are exposed to multiple languages at an early age, they tend to develop stronger cognitive skills.","options":[],"answer":"当儿童在幼年接触多种语言时，他们往往能发展出更强的认知能力。","explanation":"when 引导的状语从句译为“……时”；tend to 译为“往往”；cognitive skills 译为“认知能力”；multiple 译为“多种的”。","point":"when 状语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":17,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md"}],"id":"q-2ba8d8f7d84ed822"},{"stem":"I wish I _____ to warn him about the storm, but I forgot to make the call in time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"remembered"},{"key":"B","text":"had remembered"},{"key":"C","text":"would remember"},{"key":"D","text":"have remembered"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"wish 表遗憾“本该记得打电话”，对过去虚拟用 had remembered；remembered / would remember 不合时态。句意：我真希望我记得提醒他注意风暴，但我忘记及时打电话了。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 对过去虚拟（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-367774ce6f4f849e"},{"stem":"As long as you maintain a consistent study schedule, you will steadily improve your proficiency.","options":[],"answer":"只要你保持稳定的学习计划，你的熟练程度就会稳步提升。","explanation":"as long as 译为“只要”，引导条件状语从句；consistent 译为“稳定的”；proficiency 译为“熟练程度”。","point":"条件状语从句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-3d3658a2770ed017"},{"stem":"Excuse me, what time does the library open tomorrow morning? _____. It opens at eight on weekdays.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, it does."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm sorry, I don't go there."},{"key":"C","text":"It doesn't open at all."},{"key":"D","text":"It opens at eight o'clock."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方询问图书馆开门时间，应给出具体时间。D 直接回答，后接“工作日八点开门”进一步说明；其他选项信息缺失或态度不合适。句意：图书馆明天早上几点开门？——八点开门，工作日都是八点开门。","point":"询问时间：公共设施开放时间。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-a5ce499195f7c30a"},{"stem":"Some researchers favor quantitative methods, while others prefer qualitative case studies.","options":[],"answer":"一些研究人员偏爱定量研究方法，而另一些则更喜欢定性案例研究。","explanation":"while 表对比，译为“而”；favor 译为“偏爱”；quantitative 和 qualitative 分别译为“定量的”和“定性的”；case study 译为“案例研究”。","point":"并列对比句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-1211fcc5b584befd"},{"stem":"My grandparents often wish they _____ in the countryside rather than the crowded city.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had lived"},{"key":"B","text":"would live"},{"key":"C","text":"lived"},{"key":"D","text":"live"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"表达对现在居住地的虚拟希望，用一般过去式 lived；be 动词用 were，普通动词用过去式。had lived 表示对过去的虚拟，与本句意不符。句意：我的祖父母常常希望自己住在乡下而不是喧嚣的城市。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 对现在虚拟（一般过去式）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-4d3106885aab13c2"},{"stem":"The company specializes in software development, whereas its subsidiary focuses primarily on hardware design.","options":[],"answer":"这家公司专注于软件开发，而其子公司则主要致力于硬件设计。","explanation":"whereas 译为“而/然而”，表示对比；specialize in 译为“专注于”；primarily 译为“主要地”；subsidiary 译为“子公司”。","point":"并列对比复合句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-8800378d81020c9a"},{"stem":"If only she _____ more prepared for the negotiation! She blew her chance yesterday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"would be"},{"key":"D","text":"should be"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"yesterday 时点已过，对过去虚拟；If only 表后悔，had been 表过去相反状态“做好了准备”。句意：要是她对谈判准备得更充分就好了！她昨天错失了机会。","point":"虚拟语气：If only 从句（对过去虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-7e761935ed2d026d"},{"stem":"Do you know what time the film starts tonight? _____. Let's check the notice board over there.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's very interesting."},{"key":"B","text":"No, I don't like films."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm not quite sure."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I saw it last week."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方询问电影开场时间，自己不确定时应如实说明并给出解决办法。“I'm not quite sure”与后续“去公告栏看一下”切实可行；A、B 跑题，D 与后文逻辑不符。句意：你知道今晚电影几点开始吗？——我不太确定，咱们去看看那边的公告栏吧。","point":"交际用语：询问信息，不确定时如实说明。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-45986fbc8a60a376"},{"stem":"直到昨天我才意识到自己的错误。","options":[],"answer":"It was not until yesterday that I realized my mistake.","explanation":"考查 not until 的强调句型。句型结构：It is/was not until + 时间状语 + that + 陈述语序的从句。not until 的强调句型中，that 后面的句子必须保持正常陈述语序（I realized），绝对不能倒装；只有当 Not until 直接置于句首时，才使用部分倒装（Not until yesterday did I realize...）。","point":"强调句型（It is/was not until... that...）的陈述语序。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-b9b919adf5010107"},{"stem":"How I wish I _____ my first love's letters instead of burning them out of anger.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"kept"},{"key":"B","text":"should keep"},{"key":"C","text":"would keep"},{"key":"D","text":"had kept"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"后悔当初把信烧掉，表达希望当时保留了信；How I wish 是 If only 的同义强调语气，从句对过去用 had done。句意：我多想当初保留好那些初恋的信，而不是愤怒地烧掉。","point":"虚拟语气：How I wish（If only 同义）对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-cb70924d22af5880"},{"stem":"She wishes that her ex-boyfriend _____ constantly about his new girlfriend online.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would stop"},{"key":"B","text":"stopped"},{"key":"C","text":"stops"},{"key":"D","text":"had stopped"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对现在或将来对方的反复行为表达厌倦的请求或愿望，用 wish + would do；stopped 表一般过去不符。句意：她真希望前男友别再在网上一直炫耀新女友了。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 从句（对将来婉转请求）用 would do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-9c08854d07224206"},{"stem":"If only the company _____ its shares last week before the market collapsed!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sold"},{"key":"B","text":"would sell"},{"key":"C","text":"had sold"},{"key":"D","text":"sells"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"last week 和 before the market collapsed 双重过去提示，If only 后用 had done。句意：要是公司在上周市场崩盘前卖掉股票就好了！","point":"虚拟语气：If only 从句（对过去虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-8583a2272097e5b4"},{"stem":"Thanks for correcting the mistakes in my report. _____. Let me know if you spot anything else.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You should have been more careful."},{"key":"B","text":"It's not my job."},{"key":"C","text":"Glad to help."},{"key":"D","text":"Forget it."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"同事感谢自己帮忙改报告，应答气氛表示乐于相助。Glad to help 简洁得体，后接“有问题再找我”体现团队精神；其余选项或指责对方，或表示拒绝，都不合语气。句意：谢谢你帮我改正报告里的错误。——很高兴能帮上忙，再发现什么问题随时找我。","point":"回应感谢：乐于相助。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-e84d475edcf86312"},{"stem":"My colleague wishes she _____ the presentation last Monday instead of leaving it to her intern.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"delivered"},{"key":"B","text":"had delivered"},{"key":"C","text":"would deliver"},{"key":"D","text":"has delivered"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"last Monday 已过去，对过去虚拟，wish 后用 had done；delivered / would deliver 不合时态。句意：我同事真希望她上周一亲自做了汇报，而不是交给实习生。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-1e8f3d55ea15b72e"},{"stem":"They wish they _____ to the mountains this weekend, but they are tied up with work.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could go"},{"key":"B","text":"can go"},{"key":"C","text":"will go"},{"key":"D","text":"had gone"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"this weekend 表对将来可实现的愿望，用 could do 表委婉强烈愿望；can / will 不符虚拟。句意：他们真希望这周末能去山里玩，但工作脱不开身。","point":"虚拟语气：wish 从句（对将来婉转表达）用 could do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-0e3c8289160bda64"},{"stem":"Excuse me, which bus should I take to the railway station? _____. It stops right in front of the station.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take the No. 22 bus."},{"key":"B","text":"You can't miss it."},{"key":"C","text":"It's a long story."},{"key":"D","text":"Never mind."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方询问去火车站的公交线路，应先给出乘车建议。Take the No. 22 bus 直接给出信息，后接“车站前就是站点”作补充说明；You can't miss it 用于指路后的叮嘱而非线路本身；其余两项答非所问。句意：——打扰一下，去火车站该坐哪路公交车？——坐 22 路，它正好停在火车站门口。","point":"询问路线：公交线路。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-4ae02523b1a94282"},{"stem":"How much is the ticket for the art exhibition? _____. Students can get in at half price.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's very beautiful."},{"key":"B","text":"I like it very much."},{"key":"C","text":"Twenty yuan for adults."},{"key":"D","text":"You'd better buy one."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方问展览票价，应当首先告知价格信息。Twenty yuan for adults 直接报价，后接学生半价形成完整答复；评价展览或劝购都偏离“多少钱”这一疑问点。句意：——美术展的门票多少钱？——成人票二十元，学生可以半价入场。","point":"询问价格：票价信息。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-73d42c088acce826"},{"stem":"他不仅会说英语,而且还会说法语。","options":[],"answer":"It is not only English that he can speak, but also French.","explanation":"页面考查 not only...but also... 与强调句型的结合。强调句型结构：It is + 被强调部分（not only A, but also B）+ that + 陈述语序的从句。强调句型中，that 后面的句子必须保持正常的陈述语序（he can speak），绝对不能倒装；只有当 Not only 直接置于句首引导整个句子时，才使用部分倒装（Not only can he speak English, but also French）。","point":"强调句型（It is... that...）的陈述语序 + not only...but also... 并列结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-ab7e1110c53aa08b"},{"stem":"Thank you so much for putting me up for the weekend. _____. You're welcome to come any time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I had no choice."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't come again."},{"key":"C","text":"It was a pleasure having you."},{"key":"D","text":"That will be expensive."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"房客临走感谢周末留宿，主人应表达“接待是件乐事”并欢迎再来。It was a pleasure having you 与 You're welcome any time 前后呼应，热情周到；其余选项冷淡失礼。句意：——谢谢你周末让我住在你家，太感谢了。——接待你我很开心，随时欢迎再来。","point":"回应感谢：热情待客。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-8f41a4176664b078"},{"stem":"是李老师昨天在教室里找到了那本书。","options":[],"answer":"It was Mr. Li who found the book in the classroom yesterday.","explanation":"本题考查强调句型的基本结构与关系代词选择。句型结构：It is/was + 被强调部分 + that/who + 剩余部分。根据 yesterday 判断为过去时，故用 It was。被强调部分是“人”（Mr. Li），关系代词优先用 who，也可用 that。强调句型中，that/who 后面的从句必须保持陈述语序（found），绝不能倒装。","point":"强调句型（It was... who...）+ 关系代词选择 + 陈述语序。","category":"汉译英","topics":["定语从句","代词与限定词","强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":18,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md"}],"id":"q-9a8b39d7b53edf97"},{"stem":"They _____ nearly two hours waiting for the plane at the airport because of the heavy fog.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cost"},{"key":"B","text":"paid"},{"key":"C","text":"spent"},{"key":"D","text":"took"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"spend time (in) doing sth. 意为“花费时间做某事”，主语是人；cost 的主语通常是物；take 常用于 it takes sb. some time to do 句型；pay 与 for 连用表示“付款”。句意：由于大雾，他们在机场等了将近两个小时才等到飞机。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-c9e19245db6089aa"},{"stem":"It was _____ warm a day that we decided to go swimming in the river.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so"},{"key":"B","text":"such"},{"key":"C","text":"very"},{"key":"D","text":"quite"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"so + 形容词 + a/an + 名词 + that 为固定结构；such 后接名词时冠词位置在其前（such a warm day），very / quite 不能与 that 构成结果状语从句。句意：天气那么暖和，我们决定去河里游泳。","point":"so...that 结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-afea36d8e5e0c588"},{"stem":"How many pieces of luggage am I allowed to check in? _____. Business class passengers may take more.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Two pieces free of charge."},{"key":"B","text":"None, never."},{"key":"C","text":"I have no luggage."},{"key":"D","text":"It depends on your height."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方询问免费托运行李件数，应答应给出标准规定：Two pieces free of charge（免费两件）正面回答，后接“商务舱可更多”补充细则；其余选项与常识或问题无关。\n句意：——我可以免费托运几件行李？——免费两件，商务舱乘客可以带更多。","point":"询问规定——行李限额。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-b138a154927302aa"},{"stem":"Jane spoke so confidently at the press conference as though she _____ every question in advance.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rehearsed"},{"key":"B","text":"had rehearsed"},{"key":"C","text":"rehearses"},{"key":"D","text":"would rehearse"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"spoke 为过去时；“事先演练过”发生在记者会之前，as though 从句用过去完成时 had rehearsed 表示与过去事实相反的虚拟。\n句意：简在记者会上的发言非常自信，仿佛她事先演练过所有问题。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去事实虚拟（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-848fc5ba959812a4"},{"stem":"The night was so quiet that everything seemed as if it _____ a deep sleep.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been in"},{"key":"B","text":"is in"},{"key":"C","text":"would be in"},{"key":"D","text":"were in"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"主句 seemed 为过去时，as if 后描述与现实相反的“仿佛正在沉睡”，用 were in；be 的虚拟式为 were。\n句意：夜如此静，万物仿佛都沉入了深度睡眠。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在事实相反（be 用 were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-fb903d02ee110ed2"},{"stem":"Excuse me, how can I connect to the Wi-Fi in my room? _____. The password is also printed on it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The network name is on the desk card."},{"key":"B","text":"Wi-Fi is bad for your health."},{"key":"C","text":"I don't have a phone."},{"key":"D","text":"You shouldn't use it."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"酒店客人询问房间 Wi-Fi 连接方式，应先告知网络名所在位置：The network name is on the desk card；后接“密码也印在上面”，指引清楚实用。其余选项说教或无关。\n句意：——请问我房间的 Wi-Fi 怎么连接？——网络名称在桌上的卡片上，密码也印在上面。","point":"咨询服务——酒店 Wi-Fi。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-3240c54e13b22b08"},{"stem":"He described the small village as if he _____ its history backwards and forwards.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"knew"},{"key":"B","text":"knows"},{"key":"C","text":"had known"},{"key":"D","text":"would know"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"页面认为 described 为过去式，描述的内容与事实相反，他其实并不熟知此村庄，故 as if + had done（对过去事实虚拟）。\n句意：他描述起那个小村庄，仿佛对其历史了如指掌。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对过去事实虚拟（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":["本题 A（knew）也可自然表达“当时仿佛知道”的状态；页面按其预设的“对过去事实虚拟”选择 C，复习时注意区分题库判分与语境解释。"],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-f263ded5d4394bb9"},{"stem":"Books provide knowledge, and meanwhile they cultivate patience and empathy.","options":[],"answer":"书籍提供知识，与此同时也培养耐心与同理心。","explanation":"and 表并列；meanwhile 译为“与此同时”；cultivate 译为“培养”，empathy 译为“同理心或共情”。","point":"并列复合句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-4b1bd1198841f1e9"},{"stem":"When he heard the announcement, he stood up abruptly as if he _____ in a hurry to catch a flight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"as if 引导从句描述当时“他正匆忙赶飞机”，与事实不符（没那么急），用 were 表对现在进行状态虚拟。\n句意：他听到通告后猛地站起来，仿佛他正匆匆赶飞机。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在进行状态虚拟（be 用 were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-49cafe68fe76b924"},{"stem":"Have you heard anything from the company about the interview? _____. They said they would let me know by Friday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not yet. I'm still waiting."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, I interviewed them."},{"key":"C","text":"No, I hate interviews."},{"key":"D","text":"It's none of your business."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方询问面试结果消息；“Not yet. I'm still waiting”直接说明现状，后接“对方说周五前通知”补充预期时间，衔接自然。其他选项曲解问题或态度恶劣。\n句意：——公司那边有面试的消息吗？——还没有，我还在等。他们说周五前会通知我。","point":"询问近况——面试结果。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-071cedd6cfd0f73a"},{"stem":"He _____ the invitation to the dinner party politely because he had another appointment.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"refused"},{"key":"B","text":"denied"},{"key":"C","text":"rejected"},{"key":"D","text":"declined"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"decline 侧重“婉言谢绝（邀请、提议）”；refuse 语气较直接，deny 是“否认”，reject 为“断然拒绝”。题干有 politely 提示，故选 decline。\n句意：他礼貌地谢绝了晚宴的邀请，因为他另有约会。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-13400c6e75c4e9b4"},{"stem":"After hearing the case presented, the judge nodded gravely as though he _____ in his verdict.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"made up his mind"},{"key":"B","text":"makes up his mind"},{"key":"C","text":"would make up his mind"},{"key":"D","text":"had made up his mind"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as though 后描述对过去决定的相反假设（他其实尚未定夺），用 had made 表过去虚拟。\n句意：听完案情陈述后，法官沉重地点了点头，仿佛他已下定决心。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-40d7b511a416259f"},{"stem":"He is not a brilliant artist; rather, he is a meticulous craftsman with years of experience.","options":[],"answer":"他算不上才华横溢的艺术家，而是一位经验丰富、技艺精湛的工匠。","explanation":"并列句顺译；not ... rather 译为“不是……而是”；brilliant 译为“才华横溢的”，meticulous 译为“一丝不苟的”。","point":"并列复合句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-0559bf34e1c92072"},{"stem":"The project was challenging, yet the team managed to complete it ahead of schedule.","options":[],"answer":"这个项目充满挑战，但团队依然设法提前完成了。","explanation":"yet 表转折，译为“但或然而”；manage to do 译为“设法做”；ahead of schedule 译为“提前于计划”。","point":"转折复合句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-6e93608c43e4e1d6"},{"stem":"The company promised to _____ the salaries of its employees by 8 percent next year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"raise"},{"key":"B","text":"rise"},{"key":"C","text":"arise"},{"key":"D","text":"arouse"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"raise 是及物动词，意为“提高、增加（工资等）”，后接宾语；rise 是不及物动词“上升”；arise 是“（问题等）出现”；arouse 是“激起”。\n句意：公司承诺明年把员工的工资提高 8%。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-4365c9362f232d76"},{"stem":"How early should I get to the airport for the international flight? _____. Security checks can be slow in the morning.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As late as possible."},{"key":"B","text":"You don't need a passport."},{"key":"C","text":"The airport is far away."},{"key":"D","text":"At least two hours before departure."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方询问国际航班应提前多久到机场，应答应给出明确建议并解释原因：At least two hours before departure 直接给出时间量；后接早高峰安检慢的理由。其余选项偏离问题。\n句意：——坐国际航班我应该提前多久到机场？——至少提前两小时到，早上的安检可能会比较慢。","point":"询问建议——值机时间。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-8086a4ec7fc4aa61"},{"stem":"我发现每天早上跑步对我来说很有趣。","options":[],"answer":"I find it very interesting to run in the morning every day.","explanation":"形式宾语 find it + adj + to do；it 指代 to do 不定式；run in the morning 表“晨跑”。","point":"形式宾语 find it + adj + to do。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-80d4d5a02e056421"},{"stem":"He commands the troops as if he _____ a seasoned general rather than a junior officer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"had been"},{"key":"D","text":"should be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"他实为初级军官，却指挥部队仿佛是经验丰富的将军；as if + were 表对现在事实相反，was 不符虚拟。\n句意：他指挥部队，仿佛是一位资深将领而非下级军官。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在事实相反。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-9ebcca339122a542"},{"stem":"Since she retired, my aunt has decided to _____ yoga to keep fit.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take on"},{"key":"B","text":"take off"},{"key":"C","text":"take over"},{"key":"D","text":"take up"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"take up 意为“开始从事（某项活动、爱好）”；take on 为承担、呈现；take off 为起飞、脱下；take over 为接管。\n句意：自从退休后，我姑姑决定开始练瑜伽以保持健康。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-148117a781b87452"},{"stem":"We are going to have our computer _____ before the important meeting next week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"repair"},{"key":"B","text":"repaired"},{"key":"C","text":"repairing"},{"key":"D","text":"to repair"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"have sth. done 表示“请人做某事／使某事被完成”，宾语 computer 与 repair 之间是被动关系。\n句意：下周重要会议前，我们打算请人把电脑修好。","point":"have sth. done 结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-09d96066266dad55"},{"stem":"Did you get my email about the new schedule? _____. I'll send you a reply this afternoon.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, I'm too busy to read emails."},{"key":"B","text":"I don't have an email account."},{"key":"C","text":"That's not my schedule."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I did. Thanks for sending it."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方确认是否收到关于新日程的邮件，收到时应正面答复：Yes, I did，后接致谢和回复时间，礼貌完整；否认、推脱或回避与后文矛盾或不配合。\n句意：——你收到我发的那封关于新日程的邮件了吗？——收到了，谢谢你发给我。今天下午我会给你回信。","point":"确认信息——邮件收发。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-90f80199191f9b56"},{"stem":"What time do we have to check out of the hotel? _____. You can leave your luggage at the front desk if you need to.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can check in at any time."},{"key":"B","text":"The room is very comfortable."},{"key":"C","text":"Check-out is at twelve noon."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm not a hotel guest."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方询问退房时间，应给出准确时间点并补充行李寄存服务：Check-out is at twelve noon 直接回答；后接可把行李留在前台的说明。其余选项偏题。\n句意：——我们得几点退房？——中午十二点退房。如果需要，你可以把行李寄存在前台。","point":"咨询时间——酒店退房。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-7d9f4f9bb59de76b"},{"stem":"The bridge _____ in the 1960s is still in good condition and is widely used by the villagers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to build"},{"key":"B","text":"to be built"},{"key":"C","text":"built"},{"key":"D","text":"having built"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"过去分词短语 built in the 1960s 作后置定语，表示被动和完成，相当于定语从句 which was built in the 1960s。\n句意：那座建于 20 世纪 60 年代的桥至今仍然状况良好，村民们仍在广泛使用。","point":"过去分词作定语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-84828f64d4cfe353"},{"stem":"The doctor advised the old man to avoid _____ too much salt in his daily diet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to take"},{"key":"B","text":"take"},{"key":"C","text":"taking"},{"key":"D","text":"taken"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"avoid 后接动名词作宾语，不接不定式，即 avoid doing sth.。\n句意：医生建议那位老人在日常饮食中避免摄入过多的盐。","point":"动名词作宾语。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-02c1be67d115fa8b"},{"stem":"If only I _____ how to swim! I would not have panicked when I fell into the river.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"knew"},{"key":"B","text":"had known"},{"key":"C","text":"know"},{"key":"D","text":"would know"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"when I fell 时间已过去，If only 表后悔“本会游泳”，用 had known；knew 只表现在不表过去。\n句意：要是我会游泳就好了！我掉进河里时就不会慌了。","point":"虚拟语气——If only 从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-6e624e9a946c0c32"},{"stem":"对我来说学好英语很重要。","options":[],"answer":"It is very important for me to learn English well.","explanation":"形式主语 It is + adj + (for sb) + to do；评价动作难度用 for，评价人物性格或品质用 of。","point":"形式主语 It is + adj + to do。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-3e08c784eff292cf"},{"stem":"I wish I _____ a bit more time. The deadline is just a few hours away!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have"},{"key":"B","text":"would have"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"should have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"deadline 之前仍存可能，但 wish 常表“再多一点时间就好”；对现在未实现用 had 表反事实“拥有”；主句隐含 would finish。\n句意：我真希望再有点时间。截止时间就剩几小时了！","point":"虚拟语气——wish 对现在虚拟（had 表“拥有”）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-8d68f9cc34a531fd"},{"stem":"I still remember the day _____ I first entered this university as a freshman.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"where"},{"key":"C","text":"when"},{"key":"D","text":"what"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"先行词 the day 在定语从句中作时间状语，故用关系副词 when 引导。\n句意：我仍然记得大一新生初入这所大学的那一天。","point":"when 引导的定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-c0af3cfa2865ab7a"},{"stem":"If it _____ tomorrow, the sports meeting will have to be put off.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will rain"},{"key":"B","text":"rains"},{"key":"C","text":"rained"},{"key":"D","text":"would rain"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句用一般将来时，条件状语从句用一般现在时表示将来，即“主将从现”。\n句意：如果明天下雨，运动会就只好推迟。","point":"条件状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-b12cd5550fabc611"},{"stem":"花了我们两个小时才把作业做完。","options":[],"answer":"It took us two hours to finish the homework.","explanation":"句型 It takes sb time to do 表“做某事花了某人多少时间”；finish 表“完成”。","point":"It takes sb time to do。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":19,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第十九天.md"}],"id":"q-7a686c31c74464b6"},{"stem":"_____ more time, we could have done the task much better.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If we are given"},{"key":"B","text":"Were we given"},{"key":"C","text":"Had we been given"},{"key":"D","text":"Should we be given"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"从句表示与过去事实相反，应用 had done；省略 if 时把 had 提前，故为 Had we been given more time。\n句意：要是当初给我们更多时间，我们本可以把任务完成得好得多。","point":"虚拟语气——与过去事实相反。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-2e6ed15ef7b37aa7"},{"stem":"他既是医生，也是作家。","options":[],"answer":"He is both a doctor and a writer.","explanation":"both ... and ... 连接并列成分，表“既……又……”；主语为单数 he，谓语用单数 is。","point":"both ... and ... 并列连词。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-bf889f2b92daff4b"},{"stem":"When the lights flickered, Sue clutched my arm as though she _____ a horror film alone.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were watching"},{"key":"B","text":"had watched"},{"key":"C","text":"watches"},{"key":"D","text":"would watch"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主句动作 flickered 已过去，as though 后描述“仿佛正在看恐怖片”，与她并未观看的事实相反，用 were watching 对现在进行虚拟。\n句意：灯光闪烁时，苏抓住我的胳膊，仿佛她正一个人看恐怖片。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对现在进行状态虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-c19a1202da99d84c"},{"stem":"Online learning is convenient; however, it requires far greater self-discipline than classroom study.","options":[],"answer":"在线学习很便利，然而它比课堂学习需要更强的自律。","explanation":"however 表转折，独立成句或加“然而”；convenient 译为“便利的”，self-discipline 译为“自律”。","point":"转折复合句翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-830c0f0856bfec0e"},{"stem":"_____ is known to all, the earth moves around the sun.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Which"},{"key":"B","text":"As"},{"key":"C","text":"That"},{"key":"D","text":"What"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"as 可引导非限制性定语从句并置于句首，指代整个主句，意为“正如……”，which 引导的非限制性定语从句不能放在句首。\n句意：众所周知，地球绕着太阳转。","point":"定语从句（as 引导）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-3ffb177368af8527"},{"stem":"据说这个城市三年前发生了地震。","options":[],"answer":"It is said that an earthquake struck this city three years ago.","explanation":"It is said that ... 表“据说……”；真实主语为 that 从句，三年前发生，从句用一般过去时。","point":"It is said that（形式主语）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-3aaa26ac5cfe7332"},{"stem":"He _____ his bag on the chair and went out to answer the phone.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lied"},{"key":"B","text":"laid"},{"key":"C","text":"lay"},{"key":"D","text":"lain"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"lay（放置）的过去式为 laid，符合“把包放在椅子上”的语境。lied 是 lie（说谎）的过去式；lay 也可是 lie（躺）的过去式，不及物，不接宾语；lain 是 lie（躺）的过去分词。\n句意：他把包放在椅子上，出去接电话了。","point":"动词辨析（lie／lay 的过去式与过去分词）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-ac345b5dc915a6dc"},{"stem":"Young people today prefer sending messages _____ making phone calls.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to"},{"key":"B","text":"than"},{"key":"C","text":"better than"},{"key":"D","text":"instead"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"prefer doing sth. to doing sth. 意为“比起做某事，更喜欢做某事”，为固定搭配。\n句意：如今的年轻人更喜欢发信息，而不愿打电话。","point":"prefer 的用法。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-60e1d33e9c8d92c5"},{"stem":"The room is so dim that we feel as if a single candle _____ able to illuminate the whole space.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"had been"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"should be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"feel 后 as if 从句形容“仿佛一根蜡烛就能照亮整间屋”，与现实不符，用 were 对现在事实相反。\n句意：房间昏暗得让人觉得仿佛一根蜡烛就能照亮整个空间。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在事实相反（be 用 were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-f9a80b6924d3ece7"},{"stem":"When I entered the factory last week, a new workshop _____ in the south of it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was being built"},{"key":"B","text":"has been built"},{"key":"C","text":"is built"},{"key":"D","text":"had been built"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"was being built 为过去进行时的被动语态，表示“过去某时正在被修建”，与 last week 对应。\n句意：上周我进那家工厂时，南边正有一座新车间在建设中。","point":"被动语态。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-d8d482414515f1b9"},{"stem":"Because of the heavy snow, the football match has been _____ until next Saturday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"put forward"},{"key":"B","text":"put on"},{"key":"C","text":"put out"},{"key":"D","text":"put off"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"put off 意为“推迟、延期”；put forward“提出”；put on“穿上、上演”；put out“扑灭、出版”。句意：由于大雪，足球比赛已推迟到下周六。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-2ff2d38fba80c79d"},{"stem":"She smiled at the photographer as though she _____ in front of cameras every day of her life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had stood"},{"key":"B","text":"stood"},{"key":"C","text":"stands"},{"key":"D","text":"would stand"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"页面把 as though 从句理解为对过去持续经历的相反假设：她并非天天面对镜头，却笑得像一生中每天都站在镜头前一样，因此用过去完成时 had stood。我选 stood，把这里的既往经历误作对当时状态的假设。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去事实的虚拟（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-414e02cfe75d0c39"},{"stem":"He lit a cigarette as if he _____ to clear his mind before continuing.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had tried"},{"key":"B","text":"were trying"},{"key":"C","text":"tries"},{"key":"D","text":"would try"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"as if 描述“仿佛正努力清醒头脑”的进行状态，与事实相反，用 were trying 对现在进行动作虚拟。句意：他点了根烟，仿佛正试图在继续前理清思路。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在进行状态虚拟（were doing）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-3fbfe9fc898f1d0d"},{"stem":"How long do we have to wait for a table? _____. We have several groups ahead of you.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The food is delicious."},{"key":"B","text":"We are full already."},{"key":"C","text":"It's your turn to cook."},{"key":"D","text":"About twenty minutes."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"顾客问等位时长，服务员应直接回答预计时间。后句“前面还有几桌”进一步说明至少还需等待。\n句意：“还要等多久才有位子？”“大约二十分钟，你们前面还有几桌。”","point":"咨询服务——餐厅等位。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-cc778be012489ec5"},{"stem":"The teacher was surprised at _____ the whole examination paper in such a short time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"his students finishing"},{"key":"B","text":"his students to finish"},{"key":"C","text":"his students finish"},{"key":"D","text":"his students' finishing"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"at 是介词，后接动名词；书面语中用所有格 his students' 作 finishing 的逻辑主语。句意：学生们在这么短时间内完成整份试卷，老师感到很惊讶。","point":"动名词复合结构。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-6857ae9ecc4748d4"},{"stem":"Excuse me, which line goes to the Exhibition Center? _____. Get off at the third stop.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take Line 5 and transfer at Central Station."},{"key":"B","text":"You should walk faster."},{"key":"C","text":"The exhibition is over."},{"key":"D","text":"I've never been to a museum."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"问去会展中心的线路，应回答乘坐哪条线及换乘站点。A 给出 5 号线和中央车站换乘，与后文“第三站下车”衔接。","point":"询问路线——地铁换乘。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-4a32c2c8010302e4"},{"stem":"Looking out over the snowy field, Mike felt as though he _____ somewhere far beyond the North Pole.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were transported"},{"key":"B","text":"is transported"},{"key":"C","text":"would be transported"},{"key":"D","text":"had been transported"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"页面把“被送到远处”视为发生在 felt 之前的虚拟过去动作，因此用 had been transported（过去完成时被动式）。我选 were transported，把它理解成与 felt 同时的假想状态。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去虚拟（被动式）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-c15deca493da7100"},{"stem":"Did you watch the football game last night? What was the score? _____. It was a close game till the end.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I don't like football at all."},{"key":"B","text":"We won, three to two."},{"key":"C","text":"The score is not important."},{"key":"D","text":"I was playing basketball."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方直接问昨晚球赛的比分，应告知结果。We won, three to two 表示“我们以三比二获胜”，与后句比赛始终胶着相符。","point":"询问赛事——比赛结果。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-e1481c3ea93e9063"},{"stem":"_____ hard the task is, we will try our best to finish it on time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No matter what"},{"key":"B","text":"Whatever"},{"key":"C","text":"Even if"},{"key":"D","text":"No matter how"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"no matter how + 形容词/副词，引导让步状语从句，意为“无论多么……”。what/whatever 后接名词或作主语、宾语；even if 后接完整句子。\n句意：无论任务多难，我们都会尽最大努力按时完成。","point":"“no matter how”引导让步状语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-1df6a41c71e3cb40"},{"stem":"The police are trying to find out the _____ of the fire that destroyed the old warehouse.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reason"},{"key":"B","text":"excuse"},{"key":"C","text":"cause"},{"key":"D","text":"result"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"cause 指事故发生的直接起因，常说 the cause of the fire；reason 偏重说明理由，excuse“借口”，result“结果”。句意：警方正设法查明烧毁旧仓库那场火灾的原因。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-e78cb58b0d8fd031"},{"stem":"中译：他不仅歌唱得好，而且舞也跳得很棒。","options":[],"answer":"Not only does he sing well, but also he dances well.","explanation":"not only...but also... 放在句中时可用正常语序；当 Not only 置于句首，引导的前半句需部分倒装：Not only + 助动词 does + 主语 he + 动词原形 sing。but also 后的句子保持正常语序。","point":"倒装句——Not only...but also... 置于句首时的部分倒装。","category":"汉译英","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-598926784b3baaae"},{"stem":"Dad shouted at the TV as if the commentator _____ personally attacked him.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"would have"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"should have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"as if 从句所说的“主持人亲口攻击他”是与过去事实相反、且先于 shouted 的假设，用过去完成时 had attacked。\n句意：爸爸冲着电视大喊，好像解说员刚才亲口攻击了他似的。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 与过去事实相反（had done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-d2e55c9dc1480c04"},{"stem":"Do you know what time the bank opens on weekends? _____. It's closed on Sundays.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It opens all day long."},{"key":"B","text":"It opens at nine on Saturdays."},{"key":"C","text":"I always go there on foot."},{"key":"D","text":"Money makes the world go round."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"提问银行周末营业时间，回答应给出周六的具体开门时间，且与“周日休息”衔接。A 与周日休息矛盾。","point":"询问时间——银行营业安排。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-3ba7e60243661e81"},{"stem":"Do you think it's going to rain this afternoon? _____. The sky is getting really dark.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm afraid so."},{"key":"B","text":"I hope not, but I don't care."},{"key":"C","text":"Yes, I like rain."},{"key":"D","text":"No, it never rains here."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"天色越来越黑，说明可能下雨；I'm afraid so 表示“恐怕会”，与观察一致。","point":"询问天气——判断趋势。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-39e3d7ada66946f3"},{"stem":"英译：The new regulations will come into force starting next month across all provinces.","options":[],"answer":"新法规将于下个月起在所有省份开始生效。","explanation":"come into force 译为“生效”；starting next month 译为“从下个月起”；across all provinces 译为“在所有省份”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-399ad6b838793de7"},{"stem":"She _____ the job offer from the company in Shanghai, for she preferred to stay with her family.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"turned up"},{"key":"B","text":"turned down"},{"key":"C","text":"turned over"},{"key":"D","text":"turned out"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"turn down 意为“拒绝（邀请、工作等）”；turn up“出现、调大”；turn over“翻转、移交”；turn out“结果是、生产”。句意：她拒绝了上海那家公司的工作机会，因为她更愿意和家人待在一起。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-8b04366e294882d3"},{"stem":"英译：The startup managed to break into the highly competitive Asian market within two years.","options":[],"answer":"这家创业公司成功打入竞争激烈的亚洲市场，只用了两年时间。","explanation":"break into 译为“打入或进入”；highly competitive 译为“竞争激烈的”；within two years 译为“两年之内”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-2e2b478f5cbcf522"},{"stem":"Could you tell me when the big summer sale starts? _____. Everything will be thirty percent off.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's over already."},{"key":"B","text":"It starts next Monday."},{"key":"C","text":"I don't need to buy anything."},{"key":"D","text":"The weather is too hot."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"顾客询问夏季大促开始时间，应直接给出日期。It starts next Monday 与后文“全场七折”顺接。","point":"咨询服务——活动促销。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-7660fb3fdae133ad"},{"stem":"He rolled his eyes as if the whole meeting _____ beneath him.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been"},{"key":"B","text":"is"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"would be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"as if 后 be 动词表示与当时事实相反的假设，用 were。句意：他翻着白眼，仿佛整场会议都不值得他一提。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在事实相反（be 用 were）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-447fcbcbf2a80d1e"},{"stem":"The hall decorations looked so festive, as if a grand wedding _____ to take place here.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were about"},{"key":"B","text":"had been about"},{"key":"C","text":"is about"},{"key":"D","text":"would be about"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"looked 是过去式；as if + were about to do 表示“仿佛即将要发生”，是对当时或将来的相反假设。句意：大厅装饰得很喜庆，仿佛一场盛大婚礼马上就要在此举办。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 对现在或将来即将发生虚拟（be about to）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":20,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十天.md"}],"id":"q-a9b7695a38ec92d3"},{"stem":"He gave me that sympathetic look, as though he _____ my predicament exactly.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"understood"},{"key":"B","text":"understands"},{"key":"C","text":"would understand"},{"key":"D","text":"had understood"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"as though 表达过去“完全理解”的相反假设，用 had understood。句意：他投以同情的眼神，仿佛完全理解我当时的处境。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-e62dd7688409bbad"},{"stem":"By the time you arrive home tonight, I _____ all the housework.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have finished"},{"key":"B","text":"had finished"},{"key":"C","text":"finish"},{"key":"D","text":"will have finished"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"by the time 引导的时间状语从句用一般现在时表示将来，主句用将来完成时 will have done，表示将来某时之前已完成。句意：等你今晚到家时，我将已经做完所有家务。","point":"将来完成时。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-f655c7f5226f6d34"},{"stem":"英译：The government has called on all citizens to participate in the nationwide environmental campaign.","options":[],"answer":"政府号召全体公民参与这场全国性的环境运动。","explanation":"call on 译为“号召”；participate in 译为“参与”；nationwide environmental campaign 译为“全国性的环境运动”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-33dd72215e1a61f8"},{"stem":"The school has _____ a new teaching method to help students learn English more easily.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adapted"},{"key":"B","text":"admitted"},{"key":"C","text":"adopted"},{"key":"D","text":"adjusted"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"adopt 意为“采纳、采用”；adapt“适应、改编”，admit“承认、准许进入”，adjust“调整”。句意：学校采用一种新的教学方法来帮助学生更轻松地学习英语。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-1eba4ce970141ac3"},{"stem":"Only after the manager explained the plan again _____ the requirements.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did the employees understand"},{"key":"B","text":"the employees understood"},{"key":"C","text":"the employees understand"},{"key":"D","text":"the employees did understand"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"“only + 状语”置于句首时，主句要部分倒装，将助动词 did 提前。句意：经理又把方案解释了一遍之后，员工们才明白这些要求。","point":"倒装句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-aabe9cf1e1744b58"},{"stem":"Do you mind if I leave the office a little earlier today? I have a dentist appointment. _____. Just make sure your report is finished.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I do mind."},{"key":"B","text":"Of course not."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm afraid so."},{"key":"D","text":"That's right."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Do you mind if...? 询问是否介意；Of course not 表示不介意，与后句“只要完成报告”相符。Yes, I do mind 表示介意；I'm afraid so 通常用于答非所问；That's right 用于肯定陈述。","point":"征得许可——提前离岗。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-e202ed62cc8cb32d"},{"stem":"After the match, the captain talked as though the team _____ the championship already.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"won"},{"key":"B","text":"had won"},{"key":"C","text":"wins"},{"key":"D","text":"would win"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"as though 后描述“仿佛已经夺冠”，与事实相反（实际未夺冠），用 had won 表达过去虚拟。句意：比赛结束后，队长说话仿佛球队已经赢得了冠军。","point":"虚拟语气——as though 对过去事实虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-39a4ec1062de4877"},{"stem":"Excuse me, could you tell me how to get to the City Library? _____. You can't miss it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, I can't."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm too busy."},{"key":"C","text":"Go straight and turn left at the second crossing."},{"key":"D","text":"I have no idea about it."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"向陌生人问路，应给出具体路线；后句 You can't miss it 是加强指向。其余选项没有提供路线且与后文不合。","point":"求助——问路。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-2db68b0e3ed01d96"},{"stem":"It is absolutely essential that the temperature in the greenhouse _____ at fifteen degrees overnight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be maintained"},{"key":"B","text":"is maintained"},{"key":"C","text":"was maintained"},{"key":"D","text":"will be maintained"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is essential that... 引导的主语从句用虚拟结构 (should) + 动词原形；temperature 与 maintain 为被动关系，故用 (should) be maintained。句意：温室内夜间务必维持在 15 度。","point":"虚拟语气——It is essential that 主语从句 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-10a67fe4bcadcc17"},{"stem":"中译：她既不喜欢苹果，也不喜欢梨。","options":[],"answer":"She likes neither apples nor pears.","explanation":"neither...nor... 表示“既不……也不……”，连接主语时谓语与最近主语保持一致；本句主语是 She，谓语用 likes。","point":"neither...nor... 并列连词。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-a768faad6f273fe4"},{"stem":"中译：这部电影值得一看。","options":[],"answer":"The film is well worth watching.","explanation":"be worth + doing 主动形式表被动意义；well 加强 worth 程度；watching 是 watch 的 -ing 形式。","point":"be worth doing。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-b50c27d17d5388a9"},{"stem":"The principal demanded that the truant students _____ for the misconduct immediately.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"apologize"},{"key":"B","text":"apologizes"},{"key":"C","text":"apologized"},{"key":"D","text":"would apologize"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"demand 后宾语从句需虚拟 (should) + 动词原形，should 可省略。句意：校长要求那些旷课的学生立即为不当行为道歉。","point":"虚拟语气——demand 表要求 (should) do 虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-6a59eee58fce1945"},{"stem":"The committee suggested that the budget _____ before the fiscal year ends.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is revised"},{"key":"B","text":"was revised"},{"key":"C","text":"has been revised"},{"key":"D","text":"be revised"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"suggest 表示“建议”，其宾语从句用虚拟 (should) + 动词原形；budget 与 revise 是被动关系，故用 (should) be revised。","point":"虚拟语气——suggest 后宾语从句 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-9a43aad91b55d6a4"},{"stem":"It is important for a company to _____ good relations with its customers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"contain"},{"key":"B","text":"attain"},{"key":"C","text":"retain"},{"key":"D","text":"maintain"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"maintain 意为“维持、保持”，maintain relations with 是常用搭配；contain“包含”，attain“达到”，retain“保留”。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-34fa03cc60bcb991"},{"stem":"It was not until midnight _____ the scientists finished the experiment.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"then"},{"key":"D","text":"which"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"not...until 的强调结构为 It was not until... that...，意为“直到……才……”。句意：直到午夜，科学家们才完成这项实验。","point":"强调句型。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["强调句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-7655ee59aef5cb58"},{"stem":"Excuse me, is this seat taken? _____. I was just leaving.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, it isn't. Take a seat."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, it's very comfortable."},{"key":"C","text":"Sorry, I don't sit here."},{"key":"D","text":"This is my first time here."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方礼貌询问座位是否有人，空着应答应并请其就座；后句“我正好要走了”支持这一回答。Yes 类回答与后文矛盾。","point":"礼貌询问——座位确认。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-9f40e74e28b91b6c"},{"stem":"Would you mind giving me a hand with this heavy box? _____. Where should I put it?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, I mind a lot."},{"key":"C","text":"That's too bad."},{"key":"D","text":"I don't think so."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"Would you mind...? 问是否介意，应答“不介意”；Not at all 表“一点也不介意”，后句询问摆放位置进一步证明愿意帮忙。","point":"请求帮助——搬重物。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-89555003404923f2"},{"stem":"My proposal is that the marketing department _____ a new logo design by next month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"presents"},{"key":"B","text":"presented"},{"key":"C","text":"would present"},{"key":"D","text":"present"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"由 proposal 等表示建议的名词引导的表语从句需用虚拟 (should) + 动词原形。句意：我的建议是市场部在下月前提交一份新标志设计。","point":"虚拟语气——系动词 + that 表语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-975c4947873291f7"},{"stem":"The hotel _____ we stayed during the holiday is near the seaside.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"in that"},{"key":"C","text":"in which"},{"key":"D","text":"on which"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"先行词 the hotel 在从句中作 stay in 的地点状语，将介词 in 提前，用“介词 + which”引导定语从句；that 不能直接位于介词之后。","point":"定语从句。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-255baeabd380c40a"},{"stem":"英译：After months of negotiation, the two firms finally arrived at a mutually beneficial agreement.","options":[],"answer":"经过数月谈判，两家公司最终达成了一项互惠协议。","explanation":"arrive at 译为“达成或得出”；negotiation 译为“谈判”；mutually beneficial 译为“互惠的或互利的”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-e7f98ba472d30a65"},{"stem":"May I borrow your pen for a moment? Mine has run out of ink. _____. Here you are.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm afraid you can't."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"Sure, no problem."},{"key":"D","text":"You are welcome."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方借用钢笔，应答应并递上；Sure, no problem 表示能够应允，与 Here you are 连贯。Never mind 用于安慰；You are welcome 用于回应感谢。","point":"请求——借用物品。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-3de4f1c56d0936d4"},{"stem":"中译：这个问题值得讨论。","options":[],"answer":"This question is worth discussing.","explanation":"be worth doing 后只接 -ing 形式，不接 to do 或 being done；discuss 表示“讨论”。","point":"be worth doing。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-045dbf20c4f62f35"},{"stem":"She is busy _____ the report and cannot attend the meeting this afternoon.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"preparing"},{"key":"B","text":"to prepare"},{"key":"C","text":"prepare"},{"key":"D","text":"prepared"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"be busy (in) doing sth. 意为“忙于做某事”，介词后接动名词。句意：她正忙着准备报告，今天下午无法参加会议。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-6e068d642c96849b"},{"stem":"Excuse me, how often does the No. 5 bus run? _____. It runs less often after nine in the evening.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Every ten minutes during the day."},{"key":"B","text":"It runs very fast."},{"key":"C","text":"It's always crowded."},{"key":"D","text":"Five buses have passed."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"how often 问公交发车间隔，应回答频率；Every ten minutes during the day 说明白天的间隔，后句说明晚间班次减少，与之衔接。","point":"询问信息——公交发车频率。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-4f3994d31a175312"},{"stem":"It is imperative that every student _____ a helmet when riding in the school grounds.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"wears"},{"key":"B","text":"wear"},{"key":"C","text":"should wore"},{"key":"D","text":"wore"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is imperative that... 用虚拟语气，从句用 (should) + 动词原形 wear；should 可省略，wears/wore 不符合。","point":"虚拟语气——It is imperative that 句型 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-7bd5a7a2a50bf067"},{"stem":"It suddenly _____ to me that I had left the key to the office in the taxi.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"happened"},{"key":"B","text":"occurred"},{"key":"C","text":"reached"},{"key":"D","text":"took place"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"occur to sb. 为固定搭配，意为“（想法等）浮现于某人脑海”；happen 表“发生”，不与 to sb. 表此意。句意：我突然想起把办公室钥匙落在出租车上了。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-fd947c5be046326f"},{"stem":"The manager, as well as the workers, _____ praised for finishing the project ahead of time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was"},{"key":"B","text":"were"},{"key":"C","text":"have"},{"key":"D","text":"are"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主语后接 as well as 时，谓语与前面的主语 the manager 保持一致，用单数；动作已完成，用一般过去时。","point":"主谓一致。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-664027b0c996ece0"},{"stem":"The doctor insisted that the patient _____ a thorough examination before resuming exercise.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"undergoes"},{"key":"B","text":"underwent"},{"key":"C","text":"would undergo"},{"key":"D","text":"undergo"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"insist 表“坚决要求”时，其宾语从句用虚拟 (should) + 动词原形。句意：医生坚持要求病人在恢复锻炼前做彻底检查。","point":"虚拟语气——insist 表要求后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-fede6f829c8c93da"},{"stem":"The new machine is more _____ than the old one, for it can do the same job in half the time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"effective"},{"key":"B","text":"sufficient"},{"key":"C","text":"significant"},{"key":"D","text":"efficient"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"efficient 指“效率高的、省时省力的”；effective“有效的”，sufficient“充足的”，significant“重大的”。新机器用旧机器一半时间完成相同工作，强调效率。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-6676e82c7042bbc9"},{"stem":"英译：She eventually gave in to public pressure and issued a formal apology on national television.","options":[],"answer":"她最终屈服于公众压力，在国家电视台上发表了正式道歉。","explanation":"give in to 译为“屈服于或向……让步”；public pressure 译为“公众压力”；formal apology 译为“正式道歉”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":21,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md"}],"id":"q-ac91596cb68fc8e1"},{"stem":"I'm sorry, could you explain that point again? I didn't quite catch it. _____. Let me go through it more slowly.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course."},{"key":"B","text":"I can't agree more."},{"key":"C","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"D","text":"Never mind."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"学生没听懂请求重讲，老师应答应；Of course 直接应允，后句说明放慢速度再讲一遍。","point":"求助——请求重讲。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-cc6076643bd4e9cf"},{"stem":"It is necessary that the new policy _____ to all employees before implementation.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is communicated"},{"key":"B","text":"be communicated"},{"key":"C","text":"communicates"},{"key":"D","text":"communicated"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is necessary that 后的主语从句用虚拟，政策与 communicate 为被动关系，故用 (should) be communicated。句意：新政策在实施前必须传达给所有员工。","point":"虚拟语气——It is necessary that 句型 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-206a072efdbe58f3"},{"stem":"We are all in favor of his recommendation that the meeting _____ until next Monday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is postponed"},{"key":"B","text":"be postponed"},{"key":"C","text":"was postponed"},{"key":"D","text":"should postponed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"recommendation 后的同位语从句用 (should) + 动词原形；meeting 与 postpone 为被动关系，故用 (should) be postponed。句意：我们赞同把会议推迟至下周一的建议。","point":"虚拟语气——recommendation 后同位语从句 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-4f93def5009cd2a0"},{"stem":"The flood _____ the heavy rain in the mountain area.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"resulted in"},{"key":"B","text":"was resulted in"},{"key":"C","text":"resulted from"},{"key":"D","text":"was resulted from"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"result from 表示“起因于”（主语是结果，宾语是原因）；result in 表示“导致”（主语是原因）；result 无被动语态。句意：这场洪水是由山区的暴雨造成的。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-efae31ab50884d45"},{"stem":"Excuse me, could we have the menu, please? _____. Here are today's specials as well.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"B","text":"Certainly, sir."},{"key":"C","text":"Of course not."},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"顾客索要菜单，服务员应热情应允并递上；Certainly, sir 符合服务场景，后句还介绍今日特色菜。","point":"请求服务——索取菜单。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-0378815efb2145c0"},{"stem":"The volunteer work gave me a good _____ to practise my spoken English with foreigners.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"opportunity"},{"key":"B","text":"possibility"},{"key":"C","text":"ability"},{"key":"D","text":"personality"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"opportunity 意为“机会”，opportunity to do sth. 为常用搭配；possibility“可能性”，ability“能力”，personality“个性”。句意：志愿工作给了我与外国人练习英语口语的好机会。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-a479beadff898771"},{"stem":"Don't stand _____. Move aside and let the old man pass.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on the way"},{"key":"B","text":"by the way"},{"key":"C","text":"in a way"},{"key":"D","text":"in the way"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"in the way 意为“挡路、妨碍”；on the way“在路上”，by the way“顺便说一下”，in a way“在某种程度上”。句意：别挡着路。让到一边，让那位老人过去。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-2f058234407dfa75"},{"stem":"A good teacher should be _____ to the needs of his students.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sensitive"},{"key":"B","text":"sensible"},{"key":"C","text":"flexible"},{"key":"D","text":"visible"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"be sensitive to 意为“对……敏感，能体察”；sensible“明智的”，flexible“灵活的”，visible“可见的”。句意：一位好老师应当能体察学生的需求。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-0c9fed73f4f0ed8e"},{"stem":"It is high time that we _____ immediate action to tackle the pollution problem.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"have taken"},{"key":"D","text":"will take"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is (high) time that... 为固定虚拟句型，从句用一般过去时形式 took；这里表达现在该采取行动。句意：我们早该立即采取行动解决污染问题了。","point":"虚拟语气——It is (high) time that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-e3c96d73416f8482"},{"stem":"It is crucial that each candidate _____ a 500-word essay as part of the application.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"submit"},{"key":"B","text":"submits"},{"key":"C","text":"submitted"},{"key":"D","text":"would submit"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is crucial that... 的主语从句用虚拟 (should) + 动词原形；单数形式 submits 和虚拟被动均不符合。句意：每位候选人务必提交一篇 500 字申请短文。","point":"虚拟语气——It is crucial that 主语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-8e0d0ee7ee346d95"},{"stem":"中译：他已习惯于每天早起。","options":[],"answer":"He has got used to getting up early every day.","explanation":"get used to + doing 表“习惯于做某事”；to 是介词，后接 -ing 形式；get up 表“起床”。我的作答表达已形成的习惯，页面参考句突出“已经习惯”的过程。","point":"get used to 短语。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-d4f60b0e718d3fcd"},{"stem":"The classroom _____ since last Friday, so it is clean and tidy now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been cleaned"},{"key":"B","text":"was cleaned"},{"key":"C","text":"is cleaned"},{"key":"D","text":"has been cleaned"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"since last Friday 与现在完成时连用；classroom 与 clean 是被动关系，故用 has been cleaned。句意：教室自上星期五以来已打扫过，所以现在干净整洁。","point":"现在完成时（被动语态）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-b010b453ded7e8b8"},{"stem":"中译：他太累了，走不动了。","options":[],"answer":"He is too tired to walk any further.","explanation":"too + adj + to do 表“太……而不能……”；walk any further 表“再往前走”，更准确体现“走不动了”，注意 any 的用法。","point":"too...to...。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-2f899542e57ee299"},{"stem":"The officer ordered that the soldiers _____ the village before dawn.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"left"},{"key":"B","text":"leaving"},{"key":"C","text":"leave"},{"key":"D","text":"would leave"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"order 等表示命令、建议的动词后接宾语从句时，从句谓语用 (should) + 动词原形。句意：军官命令士兵们在黎明前离开村庄。","point":"虚拟语气。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-2410f884c9a8a6b6"},{"stem":"It's about time you _____ paying attention to your diet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"start"},{"key":"B","text":"started"},{"key":"C","text":"have started"},{"key":"D","text":"are starting"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It's about time that... 要求从句用一般过去时 started 表达虚拟；start 为现在时形式，不符合。句意：你早该注意你的饮食了。","point":"虚拟语气——It's about time that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-71029cfd461b351d"},{"stem":"Only a small number of students were given the _____ of using the school's new gym for free.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"profession"},{"key":"B","text":"privilege"},{"key":"C","text":"possession"},{"key":"D","text":"percentage"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"privilege 意为“特权、特殊待遇”；profession“职业”，possession“财产、拥有”，percentage“百分比”。句意：只有少数学生获得了免费使用学校新体育馆的特权。","point":"名词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-7757ed711afb3a9b"},{"stem":"Could you turn the music down a bit? I'm trying to study. _____. Sorry for the noise.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I can."},{"key":"B","text":"No problem."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm not sure."},{"key":"D","text":"Thank you."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方请求调低音量，No problem 爽快应允，后句致歉自然衔接；Yes, I can 虽回应能力，却没有同样自然地回应请求。","point":"请求——降低音量。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-0e59672fa664ad9a"},{"stem":"If she _____ the early bus yesterday, she would have been here on time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had caught"},{"key":"B","text":"caught"},{"key":"C","text":"should catch"},{"key":"D","text":"has caught"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"从句与过去事实相反，谓语用过去完成时 had done；主句为 would have done。句意：如果她昨天赶上了早班车，她本来会准时到这里。","point":"虚拟语气（与过去事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-c78fdf6baf771e2e"},{"stem":"The governor ordered that the contaminated water _____ from the residential area within 24 hours.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"drained"},{"key":"B","text":"is drained"},{"key":"C","text":"would drain"},{"key":"D","text":"be drained"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"order 表命令，that 从句用虚拟 (should) + 动词原形；water 与 drain 是被动关系，故用 (should) be drained。句意：州长下令污染水体必须在 24 小时内从居民区排出。","point":"虚拟语气——order 后宾语从句 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-0583b0e7137024d9"},{"stem":"The fire _____ at midnight while most people in the building were sleeping.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"broke out"},{"key":"B","text":"broke down"},{"key":"C","text":"carried out"},{"key":"D","text":"went through"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"break out 指火灾、战争等“突然爆发”，无被动语态；break down“出故障、崩溃”，carry out“执行”，go through“经历”。句意：大火是在午夜爆发的，当时楼里大多数人正在睡觉。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-f43504764ea017b1"},{"stem":"Let's clean the classroom before the visitors come, _____?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will you"},{"key":"B","text":"won't we"},{"key":"C","text":"don't we"},{"key":"D","text":"shall we"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"以 Let's 开头的祈使句，反意疑问句用 shall we；以 Let us 开头则用 will you。句意：趁参观者到来之前，我们把教室打扫一下吧，好吗？","point":"反意疑问句（祈使句）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-e06295eaff2982f7"},{"stem":"May I open the window? It's a bit stuffy in here. _____. Fresh air will do us good.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, you may not."},{"key":"B","text":"I don't care."},{"key":"C","text":"Thanks a lot."},{"key":"D","text":"Go ahead."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"May I...? 用于征求许可，应允可用 Go ahead（请便）；后句说新鲜空气有益，与允许开窗一致。","point":"征得许可——开窗透气。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-bfc1c371cdd3f80f"},{"stem":"The ordinance requires that all retailers _____ the electronic price tags by the end of the year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adopt"},{"key":"B","text":"adopts"},{"key":"C","text":"adopted"},{"key":"D","text":"would adopt"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"require 后的 that 从句用虚拟语气，谓语为“(should +) 动词原形”；adopts 是第三人称单数形式，不符合此结构。句意：规定要求所有零售商年底前采用电子价签。","point":"虚拟语气——require 后宾语从句用 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-3c5a5aa705b2ec4c"},{"stem":"The tenant's demand that the rent _____ before the fifth of every month is reasonable.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is paid"},{"key":"B","text":"was paid"},{"key":"C","text":"has been paid"},{"key":"D","text":"be paid"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"demand 后的同位语从句谓语用“(should +) 动词原形”；rent 与 pay 构成被动关系，因此用 be paid。句意：房客要求每月五日前付清房租是合理的。","point":"虚拟语气——名词后的同位语从句用 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-b062c1aaaec9a804"},{"stem":"Could I use your phone charger for a while? Mine was left at home. _____. My phone is fully charged.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, you can't."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm afraid not."},{"key":"C","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"D","text":"Sure, help yourself."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"借用充电器时，后句说自己的手机已充满电，说明愿意借出；“Sure, help yourself”表示“当然，请自便”。其他选项为拒绝或惋惜，与语境不符。","point":"请求——借用充电器。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-0d2c51be43f584da"},{"stem":"中译：我期待着下个月再见到你。","options":[],"answer":"I am looking forward to seeing you again next month.","explanation":"look forward to doing 表示“期待做某事”；to 是介词，后接动词 -ing；next month 表示“下个月”。参考答案用 again 明确表达“再”。","point":"look forward to 短语。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-73156bdfc182e7a3"},{"stem":"英译：The doctor told him to stay away from fatty foods and to cut down on sugary drinks.","options":[],"answer":"医生嘱咐他远离高脂肪食物，并减少含糖饮料的摄入。","explanation":"stay away from 表示“远离”；cut down on 表示“减少或削减”；fatty foods 表示“高脂肪食物”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-83594ca6812620f9"},{"stem":"英译：The team is determined to carry on the mission despite enormous difficulties and risks.","options":[],"answer":"团队决心继续执行这项任务，尽管面临巨大困难与风险。","explanation":"carry on 表示“继续进行或执行”；mission 表示“任务”；despite enormous difficulties 表示“尽管有巨大困难”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-8a05d322f83c46a9"},{"stem":"英译：We must figure out how to put these ideas into practice within the limited timeframe.","options":[],"answer":"我们必须想办法把这些想法在有限的期限内付诸实践。","explanation":"figure out 表示“想出或弄明白”；put ... into practice 表示“付诸实践”；limited timeframe 表示“有限的期限”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-ee16d5c27db33e9d"},{"stem":"Would it be possible for me to take a day off next Monday? _____. Make sure you hand in the report before you leave.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I suppose so."},{"key":"B","text":"You mustn't."},{"key":"C","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"D","text":"It's none of my business."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"向领导请假，对方随后叮嘱离开前交报告，说明原则上同意。“I suppose so”表示“我想可以”，语气审慎，符合语境。","point":"请求——请假。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":22,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md"}],"id":"q-428aa25ca7dc37e2"},{"stem":"While we're away on holiday, could you water the plants for us? _____. I'll come over every couple of days.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's a shame."},{"key":"B","text":"No problem."},{"key":"C","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"D","text":"You're welcome."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"请邻居代为照料花草，对方应答应并说明频次，让对方放心。“No problem”表示“没问题”；其余选项分别表示惋惜、不介意、回应感谢，均不切题。","point":"请求——邻里互助。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-fc015c28fb13789a"},{"stem":"中译：他太年轻，不能理解这样的复杂情况。","options":[],"answer":"He is too young to understand such a complicated situation.","explanation":"too + 形容词 + to do 表示“太……而不能……”；such + a + 形容词 + 单数可数名词表示“这样的……”；understand 表示“理解”。","point":"too...to...。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-731b52ddc2e97439"},{"stem":"It is vital that any unauthorised personnel _____ the control room without clearance.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"not enter"},{"key":"B","text":"doesn't enter"},{"key":"C","text":"didn't enter"},{"key":"D","text":"won't enter"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is vital that 后的主语从句用虚拟语气，谓语为“(should +) 动词原形”；否定形式为 (should) not enter。句意：未经授权的人员不得进入控制室。","point":"虚拟语气——It is vital that 否定结构 (should) not do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-ca555ce02cc09c12"},{"stem":"It is advisable that applicants _____ their forms one week before the deadline.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"submits"},{"key":"B","text":"submitted"},{"key":"C","text":"submit"},{"key":"D","text":"should submitted"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It is advisable that 引导的主语从句用虚拟语气，谓语为“(should +) 动词原形”；其他形式不符合。句意：建议申请人在截止时间前一周提交表格。","point":"虚拟语气——It is advisable that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-c01dc66e7b5f6311"},{"stem":"The board deemed it urgent that the financial report _____ to the shareholders without delay.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is submitted"},{"key":"B","text":"should submit"},{"key":"C","text":"be submitted"},{"key":"D","text":"submit"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"deem it urgent that 中 it 为形式宾语，真正宾语是 that 从句；从句谓语用虚拟语气“(should +) 动词原形”。report 与 submit 构成被动关系，故用 be submitted。句意：董事会认为应立即向股东提交财务报告。","point":"虚拟语气——deem it urgent that 句型中的 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-6b21e19e3de80eea"},{"stem":"Could you say that again? _____. Sure. I said the meeting has been moved to Friday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I agree."},{"key":"B","text":"It's my turn."},{"key":"C","text":"Good idea."},{"key":"D","text":"The connection is not very good."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"电话中没听清，请求重复时解释信号不好，能让对方理解为何没听清并重述信息；其他选项与要求重复的语境无关。","point":"请求——通话中要求重复。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-5d56ff4906126a57"},{"stem":"We are all looking forward to _____ you again at the graduation party.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"see"},{"key":"B","text":"seeing"},{"key":"C","text":"have seen"},{"key":"D","text":"saw"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"look forward to 中的 to 是介词，后接名词或动名词，即 look forward to doing sth.。句意：我们都盼望在毕业晚会上再次见到你。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-d501e254c0921248"},{"stem":"英译：The mayor took the opportunity to reach out to the local business community last Friday.","options":[],"answer":"市长上周五借机与当地商界进行了接触与交流。","explanation":"take the opportunity to 表示“借机做”；reach out to 表示“接触或联系”；business community 表示“商界”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-30085ac9f649ad0b"},{"stem":"Could you possibly give me a ride to the airport tomorrow morning? _____. What time do you need to be there?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"B","text":"I'd be glad to."},{"key":"C","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm afraid I do."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"请朋友开车送机场，后句询问具体时间以便安排，说明答应帮忙。“I'd be glad to”表示“我很乐意”；其余选项不符合请求搭车的语境。","point":"请求——搭车。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a9426dbf923b6787"},{"stem":"The heavy rain _____ the whole crop of the farmers last autumn.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"destroyed"},{"key":"B","text":"damaged"},{"key":"C","text":"harmed"},{"key":"D","text":"wounded"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"destroy 指“彻底摧毁”；damage 指“部分损坏”；harm 多指身心、健康受损；wound 指刀枪等造成的受伤。这里说暴雨毁掉全部庄稼，选 destroyed。","point":"动词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-95fe24ac2198128d"},{"stem":"While tidying the drawer, I _____ some photos taken in my childhood.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"came up with"},{"key":"B","text":"came about"},{"key":"C","text":"came across"},{"key":"D","text":"came up to"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"come across 表示“偶然遇到、无意中发现”；come up with 表示“想出”；come about 表示“发生”；come up to 表示“达到”。句意：整理抽屉时，我无意中发现了一些童年照片。","point":"动词短语辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-e1da3b60618cf608"},{"stem":"中译：天太冷了，我们不能出去游泳。","options":[],"answer":"It is too cold for us to go swimming.","explanation":"It is too + 形容词 + for sb + to do；go swimming 表示“去游泳”；go + V-ing 表示运动。","point":"too...to...。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-302f9de2c0e2700a"},{"stem":"I'm really sorry I'm late. The traffic was terrible. _____. We haven't started yet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, thanks."},{"key":"B","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"C","text":"Of course not."},{"key":"D","text":"With pleasure."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方为迟到致歉，应宽慰使其安心。“That's all right”表示“没关系”，后句“我们还没开始”进一步消除顾虑；其他选项不适合回应道歉。","point":"道歉——迟到谅解。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-5c0d81a62a8eff7a"},{"stem":"_____ our great surprise, the little girl could recite the whole poem without any mistake.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In"},{"key":"B","text":"For"},{"key":"C","text":"At"},{"key":"D","text":"To"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"to one's surprise 为固定搭配，意为“令某人惊讶的是”。句意：令我们大为惊讶的是，那个小女孩竟能一字不差地背出整首诗。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-6f60f072966adabb"},{"stem":"Oh, I'm so sorry. I stepped on your foot. _____. It happens all the time on a crowded bus.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"C","text":"It's nothing."},{"key":"D","text":"I think so."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"无心踩脚后道歉，对方应表示不介意。“It's nothing”表示“没什么”，后句以公交车拥挤解释，宽容得体；其他选项不适合回应道歉。","point":"道歉——无意冒犯。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-824ce9fb3de21a38"},{"stem":"Weather _____, the sports meeting will be held as planned next Monday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"permitted"},{"key":"B","text":"permitting"},{"key":"C","text":"to permit"},{"key":"D","text":"permits"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"weather permitting 是独立主格结构“名词 + 现在分词”，作条件状语，相当于 if weather permits。句意：如果天气允许，运动会将按计划于下周一举行。","point":"独立主格。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a0854ab76b94bdf0"},{"stem":"The minister recommended that the proposed tax _____ entirely.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is abolished"},{"key":"B","text":"was abolished"},{"key":"C","text":"should abolish"},{"key":"D","text":"be abolished"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"recommend 后的 that 从句用虚拟语气，谓语为“(should +) 动词原形”；tax 与 abolish 构成被动关系，所以用 (should) be abolished。句意：部长建议废除该拟议税款的全部内容。","point":"虚拟语气——recommend 后宾语从句用 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-f5ffc00e7c600ae5"},{"stem":"The ground is still wet. It _____ last night.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"must rain"},{"key":"B","text":"must have rained"},{"key":"C","text":"should have rained"},{"key":"D","text":"can have rained"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"must have done 表示对过去已发生事情的肯定推测，即“一定做过”；should have done 表示“本应做而未做”；can 表推测通常用于否定或疑问句。句意：地面还是湿的，昨晚一定下过雨。","point":"情态动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-8a815ca902652719"},{"stem":"The fire safety code requires that every exit _____ clearly marked in green.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be"},{"key":"B","text":"be marked"},{"key":"C","text":"is"},{"key":"D","text":"should be mark"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"页面解析称 require 后的 that 从句用虚拟语气“(should) be done”，出口与标记构成被动关系。但页面题干在空格后已有 clearly marked，填 A 构成合语法的“every exit be clearly marked”；填 B 则成为“every exit be marked clearly marked”，重复且不合语法。这里很可能是题干或参考答案排版错误，复习时应按“require that every exit (should) be clearly marked”理解。","point":"虚拟语气——require 后同位语从句用 (should) be done（页面所列考点）；同时留意题干排版错误。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-eaea142d0a29688a"},{"stem":"Tired _____ he was, he went on working until midnight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"although"},{"key":"B","text":"so"},{"key":"C","text":"as"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"“表语 + as + 主语 + be”构成让步状语从句，相当于 Although he was tired；although 引导的从句不能这样倒装。句意：尽管他很累，仍一直工作到午夜。","point":"让步状语从句（倒装）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句","倒装句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-e1af4cd9b511e9d1"},{"stem":"The CEO's preference that the merger _____ publicly drew criticism from minority shareholders.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be not announced"},{"key":"B","text":"not to announce"},{"key":"C","text":"not be announced"},{"key":"D","text":"shouldn't announce"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"preference 表示“倾向、主张”，其后同位语从句用“(should +) 动词原形”；否定形式在动词原形前加 not。merger 与 announce 构成被动关系，因此用 not be announced。句意：CEO 主张不对外宣布合并事宜，此举引来小股东批评。","point":"虚拟语气——preference 后同位语从句用 (should) not do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-c646ca144ed834db"},{"stem":"Do you think you could work my shift on Saturday? I have a family event. _____. I don't have anything planned.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I can't agree more."},{"key":"B","text":"Never say that."},{"key":"C","text":"Sure, I can do that."},{"key":"D","text":"Forget it."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"请同事代班，对方有空时应爽快答应。“Sure, I can do that”直接应承，后句说明自己无安排；其他选项不适合回应请求。","point":"请求——同事换班。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-beb8535613a7767c"},{"stem":"He gained much valuable experience from his _____ job in the foreign company.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"precious"},{"key":"B","text":"previous"},{"key":"C","text":"curious"},{"key":"D","text":"serious"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"previous 意为“先前的、以往的”；precious 意为“珍贵的”；curious 意为“好奇的”；serious 意为“严肃的、严重的”。句意：他在那家外企的上一份工作中积累了宝贵经验。","point":"形容词辨析。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-5b12c79c61934eac"},{"stem":"英译：Her proposal ran into strong opposition from the conservative wing of the committee.","options":[],"answer":"她的提案遭到了委员会保守派的强烈反对。","explanation":"run into 表示“遭遇或碰上”；opposition 表示“反对”；conservative wing 表示“保守派”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-b4e98b5e2023b6f2"},{"stem":"The lawyer's advice that the defendant _____ the witness before testifying is highly questionable.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"not interrogates"},{"key":"B","text":"not interrogate"},{"key":"C","text":"did not interrogate"},{"key":"D","text":"doesn't interrogate"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"advice 后的同位语从句用虚拟语气“(should +) 动词原形”，否定形式为 (should) not interrogate；其他选项不符合此结构。句意：律师建议被告在作证前不要盘问证人，是极可疑的。","point":"虚拟语气——advice 后同位语从句用 (should) not do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-d6a00bb1353d92f9"},{"stem":"中译：这道题太难了，我做不出来。","options":[],"answer":"This question is too difficult for me to work out.","explanation":"too + 形容词 + for sb + to do 表示“对某人来说太……而不能……”；work out 表示“算出或解决”。我的 solve 与参考答案 work out 语义相近。","point":"too...to... (for sb)。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-53540fc84c46db55"},{"stem":"英译：Volunteers from all walks of life pitched in to help rescue the flood-stricken villagers.","options":[],"answer":"各行各业的志愿者纷纷出力，帮助营救遭受洪灾的村民。","explanation":"pitch in 表示“出力或纷纷帮忙”；all walks of life 表示“各行各业”；flood-stricken 表示“遭受洪灾的”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-a39cf5bcc85835c2"},{"stem":"Please remember _____ the windows when you leave the classroom.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"closing"},{"key":"B","text":"to close"},{"key":"C","text":"closed"},{"key":"D","text":"close"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"remember to do sth. 表示“记得去做某事”（尚未做）；remember doing sth. 表示“记得做过某事”。此处动作尚未发生，用不定式。句意：离开教室时请记得关窗。","point":"非谓语动词。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-9c72c1a996135819"},{"stem":"When the foreign students first arrived in China, they were not used to _____ with chopsticks.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"eat"},{"key":"B","text":"have eaten"},{"key":"C","text":"eating"},{"key":"D","text":"be eaten"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"be used to doing sth. 意为“习惯于做某事”，to 为介词，后接动名词；used to do 则表示“过去常常做”。句意：那些外国学生初到中国时，不习惯用筷子吃饭。","point":"固定搭配。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-beaa985795d24959"},{"stem":"The ambassador's order that the military attaché _____ diplomatic immunity caused controversy.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"enjoys"},{"key":"B","text":"enjoy"},{"key":"C","text":"enjoyed"},{"key":"D","text":"should enjoyed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"order 后的同位语从句用虚拟语气，谓语为“(should +) 动词原形”，即 enjoy；其余形式不符合。句意：大使关于武官享受外交豁免的命令引起争议。","point":"虚拟语气——order 后同位语从句用 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":23,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十三天.md"}],"id":"q-39f6aeb81dbca50a"},{"stem":"The coach blamed the failure of the game _____ the players' lack of teamwork.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"for"},{"key":"B","text":"to"},{"key":"C","text":"on"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"blame sth. on sb./sth. 意为“把某事归咎于……”。这里是把失利归咎于队员缺乏团队合作。","point":"动词辨析（blame sth. on）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-b970d9faa4447df1"},{"stem":"Just a reminder: the application deadline is this Friday. _____. I'll mail mine tonight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Thanks for the heads-up."},{"key":"B","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"C","text":"Same to you."},{"key":"D","text":"Forget it."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方提醒申请截止日期，应感谢提醒，再说自己今晚邮寄材料。Thanks for the heads-up 意为“谢谢提前告知”。","point":"提醒——截止日期。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-85c7daa503561f4d"},{"stem":"英译：She attributes her success to perseverance, careful planning, and a little bit of good luck.","options":[],"answer":"她把自己的成功归功于毅力、细致的规划，以及一点好运气。","explanation":"attribute...to 译为“将……归功于或归因于”；perseverance 译为“毅力或坚持”；a little bit of 译为“一点”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-c03ff61204bc0cc2"},{"stem":"中译：昨天晚上八点我在读英语。","options":[],"answer":"I was reading English at eight last night.","explanation":"at eight last night 表示过去某一时刻正在进行的动作，用过去进行时 was + V-ing。","point":"过去进行时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-0ac8c6b0ef799384"},{"stem":"中译：昨天晚上我读了一本很有趣的书。","options":[],"answer":"I read a very interesting book last night.","explanation":"last night 决定用一般过去时；read 的过去式与原形同形；interesting 意为“有趣的”。","point":"一般过去时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-76b0c138339568e1"},{"stem":"It is essential that the chairman _____ the meeting before any decision is finalised.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"presides over"},{"key":"B","text":"preside over"},{"key":"C","text":"presided over"},{"key":"D","text":"would preside over"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is essential that... 后的主语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形。preside over 意为“主持”。","point":"虚拟语气——It is essential that + 主语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-4ff9e5c1ed779edd"},{"stem":"Sorry I didn't answer your call last night. _____. I only wanted to tell you the good news.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"With pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"Good for you."},{"key":"C","text":"That's fine."},{"key":"D","text":"Help yourself."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方为未接电话道歉，应回答“没关系”；That's fine 符合语境。后句表示打电话只是想分享好消息。","point":"道歉——未接来电。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-aa1125b2fcabf1a6"},{"stem":"The union's demand that the workers _____ a 10% pay rise finally gained the management's attention.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"receives"},{"key":"B","text":"received"},{"key":"C","text":"should received"},{"key":"D","text":"receive"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"demand 后的同位语从句使用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形。should received 形式错误。","point":"虚拟语气——demand 后同位语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7b97dff376c56f12"},{"stem":"I'm terribly sorry, but I broke your favourite cup. _____. It was quite old anyway.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Forget it."},{"key":"B","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"C","text":"That's too bad."},{"key":"D","text":"I'm not surprised."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"打碎物品后道歉，对方宽慰说“算了吧”，后句“杯子本来就旧了”降低对方负罪感，故选 Forget it。","point":"道歉——物品损坏。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-1fdfdf2842b144b2"},{"stem":"Don't forget the staff meeting at three o'clock. _____. I have it on my calendar.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It's my pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"That's a pity."},{"key":"C","text":"Thanks for reminding me."},{"key":"D","text":"Not at all."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方善意提醒，应表示感谢；后句说“我已经记在日历上了”，故选 Thanks for reminding me。","point":"提醒——会议时间。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-adf5b0256fa9b514"},{"stem":"The legislator proposed that the bill _____ a second reading before being voted on.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"undergoes"},{"key":"B","text":"underwent"},{"key":"C","text":"undergo"},{"key":"D","text":"would undergo"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"propose 后宾语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形 undergo。","point":"虚拟语气——propose 后宾语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7bf25493dba4b06f"},{"stem":"The old song _____ me of the happy days we spent together at college.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recalls"},{"key":"B","text":"remembers"},{"key":"C","text":"refreshes"},{"key":"D","text":"reminds"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"固定搭配 remind sb. of sth.，意为“使某人想起某事”。recall 不用于 recall sb. of sth.。","point":"动词辨析（remind sb. of sth.）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7c4b157657672837"},{"stem":"The results of the experiment _____ us that the new drug is really effective against the disease.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"suggested"},{"key":"B","text":"informed"},{"key":"C","text":"reminded"},{"key":"D","text":"convinced"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"convince sb. that... 意为“使某人相信……”。实验结果令人信服，故选 convinced。","point":"动词辨析（convince sb. that）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-146cc4102d5a4fac"},{"stem":"It is time that the administration _____ stern measures to curb plastic waste.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take"},{"key":"B","text":"took"},{"key":"C","text":"takes"},{"key":"D","text":"has taken"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is time that... 为虚拟句型，从句用一般过去时表达现在应该采取的行动。","point":"虚拟语气——It is time that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-14f18a985c671651"},{"stem":"It's going to rain this afternoon. _____. Oh, thanks. I'll grab my umbrella on the way out.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't forget to take an umbrella with you."},{"key":"C","text":"What's the matter?"},{"key":"D","text":"You look tired."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"预测下午下雨，接着提醒对方带伞；后句回答“我出门时会带上伞”，与 B 呼应。","point":"提醒——天气变化。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-2eebe983b829b4b4"},{"stem":"I must apologize for forgetting our appointment yesterday. _____. We can meet again this week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm afraid not."},{"key":"B","text":"Never say that."},{"key":"C","text":"With great pleasure."},{"key":"D","text":"Don't worry about it."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方为忘记约定道歉，后句表示可再约时间，故应宽慰“别放在心上”。","point":"道歉——忘记约定。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-5f9e989890dca7bb"},{"stem":"In the fairy tale, the magician _____ the ugly duckling into a beautiful white swan.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"transferred"},{"key":"B","text":"transported"},{"key":"C","text":"transformed"},{"key":"D","text":"transplanted"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"transform A into B 意为“把 A 变成 B”；其余选项分别偏向转移、运输、移植。","point":"动词辨析（transform...into）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-feddf1d104b93405"},{"stem":"The professor's insistence that the lab report _____ verbatim was difficult to meet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is quoted"},{"key":"B","text":"should quote"},{"key":"C","text":"be quoted"},{"key":"D","text":"be quoting"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"insistence 后同位语从句用 (should) + 动词原形；lab report 与 quote 是被动关系，故用 (should) be quoted。","point":"虚拟语气——insistence 后同位语从句 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-ccf738b85c625be6"},{"stem":"中译：他上周买了一辆新自行车。","options":[],"answer":"He bought a new bike last week.","explanation":"last week 用一般过去时；buy 的过去式是 bought；a new 表示“一辆新的”。bicycle 与 bike 同义。","point":"一般过去时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-8ce3313c622e47a5"},{"stem":"I would greatly _____ it if you could spare a few minutes to help me with this problem.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"admit"},{"key":"B","text":"apply"},{"key":"C","text":"approach"},{"key":"D","text":"appreciate"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"固定句型 appreciate it if...，意为“如果……，我将非常感激”。","point":"动词辨析（appreciate it if）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-567bf064cfe13784"},{"stem":"It is appropriate that the auditor's findings _____ to the board on a quarterly basis.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are reported"},{"key":"B","text":"were reported"},{"key":"C","text":"be reported"},{"key":"D","text":"have been reported"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It is appropriate that... 从句用虚拟语气；findings 与 report 是被动关系，故用 (should) be reported。","point":"虚拟语气——It is appropriate that 句型 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-04e75429d907a8c0"},{"stem":"You _____ it to yourself to take a good rest after working so hard for months.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"owe"},{"key":"B","text":"own"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"pay"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"owe it to oneself to do sth. 意为“认为自己理应做某事／该为自己做某事”。","point":"动词辨析（owe it to oneself to do）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-53e6fb31b99dc708"},{"stem":"英译：Once the new system is in place, employees should adapt to the revised workflow gradually.","options":[],"answer":"新系统上线后，员工应逐步适应修订后的工作流程。","explanation":"be in place 意为“就位或上线”；adapt to 意为“适应”；revised workflow 意为“修订后的工作流程”。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-2a80e45806978652"},{"stem":"英译：The committee decided to set aside additional funding for the preservation of historic buildings.","options":[],"answer":"委员会决定为历史建筑的保护拨出额外资金。","explanation":"set aside 意为“拨出或留出”；additional funding 是额外资金；preservation 是保护。","point":"短语的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-cabd1db0e0bd75e9"},{"stem":"The factory manager arranged that the safety inspection _____ the upcoming holiday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"takes place during"},{"key":"B","text":"is taken place during"},{"key":"C","text":"take place during"},{"key":"D","text":"took place during"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"arrange 后 that 从句用虚拟语气 (should) + 动词原形；take place 无被动形式。","point":"虚拟语气——arrange 后 that 从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-02a44201e92ea900"},{"stem":"It's high time the children _____ off their electronic devices and played outdoors.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stay"},{"key":"B","text":"have stayed"},{"key":"C","text":"are staying"},{"key":"D","text":"stayed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It's high time that... 用一般过去时表达“早该做……”，并与后面的 played 并列。","point":"虚拟语气——It's high time that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-04d0d89019b21c15"},{"stem":"Many problems _____ from the poor management of the small factory, so the manager had to change his ways.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"raised"},{"key":"B","text":"rose"},{"key":"C","text":"arouse"},{"key":"D","text":"arose"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"arise from 意为“由……引起／产生”，过去式 arose；problems 为复数，句子用一般过去时。","point":"动词辨析（arise from）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-6cf6df321970c863"},{"stem":"The famous professor will _____ a lecture on Chinese traditional culture next Monday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"address"},{"key":"B","text":"deliver"},{"key":"C","text":"perform"},{"key":"D","text":"conduct"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"deliver a lecture 是固定搭配，意为“发表演讲／讲课”。","point":"动词辨析（deliver a lecture）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-29f2460f108acc14"},{"stem":"The outdoor concert was _____ because of the sudden thunderstorm.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"called on"},{"key":"B","text":"called off"},{"key":"C","text":"called for"},{"key":"D","text":"called up"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"call off 意为“取消”；露天音乐会因突然的雷暴而被取消。","point":"动词短语辨析（call off）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-4cb6bec7694fb3e9"},{"stem":"The continuous heavy rain has seriously _____ the traffic in many parts of the city.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"effected"},{"key":"B","text":"affected"},{"key":"C","text":"infected"},{"key":"D","text":"rejected"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"affect 为动词，意为“影响”；effect 作名词常意为“影响／效果”，作动词意为“使发生／实现”。此处表示大雨影响交通，用 affected。","point":"动词辨析（affect/effect）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":24,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十四天.md"}],"id":"q-7398ca2f686984a7"},{"stem":"The opening of the new railway has _____ great changes in the life of the mountain people.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"brought about"},{"key":"B","text":"brought up"},{"key":"C","text":"brought in"},{"key":"D","text":"brought back"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"bring about 意为“引起／导致”；新铁路的开通给山里人的生活带来巨大变化。","point":"动词短语辨析（bring about）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-08300e14451d8f8d"},{"stem":"Don't _____ easily even if you fail the first time; success often comes after many attempts.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"give away"},{"key":"B","text":"give off"},{"key":"C","text":"give up"},{"key":"D","text":"give out"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"give up 意为“放弃”。句意为“即使第一次失败也不要轻易放弃；成功往往在多次尝试后才来到”。","point":"动词短语辨析（give up）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-ca50481f9c192eba"},{"stem":"A little cat was nearly _____ by a speeding car in the street yesterday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"run out"},{"key":"B","text":"run over"},{"key":"C","text":"run into"},{"key":"D","text":"run away"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"run over 意为“车辆碾过”；此处猫险些被车碾过，用被动结构 was nearly run over。","point":"动词短语辨析（被动 run over）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-d0f15a6a321ed06a"},{"stem":"英译：The new manager is widely regarded as a breath of fresh air for the entire department.","options":[],"answer":"新经理被普遍视为整个部门的一股清新之风。","explanation":"a breath of fresh air 为比喻，译为“清新之风”；be regarded as 意为“被视作”。","point":"比喻的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-1ddf8c5aeaa0df37"},{"stem":"It is desirable that the construction _____ completed before the rainy season sets in.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"should be completing"},{"key":"D","text":"be"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It is desirable that... 用虚拟语气；construction 与 complete 是被动关系，故用 (should) be completed。","point":"虚拟语气——It is desirable that 句型 (should) be done。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-7d4f66d6da853047"},{"stem":"The dean's preference that the new policy _____ immediate effect has been communicated to faculty.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"takes"},{"key":"B","text":"take"},{"key":"C","text":"took"},{"key":"D","text":"would take"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"preference 后同位语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形。take immediate effect 意为“立即生效”。","point":"虚拟语气——preference 后同位语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-2d1203b22704243c"},{"stem":"Remember to lock the door when you leave. _____. I won't forget this time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Neither did"},{"key":"B","text":"So do"},{"key":"C","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"D","text":"OK, I will."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方提醒离开时锁门，回答应承诺做到；OK, I will 与“这次不会忘记”自然衔接。","point":"提醒——安全事项。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-f0d6949798857306"},{"stem":"The HR department mandates that new hires _____ a corporate training program within their first month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"completes"},{"key":"B","text":"completed"},{"key":"C","text":"would complete"},{"key":"D","text":"complete"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"mandate 后的 that 从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形 complete。","point":"虚拟语气——mandates 后 that 从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-2cc5b0e10f7ee97d"},{"stem":"If you come across a new word while reading, you can _____ it in the dictionary.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"look up"},{"key":"B","text":"look after"},{"key":"C","text":"look into"},{"key":"D","text":"look for"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"look up (in the dictionary) 意为“在词典中查找”；look after 照顾，look into 调查，look for 寻找。","point":"动词短语辨析（look up）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-251a99ef758f9024"},{"stem":"After a short break, the workers _____ building the bridge in spite of the cold weather.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"carried out"},{"key":"B","text":"carried away"},{"key":"C","text":"carried on"},{"key":"D","text":"carried off"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"carry on (doing) sth. 意为“继续做某事”；短暂休息后工人继续建桥。","point":"动词短语辨析（carry on doing）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-aa4ee9cd6425273e"},{"stem":"英译：His childhood in the village was a golden chapter that he often revisits in his memory.","options":[],"answer":"他在乡村度过的童年是他时常在记忆里重温的黄金篇章。","explanation":"a golden chapter 译为“黄金篇章”，是比喻；revisit in one's memory 译为“在记忆中重温”。","point":"比喻的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-aed26f51ec6daee4"},{"stem":"I can't find my phone anywhere. It has all my photos on it. _____. Let's think where you used it last.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I told you to be careful."},{"key":"B","text":"That's really bad."},{"key":"C","text":"Calm down. Don't worry."},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方找不到手机很着急，应先安抚再引导回忆。Calm down. Don't worry. 意为“冷静，别慌”；后句“想想最后一次用它在哪里”是在提供帮助。其余选项分别为事后指责、消极评价和轻描淡写，不合时宜。","point":"安慰——物品丢失。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-a4d780ae42c50b50"},{"stem":"中译：当她进来时，我正在做作业。","options":[],"answer":"I was doing my homework when she came in.","explanation":"when 引导过去时间状语从句；主句用过去进行时 was doing 表示当时正在进行，come in 表示“进来”。","point":"过去进行时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-83ccf0eaf76bd401"},{"stem":"中译：明天下午两点开会，不要迟到。","options":[],"answer":"The meeting will begin at two tomorrow afternoon. Don't be late.","explanation":"页面使用 will + 动词原形表达一般将来时；begin 表示“开始”，Don't be late 表示“不要迟到”。我的译法以 is 表示安排好的会议时间，意思相符。","point":"一般将来时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-ea76897db0f59304"},{"stem":"The cabinet's resolution that the minister _____ in person was upheld.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"appears"},{"key":"B","text":"appeared"},{"key":"C","text":"appear"},{"key":"D","text":"would appear"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"resolution 后的同位语从句用虚拟语气 (should) + 动词原形 appear。句意：内阁要求部长亲自出席的决议获得通过。","point":"虚拟语气——resolution 后同位语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-0895a4dd56d4c513"},{"stem":"It took the little girl several weeks to _____ the shock caused by the earthquake.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"get off"},{"key":"B","text":"get on"},{"key":"C","text":"get away"},{"key":"D","text":"get over"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"get over 表示“从打击、疾病中恢复”；get off 表示下车或出发，get on 表示上车或进展，get away 表示离开或逃脱。句意是小女孩花了几周才从地震造成的惊吓中恢复。","point":"动词短语辨析（get over）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-4e70476a41dd67a0"},{"stem":"It was so dark that we could hardly _____ the words on the sign.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"make up"},{"key":"B","text":"make for"},{"key":"C","text":"make out"},{"key":"D","text":"make sure"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"make out 表示“辨认出、勉强看清”，符合天黑、看不清招牌字的语境。make up 为编造、化妆或组成；make for 为走向或有助于；make sure 为确保。","point":"动词短语辨析（make out）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-321a6a49d22ff83e"},{"stem":"I've got a bad cold and a terrible cough. _____. Drink more water and have a good rest.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Good luck!"},{"key":"B","text":"Take good care of yourself."},{"key":"C","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"D","text":"Well done!"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"朋友生病，应关心慰问，Take good care of yourself 意为“好好照顾自己”，与多喝水、多休息的建议衔接。其余选项为祝福好运、祝贺或表扬，不合语境。","point":"安慰——身体不适。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-d96248bfee4f5a3c"},{"stem":"The young couple set _____ some money every month so that they could buy their own house.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"off"},{"key":"B","text":"out"},{"key":"C","text":"up"},{"key":"D","text":"aside"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"set aside 表示“留出、拨出（钱或时间）”；set off 为出发或引爆，set out 为出发或着手，set up 为建立。句意是每月留钱以便买房。","point":"动词短语辨析（set aside）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-a76c0376a7a2171b"},{"stem":"I'm so nervous about my job interview tomorrow. _____. You've prepared well and you'll do fine.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Hurry up."},{"key":"B","text":"Take it easy."},{"key":"C","text":"It's up to you."},{"key":"D","text":"You're welcome."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方面试前紧张，应安抚情绪。Take it easy 意为“放轻松”，与后面肯定其准备充分的鼓励相接。其余选项为催促、交由对方决定、回应感谢。","point":"安慰——紧张情绪。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-e28b6464b2a1bcd4"},{"stem":"I was laid off from my job yesterday. I don't know what to do now. _____. I'm sure you'll find a better one soon.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't worry. Everything will be fine."},{"key":"B","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"C","text":"That's the way it is."},{"key":"D","text":"When did it happen?"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方失业沮丧，应安慰并给予希望。Don't worry. Everything will be fine 与“相信你会找到更好的工作”呼应。其他选项显得冷淡、消极或未回应情绪。","point":"安慰——失业困境。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-ed4e9dc88b0f2796"},{"stem":"中译：下个月我要去北京出差。","options":[],"answer":"I am going to Beijing on business next month.","explanation":"next month 表示将来时间；on business 表示“出差”，go on business 也是搭配。我的 on a business trip 也表达出差。","point":"一般将来时。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-2ff70eafb2b5a013"},{"stem":"Nobody can _____ such rude behavior for a long time, so the boss decided to fire the man.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"put away"},{"key":"B","text":"put on"},{"key":"C","text":"put aside"},{"key":"D","text":"put up with"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"put up with 表示“容忍、忍受”；put away 为收起来或储存，put on 为穿上或上演，put aside 为留出或搁置。句意是没人能长期忍受粗鲁行为。","point":"动词短语辨析（put up with）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-f945634a75cfe615"},{"stem":"The judge ordered that the suspect _____ no contact with the witness during the trial.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have"},{"key":"B","text":"has"},{"key":"C","text":"had"},{"key":"D","text":"should has"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"order 后 that 从句用虚拟语气 (should) + 动词原形 have。句意是法官命令嫌疑人在审讯期间不得接触证人。","point":"虚拟语气——order 后 that 从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-c33ff73a72eef7aa"},{"stem":"It is fitting that the company's founder _____ the opening address of the anniversary gala.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"delivers"},{"key":"B","text":"delivered"},{"key":"C","text":"would deliver"},{"key":"D","text":"deliver"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It is fitting that 主语从句用虚拟语气 (should) + 动词原形 deliver。句意是公司创始人在周年庆典上致开幕辞很合适。","point":"虚拟语气——It is fitting that 主语从句 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-575b1baabc3d8603"},{"stem":"House prices in this district have _____ by nearly 30 percent over the past three years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gone down"},{"key":"B","text":"gone up"},{"key":"C","text":"gone off"},{"key":"D","text":"gone by"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"页面按“上涨”语境选 go up，表示上升。go down 为下降，go off 为离开、爆炸或变质，go by 为时间流逝或经过。句意：过去三年房价上涨近 30%。","point":"动词短语辨析（go up）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-e87487b6215fd5ad"},{"stem":"I failed the driving test again. I feel so discouraged. _____. Practice more and you'll make it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't be so upset."},{"key":"B","text":"I told you so."},{"key":"C","text":"What's the matter?"},{"key":"D","text":"Help yourself."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方考试受挫，应先安慰，再鼓励其多练习。Don't be so upset 意为“别太难过了”。其余选项是责备、询问已知原因或请自便，均不合语境。","point":"安慰——考试失利。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-26593a5555d0c609"},{"stem":"It's about time our neighbors _____ down on their late-night parties.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"calm"},{"key":"B","text":"have calmed"},{"key":"C","text":"will calm"},{"key":"D","text":"calmed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"It's about time that ... 用虚拟语气，从句用一般过去式 calmed；calm down 表示“安静下来、减少喧闹”。","point":"虚拟语气——It's about time that 句型。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-0ede6aec1a84c5bd"},{"stem":"英译：The sudden resignation of the CEO has raised serious concerns about the continuity of the project.","options":[],"answer":"首席执行官突然辞职，引发了对项目延续性的严重担忧。","explanation":"raise concerns about 译为“引发对……的担忧”；sudden resignation 译为“突然辞职”；continuity 译为“延续性”。","point":"名词短语翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-f5893f4dc3374651"},{"stem":"Without the help of local volunteers, the stranded tourists _____ lost in the mountains.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be"},{"key":"B","text":"would have been"},{"key":"C","text":"will be"},{"key":"D","text":"are"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"without 表示“如果当时没有”，隐含与过去事实相反的假设；tourists 与 lose 为被动关系，故用 would have been lost。句意：若没有当地志愿者帮助，游客本会迷失在山中。","point":"虚拟语气——without 引导含蓄虚拟条件（被动）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":25,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十五天.md"}],"id":"q-ffff056752a55e1e"},{"stem":"中译：这个问题据说已经解决了。","options":[],"answer":"The problem is said to have been solved.","explanation":"“据说”用被动结构 is said；对过去已发生动作的推测，用不定式完成被动式 to have been done。","point":"被动语态（is said to have done）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-42e00655cd1740cf"},{"stem":"中译：火车再过五分钟就要开了。","options":[],"answer":"The train is leaving in five minutes.","explanation":"in + 时间段表示将来、倒计时；现在进行时 is leaving 可表示即将发生的动作，常见于移动词。我的 will leave 也表达将来。","point":"一般将来时（现在进行表将来）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-8b69122daac60f60"},{"stem":"英译：The harder you practice, the more confident you will become when delivering a speech.","options":[],"answer":"练习得越多，你在演讲时就会越自信。","explanation":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级表示“越……就越……”；delivering a speech 表示进行演讲。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-e33c100794904964"},{"stem":"中译：这座桥是三年前建成的。","options":[],"answer":"This bridge was built three years ago.","explanation":"桥是建造动作的承受者，用一般过去时被动语态 was built；build—built—built 是不规则变化。","point":"被动语态。","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-98cad9845018ce35"},{"stem":"英译：The more time you devote to reading, the broader your perspective will grow.","options":[],"answer":"你花在阅读上的时间越多，你的视野就会越宽广。","explanation":"the 加比较级，the 加比较级表示“越……就越……”；devote...to 译为“奉献给、花……在”；broader 译为“更宽广的”。","point":"the+比较级，the+比较级结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-bf81f9243efd8cbb"},{"stem":"英译：Her calmness under immense pressure reveals remarkable maturity and emotional resilience.","options":[],"answer":"她在巨大压力下的冷静表现出非凡的成熟与情绪韧性。","explanation":"under immense pressure 译为“在巨大压力下”；reveals 译为“表现出”；emotional resilience 译为“情绪韧性”。","point":"名词短语翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":26,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十六天.md"}],"id":"q-6a8c756f204f74f0"},{"stem":"Are you ready to order, sir? _____. I'll have the fried rice and a soup.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"B","text":"No, thanks."},{"key":"C","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"D","text":"You bet."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"服务员询问是否可以点餐，应确认并报出菜名。Yes, please 表示“好的，要点餐”；No, thanks 表示谢绝；Not at all 是回应感谢；You bet 不符合点餐语境。","point":"消费——餐厅点餐。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-fcf4b96f818036be"},{"stem":"Tom would rather his supervisor _____ him about the deadline change in advance.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had informed"},{"key":"B","text":"inform"},{"key":"C","text":"informs"},{"key":"D","text":"would inform"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"实际未被提前通知；would rather + sb had done 表示对过去的虚拟遗憾。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句对过去虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-739af0dccbb3d9c6"},{"stem":"_____ early in the morning is a good habit which will benefit you all your life.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Get up"},{"key":"B","text":"Got up"},{"key":"C","text":"Getting up"},{"key":"D","text":"To be got up"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"动名词短语作主语。A 为动词原形，不能作主语；B 为过去式；D 为不定式被动式，语态错误。","point":"非谓语动词（动名词作主语）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-31b5b37eeef43735"},{"stem":"中译：他看起来很兴奋。","options":[],"answer":"He looks very excited.","explanation":"look（系动词）+ 表语；excited 表示“感到兴奋的”，以人为主语；exciting 表示“令人兴奋的”，以物为主语。","point":"主系表结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-d1730c0fc7e2c83b"},{"stem":"中译：这项工作似乎变得越来越重要。","options":[],"answer":"This job seems to be getting more and more important.","explanation":"seem + to do；more and more + 原级表示“越来越……”；get 表示“变得”，可作系动词。","point":"主系表结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-5ebb36e038bf233e"},{"stem":"How much are the apples? _____. They're fresh from the farm.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"B","text":"Five yuan a kilo."},{"key":"C","text":"It's my turn."},{"key":"D","text":"Never mind."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"询问价格，摊主应直接报价。Five yuan a kilo 意为“一公斤五元”；其他选项是回应感谢、轮到我、安慰语。","point":"消费——询价。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-07a99a465f6f88b0"},{"stem":"This skirt looks nice, but it's a bit tight. _____? Sure. I'll get you the next size.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How much is it?"},{"key":"B","text":"Can I pay by card?"},{"key":"C","text":"Is there a discount?"},{"key":"D","text":"Do you have it in a larger size?"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"试穿发现偏紧，需要换大一码；店员说会拿下一个尺码，故应询问是否有更大的尺码。价格、支付、折扣均不符合回答。","point":"消费——试穿换码。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-6119748feeca31d6"},{"stem":"The bridge was damaged; otherwise the rescue team _____ the disaster area sooner.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"could reach"},{"key":"B","text":"should have reached"},{"key":"C","text":"could have reached"},{"key":"D","text":"would reach"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"桥损坏已经是过去事实；otherwise 表示“如果桥未坏”，主句 could have reached 表示过去本可达。","point":"虚拟语气——otherwise 含蓄虚拟条件（过去，情态）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-3d3a0e6b74142c23"},{"stem":"英译：The better you understand your audience, the more persuasive your argument will appear.","options":[],"answer":"你越了解你的听众，你的论点就显得越有说服力。","explanation":"the 加比较级，the 加比较级表示“越……越……”；persuasive 译为“有说服力的”；appear 译为“显得”。","point":"the+比较级，the+比较级结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-b7f24a0c4ba04269"},{"stem":"中译：这本书没有那本书有趣。","options":[],"answer":"This book is not as interesting as that one.","explanation":"“不如……”用 not as + 形容词原级 + as；that one 代替 that book，避免重复。","point":"形容词比较级（not as...as）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配","比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-9bfdd9e5f094ce4f"},{"stem":"_____ the heavy rain, the farmers went on working in the fields.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In spite of"},{"key":"B","text":"In case of"},{"key":"C","text":"Instead of"},{"key":"D","text":"In favor of"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"in spite of 意为“尽管”；in case of 意为“万一”；instead of 意为“代替”；in favor of 意为“赞成”。下着大雨仍继续劳作，表示让步。","point":"固定搭配（in spite of）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0edd86cb0f6ae3f3"},{"stem":"We had hoped that John _____ a doctor, but he ended up as a software engineer.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should become"},{"key":"B","text":"became / had become"},{"key":"C","text":"would have become"},{"key":"D","text":"would become"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"had hoped 后接 that 从句，用 would do 表达过去的希望（后来未实现）；would have become 表示完成后的虚拟，与本句时间未到不符。","point":"虚拟语气——had hoped + that 从句（would do）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-7402a68430911898"},{"stem":"I'd like to return this shirt. It's too small for me. _____. Do you have the receipt?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I don't think so."},{"key":"B","text":"It's up to you."},{"key":"C","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"D","text":"Certainly. Let me check."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"顾客要求退货，店员应礼貌受理并核实。Certainly. Let me check 意为“好的，我核实一下”；后句索要小票，符合流程。","point":"消费——退换货。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-682c61a48954ab27"},{"stem":"Without your constant encouragement, I _____ so confident about taking the exam.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would not be"},{"key":"B","text":"would not have been"},{"key":"C","text":"wouldn't been / might not have been"},{"key":"D","text":"did not have been"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"页面按过去事实理解：你过去一直鼓励我，因此考试前或考试时很有信心。without 引导含蓄虚拟条件；与过去事实相反，主句用 would not have been。A 表示与现在事实相反，和页面设定的时间不符。","point":"虚拟语气（without 含蓄条件 + 与过去事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-e9fba1ff03658427"},{"stem":"英译：The more transparent the management is, the greater the trust employees will place in the company.","options":[],"answer":"管理层越透明，员工对公司就越信任。","explanation":"the 加比较级，the 加比较级表示“越……越……”；transparent 译为“透明的”；place trust in 译为“信任”。","point":"the+比较级，the+比较级结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-25c86c0ed360e07b"},{"stem":"The injured driver remained _____ all the way to the hospital and could tell the doctor his name.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"conscious"},{"key":"B","text":"conscientious"},{"key":"C","text":"subconscious"},{"key":"D","text":"consciousness"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"conscious 意为“清醒的、有意识的”；conscientious 为“认真的、尽责的”；subconscious 为“下意识的”；consciousness 为名词。remain 后接形容词作表语。","point":"形容词辨析（conscious）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-1dd81ce9e5137dd0"},{"stem":"We had hoped that the rain _____ by the morning, but it was still pouring down.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would have stopped"},{"key":"B","text":"stopped"},{"key":"C","text":"would stop"},{"key":"D","text":"had stopped"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"页面将 had hoped that 从句按“过去对未来的希望（未实现）”处理，选 would + 动词原形。句意：我们原指望雨到早上会停，但雨仍在倾泻。注意：我选的 would have stopped 在一般英语中也可能表达“到早上已经停止”的预期，但此题页面指定 C。","point":"虚拟语气——had hoped + that 从句（would do）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-1dce0a7c666a774e"},{"stem":"_____ the terrible weather, the football match had to be put off until next week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Because"},{"key":"B","text":"As"},{"key":"C","text":"Owing to"},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"owing to 意为“由于”，后接名词短语；because / as 是从属连词，须引导从句；thanks 后缺 to。横线后为名词短语 the terrible weather。","point":"固定搭配（owing to）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-c953384c593ee8e2"},{"stem":"It was very _____ of you to lend me your umbrella when you saw me standing in the rain.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"considerable"},{"key":"B","text":"considering"},{"key":"C","text":"considerate"},{"key":"D","text":"considered"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"considerate 意为“体贴的、考虑周到的”；considerable 为“相当大的、可观的”；considering 为“考虑到”；considered 为“被考虑的”。雨中借伞是体贴的行为。","point":"形容词辨析（considerate / considerable）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0a3044f48a552c0a"},{"stem":"I would rather you _____ anything about the surprise party until the birthday itself.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"don't say"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't say"},{"key":"C","text":"won't say"},{"key":"D","text":"haven't said"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"would rather + sb + 过去式，表示对现在或将来的虚拟愿望；否定用 didn't do。句意：我宁愿你直到生日当天都不要透露惊喜派对的事。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句否定（对现在/将来）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-452038e96c705585"},{"stem":"The teacher spoke in a loud voice so as _____ by all the students in the hall.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to hear"},{"key":"B","text":"hearing"},{"key":"C","text":"heard"},{"key":"D","text":"to be heard"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"so as to 后接动词原形；老师与 hear 之间是被动关系（被学生听到），故用不定式被动式 to be heard。","point":"非谓语动词（不定式被动式）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-c770b0e1977c411a"},{"stem":"_____ from the top of the mountain, the whole city looks like a beautiful picture.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Seen"},{"key":"B","text":"Seeing"},{"key":"C","text":"To see"},{"key":"D","text":"See"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"主语 the city 与 see 是被动关系，用过去分词 Seen 作状语，相当于 When it is seen from...。Seeing 为主动分词，会造成逻辑主语不符。","point":"非谓语动词（过去分词作状语）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-bf8dcc1f362c894d"},{"stem":"That'll be ninety-eight yuan altogether. _____? Cash, please. Here you are.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How about a discount?"},{"key":"B","text":"Do you like it?"},{"key":"C","text":"When did you buy it?"},{"key":"D","text":"Will that be cash or card?"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"收银员结账时应询问支付方式；顾客答“Cash, please”，内容与现金或刷卡衔接。其他选项与结账环节不符。","point":"消费——结账方式。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["其他考点"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-825147facb15f1b9"},{"stem":"In the English class, the teacher divided the whole class _____ four groups for the discussion.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"among"},{"key":"B","text":"into"},{"key":"C","text":"between"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"divide sth. into... 意为“把……分成……”；divide...among 指在多者间分配，divide...between 指在两者之间分配，均不符合分成四组的结构。","point":"固定搭配（divide...into）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-ef8647140bdb6056"},{"stem":"She would rather her husband _____ the household chores over the weekend.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shared"},{"key":"B","text":"share"},{"key":"C","text":"shares"},{"key":"D","text":"had shared"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"would rather + sb + 过去式，表示对现在或将来的愿望；had shared 是对过去虚拟，而家务尚未分担。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句（对现在/将来）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-68c6a51eeecaf1bb"},{"stem":"_____ my opinion, reading is one of the most useful ways to improve your writing.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"On"},{"key":"B","text":"In"},{"key":"C","text":"For"},{"key":"D","text":"To"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"in one's opinion 意为“依某人看来”；其他介词不能与 opinion 构成该固定搭配。","point":"固定搭配（in one's opinion）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-0cc0c09e96f476b4"},{"stem":"I would just as soon she _____ the dishes right after the meal instead of leaving them in the sink.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"wash"},{"key":"B","text":"washes"},{"key":"C","text":"would wash"},{"key":"D","text":"washed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"would just as soon = would rather；后接从句用过去式，表示对现在或将来的愿望。","point":"虚拟语气——would just as soon 从句（对现在虚拟）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-2894f1e6a3304951"},{"stem":"英译：It was such a moving performance that the entire audience rose to their feet in applause.","options":[],"answer":"演出如此感人，以至于全场观众都起立鼓掌。","explanation":"such...that 表示“如此……以至于”；moving 译为“感人的”；rise to one's feet 译为“起立”。","point":"such...that 结构。","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-ea42756d02d20eda"},{"stem":"_____ the age of six, the little boy could already play the piano and draw beautiful pictures.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"At"},{"key":"B","text":"In"},{"key":"C","text":"On"},{"key":"D","text":"For"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"at the age of... 意为“在……岁时”。","point":"固定搭配（at the age of）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-f36b35578383366a"},{"stem":"Excuse me, do you have the latest novel by Mo Yan? _____. Let me check the shelf for you.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm not sure. I'll have a look."},{"key":"B","text":"Sorry, I don't read novels."},{"key":"C","text":"Why do you ask?"},{"key":"D","text":"That's none of your business."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"顾客询问书店库存，店员应主动查找。I'm not sure. I'll have a look 与后句 Let me check the shelf for you 连贯；其他回答不合服务语境。","point":"消费——询问库存。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":27,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十七天.md"}],"id":"q-6b1769e38c060ad9"},{"stem":"I enjoy listening to light music when I'm reading. _____. It helps me relax too.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Neither do"},{"key":"B","text":"So do"},{"key":"C","text":"So I am."},{"key":"D","text":"I am too."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方表达与自己相同的爱好，用“So + 助动词 + I”表示“我也一样”。前句 enjoy 是一般现在时的实义动词，借助 do 呼应，故选 So do。Neither do 用于否定句；So I am 和 I am too 的主谓结构不匹配。句意：我读书时喜欢听轻音乐。我也是，它也能让我放松。","point":"语法型——So+助动词呼应","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-98be238ef4b9427d"},{"stem":"Is this the town _____ the famous scientist was born about a hundred years ago?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"先行词是 the town，关系词在从句中作地点状语（was born in the town），故用 where。句意：这就是那位著名科学家约一百年前出生的那个小镇吗？","point":"定语从句（关系副词 where）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-5df342b388eb5c9d"},{"stem":"When the firemen arrived, they found the windows _____ and thick smoke coming out of the house.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"breaking"},{"key":"B","text":"to break"},{"key":"C","text":"broken"},{"key":"D","text":"break"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"考查“find + 宾语 + 宾补”。windows 与 break 是被动关系，且强调“窗户已被打破”的状态，用过去分词 broken 作宾补。句意：消防队员赶到时，发现窗户破了，浓烟正从屋里冒出来。","point":"非谓语动词（过去分词作宾补）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-90b8c0074efc87d4"},{"stem":"中译：他比他想象的更成功。","options":[],"answer":"He is more successful than he imagined.","explanation":"than 从句中谓语用一般过去时 imagined；比较级 more + 形容词 successful。","point":"形容词比较级","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配","比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-a27383e039e5374d"},{"stem":"He would rather his assistant _____ the documents before the lawyer's arrival.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"prepare"},{"key":"B","text":"prepares"},{"key":"C","text":"would prepare"},{"key":"D","text":"had prepared"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"这里表达对过去事实的遗憾：助手过去并未提前准备好文件。would rather + sb + had done 表示对过去的虚拟。句意：他宁愿助手在律师到来前就准备好了文件。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 对过去虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-ebdbcc4f72585164"},{"stem":"She seldom goes to the cinema on weekdays, _____? Right. She only goes on weekends.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doesn't she"},{"key":"B","text":"does she"},{"key":"C","text":"is she"},{"key":"D","text":"did she"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"seldom 是否定含义的副词，陈述部分 goes 为一般现在时、第三人称单数，附加问句须用肯定形式 does she。句意：她工作日很少去看电影，是吗？——对，她只在周末去。","point":"语法型——含否定副词反问","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-b2e7c55c4df9ce13"},{"stem":"The scientist _____ name is known to people all over the world will give us a talk tomorrow.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"whom"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"whose"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"name 与先行词 the scientist 是所属关系（科学家的名字），用 whose 在从句中作定语。句意：那位名字享誉全球的科学家明天将给我们作报告。","point":"定语从句（whose 作定语）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-55e9060cce92b713"},{"stem":"Let's go to the new restaurant for dinner, _____? Good idea! I heard their steak is excellent.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shall we"},{"key":"B","text":"will you"},{"key":"C","text":"do we"},{"key":"D","text":"don't we"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"以 Let's 开头表示建议，附加问句固定用 shall we；will you 常用于一般祈使句。句意：我们去那家新餐厅吃晚饭吧，好吗？——好主意！听说他们的牛排特别棒。","point":"语法型——Let's 反意问句","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-61b031d7c9a7aa49"},{"stem":"I'd rather you _____ to me like that in front of the customers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"don't speak"},{"key":"B","text":"didn't speak"},{"key":"C","text":"won't speak"},{"key":"D","text":"hadn't spoken"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"would rather + 从句用过去式，对现在或将来虚拟请求；否定式 didn't speak。句意：我希望你不要在客户面前那样对我说话。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句否定","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-fda3430b35c75261"},{"stem":"Every time I watch the funny show, I can't help _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to laugh"},{"key":"B","text":"laughing"},{"key":"C","text":"laugh"},{"key":"D","text":"laughed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"固定搭配 can't help doing sth. 表示“忍不住做某事”。can't help to do 表示“不能帮忙做”，与语境不符。句意：每次看那个滑稽节目，我都忍不住大笑。","point":"非谓语动词（can't help doing）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-99adea20f892bcf6"},{"stem":"_____ so much work to do, the manager decided to stay in the office until midnight.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"With"},{"key":"B","text":"As"},{"key":"C","text":"Because"},{"key":"D","text":"Though"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"with + 宾语 + 不定式构成复合结构，“With so much work to do”作原因状语；as、because、though 为连词，后面须接句子。句意：由于有这么多工作要做，经理决定在办公室待到半夜。","point":"非谓语动词（with 复合结构）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-2d9311a8acb514e3"},{"stem":"This is the very dictionary _____ I have been looking for these days.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"who"},{"key":"D","text":"whose"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"先行词 dictionary 前有 the very 修饰时，定语从句关系代词只能用 that；关系词作 look for 的宾语。句意：这正是我这几天一直在找的那本词典。","point":"定语从句（the very 修饰先行词用 that）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-383a594e20fa2a92"},{"stem":"I'd rather the children _____ in the garden rather than in front of the screen all afternoon.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"play"},{"key":"B","text":"are playing"},{"key":"C","text":"played"},{"key":"D","text":"had played"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"would rather + 从句过去式 played 表达对现在或将来的虚拟请求，与玩耍而非刷屏的事实对比。句意：我宁愿孩子们在花园里玩，也不希望他们整个下午看屏幕。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句（对现在/将来虚拟）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-b386e1f8e4740518"},{"stem":"中译：你越努力，进步就越大。","options":[],"answer":"The harder you work, the greater progress you will make.","explanation":"“the + 比较级 ..., the + 比较级 ...”表示“越……越……”；第二个 the 从句为主句，用将来时 will make。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-0898efcb6e304e3a"},{"stem":"_____ he was very tired after the long journey, he still went to the meeting at once.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Because"},{"key":"B","text":"Unless"},{"key":"C","text":"Although"},{"key":"D","text":"Since"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"前后句意为“虽然……但是……”，用 Although 引导让步状语从句；although 不能与 but 连用。句意：虽然长途旅行后他很累，但他仍然立刻去开会。","point":"状语从句（although 让步）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-eb848ccde6a7b249"},{"stem":"The board had hoped that the merger _____ by Q2, but the regulator raised concerns.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"should be approved"},{"key":"B","text":"would be approved"},{"key":"C","text":"would approve"},{"key":"D","text":"were approved"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"had hoped 表达过去未实现的希望，that 从句用 would + 动词原形；merger 与 approve 是被动关系，故用 would be approved。句意：董事会原本希望并购在第二季度获批，但监管机构提出了疑虑。","point":"虚拟语气——had hoped + that 从句 (would) be done","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-b49e22f5f5a966fa"},{"stem":"I would just as soon you _____ interrupting me when I'm on a conference call.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stop"},{"key":"B","text":"stops"},{"key":"C","text":"stopped"},{"key":"D","text":"had stopped"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"would just as soon 后的从句用一般过去式 stopped 表示对现在或将来行为的虚拟请求；与 but 无关。句意：我在开视频会议时，真希望你别来打断我。","point":"虚拟语气——would just as soon 从句虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-897b58458c37690a"},{"stem":"The weather is really lovely today, _____? Yes, it is. Perfect for a picnic.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doesn't it"},{"key":"B","text":"is it"},{"key":"C","text":"isn't it"},{"key":"D","text":"wasn't it"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"陈述部分 The weather is ... 为肯定句，附加问句用否定形式 isn't it，且沿用 is 的现在时。句意：今天天气真好，是吧？——是啊，太适合去野餐了。","point":"语法型——反意疑问句","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-2fbaaafc12d81fd8"},{"stem":"_____ you like to come to my birthday party on Saturday? I'd love to. Thanks for asking.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Do"},{"key":"B","text":"Are"},{"key":"C","text":"Will"},{"key":"D","text":"Would"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"Would you like to do sth 是发出邀请的标准、委婉句式；I'd love to 是接受邀请的典型回应。句意：周六你愿意来参加我的生日聚会吗？——我很乐意，谢谢你的邀请。","point":"语法型——Would you like 邀请","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-51a7fa1bc56c8f80"},{"stem":"中译：这本书越读越有趣。","options":[],"answer":"The more you read this book, the more interesting it becomes.","explanation":"the more ..., the more ... 表示“越……越……”；主句系动词 becomes 表达状态变化。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-14a15ce7330095e4"},{"stem":"She would rather that he _____ the meeting for her so she could pick up her child from school.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attend"},{"key":"B","text":"attends"},{"key":"C","text":"attended"},{"key":"D","text":"had attended"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"would rather + 从句过去式 attended，表示对现在或将来的请求，即希望他代她出席会议。句意：她倒希望他能代她开会，这样她就可以去学校接孩子。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句（对现在/将来）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-694cf0c5f0c2213e"},{"stem":"英译：He has accumulated such a wealth of experience that younger colleagues frequently seek his advice.","options":[],"answer":"他积累了如此丰富的经验，以至于年轻同事经常向他请教。","explanation":"such ... that 结构译为“如此……以至于”；wealth of experience 译为“丰富的经验”；seek advice 译为“寻求建议”。","point":"such ... that 结构","category":"汉译英","topics":["翻译技巧"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-a332149315203280"},{"stem":"英译：When the report was finally released, it immediately triggered heated debate among economists.","options":[],"answer":"报告最终发布时，它立刻引起了经济学家之间的激烈讨论。","explanation":"代词 it 指代前文 the report，翻译时需保留明确指代关系；trigger heated debate 译为“引发激烈讨论”。","point":"代词的补译 + 上下文衔接","category":"汉译英","topics":["代词与限定词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-86b6eeb4a3eb23ba"},{"stem":"You will never pass the driving test _____ you practise driving more often.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"if"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"unless"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"unless = if ... not，表示“除非/如果不”。句意：如果你不更经常练习开车，就永远也通不过驾照考试。","point":"状语从句（unless 条件）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-59000d91f1d5479b"},{"stem":"He would rather she _____ no longer the topic publicly at the town hall meeting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bring up"},{"key":"B","text":"brings up"},{"key":"C","text":"had brought up"},{"key":"D","text":"brought up"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"实际她仍会提出话题，would rather + 从句过去式 brought up 表示对将来或现在的虚拟。句意：他倒希望她在市民大会上别再提这个话题了。","point":"虚拟语气——would rather 从句对现在虚拟","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-4d29d70d4378fd29"},{"stem":"The pupils didn't go to bed _____ their parents came back from the evening party.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"after"},{"key":"B","text":"as"},{"key":"C","text":"while"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"not ... until ... 句型表示“直到……才……”。主句用了 didn't，表示动作直到从句动作发生时才结束。句意：学生们直到父母参加晚会回来后才上床睡觉。","point":"状语从句（not ... until）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-415e2bf58c698afe"},{"stem":"We had hoped the airline _____ our tickets without charging a rebooking fee, but they refused.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would rebook"},{"key":"B","text":"should rebook"},{"key":"C","text":"had rebooked"},{"key":"D","text":"would have rebooked"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"had hoped 表示“过去希望未实现”，that 省略后从句用 would rebook；不用 had/would have 完成式。句意：我们原本希望航空公司免费改签，但被拒绝了。","point":"虚拟语气——had hoped that 从句 (would do)","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-72790fd4385aca92"},{"stem":"The small company cannot _____ such high salaries to the newly recruited engineers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"afford to pay"},{"key":"B","text":"afford paying"},{"key":"C","text":"afford pay"},{"key":"D","text":"afford paid"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"afford 表示“负担得起”时，后接不定式：afford to do sth，故用 afford to pay。句意：这家小公司负担不起向新招聘的工程师支付这么高的薪水。","point":"非谓语动词（afford to do）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["非谓语动词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-80096798523f94d2"},{"stem":"英译：Although the proposal has obvious merits, it has met with strong resistance from senior staff.","options":[],"answer":"尽管这项提案有着明显的优点，但它遭到了资深员工的强烈抵制。","explanation":"代词 it 需补译出实际主语，即该提案或这项方案；meet with resistance 译为“遭到抵制”。","point":"代词的补译","category":"汉译英","topics":["代词与限定词"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-34dcd22a910a8934"},{"stem":"I didn't sleep well last night. _____. The heat kept me awake too.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"So did"},{"key":"B","text":"Neither did"},{"key":"C","text":"So do"},{"key":"D","text":"Neither do"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"前句 didn't sleep 是否定的一般过去时，表示“我也没睡好”用 Neither did I；So did I 用于肯定回应，Neither do I 时态不符。句意：我昨晚没睡好。——我也是，天气太热也让我睡不着。","point":"语法型——Neither 呼应否定","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":28,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十八天.md"}],"id":"q-2bdfea7a521b2e70"},{"stem":"Look out of the window! It _____ heavily, so you'd better take an umbrella with you.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rains"},{"key":"B","text":"rained"},{"key":"C","text":"is raining"},{"key":"D","text":"has rained"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"Look! 提示动作此刻正在进行，用现在进行时 is raining；一般现在时 rains 表示经常性动作。句意：看看窗外！雨下得很大，你最好带把伞。","point":"时态语态（现在进行时）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-7992a0e70dca9f92"},{"stem":"Rice _____ in the south of China, where the climate is warm and wet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is grown"},{"key":"B","text":"grows"},{"key":"C","text":"grew"},{"key":"D","text":"has grown"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"描述普遍事实，用一般现在时；rice 与 grow 是被动关系（被种植），故用 is grown。句意：水稻种植在中国南方，那里气候温暖湿润。","point":"时态语态（一般现在时被动）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-723406f8ef5ebd3a"},{"stem":"I got promoted to manager yesterday! _____. You really deserve it.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What a pity!"},{"key":"B","text":"Hard luck."},{"key":"C","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"D","text":"Take care."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方晋升应热烈祝贺，Congratulations! 与后句“你实至名归”衔接；其余选项表示遗憾或道别。句意：我昨天升职当经理了！——恭喜你！你实至名归。","point":"祝愿——晋升祝贺","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-dbe518cc951be43f"},{"stem":"_____ you _____ the new movie about the space station yet? It is really worth watching.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Did; see"},{"key":"B","text":"Do; see"},{"key":"C","text":"Will; see"},{"key":"D","text":"Have; seen"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"yet 常用于现在完成时疑问句或否定句，表示“已经/还”，故用 Have ... seen。句意：你看了那部关于空间站的新电影吗？它真的很值得一看。","point":"时态语态（现在完成时与 yet）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-7f1fbf98b83e741b"},{"stem":"中译：天气越冷，我越不想出门。","options":[],"answer":"The colder it is, the less I want to go out.","explanation":"less + 原级表示“更不”；it 指代天气；want 表示“想要”。","point":"the + 比较级，the + 比较级","category":"汉译英","topics":["比较结构"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-321558fe8826e3a9"},{"stem":"Mary _____ my invitation; otherwise she would have responded by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"must not have received"},{"key":"B","text":"shouldn't receive"},{"key":"C","text":"can't have received"},{"key":"D","text":"must not receive"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"otherwise + would have done 表对过去的反向结果，由此推断“过去不可能收到信”，用 can't have done 表否定推测；must not 表禁止。句意：玛丽一定没收到我的邀请，不然她现在早就回复了。","point":"虚拟语气 + 情态推测综合——can't have done 否定推测","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-2cf791a2086bf1dd"},{"stem":"Hello, may I speak to Miss Green? _____. Who's calling, please?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"She is out at the moment."},{"key":"B","text":"You've dialed the wrong number."},{"key":"C","text":"This is she speaking."},{"key":"D","text":"Please call back later."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"要找的人正是接电话者本人，应回答 This is she speaking（我就是），随后询问对方是谁。其余选项与“本人正在接听”矛盾。","point":"电话——自报身份","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-4b818a38c597a531"},{"stem":"中译：每个学生都应该努力学习。","options":[],"answer":"Every student should study hard.","explanation":"every + 单数名词，谓语单数；should + 动词原形表“应该”；hard 表副词“努力地”。","point":"主谓一致（every + 单数）","category":"汉译英","topics":["主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-ae1beaa31af7b13a"},{"stem":"If it rains tomorrow, the outdoor concert _____ as scheduled.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would be cancelled"},{"key":"B","text":"would have been cancelled"},{"key":"C","text":"will be cancelled"},{"key":"D","text":"is cancelled"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"真实条件句主将从现：if + 现在时，主句用 will；concert 与 cancel 是被动关系，用 will be cancelled。句意：要是明天下雨，户外音乐会就会按原计划取消。","point":"虚拟语气陷阱——真实 if 条件句（主将从现）","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-e9408e8e2e7d667f"},{"stem":"英译：After the scandal was exposed, the senator was forced to resign from his position.","options":[],"answer":"丑闻被揭露后，这位参议员被迫辞去其职务。","explanation":"被动语态 was exposed 译为“被揭露”，was forced 译为“被迫”；resign from 译为“辞去”。","point":"被动语态翻译","category":"汉译英","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-21cf76e333427861"},{"stem":"I _____ my homework in my room when suddenly the lights went out.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did"},{"key":"B","text":"have done"},{"key":"C","text":"was doing"},{"key":"D","text":"would do"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"when 引导的短暂动作（停电）打断过去某一时刻正在进行的动作，主句用过去进行时 was doing。句意：我正在房间里做作业，突然灯灭了。","point":"时态语态（过去进行时）","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-248c320b7249244b"},{"stem":"英译：The digital textbook, free to all enrolled students, has dramatically lowered education expenses.","options":[],"answer":"这本数字教科书免费提供给所有在校学生，大幅降低了教育开支。","explanation":"形容词短语 free to all enrolled students 作后置定语，前置译为“免费提供给所有在校学生的”；dramatically 译为“大幅地”。","point":"形容词短语作定语","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-fe770a6fe58b9073"},{"stem":"We would just as soon they _____ in their opinions about the new policy.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moderate"},{"key":"B","text":"moderated"},{"key":"C","text":"moderates / are moderating"},{"key":"D","text":"had moderated"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"would just as soon = would rather；后接虚拟过去式 moderated，对现在或将来温和表达意见的虚拟请求。句意：我们倒希望他们能就新政策稍微缓和一下言辞。","point":"虚拟语气——would just as soon 从句虚拟。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-3d96e491df7993bb"},{"stem":"Happy birthday, Lily! Many happy returns of the day! _____. I'm so glad you came.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The same to you."},{"key":"B","text":"Thank you very much."},{"key":"C","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"D","text":"You're welcome."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"收到生日祝福应真诚致谢，用 Thank you very much。“The same to you”通常回应双方的祝愿；“Not at all”和“You're welcome”用于回应感谢。","point":"祝愿——生日祝福。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-fff9ebc1250e5efd"},{"stem":"Is that 555–2168? I'd like to order a pizza. _____. This is a private house.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, it is."},{"key":"B","text":"Sorry, you've got the wrong number."},{"key":"C","text":"Speaking, please."},{"key":"D","text":"Who's that?"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"对方拨错号码，应礼貌说明“Sorry, you've got the wrong number”。后句说明这里是私人住宅，与前面的订餐请求不符。","point":"电话——拨错号码。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-1260e64971d46695"},{"stem":"He looks as if he _____ the news. He is still stunned.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"didn't hear"},{"key":"B","text":"hasn't heard"},{"key":"C","text":"hadn't heard"},{"key":"D","text":"wouldn't hear"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"as if 引导与过去事实相反的虚拟语气，用过去完成时 hadn't heard；“He is still stunned”表明他实际上已经听到消息。","point":"虚拟语气——as if 与过去事实相反（hadn't done）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-c5ec279b1e128600"},{"stem":"The ancient temple was gradually swallowed by the surrounding jungle over several centuries.","options":[],"answer":"这座古庙在几个世纪里逐渐被周围的丛林所吞没。","explanation":"被动语态 was swallowed 译为“被……所吞没”；over several centuries 译为“在几个世纪里”。","point":"被动语态翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-8b38c09c47294af3"},{"stem":"_____ the teacher said at the meeting left a deep impression on every student.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That"},{"key":"B","text":"What"},{"key":"C","text":"Which"},{"key":"D","text":"Whether"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"从句作主语，且 said 后缺宾语，表示“老师所说的话”，用兼有连接与指代作用的 What。that 引导名词性从句时不在从句中作成分。","point":"名词性从句（what 引导主语从句）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-acecf0d9bd94f354"},{"stem":"If you had taken the medication earlier, you _____ so ill by now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"would not have been"},{"key":"B","text":"would not be"},{"key":"C","text":"won't be"},{"key":"D","text":"should not be"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"错综时间虚拟语气：从句 had taken 与过去事实相反；主句 by now 指现在的结果，故用 would not be。would not have been 与“by now”冲突。","point":"虚拟语气——错综时间（从句对过去，主句对现在）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-e88245570742279a"},{"stem":"数学对他来说很难。","options":[],"answer":"Math is very difficult for him.","explanation":"math 为不可数名词，谓语用单数 is；difficult for him 表示“对他来说很难”。Mathematics 也是“数学”的表达。","point":"主谓一致（不可数名词作主语）。","category":"汉译英","topics":["词汇与搭配","主谓一致"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-62d9e12a9d7d93a3"},{"stem":"Happy New Year! _____! And I wish you every success in the new year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"B","text":"With pleasure."},{"key":"C","text":"No problem."},{"key":"D","text":"Happy New Year to you, too."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方祝新年快乐，应回赠同样祝愿“Happy New Year to you, too.”，再祝新年事业有成。其余选项分别用于回应感谢或请求，不适合。","point":"祝愿——新年问候。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-e417cc725d780b6c"},{"stem":"If the traffic had been lighter yesterday, the ambulance _____ in time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will arrive"},{"key":"B","text":"would arrive"},{"key":"C","text":"arrived"},{"key":"D","text":"would have arrived"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"过去事实条件“昨天交通拥堵”的反向假设：if 从句 had been，主句用 would have done。句意：昨天要不是交通堵塞，救护车本应能准时到达。","point":"虚拟语气——与过去事实相反（过去真实反向假设）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-b127b3bde9edcad3"},{"stem":"I'm taking the final exam tomorrow. _____. I'm sure you'll pass with flying colors.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Have fun!"},{"key":"B","text":"So what?"},{"key":"C","text":"Slow down!"},{"key":"D","text":"Good luck!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对方明天考试，应送上祝福“Good luck!”；后句“我相信你一定能顺利通过”也体现鼓励。Have fun 用于轻松娱乐，其他选项不合语境。","point":"祝愿——考试顺利。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-751dbb3f062498ae"},{"stem":"The doctor suggested that my grandfather _____ more water and take more exercise every day.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"drinks"},{"key":"B","text":"drank"},{"key":"C","text":"drink"},{"key":"D","text":"drinking"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"suggest 表示“建议”时，其宾语从句用 (should) + 动词原形，should 可省略；drink 与 take 并列，均用原形。","point":"虚拟语气（suggest + should do）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-ad7aaa0811e6187c"},{"stem":"The news _____ our volleyball team had won the championship soon spread all over the campus.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"whether"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"news 后的从句内容完整，用 that 引导同位语从句，说明消息的具体内容。what 需在从句中作成分。","point":"名词性从句（that 引导同位语从句）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["名词性从句","词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-88dbe030332f2844"},{"stem":"The speaker raised his voice _____ everyone in the back row could hear him clearly.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"even if"},{"key":"B","text":"so that"},{"key":"C","text":"as if"},{"key":"D","text":"now that"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"so that 引导目的状语从句，表示“以便”。演讲者提高嗓门，目的是让后排的人也听清楚。","point":"状语从句（so that 表目的）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-074454dfe123409d"},{"stem":"If I _____ in your position, I would not give up this golden opportunity so easily.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were"},{"key":"B","text":"am"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"与现在事实相反的虚拟条件句：if 从句用过去式，be 动词一律用 were；主句用 would + 动词原形。","point":"虚拟语气（与现在事实相反）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-451349959bcf7109"},{"stem":"I should not be surprised if Tom _____ the lottery someday, given how lucky he always seems.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"won"},{"key":"B","text":"wins"},{"key":"C","text":"would win"},{"key":"D","text":"will win"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"这里是真实条件句，不是虚拟语气。given how lucky he always seems 表明中奖有可能；if 从句表示将来可能发生的事，用一般现在时 wins。“should not be surprised”是主句的情态动词，不能据此判断为虚拟语气。","point":"真实条件句与虚拟语气区分（if + 一般现在时）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气","时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-f33b06622637d303"},{"stem":"The headmaster had hoped that the issue _____ resolved by the end of the week.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will be / should be / had been"},{"key":"B","text":"should have been"},{"key":"C","text":"would be"},{"key":"D","text":"would have been"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"页面说明 had hoped 表示过去希望未来实现；that 从句虚拟用 would + 动词原形，即 would be resolved（被动），表示“过去本希望会被解决”。我的 D 把从句误写成对过去完成结果的虚拟。","point":"虚拟语气——had hoped + that 从句（would be）。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-515fc0234936954f"},{"stem":"By the time we got to the cinema, the film _____ for about twenty minutes.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had begun"},{"key":"B","text":"had been on"},{"key":"C","text":"has been on"},{"key":"D","text":"was on"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"by the time + 一般过去时，主句用过去完成时；for about twenty minutes 要求延续性动词，begin 为瞬间动词，应改用 had been on。","point":"时态语态（过去完成时 + 延续性动词）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["时态与语态"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":29,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第二十九天.md"}],"id":"q-f015665a6bfe575c"},{"stem":"Your report on the sales figures was really impressive. I learned a lot from it. _____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"No, it's not worth mentioning."},{"key":"B","text":"You are flattering me too much."},{"key":"C","text":"Thank you. I'm glad you found it useful."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I worked very hard on it."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"回应赞美应先致谢，再表达对对方认可的高兴。C 既礼貌又切合报告“有用”的语境。","point":"回应赞美——致谢并回应对方感受。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":1,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-892aeba1084c244f"},{"stem":"The little girl has an _____ mind and is always inventing stories about her toys.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"imaginary"},{"key":"B","text":"imaginable"},{"key":"C","text":"imaging"},{"key":"D","text":"imaginative"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"imaginative 表示“富于想象力的”，可修饰人或 mind；imaginary 是“虚构的、想象中的”，imaginable 为“可想象的”。","point":"形容词辨析（imaginative / imaginary）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":2,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-3f8ce60ed4b60c9a"},{"stem":"Students are expected to be _____ to their teachers and to show respect in class.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"respectful"},{"key":"B","text":"respectable"},{"key":"C","text":"respective"},{"key":"D","text":"respected"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"respectful 表示“恭敬的、尊重的”，be respectful to sb. 表示尊敬某人；respectable 表示“体面的、可敬的”，respective 表示“各自的”。","point":"形容词辨析（respectful / respectable）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":3,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-2d242571e3400b16"},{"stem":"他一完成报告就把它交给了经理。","options":[],"answer":"As soon as he finished the report, he handed it to the manager.","explanation":"as soon as 引导时间状语从句，表示“一……就……”。两个动作都发生在过去，主从句时态一致；hand ... to ... 表示“把……交给……”。","point":"时间状语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":4,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-8c25f7eca36a5a4f"},{"stem":"Congratulations! I heard you passed the entrance exam with a high score. _____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You must be joking."},{"key":"B","text":"It's nothing serious."},{"key":"C","text":"I'm sorry to hear that."},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks. I couldn't have done it without your help."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"回应祝贺应致谢，并可归功于他人的帮助。“Thanks. I couldn't have done it without your help.”切合语境。","point":"回应祝贺——致谢并归功他人。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":5,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-c3463f5d44c04aab"},{"stem":"I can't decide whether to spend the holiday at the seaside or in the mountains. _____. The mountains are much cooler at this time of year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'd go for the mountains."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, I'd love to."},{"key":"C","text":"It's up to you to decide."},{"key":"D","text":"That's a good idea, but I'm afraid not."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方在两个目的地之间犹豫，后句说明山里更凉爽，应明确建议选择山里。“I'd go for the mountains”表达个人倾向；C 把决定权推回去，与后句建议不合。","point":"征询意见——给出倾向性建议。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":6,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-802c0103b5665629"},{"stem":"The doctor suggested that the patient _____ in bed for another week to make a full recovery.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stay"},{"key":"B","text":"stays"},{"key":"C","text":"stayed"},{"key":"D","text":"staying"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"suggest 表“建议”时，后接宾语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形；should 常省略，故用 stay。","point":"虚拟语气——suggest 后接 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":7,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-bc4fcbcfb51b31fb"},{"stem":"We're going hiking in the western hills this Saturday. Would you like to join us? _____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I'd rather stay at home."},{"key":"B","text":"No, I don't like hills at all."},{"key":"C","text":"That's very kind of you to say so."},{"key":"D","text":"I'd love to, but I have to work overtime."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"对邀请的委婉谢绝应先表示愿意，再说明原因。“I'd love to, but...”是标准表达；A 前后矛盾，B 过于生硬。","point":"邀请回应——委婉谢绝并说明原因。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":8,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-6060bc41f75af075"},{"stem":"The economic _____ of the small town has improved a great deal since the new railway was built.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"progress"},{"key":"B","text":"environment"},{"key":"C","text":"situation"},{"key":"D","text":"surrounding"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"economic situation 表示“经济形势”，与 improve 搭配自然。economic progress 虽可表达“经济进步”，但在此处不如 situation 合适；environment 表示“环境”。","point":"名词辨析（situation / condition）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":9,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-241045252b8044be"},{"stem":"那位在门口等了一个小时的女士是我们的新校长。","options":[],"answer":"The lady who waited at the gate for an hour is our new headmistress.","explanation":"who 引导定语从句修饰 the lady，表示“在门口等了一个小时的”；主句描述现在的身份，页面用一般现在时 is。我的译文主句用了 was，复习时要注意保留原句时态。","point":"定语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":10,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-87180c4e7518cbe3"},{"stem":"It is necessary that every new employee _____ a copy of the company's safety regulations.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gets"},{"key":"B","text":"got"},{"key":"C","text":"get"},{"key":"D","text":"getting"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It is necessary/important/vital + that 从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形，should 可省略，故用 get。","point":"虚拟语气——It is necessary that + (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":11,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-1f7569b8cc590c43"},{"stem":"The manager asked him to _____ why the sales figures had dropped so sharply last quarter.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"account for"},{"key":"B","text":"count on"},{"key":"C","text":"call for"},{"key":"D","text":"look for"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"account for 表示“解释、说明……的原因”，也可表示“占（比例）”；count on 为“依靠”，call for 为“需要”，look for 为“寻找”。","point":"动词短语辨析（account for）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":12,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-e28bca48b748ff8c"},{"stem":"It is important that we _____ our promise to our customers, whatever difficulties we may meet.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"kept"},{"key":"B","text":"keep"},{"key":"C","text":"will keep"},{"key":"D","text":"keeping"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is important that... 的主语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形，故用 keep。whatever 引导让步状语从句，不影响主句中的虚拟形式。","point":"虚拟语气——It is important that + (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":13,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-649877737e5926ec"},{"stem":"The volunteers who arrived early helped prepare all the materials for the workshop.","options":[],"answer":"早早到达的志愿者们帮忙准备了工作坊所需的全部材料。","explanation":"who arrived early 是修饰 volunteers 的定语从句，译为“早早到达的”；prepare ... for ... 译为“为……准备……”。","point":"定语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["定语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":14,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-30dcca895dfe6a68"},{"stem":"The professor requested that all the students _____ quiet during the listening examination.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"kept"},{"key":"B","text":"would keep"},{"key":"C","text":"keep"},{"key":"D","text":"keeping"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"request 表“请求、要求”时，宾语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形，should 可省略，因此用 keep。","point":"虚拟语气——request 后接 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":15,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-9bd52786e42867e0"},{"stem":"The manager gave orders that the annual meeting _____ put off until the following Monday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"be"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"will be"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"order 表“命令”，其同位语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形；meeting 与 put off 是被动关系，用 (should) be put off。","point":"虚拟语气——order 后接 (should) do 的被动式。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":16,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-8c82dd146b4e8af9"},{"stem":"I'm a little nervous about my job interview tomorrow morning. _____. You've been preparing for it for weeks.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Take it easy."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"D","text":"You are welcome."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方表达紧张，应给予宽慰。Take it easy 表示“放轻松”，与“你已经准备了几周”衔接自然；Never mind 多用于安慰对方不必在意某事。","point":"宽慰鼓励——缓解面试紧张。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":17,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-c559b741a2576da0"},{"stem":"The committee demanded that all the relevant documents _____ submitted to the office before Friday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"be"},{"key":"B","text":"are"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"will be"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"demand 表“要求”，宾语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形；documents 与 submit 是被动关系，故用 be submitted。","point":"虚拟语气——demand 后接 (should) do 的被动式。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":18,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-a4dc7b88658ef4cc"},{"stem":"The _____ reason for the failure of the plan was that we had underestimated the cost.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"principle"},{"key":"B","text":"principal"},{"key":"C","text":"prince"},{"key":"D","text":"primarily"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"principal 作形容词意为“主要的、首要的”，principal reason 为“主要原因”；principle 是名词“原则”，primarily 是副词。","point":"形容词辨析（principal / principle）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":19,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-972a1d4c94363398"},{"stem":"His parents insisted that he _____ to bed before eleven every night during the school term.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"goes"},{"key":"B","text":"went"},{"key":"C","text":"go"},{"key":"D","text":"going"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"insist 表“坚持要求”时，宾语从句用虚拟语气：(should) + 动词原形，故用 go；若表示“坚持说”则用陈述语气。","point":"虚拟语气——insist 后接 (should) do。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":20,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-cca16b7095b6d7d0"},{"stem":"Unless the weather improves, the outdoor performance will be moved indoors.","options":[],"answer":"除非天气好转，否则户外演出将改在室内举行。","explanation":"unless 表示“除非”，引导否定条件状语从句；主将从现。be moved indoors 为被动语态，译为“改在室内举行”。","point":"条件状语从句的翻译。","category":"英译汉","topics":["状语从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":21,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-9c97849a6db2d2dc"},{"stem":"It was very _____ of you to bring an umbrella, since the weather forecast said it would rain.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sensitive"},{"key":"B","text":"senseless"},{"key":"C","text":"sensible"},{"key":"D","text":"sensational"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"sensible 表示“明智的、通情达理的”，常用于 It is sensible of sb. to do sth.；sensitive 为“敏感的”，senseless 为“无意义的、失去知觉的”。","point":"形容词辨析（sensible / sensitive）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":22,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-c4b056eef2523078"},{"stem":"The engineers worked day and night and finally _____ a creative solution to the technical problem.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"put up with"},{"key":"B","text":"came up with"},{"key":"C","text":"kept up with"},{"key":"D","text":"got along with"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"come up with 表示“想出、提出（主意或办法）”；put up with 为“忍受”，keep up with 为“跟上”。","point":"动词短语辨析（come up with）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":23,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-7bce81e3c4894766"},{"stem":"When choosing a product, consumers should pay attention to its _____ as well as its price.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"qualification"},{"key":"B","text":"quality"},{"key":"C","text":"quantity"},{"key":"D","text":"quarter"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"quality 表示“质量”，与 price 并列，符合“既要看质量又要看价格”的语境；quantity 是“数量”，qualification 是“资格、条件”。","point":"名词辨析（quality / quantity）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":24,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-8d28249949e05bf4"},{"stem":"中译：我认为这项新政策会对中小企业产生积极的影响。","options":[],"answer":"I believe that this new policy will have a positive impact on small and medium-sized enterprises.","explanation":"believe 后接 that 宾语从句，that 无词义可省；have a positive impact on 译为“对……产生积极影响”。","point":"宾语从句。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":25,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-845d17b2d7ec675d"},{"stem":"If I ______ you, I would accept the job offer without any hesitation.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was"},{"key":"B","text":"am"},{"key":"C","text":"had been"},{"key":"D","text":"were"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"与现在事实相反的假设，从句谓语用过去式，be 动词统一用 were；主句用 would + 动词原形。句意：如果我是你，我会毫不犹豫地接受这份工作邀请。","point":"虚拟语气——与现在事实相反的 if 条件句。","category":"虚拟语气","topics":["虚拟语气"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":26,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-b46f3a619c7c5cd6"},{"stem":"英译：The researchers concluded that regular exercise can significantly improve mental health.","options":[],"answer":"研究人员得出结论，定期锻炼能显著改善心理健康。","explanation":"宾语从句顺译；concluded 后接 that 从句，从句时态依句意用一般现在时表达客观规律；significantly 译为“显著地”。","point":"宾语从句的翻译。","category":"汉译英","topics":["名词性从句"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":27,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-1c2bffcbf530f885"},{"stem":"The community is looking for volunteers to help clean up the riverside park this weekend. ______","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why not sign up together?"},{"key":"B","text":"I have no idea about it."},{"key":"C","text":"That's none of my business."},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter to me."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方告知招募志愿者，最得体的是积极建议共同参与。Why not...? 表示“何不……”，语气自然；其余选项语气冷淡或漠不关心。句意：社区正在招募志愿者，这个周末帮忙清理河滨公园。——我们何不一起报名呢？","point":"提建议——倡议共同参与活动。","category":"交际用语","topics":["交际用语"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":28,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-5e77ad1a762c9978"},{"stem":"Buying a second-hand car is far more ______ for a young couple with a limited budget.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"economical"},{"key":"B","text":"economic"},{"key":"C","text":"economics"},{"key":"D","text":"economy"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"economical 意为“经济的、节约的”，指省钱、划算；economic 指“经济（上）的”，如 economic growth。economics 是“经济学”；economy 是“经济、节约（名词）”。句意：对预算有限的年轻夫妇来说，买二手车更划算。","point":"形容词辨析（economical / economic）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":29,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-eee4d1d54a6c399b"},{"stem":"The kind couple decided to ______ a boy from the orphanage and raise him as their own.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adapt"},{"key":"B","text":"accept"},{"key":"C","text":"adopt"},{"key":"D","text":"receive"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"adopt 意为“收养、领养”，也指“采纳”；adapt 意为“适应、改编”；accept 意为“接受”。句意：这对善良的夫妇决定从孤儿院领养一个男孩，把他当作亲生孩子抚养。","point":"动词辨析（adopt / adapt）。","category":"词汇与语法","topics":["词汇与搭配"],"notes":[],"sources":[{"bank":"daily","day":30,"number":30,"group":"","file":"英语刷题打卡第三十天.md"}],"id":"q-a26f2e262e74a128"}],"articles":[{"id":"r-人文英语3-1-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Families Having Fewer Children Nowadays","subtitle":"如今家庭里孩子数少了","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Most couples who get married or decide to live together generally plan to have children. Several years ago, having big families was common and people thought of this as an advantage. That was mainly because children began working at an early age to help provide for the family. But with the changing times and with the cost of living getting higher every single year, having a big family is no longer considered a practical option . In fact, more and more couples choose to have only one child and some do not have any desire to become parents at all."},{"lang":"zh","text":"绝大多数已婚夫妇或者住在一起的伴侣都有要孩子的计划。几年前，人们认为有个大家庭司空见惯，而且还被认为是个优势。主要原因在于孩子们很早就出来工作，帮助养家。但是随着时间的推移和生活成本的逐年提高，拥有一个大家庭不再被认为是一个很可行的选择。事实上，越来越多的夫妇选择只生一个孩子，有些人甚至根本不想要孩子。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Indeed, the trend of having fewer children started a few decades ago. According to the Australian Institute of Family Studies, by 1986, women aged 40 to 44 years, were considerably more likely to have given birth to two children than three children (36% vs. 27%) or four or more children (19%). However, taken together, women were still more likely to have had three or more children than to have had two children (46% vs. 36%)."},{"lang":"zh","text":"的确，这种少生孩子的趋势在二三十年前就出现了。根据澳大利亚家庭研究院的研究，截至1986 年，40~44岁年龄段的妇女生两个孩子的（36%）远远多于生三个（27%）或四个（含）以上的（19%）。然而，综合来看，生三个以上孩子的妇女（46%）仍然要多于生两个的（36%）。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Two decades ago, women were more likely to have had two children than three or more children — a trend that was most marked in the most recent period (38% vs. 25% in 1996; 38% vs. 22% in 2006). Nowadays, most families in Australia have two children. But the number of women who had given birth to a single child increased progressivelyfrom only 8% in 1981 to 13% in 2006, and it should be even bigger nowadays."},{"lang":"zh","text":"二十年以前，生两个孩子的妇女比生三个（含）以上的妇女多，这个趋势在近年来变得更加明显。（两者的数量百分比在1996年分别为38%和25%，在2006年分别为38%和22%。）如今，大多数的澳大利亚家庭中有两个孩子。但只生育一个孩子的妇女数量比例在逐渐增加，从1981年的8%上升为2006年的13%，现在的比例会更大。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The U.S. Census Bureau states that there are approximately 14 million only children in America today. This comprises 20% of the children's population compared to only 10% around fifty years ago."},{"lang":"zh","text":"据美国人口普查局报道，美国如今有接近1400万的独生子女。这个数占孩子总数的20%，而50 年前仅占10%。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":261},{"id":"r-人文英语3-1-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Stop Yelling at Your Kids","subtitle":"别再对你的孩子大吼大叫","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Parenting is hard. If you're a parent, I'm sure that I don't need to tell you that our job is a tough one. When you're managing children, it can be difficult to remember that they are still learning. If you find that you are yelling at your kids more often than you want to, here are some ways that can help you reduce the yelling. I've been working on this for the past few months and I have to say, it's been amazing for both the kids and me."},{"lang":"zh","text":"养儿育女不容易。如果你已为人父母，我觉得就不需要告诉你这是一项多么艰巨的任务了。当你在管理孩子的时候，很难时刻记得他们还在学习的过程中。如果你发现自己常常对孩子大吼大叫，而你并不想这样，这里有一些方法也许能帮助你减少这种行为。在过去的几个月里我一直都在探索，我不得不说，这些方法对我和我的孩子们都很有效。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If you are having an argument with your child, you need to make sure you both take the time to really listen. It gives both of you time to think and really listen to each other, which is important. Kids are more likely to listen to you if you listen to them!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你和孩子之间发生争执，你应该确保你们彼此花时间互相倾听对方。给双方时间去思考和认真倾听对方的心声，这是非常重要的。如果你愿意倾听孩子们的心声，孩子们也非常乐意倾听你的想法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"One of your biggest struggles is to remind yourself of appropriate expectations. You can't expect that your youngest acts as responsibly as your oldest. You should lower what you expect — taking into consideration things like their age — it can make a big difference."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你最大的一个纠结就是提醒自己对孩子要有合理的期望。你不应该期望最小的孩子能和最大的孩子那样，做事认真负责。你应该降低你的期望值，要考虑他们的年龄等因素，这样做会产生很大的变化。"},{"lang":"en","text":"You should do your best to take a moment before yelling and take in a deep breath. It makes a world of difference for you. Instead of yelling, you'd better whisper. It can also help diffuse any situation by making things quieter, not louder. Besides, the more time you spend with your kids, the better you'll get at communicating with them. You're both more likely to understand each other."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在你发火吼叫之前用一点时间做个深呼吸，会有天壤之别的。不要大声吼叫，而要轻声细语，这样，可以帮助缓和当时的情况。此外，你陪伴孩子的时间越长，你就越能更好地和他们沟通，你们就越容易理解对方。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If your children aren't listening or it seems they only don't listen to you, you don't take it personally. You should remind yourself that your kids are still learning and they're not going to be perfect."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果孩子们没有认真倾听或者看上去就是不听你的话，你也不要太在意。你要提醒自己孩子们还在学习的过程中，他们并不完美。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":289},{"id":"r-人文英语3-2-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Caring for the Elderly","subtitle":"关爱老人","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Caring for the elderly is not an easy task, and there are no hard and fast rules on how it should be done. Here are some tips you can apply to make life easier and happier for both you and the person in your care."},{"lang":"zh","text":"关爱老人不是一件容易的事，该如何做，缺乏严格的规则。这里有一些建议，可以让你和你关爱的老人相处得更加轻松和愉快。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 1 Establish a routine建立日常惯例"},{"lang":"en","text":"Organize the performance of daily activities in a routine manner, so that they are performed in the same way and at the same time every day. This routine will establish a sense of structure and increase feelings of control and safety. However, this routine can be broken with unplanned events occasionally, as elderly people may find the routine structure too boring and restrictive ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"以常规方式组织日常活动，以便每天在相同时间以相同方式来完成这些活动。这种惯例会形成一种按部就班的感觉，并增加控制感和安全感。然而，由于老人可能认为这样的惯例安排既枯燥又受限制，所以这种惯例偶尔会被计划外的事情所打破。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Para 2 Get to know them逐渐了解老人"},{"lang":"en","text":"It is important that you get to know the elderly in your care, their daily habits, likes and dislikes, etc. The better you know the person, the higher the quality of care you can provide."},{"lang":"zh","text":"逐渐去了解你所关爱的老人，了解他们的日常习惯与好恶，这点很重要。你越了解老人，你给他们提供的关爱质量就越好。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Para 3 Treat them with respect以尊重的态度对待他们"},{"lang":"en","text":"If elderly people do not have your respect, they will feel like they are being pushed around or asked to do things that they don't want to. This can lead to a bad relationship. By treating elderly persons in your care with respect, you can develop a strong bond with them. Besides, you can talk to them like adults, show your love and respect, which will not only make them feel good, but may also gain you their respect in return."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果老年人得不到尊重，他们就会感到被人摆布或者被要求做他们不想做的事。这会导致糟糕的关系。以尊重的态度对待你所关爱的老人，你会和他们形成牢固的关系。此外，你可以像和成年人那样与他们谈话，表达你的爱和尊重。这不仅能让他们感觉良好，还能使你获得他们对你的尊重。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 4 Mental stimulation进行心理刺激"},{"lang":"en","text":"It is better to try to keep them occupied with challenging games, like crosswords or chess, which will keep their minds sharp. They like to discuss world events and their life histories with you. This will give the elderly people a feeling of self-worth and make them feel needed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最好让他们总是忙于具有挑战性的游戏，比如填词游戏或下棋，这会让他们的头脑保持灵活。他们喜欢和你讨论世界大事和生活经历。这会让老年人感觉有自我价值和被需要的感觉。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 5 Social interaction参与社交活动"},{"lang":"en","text":"Organize and encourage social interaction. Remaining connected to other people and the world is important for the elderly. It keeps the elderly feeling more engaged. Encourage them to talk to other residents or participate in games, discussions or day trips. Help them to develop a strong relationship with a neighbor. It is important for the elderly to talk to others and make friends."},{"lang":"zh","text":"组织并鼓励老年人参与社交活动。与其他人及外界保持联系，对于老年人来说非常重要。这会让老年人会感到更加投入。鼓励他们与其他居民聊天或参与游戏、讨论或一日游活动。帮助他们与邻居建立牢固的关系。与他人聊天并交朋友对于老年人来说是很重要的。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":347},{"id":"r-人文英语3-2-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Demand for Elderly Care Services in China Is Rising Continually","subtitle":"中国老人关爱服务需求不断增长","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The number of elderly people aged above 60 has increased. Demand for elderly care services in China will continue to rise due to the increased aging population.The number of elderly people aged above 60 was over 200 million in 2012, and will be 300 million in 2025 and 400 million in 2034, according to the experts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"60岁以上老年人口数量已经增长。在中国，由于老年人口数量不断增长，对老年人关爱服务的需求也将会持续增加。根据专家统计，2012年60岁以上老年人口的数量超过2亿，到2025年和2034年将分别达到3亿和4亿。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It will be a tough challenge for China to deal with, due to the increasing rates of urbanization and a decreasing birth rate. The Chinese people will be facing a big challenge if we do not have enough money when we get older."},{"lang":"zh","text":"由于城镇化率的不断提高和人口出生率的不断下降，老龄人口增长对于中国来说是一个艰巨的挑战。当我们中国人变老的时候，如果没有足够的金钱，将会面临很大的挑战。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The United Nations defines an aging society as one that has 10 percent of its population at or above the age of 60."},{"lang":"zh","text":"联合国把老龄化社会定义为60 岁（含）以上老人达到总人口的10%。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When most developed countries were classed as an aging society, their gross domestic product (GDP) per capita stood at between 5,000 to 10,000 U.S. dollars or above. However, China became an aging society in 2001, and its GDP per capita was only 1,000 U.S. dollars. It was 6,000 U.S. dollars in 2012. China's economic foundation for an elderly society is fragile."},{"lang":"zh","text":"大多数发达国家被界定为老龄化社会时，其人均国内生产总值为5000 ~10000 美元，或者更高。然而，2001年中国开始步入老龄化社会，其人均国内生产总值仅有1000美元。2012年达到6000美元。中国老龄社会的经济基础是脆弱的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"On September 13, 2013, the State Council issued a guideline to speed up the development of China's elderly care services, hoping to complete a social care network for its elderly by 2025."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2013年9月13日，国务院已经颁布了加快中国老年人关爱服务的发展纲要，希望到2025年建设完成老年人社会关爱网。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":200},{"id":"r-人文英语3-3-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"A Safer Community","subtitle":"一个更加安全的社区","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The Wichita Falls Police Department is trying to help curb crime in neighboring communities throughout the city. On Saturday Wichita Falls Police gave a free two-hour presentation to help locals keep their community crime free."},{"lang":"zh","text":"威奇塔福尔斯警局镇正努力遏制整个城市相邻社区犯罪的发生。本周六，该警局的警察就如何保持社区零犯罪记录给当地居民做了两小时的免费讲座。"},{"lang":"en","text":"More than 20 people showed up at the Martin Luther King Center in east Wichita Falls to be part of the presentation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当日，20多人来到位于威奇塔福尔斯东部的马丁路德金中心，参加了讲座。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Wichita Falls Police Officer Jeff Hughes said that they wanted to make sure the folks out there were aware they were doing everything to take away the opportunity from a bad guy."},{"lang":"zh","text":"以威奇塔福尔斯警局的警官杰夫·休斯说，他们想让所有人都意识到警察正在尽一切努力不给坏人留有任何机会。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Hughes reminded those in attendance that their homes could be an open invitation to criminals. One of the biggest ways to prevent crime, according to Hughes, is to use CPTED, also known as Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design."},{"lang":"zh","text":"休斯警官提醒在场的人们，他们的家园对犯罪分子来说，可是很有吸引力的。（言下之意，家庭要做好防盗保护。）根据休斯警官的建议，最好的预防措施就是使用CPTED，即通过环境设计预防犯罪。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“The biggest site, that we are dealing with now, that we are endorsing fully, is Nextdoor and it's simply just nextdoor.com.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"休斯警官说：“我们现在正在搭建的最大的网站，也是我们全力支持的，就是nextdoor.com这个网站。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The site is free and it helps locals set up a virtual community that they can interact with from the comfort of their own home."},{"lang":"zh","text":"该网站是免费的，旨在帮助当地居民建立一个虚拟社区，在这个社区里居民可以足不出户，互相联动。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“With www.nextdoor.com it all happens in a web based program where if you send something out it gets to that group or that person instantly, and they will get an alerton their phone or an email, ” said Hughes."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“在www.nextdoor.com网站上，你通过网络程序向任何人或群组发送任何消息，他们的电话或电子邮件里会马上会收到一个提醒。”修斯说。"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to Hughes, he has already seen a positive impact locally from the site and hopes it can continue to expand in Wichita Falls."},{"lang":"zh","text":"休斯警官认为，他已经从网站上看到了对当地产生的积极效应，并希望可以在威奇塔福尔斯市继续推广使用。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":238},{"id":"r-人文英语3-3-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Making Your Home a Safer Place","subtitle":"让你的家成为一个更加安全的地方","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"We all tend to think that we are safe in our homes, but unfortunately, many homes are not as safe as they are supposed to be. It is impossible to make your home 100% burglar-proof but there are ways to improve your home safety."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们总是以为待在家中是安全的，但遗憾的是，很多时候家并不像人们想象的那样安全。让你的家百分百防盗是不可能的，但还是有很多方法可以提高家的安全性。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Always lock the door and windows when you go out for work or even if you are inside the house. The burglars can take advantage of the opportunity in a minute."},{"lang":"zh","text":"外出上班甚至即使在家，也永远记住要锁好门窗。入室盗窃者可以在瞬间就抓住可乘之机。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Be suspicious of strangers. You can never know who is pretending to conduct a research or who is using it as a disguise to see if your home is worth breaking in."},{"lang":"zh","text":"要当心陌生人。你根本不知道哪些人在假装进行调研，或者只是把它作为幌子来查看你家是否值得破门而入。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Never leave valuables or cash in visible places. Hide them out of sight because they may attract burglars."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不要把贵重物品或现金放在显眼之处。把它们存放在不易被发现的地方，否则会引起盗窃者的注意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Do not leave the door key under planters , doormats or similar hiding places. The burglars know exactly where to look for it."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不要把钥匙放在花盆、门垫或类似的存放之处，抢劫者清楚地知道从哪儿找钥匙。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Teach your children not to open the door or answer the phone when they are home alone. Although it is better to make an impression that your house is not empty, children may unintentionally reveal too much, for example, when the home is empty."},{"lang":"zh","text":"教育孩子独自在家的时候不要打开房门或接电话。最好是让盗窃者以为家中有人，但孩子无意之间会透漏出一些信息，比如家里什么时候没有人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Consider install an alarm system. A loud sound alarm usually drives the burglars away before they can steal anything from your home."},{"lang":"zh","text":"考虑安装一个防盗报警系统，响亮的报警声通常可以迫使盗匪在盗窃之前仓皇而逃。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Make sure you have good lighting outside during the night. Well-lit homes are deterring the burglars because they increase the risk of being noticed while sticking around the house or trying to break in."},{"lang":"zh","text":"确保屋外夜间有良好的灯光。家里灯火通明对盗贼是个威慑，因为当盗贼在房子周围逗留或者企图破门而入的时候，灯光会增加他们被发现的概率。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":248},{"id":"r-人文英语3-4-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Crime Prevention","subtitle":"预防犯罪","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The law defines youthful offenders (age 18 or under) as “ delinquent” if they commit offenses . As for the same offenses, the court would consider an adult as a “criminal”. “ Status offenders” are juveniles who commit offenses appropriate only to juveniles, such as truancy from school. Here are a few ideas to help prevent your children from becoming delinquent."},{"lang":"zh","text":"法律规定，18岁以下（含18岁）的未成年人违法，称为“少年犯”。同样的违法情形，法庭会将成人视为“罪犯”。“不良青少年”指存在不良行为的青少年，这些行为仅限于青少年，如逃学。以下这些方法可以预防你的孩子违法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Keep your children in school to help prevent delinquency. Minor offenses, such as truancy, can lead to more serious offenses. Make clear to your children your expectations about their school attendance. Meet with school officials if necessary."},{"lang":"zh","text":"让孩子坚持去上学可以预防犯罪。轻微的不良行为如逃学可以导致严重的犯罪。让孩子明白你期望他们去上课。如果有必要，约见学校管理人员。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Exercise adequate supervision. Juveniles rarely commit serious offenses while under the supervision of an adult. Seek the assistance of your local service agencies if you feel you cannot control your children. Attend parenting classes, or join a local support group if you are having trouble understanding how to exercise discipline."},{"lang":"zh","text":"加强监管。在成人的监管下，青少年鲜有严重的罪行发生。如果你感到对管教孩子束手无策时，可以寻求当地服务机构的支持。如果你在理解如何管教孩子方面有困难，可以参加家长学校或者加入当地的咨询机构。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Educate your children about the dangers of drugs. Drug offenses and addiction can have serious consequences for your children. Let your children know you will not tolerate drug use. Stay informed about drug use trends in children."},{"lang":"zh","text":"让孩子了解毒品的危害。毒品犯罪和吸食成瘾会给你的孩子带来严重的后果。向孩子表明你对毒品是零容忍的态度。及时了解孩子们沾染毒品的趋势。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Get your children involved in after-school recreational activities, sports, community service or other positive activities. Young people with positive"},{"lang":"en","text":"outlets for their energy are more likely to do well in school and avoid the problems of delinquency."},{"lang":"zh","text":"鼓励孩子参与课外活动、体育项目、社区服务或者其他有益的活动。能够正面释放精力的年轻人在学校里能够表现更好，而且能够避免犯罪问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Know who your children's friends are. Show an interest in your children's social life and peer groups. Peer pressure may have a bad effect on teenagers and young people. Do not allow your children to associate with juvenile delinquents."},{"lang":"zh","text":"了解孩子结交的朋友。关注孩子的社交生活和伙伴。同伴之间的压力有时会对青少年和年轻人带来负面的影响。不要让孩子跟未成年犯来往。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":258},{"id":"r-人文英语3-4-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"Steps to Prevent Internet Crimes","subtitle":"预防网络犯罪的步骤","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The Internet has been a common part of our daily life. As millions of people have access to the Internet, criminals look for potential victims"},{"lang":"en","text":"online. Children are especially vulnerable to online predators . Criminals may lure them into inappropriate chat rooms or ask them to go out, which may do them great harm. Here are a few ideas to protect yourself and your family from becoming a victim of Internet crimes."},{"lang":"zh","text":"网络已成为我们日常生活中的一部分。由于成百上千万人们具备了上网条件，犯罪分子会在线物色潜在的受害者。儿童尤其容易成为网络猎手的受害者。罪犯或是诱惑儿童进入不适宜的聊天室，或是诱骗他们出来，这些都会对儿童带来严重危害。下面一些方法可以保护你和你的家人不受网络犯罪的侵害。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Install anti-spyware and antivirus software. Anti-spyware helps prevent spyware from being used. Installing antivirus software helps prevent your computer from being infected with a virus."},{"lang":"zh","text":"安装反间谍和防病毒软件。反间谍软件可以预防间谍软件的使用。安装防病毒软件可以防止电脑中毒。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Turn on your firewall . This helps prevent hackers from getting information such as passwords to bank accounts and other information they could use to steal funds or steal your identity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"启动防火墙，这样可以防止黑客获取您的个人信息，如登陆银行账户的密码以及其他可能会盗取你的资金和身份的信息。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Help your children choose the websites they go to. Set rules and limits for your children to use the Internet. Use software that blocks out certain inappropriate websites in case you can't keep an eye on all the time."},{"lang":"zh","text":"帮助你的孩子选取他们适宜浏览的网站。为孩子使用网络制定规则并且进行一定限制。万一有时你无暇留意，可以利用软件阻止一些不良网站。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Talk with your children about Internet crimes. Tell children to talk to you about anything that happens inappropriate to them online."},{"lang":"zh","text":"跟孩子讲讲有关网络犯罪的事，要求孩子把他们在网上碰到的任何不宜的情况告诉你。进行在线购物和提供信用卡信息时，确保使用安全网站。当你觉得网站可疑时，在支付之前应该好好核查。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Use secured websites when purchasing items online and giving credit card numbers. When you are suspicious of the website, check it out before you pay any money."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在线购物并使用信用卡号码时，要使用安全的网站。如果怀疑网站安全，付账前务必核查清楚。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Report suspected Internet crimes. You can contact your local police office to report Internet crimes and they will send a special agent to look into the matter."},{"lang":"zh","text":"及时报告可疑的在线犯罪线索。你可以向当地警局报告网络犯罪，他们会安排专人进行调查。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":242},{"id":"r-人文英语3-5-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Public Speaking","subtitle":"公开演讲","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Public speeches are speeches delivered in public for a special purpose such as open class lectures or seminars in a university, religious preachings"},{"lang":"en","text":"in the church, speeches at meetings or conferences, the inaugural address of the president elect, etc. In terms of mode , there are impromptu speeches,"},{"lang":"en","text":"extemporaneous speeches, speeches from reciting, speeches from manuscript , but many of the speeches are written to be spoken before an audience. Most of these have something in common: to define, to explain something in order to arouse the interest of the audience and to obtain their support,"},{"lang":"en","text":"approval or consent. For those purposes, the speaker will have to appear to be friendly to the audience in order to identify himself with them and to"},{"lang":"en","text":"evolve their emotional support. At the same time he will have to use every means to make his speech persuasive, engaging and convincing ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"公开演讲是为了某一特定目的而公开进行的演讲，如大学里的公开课讲座或研讨会、教堂里的布道、会议上的演说、当选总统的就职演说等。就方式而言，有即兴演讲、脱稿演讲、背诵演讲、按手稿演讲，但是大多数演讲稿都是在演讲前写好的。多数演讲有一些共同之处：界定或解释某件事情，为了激发听众的兴趣，得到他们的支持、赞成或同意。为了这些目的，演讲者必须表现友好，与听众打成一片，并逐渐得到他们的情感支持。同时，演讲者还必须想方设法使他的演讲具有说服力、耐人寻味、令人信服。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Public speeches are delivered orally, but they are often well prepared in writing and delivered on formal occasions. So they are strongly influenced by the characteristics of the written language. For instance, they are often polite in tone, formal in style. Big and abstract words, noun phrases, complete sentences, complicated sentence structures, parallelisms and rhetorical devices are often found in public speeches. Generally speaking, the language used in public speeches is formal in style, clear and vivid in tone, and persuasive in purpose."},{"lang":"zh","text":"公共开演讲是通过口头表达的，但通常都是认真完成稿件后才在正式场合进行演讲。因而明显受到书面语言特征的影响。例如，演讲通常采用礼貌语气，风格上比较正式。公开演讲常常会使用大而抽象的词汇、名词短语、完整的句子、复杂的句型、并列结构和较多修辞手段等。总的说来，公开演讲中所使用的语言文体比较正式，语气清晰生动，说服力强。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As far as type is concerned, there are: the informative speech, the persuasive speech, the entertaining speech and stimulating speech."},{"lang":"zh","text":"就类型而言，有信息型演讲、劝说型演讲、娱乐型演讲和激励型演讲。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Generally speaking, there are four ways to deliver a speech: reading from a manuscript, reciting from memory, impromptu speaking, and extemporaneous speaking."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一般来说，演讲方式有四种：按手稿演讲、背诵演讲、即兴演讲和脱稿演讲。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":269},{"id":"r-人文英语3-5-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"A Speech — Better Lives for All","subtitle":"演讲：让生活更美好","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In today's society, working people can seldom find time to relax in their busy schedules . They often work overtime because of too much work waiting in queue, which ends up causing a lot of physical and mental problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在当今社会，上班族很少能在繁忙的工作日程中找到时间去放松一下。他们经常加班，因为太多的工作一个接一个地等着他们去完成，结果引发了身体和精神方面的诸多问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fortunately, more and more people are now aware that relaxation and stress-relief are necessary for life. One's health should never be sacrificed for a need to work hard. Indeed, finding time to relax makes people work more efficiently."},{"lang":"zh","text":"幸运的是，越来越多的人现在意识到放松和减压对于生活是必需的。永远不应该为了努力工作的需要而牺牲人的健康。事实上，抽出时间去放松一下会提高工作效率。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Many people plan trips to spend their free time traveling with their loved ones. This may have been a luxury in the past, but it has become more common in recent years. Traveling at home and abroad has now become convenient and affordable"},{"lang":"zh","text":"许多人计划和亲人们利用闲暇时间去旅行。这在过去可能很奢侈，但近年来已经比较普遍。现在，在国内外旅游已经很方便而且能够负担得起了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Going jogging and going to the gym after work have also become more popular, as they are rather convenient ways to exercise and stay fit. Exercising helps relax your body and has been shown to relieve mental stress as well. This demand for recreation and leisure service has also stimulate"},{"lang":"en","text":"the economy, as new businesses are created to meet these needs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"下班后去慢跑和去健身房也更受欢迎，因为这些都是便捷的锻炼形式和保持健康的方法。锻炼有助于放松身体，也可以缓解精神压力。这些娱乐和休闲服务的需求也刺激了经济，新的商机伴随着这些需求应运而生。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In sum, working hard is important, but having a good quality of life can actually facilitate your success at work. Knowing when and how to relax should be a part of well-balance lifestyles. Take a walk outdoors, visit the gym, or go jogging. You will find that your time was not wasted, even if it was not spent working in your office."},{"lang":"zh","text":"总之，努力工作是重要的，但拥有好的生活质量实际上可以帮助你在工作上获得成功。懂得何时和如何放松应该是均衡生活方式的一部分。出去户外散步，去健身房，或去慢跑。你会发现即使你不在办公室工作，你的时间也没有被浪费掉。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":244},{"id":"r-人文英语3-6-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"Importance of Learning a Foreign Language","subtitle":"学习外语的重要性","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"There are a number of reasons why we should learn a foreign language. Learning another language is important for both work and travel. It is also important for making real connections with other people. Lastly, it can give us a greater understanding of our own language."},{"lang":"zh","text":"学习外语有很多种原因。学习另外一门语言，对工作和旅游都很重要。想要与其他民族的人进行交流，学习外语也很重要。此外，学习外语还能帮助我们进一步了解自己的母语。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Learning a foreign language would definitely enhance our chances of getting a job. When we work in a foreign country, it will benefit us immensely if we can speak its language. We would be able to work with all different types of employees, and this will give us a long-term career"},{"lang":"en","text":"success."},{"lang":"zh","text":"学习外语肯定会提高我们找到工作的几率。当我们在国外工作时，会讲该国的语言将会非常便利。我们可以与不同类型的员工一起工作，这将带来长期的职业生涯成就。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Speaking a foreign language gives us understanding of a country's culture; it enables us to see how other people see the world around them. If we travel or work in a foreign country, think how much easier everything would be if we could speak the local language. It would be easier to find different places, ask for directions, and even order food."},{"lang":"zh","text":"掌握一门外语可以帮助我们知晓一个国家的文化，了解其他国家人民的世界观。当我们在异国工作或旅行时，会说当地语言可以使事情变得简单。找地方、问路和点餐时都会很方便。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Finally, if we speak a foreign language we will actually improve our own first language. Other languages open our minds to new ways of thinking. For example, Inuits have more words to describe snow and ice as it is such an important part of their lives."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最后，如果能掌握一门外语，我们的母语水平也会有所提升。其他语言会拓展我们的思维方式。例如，因纽特人有更多的词汇来描绘雪和冰，因为冰雪是他们日常生活的重要组成部分。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Language is what makes us human. It is how we share our thoughts with the world. Without language, there would be no way to communicate and express ourselves. The more languages we know, the more ways we have to communicate and express ourselves. 8 This is why learning many languages should be important, and why one language simply won't do."},{"lang":"zh","text":"语言使我们区别于其他动物。语言是我们与世界交流想法的方式。没有语言，我们将无法与人沟通和表达自我。我们懂的语言越多，沟通和表达方式就会越多。这也是我们学习多门语言的重要性，也是为什么学习单一语言所做不到的。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":266},{"id":"r-人文英语3-6-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"English, the Global Language","subtitle":"全球通用语言——英语","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"English is spoken as a native language by around 377 million people, and as a second language by around 375 million speakers in the world. Speakers of English as a second language will soon outnumber those who speak it as a first language. Around 750 million people are believed to speak English as a foreign language. English has an official or a special status in 75 countries with a total population of over 2 billion."},{"lang":"zh","text":"世界上以英语作为母语的人接近3.77 亿, 而作为第二语言的人约有3.75亿人。英语作为第二语言的人数将很快超过作为母语的人数。把英语当成外语的人据说有7.5亿人。英语在75个国家占据一定官方地位或特别地位，约占20亿人口。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The domination of the English language globally is a sure thing. English is the language of international communications, business, tourism, education, science, computer technology, media and the Internet. Surprisingly, 70% of all information stored in the Internet is in English."},{"lang":"zh","text":"英语全球化的主导地位已经不容置疑，英语是国际交流、商务、旅游、科技、电脑技术、媒体和网络等方面通用语言。令人惊讶的是，70% 的网络信息都是用英语存储的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"British colonialism in the 19th century and American capitalism and technological progress in the 20th century were undoubtedly the main causes for the spread of English throughout the world. From the fifteenth century, the British began to sail all over the world and became explorers, colonists"},{"lang":"en","text":"and imperialists. They took the English language to many places. For the last hundred years, the U.S.A. has played a leading role in most parts of the world. The Hollywood film industry also attracted many foreign artists in quest of fame and fortune and the number of American films produced every year soon flooded the market."},{"lang":"zh","text":"19世纪的英国殖民主义以及20世纪的美国资本主义与技术进步，无疑都是推动英语在全球范围内传播的主要原因。15世纪以来，英国人就开始航游世界并成为探索险者、殖民者、帝国主义者。他们将英语传播到许多地区。在上个世纪，美国在世界的大部分地区发挥主导作用。好莱坞蓬勃的电影产业也吸引了许多追逐名利的外国艺术家，每年大量美国影片如洪水般涌入市场。"},{"lang":"en","text":"However, the future of English as a global language will depend very largely on the political, economic, demographic and cultural trends in the world."},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而，英语作为全球语言的未来很大程度上还将取决于全球的政治、经济、人口和文化等方面的发展趋势。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":237},{"id":"r-人文英语3-7-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Free Massive Online Open Courses (MOOCs)","subtitle":"免费大规模在线开放课程（慕课","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A class with hundreds or even thousands of students might sound like a teacher's worst nightmare . But a big idea in higher education these days is Massive Open Online Courses, or MOOCs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一堂课有成千上万学生，这听起来是老师最可怕的噩梦。但是，近来在高等教育领域产生一个伟大构想——大规模在线开放课程，也称慕课。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Some universities offer free, non- credit MOOCs available to anyone in the world. Others charge for courses and provide credits. The idea is still developing. The Massachusetts Institute of Technology started its first MOOC in 2012. The school plans to offer many free, non-credit courses through a project called MITx. Many Chinese universities are beginning to offer free MOOCs now, too."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一些高校向全世界所有人提供免费的无学分在线开放课程。一些高校则提供收费的有学分课程。这个构想仍在不断发展。麻省理工学院于2012年开设了最早的一堂慕课。该校计划通过一个名为MITx的项目，提供大量免费的无学分课程。现在，许多中国高校也开始提供免费慕课。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Nowadays, MOOCs almost cover every topic, like computer science, technology, mechanics, engineering, languages, etc."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如今，慕课几乎涉及所有主题，如计算机科学、技术、机械、工程、语言等。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Generally speaking, there are no formal education requirements for these free online courses. Students watch short videos. Then, they take informal, ungraded quizzes after the videos each week for certain weeks. Quizzes are part of the lecture program to keep students engaged and keep them thinking, for students to be able to check that they understood what was covered. They can repeatedly watch the videos and take the quizzes whenever they want. Students receive homework. They can join online groups to exchange questions and answers about the courses. The teachers hold virtual office hours to answer questions that the students have posted. They also present their own questions and observations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一般来说，这些免费在线课程没有正式的教学要求。学生观看短视频。然后，他们每周参加非正式的不分级测验，并持续几周。小测验是讲座课程的一部分，可以吸引学生参与，不断思考，并且检验自己是否理解了所学内容。他们可以随时反复看录像并做测验。学生也有作业。他们加入在线小组，交流与课程相关的问题和答案。老师们提供虚拟办公时间回答学生发帖中的问题。他们也提出自己的问题和见解。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Some supporters claimed that there are things that we can do better in the online format . We can certainly deliver high-quality education to many students at a much lower cost."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一些支持者声称，有些事情在线情况下可以做得更好。我们一定能够以更低成本为更多学生提供高质量的教育。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":248},{"id":"r-人文英语3-7-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Apple Enters a New Market","subtitle":"苹果进军新市场","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Apple has entered the textbook market. The tech giant introduced iBooks textbooks in 2012 when it announced its iBooks 2 platform. They are digital books in a variety of subjects from astronomyto zoology , science, math, history, geography , etc."},{"lang":"zh","text":"苹果已进军教材市场。这个科技巨头在2012年iBooks 2平台的发布会上正式推出iBooks教科书。这些是数字图书，涉及各种内容，包括天文学、动物学、科学、数学、历史、地理等。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Apple developed its iPad-based textbooks in conjunction with major textbook publishers. The company offers a collection of textbooks for high school students. Apple claims it offers a “new textbook experience” and suggests its interactive iBooks textbooks are “the next chapter in learning”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"苹果公司和主要的教材出版商一起开发了基于iPad的教材。苹果公司已经推出了一套高中电子教材。苹果宣称它提供的是一种“教科书全新体验”，并暗示这种互动式的电子教科书将开启“学习的新篇章”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It sounds like good news for pupils and students. Think of it. No more carrying heavy backpacks full of textbooks. Every textbook you require can be stored on your iPad. No more having to buy expensive textbooks which you will only use for a year or two and then sell or give away."},{"lang":"zh","text":"对于中小学生而言，这听起来是个好消息。试想，不用再背装满课本的沉重的书包。你所需要的所有教科书都可以储存在你的iPad里。也不用再买那些昂贵的课本，这些课本你只会用一两年，然后要么卖掉，要么送人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Instead of boring old textbooks which are quickly out of date you can have an interactive learning experience. You can play videos, examine"},{"lang":"en","text":"geometrical problems in 3D, listen to music and commentary , make notes and mark passages electronically . You can also share stuff on social networking sites with fellow students."},{"lang":"zh","text":"用电子教材代替即将过时的乏味的老式教材，给人一种交互性强的学习体验。你可以播放视频，通过3D形式来研究几何难题，听音乐和评论，做电子笔记和在段落上做标注。你还可以与同学在社交网站分享资料。"},{"lang":"en","text":"And the rest, as they say, is history. Will Apple revolutionize learning? That remains to be seen."},{"lang":"zh","text":"正如他们所说，其他的东西都已经成为历史。那么，苹果会引领学习的革命吗？让我们拭目以待吧！"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":199},{"id":"r-人文英语3-8-1","book":"人文英语3","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Lifelong Learning & Distance Education","subtitle":"终身学习和远程教育","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The term “lifelong learning” is very popular nowadays. It describes the need for people to continue their education and training throughout their lives. Lifelong learning is more and more important for everyone because people are now facing different career choices in changing economies. It is believed lifelong learning is a crucial response to the challenges of the global knowledge economy."},{"lang":"zh","text":"现在，“终身学习”这个词非常流行。这反映了人们对继续教育和培训的终生需求。终身学习对每个人来说都越来越重要，因为在不断变化的经济环境中，人们正面临不同的职业选择。终身学习被认为是应对全球知识经济挑战的关键所在。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Currently, most universities have reacted to the era of lifelong learning by adding new programs and services for adults who seek to combine employment with part-time study. Special arrangements have been developed for these students but the core activity of the university, providing teaching to full-time young undergraduates , often goes on much as before."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当前，为了应对终身学习时代的需求，很多大学都为那些希望将工作和业余学习结合起来的成年人增设新课程和新服务。学校针对这些学生做了特别的教学安排，但是大学的核心任务仍然是为年轻的全日制学生提供教学，和以往一样照常进行。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Lifelong learning is both formal and non-formal; and the boundaries between face-to-face teaching and distance education are increasingly"},{"lang":"en","text":"blurred ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"终身学习既是正式学习，又是非正式学习。同时，面授教学和远程教学的界限变得越来越模糊。"},{"lang":"en","text":"By making learning possible anytime and anywhere, distance education is a powerful tool for supporting lifelong learning. Technology-based teaching is creating new educational systems that anyone from anywhere can access. The key challenge for universities is to evolve from a teacher-centered model of education to a student-centered model. The challenge for governments is that they have to develop new funding approaches and new quality assessment procedures."},{"lang":"zh","text":"远程教育可以让学习随时随地发生，是支持终身学习的强有力工具。以技术为支撑的教学正在创造新的教育体系，任何人在任何地方都可以进行学习。对于大学的主要挑战是从以教师为中心的模式转变为以学生为中心的模式。而各级政府所面临的挑战则是必须建立新的资助方式和新的质量评估流程。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":207},{"id":"r-人文英语3-8-2","book":"人文英语3","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"Lifelong Education in a Learning Society","subtitle":"学习型社会中的终身教育","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"As we enter the 21st century, the information age, your ability to expand your mind and strive for continuing education is critical to your success."},{"lang":"en","text":"By dedicating yourself to lifelong learning, you can leapfrog ahead of your competition."},{"lang":"zh","text":"随着我们进入21 世纪这个信息时代，开拓思维与参与继续教育的能力对于成功至关重要。活到老学到老，你才可以超越你的竞争对手。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The highest paid people in America today work an average of 59 hours per week. They read an average of 2-3 hours per day. They belong to industry associations and organizations that encourage individuals to dedicate themselves to lifelong learning with current information and ideas in their fields. Continuing education for them means that they attend annual meetings and go to every session available that has new insights that can help them to be more effective."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当前，美国收入最高的人群平均每周工作59小时。这些人平均每天阅读2~3小时。他们属于行业协会或组织，鼓励个人致力于终身学习，了解各自领域的最新信息和理念。对他们而言，继续教育意味着参加各种年度会议，出席每一个能带来新理念的会议，这些新理念能帮助他们变得更有效率。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Lifelong learning is the minimum requirement for success in your field. Since information and knowledge in every field is doubling every 2-3 years, this means that your knowledge has to double every 2-3 years as well."},{"lang":"zh","text":"终身学习是你事业成功的最低要求。由于每个领域中的知识和信息每两到三年就增加一倍，这就意味着你的知识也得每两到三年翻倍。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Knowledge is the primary source of value in our world today and your ability to expand your mind and devote yourself to lifelong learning is the key to breaking any success barriers that may be in front of you."},{"lang":"zh","text":"知识是我们当前社会中价值的主要来源，而开拓思维和积极参与终身学习的能力则是清除成功路途上障碍的关键所在。"},{"lang":"en","text":"You can acquire information and strive for lifelong learning by just reaching out your hand and picking it up in the form of books, articles, tapes, face-to-face training, and online courses or MOOCs. I hope you are making room for continuing education in your life."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你只需要从书本、文章、磁带、面授培训、在线课程、慕课等方式中进行选择，便可获取信息，并进行终身学习。我希望你在生活中为继续教育留点空间。"}],"source":"人文英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":232},{"id":"r-人文英语4-1-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"British TV","subtitle":"英国电视","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Television broadcasting started in the United Kingdom in 1936 as a public service free of advertising. Now there is a collection of free and"},{"lang":"en","text":"subscription services over a variety of distribution media, through which there are over 480 channels for consumers as well as on-demand content."},{"lang":"en","text":"There are six main channel owners who are responsible for most viewing. On October 24, 2012, all television broadcasts in the United Kingdom were in a digital format. Digital content is delivered via terrestrial means, satellite and cable as well as over IP."},{"lang":"zh","text":"1936年，电视广播最初作为一项没有广告的公共服务媒体在英国兴起。现在，各种传播媒体可为消费者提供480多个频道及点播内容，其中既有免费服务也有付费服务。有六大频道经营商负责绝大部分电视节目的播出和收视。2012年10月24日，英国所有的电视广播都采用了数码格式。数字内容是通过地面设施、卫星、电缆以及互联网协议传送的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In 1953 the Conservative Government introduced a bill to make arrangements for commercial television. This was opposed very strongly by the Labor and Liberal Parties, but the bill was passed and commercial television now flourishes. The Independent Television Act created an Independent Television Authority, which exercises general supervision."},{"lang":"zh","text":"1953年，保守党政府提出了一项议案，安排设立商业电视。这遭到工党和自由党的强烈反对，但这项议案最终得以通过。现在，商业电视遍地开花，欣欣向荣。独立电视法案促成独立电视管理局的设立，由其行使监管权。"},{"lang":"en","text":"One disadvantage of the present system is that the BBC and Independent Television often both put out programs of the same type at the same time. This forces the viewer to choose between two similar things but not two entirely different forms of entertainment."},{"lang":"zh","text":"现有系统的一个缺点是，BBC和独立电视台经常在同一时段播放相同类型的节目。这迫使观众在两种相似的东西中做选择，而不是两种完全不同的娱乐形式。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In the United Kingdom and the Crown Dependencies, any household watching or recording live television transmissions as they are being broadcast (terrestrial, satellite, cable, or internet) is required to hold a television license. Since April 1, 2010 the annual license fee has been £145.50 for color and £49.00 for black and white. Thus, the license fee made up the bulk of the BBC's total income of £5.102 billion in 2012–2013."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在联合王国和皇家属地，任何通过广播（地面、卫星、有线或互联网）收看或录制直播电视节目的家庭都必须持有电视收视许可证。自2010年4月1日起，彩色电视机和黑白电视机的年度收视许可证费分别为145.5英镑和49英镑。因此，在BBC2012~2013年51.02亿英镑的总收入中，收视许可证费占了其中大部分。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":241},{"id":"r-人文英语4-1-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Graffiti","subtitle":"涂鸦艺术","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Graffiti painting is traditionally a daredevil pursuit . Teenagers dodge security guards to put their names on trains and buses. But over the past decade , graffiti has all but disappeared from Britain's cities. Between 2007 and 2012 the number of incidents of graffiti recorded by the British Transport Police fell by 63%. A survey by the Environment Ministry shows that fewer places are blighted by tags than ever. Graffiti are increasingly confined to sanctioned walls ,such as the Stockwell Ball Courts. In time the practice may die out entirely."},{"lang":"zh","text":"涂鸦传统上是一个冒险的追求。青少年们避开保安人员，把自己的名字涂在火车和公交车上。但在过去十年，涂鸦几乎从英国城市中消失了。2007~2012年，英国交通警察局记录的涂鸦事件下降了63%。环境部的一项调查显示，被乱涂乱画破坏的地方比以前少了。涂鸦越来越被限制在被批准的墙上进行，比如斯托克韦尔球场。最终涂鸦也许会完全消失。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The most obvious reason for the decline in tagging and train-painting is better policing. Numerous CCTV cameras mean it is harder to get away with painting illegally . And punishments are more severe . A generational shift is apparent , too. Fewer teenagers are getting into painting walls. They prefer to play with iPads and video games. Some have gone to art school and want to make money from their paintings. The Internet means that painters can win far more attention by posting pictures online than they can by breaking into a railway yard."},{"lang":"zh","text":"乱涂乱画和火车涂鸦风靡程度下降最主要的原因是政策法规更加完备。非法在墙上绘图越来越难以逃离无处不在的闭路电视监控系统摄像头，相应的惩罚也更加严厉了。代际变化也很明显。现在越来越少的年轻人想参与墙上涂鸦活动。他们更喜欢玩iPad和电子游戏。他们中有一些人去了艺术学校，他们想通过绘画挣钱。网络的普及意味着这些人可以把自己的绘图在线上传，相较于把它们画在铁路调车场，这样更能吸引别人的注意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Taggers and graffiti artists mostly grew up in the 1980s and 1990s. Those men — and almost all men — are now older and less willing to take risks. Graffiti may eventually disappear. But for now the hobby is almost respectable . The former graffiti artists paint abandoned warehouses during the weekend. It has become something to do on a Sunday afternoon — a slightly healthier alternative to sitting and watching football."},{"lang":"zh","text":"涂鸦艺人大都是80或90后。这个群体——大多是男士——现在年纪越来越大，不太愿意冒险了。涂鸦最终可能会消失。但是直至现在，这种爱好仍然受到人们的尊敬。前涂鸦艺术家们会在周末去废弃的仓库墙上大展身手。这已经成为周日下午必做之事——一个比坐着看足球稍微更利于健康的选择。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":245},{"id":"r-人文英语4-2-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Life in the Country","subtitle":"乡村生活","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"I've been living in the country for more than 10 years. It means quietness, privacy , harmony and peace for me."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我在乡下住了10多年了。对我而言，这里意味着安静、私密、和谐和安宁。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Living in the country requires an active lifestyle. It involves activities like doing daily chores , preparing firewood for winter heating, feeding animals including pets and livestock , tending the garden, or securing fences, etc. For me, the most attractive activities are fishing, hunting and hiking. I enjoy seeing what nature has to offer every day through a simple walk down a little trail, or a relaxing drive along the country road with patches of green grass ornamented with wildlife sightings of birds, moose, bears, deer, etc."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在乡下生活需要积极的生活方式。它包括做日常家务、准备过冬取暖的柴火、喂养宠物和牲畜、修整花园或加固栅栏等许多事情。对我来说，最吸引人的活动是钓鱼、打猎和徒步旅行。我享受着大自然每天的恩赐，悠闲地在乡间小道散步，或驱车惬意地行驶在绿意浓浓的乡间公路上，各种鸟、驼鹿、熊、鹿等动物的身影点缀其中。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Living a country life helps us appreciate some of the simpler things, things that make us feel good about ourselves and the world. It may be just a get-together on a Saturday at the local farmers market, or a project or a problem that the community might pull together to help solve. I have participated in a few community projects, like dealing with out-of-control grass fires, a roof that collapsed from a large snow fall, or even helping a recent widow with fire wood for the winter. Sometimes I am surprised by how much benefit we receive from helping others and as for this community I can't say enough."},{"lang":"zh","text":"乡村生活使我们学会欣赏一些简单的东西，这些东西让我们感受到生活和这个世界的美好。它或许仅仅是周六当地农贸市场里的一次小聚，或是社区合力解决的一个事情或者问题。我曾参加过一些社区活动，比如处理失控的草地火灾、修葺被大雪压塌的屋顶，甚至帮助刚失去丈夫的妇女准备过冬的柴火。有时我会感叹帮助他人会使我们受益良多，而社区叫我受益的地方更是多得举不胜举了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"I really enjoy living a country life. I know it's not for everyone, but I know it's for me."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我真的很享受乡村生活。我知道这不一定适合每个人，但却适合我。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":235},{"id":"r-人文英语4-2-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Turning Trash into Art","subtitle":"变废物为艺术","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"I have developed a habit of collecting trash. I leave my house around midnight a few times a week and walk around the city gathering what I find: old toys, used appliances , broken furniture, the list goes on. I usually have no problem filling the two bags I bring with me. The next day, I sort through what I collected and make two piles: a useable one and an unuseable one. I take the useable pile to my studio and start creating art."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我已经养成了收集废物的习惯。我每周都会有几次在半夜离开家去城里到处转转。我将自己收集的东西列成一张表：旧玩具、用过的电器、家具碎片等。我经常能轻松地把随身携带的两个包装满。第二天，我把收集到的废物分成两堆：可用的和不可用的。我把可用的一堆拿到工作室，开始进行艺术创作。"},{"lang":"en","text":"What other people see as garbage , I see as potential art . Of course, it's not art in the state I find it. Through creativity and trial-and-error , it becomes art. The pieces I create are mostly animals and robot. sculptures The process I go through from the raw materials to a finished piece is not complex at all. First, I take the materials I have collected and play around with different combinations and configurations to see if I can find some inspiration. I typically do this for a few days or a week before something “ clicks ” and I have an idea about what I want to create. After that, it is only a matter of realizing my vision ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"别人视为垃圾，在我看来却是潜在的艺术品。当然，起初我拿到这些东西时，它们可不是艺术品，得通过创造和反复试验才能变成艺术品。我创作的作品大多是动物和机器人雕塑。从原材料到成品的过程一点也不复杂。首先，我把收集的材料排列成不同的组合并进行不同的布局，寻找灵感。这件事我通常会做上几天或一周的时间，直到茅塞顿开，我会弄明白自己的创意所在。剩下的就是去实现我的想法了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"I also create more practical, useable art out of the trash I find. Some examples include vases made from glass bottles, lamps made from old appliances like irons or blow dryers, and pencil boxes made from plastic containers. I take these items to the local market and sell them. A few times a year I get invited to display my favorite sculptures at exhibitions . Overall, I couldn't be happier. I am doing something I love, making a good amount of money, and showing others both useful and artistic possibilities of trash."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我还从发现的废物中创造了更实用、更有用的艺术品。比如玻璃瓶制成的花瓶、用熨斗或吹风机等旧电器制成的灯，还有用塑料容器制成的铅笔盒。我把这些东西拿到当地市场去卖。每年人们都会邀请我做几次展览，展示我最喜欢的雕塑作品。总之，没有比这更令我高兴的了。做喜欢做的事，还能赚很多钱，同时也向人们展示废物变成有用的东西和成为艺术品的可能性。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":293},{"id":"r-人文英语4-3-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"Creating Equal Access to Education","subtitle":"造平等的受教育机会","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The celebration of International Women's Day (IWD) in 2011 was special as it marked the 100th anniversary of IWD. The United Nations' theme for the 2011 IWD was “Equal access to education, training and science and technology: Pathway to decent work for women”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2011年国际妇女节（IWD）的庆祝活动是特别的，因为它标志着国际妇女节100周年。联合国2011年国际妇女节的主题是“平等获得教育、培训和科学技术：为女性提供获得体面工作的途径”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"One hundred years ago, gender equality and women's empowerment were largely radical ideas. One hundred years later, there has been significant progress in women's empowerment and participation through determined advocacy , practical action and enlightened policy making. However, in too many countries and societies, women's social position is still low and lots of women are still trapped by poverty , discrimination , unemployment, illiteracy and violence ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一百年前，两性平等和女性权益基本上是激进的想法。一百年后，通过坚决倡导、实际行动和制定开明政策，女性在权益与参与方面取得了显著进步。然而，在许多国家和社会中，女性的社会地位仍然很低，许多女性仍然受困于贫穷、歧视、失业、文盲和暴力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As a basic human right, education is a key driver of economic growth and social change and the basis of women's empowerment. The global economy is increasingly knowledge-driven, and requires an educated workforce able to apply the existing technology and to develop new science and technologies to combat poverty and adapt to emerging issues."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为一项基本人权，教育是经济增长和社会变革的重要驱动力，也是赋予女性权益的基础。全球经济日益受知识驱动，社会需要受过教育的劳动者能够应用现有技术和开发新的科学技术，以消除贫困并应对新出现的问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As education is the key to greater empowerment for women ,investing in women and girls through the education sector has therefore a positive effect on the well-being of their families, their communities and nations. Strengthening the bridges between education, training, science and technology and the labor market is important in order to promote equal opportunity to decent employment for women."},{"lang":"zh","text":"由于教育是赋予女性更大权益的关键，因此，教育部门为妇女和女孩投资会对她们的家庭、社区和国家产生积极影响。为了促进女性拥有体面就业的平等机会，加强教育、培训、科学技术与劳动力市场之间的沟通是非常重要的。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":220},{"id":"r-人文英语4-3-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Equal Access to Education Means an Equal Society","subtitle":"平等社会意味着平等受教育","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The National Union of Students (NUS) welcomes the news that greater numbers of black and disabled students are studying at UK universities, but there is still a lot of work to be done on widening access, writes the union's president, Gemma Tumelty."},{"lang":"zh","text":"全国学生联合会（NUS）高兴地得知将有更多的黑人和残疾学生在英国大学学习的消息。“但在扩大入学机会方面仍有很多工作要做，”工会主席杰玛·塔梅尔蒂写道。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A recent Department of Communities and Local Government (DCLG) equalities review showed that significant numbers of potential students felt their disability was a major barrier to accessing higher education (HE). This is simply unacceptable ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"社区与地方政府部近期的一份平等审查表明，大量潜在的学生感觉他们的残疾是他们进入高等教育的障碍。这简直是不可接受的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Equality and diversity is not entirely a “numbers game” and before too much praise is given we need to hear more from non-traditional students, not just about their experience of accessing higher education but also going through the system."},{"lang":"zh","text":"平等和多元化并不完全是一种“数字游戏”，在大肆赞扬之前，我们需要多听非传统学生的意见，不仅听他们讲接受高等教育的经验，还听他们讲述高等教育的过程。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Equality in society is absolutely , and fundamentally , linked to equality in access to education."},{"lang":"zh","text":"社会平等，从根本上讲，与获得平等的教育有关。"},{"lang":"en","text":"For many students, university is the place where they will be first exposed to different cultures and different people. As well as fighting for better access, the NUS wants to see diversity properly valued and promoted within the student experience. Many pay lip service to the value of diversity, but is this recognized and promoted as a core asset to those who go through the HE system?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"对于许多学生来说，大学是他们首次接触不同文化和不同人的地方。除了力争提供更好的机会，全国学联希望看到多元化在学生体验中得到应有的重视和推崇。许多人口头上对多元化的价值表示支持，但是对于那些接受高等教育的人，它能否作为核心价值而被认可和倡导呢？"},{"lang":"en","text":"Equality in society can be promoted by equality and diversity at university. But the benefits of university as a positive, diverse environment must be seen by students as adding “value” as much as any other factor before the numbers game is really won by the champions of diversity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"大学里的平等和多元化可以促进社会平等。但是在支持多元化的人占多数之前，学生们必须看到大学的好处，它是一个积极的多元的环境，可以和其他任何因素一样增加“价值”。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":245},{"id":"r-人文英语4-4-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Quality Education and Education for All","subtitle":"素质教育与全民教育","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Educators , parents, students and community members in Miami-Dade and Broward counties are joining together to reclaim the promise of public education. This important effort is co-sponsored by the American Federation of Teachers and National Education Association and is a vital step forward for our schools in South Florida."},{"lang":"zh","text":"迈阿密-戴德县和布鲁瓦德县的教育工作者、家长、学生和社区成员正在联合起来要求履行公共教育的承诺。这项重要的工作是由美国教师联合会和国家教育协会共同发起的，是南佛罗里达州学校向前迈进的重要一步。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Educators, parents and community members are working together to provide all students with the opportunity to attend quality public schools. Equal access to a public education is a right that should be afforded to all students. We cannot expect our students to succeed if they do not have the right tools to do so."},{"lang":"zh","text":"教育工作者、家长和社区成员正在共同努力，为所有学生提供就读高质量公立学校的机会。平等接受公共教育应该是为所有学生提供的一项权利。如果学生没有正确的工具，我们就不能指望他们能成功。"},{"lang":"en","text":"I've been working as a teacher and lawyer for many years ,so I know firsthand the obstacles teachers and students face every day. There is no simple solution for our public schools' challenges, but one thing is for sure: We must all work together in order to better our schools. There is no time to waste because the future of schools and students is on the line. We must all get involved now."},{"lang":"zh","text":"多年来，我一直从事教师和律师工作，所以我知道老师和学生每天面对的障碍是什么。对于公立学校的挑战，没有简单的解决办法，但有一件事情是可以确定的：我们必须共同努力，以使我们的学校变得更好。时间不容浪费，因为学校和学生的未来已经处于危险之中。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Educators need proper teaching resources in order for students to achieve. Just like in other careers, educators should receive ample opportunities for professional development."},{"lang":"zh","text":"教育工作者需要有适合的教学资源，让学生能够获得。就像其他职业一样，教育工作者应获得充分的职业发展机会。"},{"lang":"en","text":"South Florida teachers and support staff are doing the best they can, but we need everyone to actively participate in the educational process."},{"lang":"zh","text":"南佛罗里达州的教师和支持者正在为此尽最大努力，但我们也需要每个人都积极参与教育过程。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Florida receives the least amount of funding for public education compared to nearly all other states, but that will never stop our drive for success. We still have hope for our schools and students because the nation's public education system makes up the foundation of our future."},{"lang":"zh","text":"与所有其他州相比，佛罗里达州获得的公共教育的财政支持最少，但这不会阻止我们对成功的追求。我们对学校和学生仍然抱有希望，因为国家的公共教育体系是我们未来的基础。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":271},{"id":"r-人文英语4-4-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"The Importance of Quality Education","subtitle":"保证教育质量的重要性","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Education and academic quality can mean different things to different people, depending on their perspective , role and context and, in part because of this, quality is notoriously difficult to evaluate. The question of how to do this has been pursued for many years."},{"lang":"zh","text":"教育与学术质量，对于不同的人来说含义不同，这取决于各自的角度、职责与环境，也正是这部分原因，众所周知，质量难以测量。多年来，人们一直在这方面进行着探索。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Nevertheless, the goal of improving educational quality is agreed by all and stimulated further by the recent worldwide economic downturn and the need to counteract the impact of the crisis on economic growth and prepare for economic recovery."},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而，提高教育质量的目标是大家一致认可的。同时，近来全球经济的下滑，以及抵制经济危机对经济增长的影响和复苏经济的需求也进一步推动了这个目标。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As the World Bank and UNESCO said 10 years ago: “The quality of knowledge generated within higher education institutions, and its availability to the wider economy, is becoming increasingly critical to national competitiveness . ” They also rightly emphasized that “A strong research system at the national level opens up the possibility that substantial additional public benefits can be realized through international links."},{"lang":"zh","text":"正如世界银行和联合国教科文组织十年前所说的那样：“高等教育机构所产生的有质量的知识及其在更加广泛经济体内的应用，对于国家竞争力来讲，越来越起到至关重要的作用。”他们也恰如其分地强调“国家层面的强大的研究系统可以通过国际联系，为大幅增加额外的公共福利提供可能性。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"This is precisely why Chinese students and academics should contribute to these global benefits, reforming and improving evaluation systems for educational and academic quality. Original and good research, especially in science, economics and social sciences, has a trickle-down effect on society. And it offers additional benefits even without international links, though international collaboration and exchange of the best evaluation policy and practice can bring substantial advantages to all partners in relation to lessons learned elsewhere."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这正是为什么中国学生和学者应该为了全球的利益做出贡献，同时改革和完善教育和学术质量的评价体系。原创的优秀的研究成果，尤其在自然科学、经济学和社会学领域，都会对社会产生涓滴效应。这些研究即便不与国际合作，也会带来诸多益处，但是国际合作以及最优评价体系的交流和实践会给所有合作伙伴在分享经验教训方面带来巨大的优势。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":217},{"id":"r-人文英语4-5-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"The Communication Model-Interpersonal Communication","subtitle":"交流模式——人际沟通","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"All communication begins with the sender and ends with the receiver. The sender is responsible for successful conveyance . The sender's personality , beliefs, cultural and educational background all influence the message and it is important for the sender to be aware of this as he or she is encoding the message. Simply put, encoding is translating information into symbols that represent the ideas or concepts of the message that needs sending. These symbols are usually words in written or spoken form. To ensure successful communication, the sender should know as much about his or her audience — the receiver — as possible in order to focus on and support the encoding process."},{"lang":"zh","text":"所有的交流都始于发送者，终于接收者。发送者的主要责任是负责成功的传递。发送者的个性、信仰、文化和教育背景都会影响信息的传播，因此，当发送者对信息进行编码时，意识到这一点非常重要。简单地说，编码就是把信息翻译成包含它需要传达的观点或者概念的符号。这些符号通常是书面或口头形式的。为了确保沟通的成功，发送者应该尽可能多地了解他或她的听众，即接收者，以便接收者能够集中精力并且支持编码过程的完成。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In addition to this awareness of self and encoding, the sender must choose the proper channel for conveying the message. Using the wrong channel may result in miscommunication. Like the sender, receivers are influenced by internal factors: their personality, their receptivity to the message or their relationship to the sender. Additionally, their current feelings, mood, or state of mind can affect a message. Once the message moves through the channel, the receiver then decodes it. The receiver uses his or her own experience and the context of the message to interpret its meaning."},{"lang":"zh","text":"除了要了解自身和编码问题以外，发送者必须要为信息的传递选择正确的渠道。使用了错误的渠道有可能会导致沟通有误。与发送者一样，接收者也受到内部因素的影响，包括他们的个性、对信息的接收能力或者他们与发送者之间的关系。除此之外，他们当下的感受、心情或者心理状态都能够影响信息的接收。一旦信息通过渠道传播过去，接收者就会对信息进行解码。接收者用自己的经验和所掌握的相关信息对信息进行解读。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Feedback is the return message from the receiver to the sender.It is feedback that enables the sender to know whether the message was received successfully or not. Therefore it is essential to the communication process."},{"lang":"zh","text":"反馈就是接收者返回给发送者的信息。正是反馈让发送者获知信息是否已经被成功接收，因此，它对整个交流过程至关重要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This process, though very common, is fraught with potential breakdown at every turn. Spoken or written language is inherently easy to misinterpret. In conclusion, effective and successful communication takes place when the message is successfully received and the receiver provides the sender with desirable feedback."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这个过程虽然很常见，但却很容易出现联系中断。口头或者书面的语言本身就很容易被误解。总之，当消息被成功接收，接收者向发送者提供了满意的反馈时，沟通才是有效和成功的。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":283},{"id":"r-人文英语4-5-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"The Importance of Intercultural Communication in the Workplace","subtitle":"跨文化交际在职场中的重要性","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Para 1 Intercultural communication跨文化交际"},{"lang":"en","text":"Intercultural communication refers to messages transmitted between members of two or more different societies. Effective intercultural communication helps firms avoid conflict, prevent misunderstandings, and foster respect."},{"lang":"zh","text":"跨文化交际是指在两个或者多个不同社会背景之间进行的信息传递。有效的跨文化交际能够帮助公司避免冲突，防止误解并且培养相互尊重之风。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 2 Avoiding conflict避免冲突"},{"lang":"en","text":"The workplace is growing more diverse every day. Managers can not assume that what they find inoffensive will also be inoffensive to their subordinates . A lack of sensitivity can lead to claims of discrimination or harassment , which costs firms big money. Intercultural communication involves exercising sensitivity and tact to avoid such conflicts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"工作场所每天都在变得越来越多样化。领导者不能认为不冒犯自己的事情也不会冒犯自己的下属。缺乏敏感度就可能会导致歧视或伤害方面的投诉，这会使公司损失一大笔钱。跨文化交际需要运用敏感性和机智来避免这些冲突。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 3 The inexactitude of language语言的不精确"},{"lang":"en","text":"We human beings have developed language to communicate ideas to one another. Still, our language represents an imperfect form of communication. Sometimes, words can not accurately convey an idea, because the information might be highly complex. Also, a concept that exists in one culture or language might not be part of another. Effective intercultural communication tries to bridge language gaps as effectively as possible so that everyone at the workplace finds themselves on the same page."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们人类已经发明了语言来互相交流思想。尽管如此，我们的语言是一种不完美的交流方式。有的时候，言语无法准确地表达一个想法，因为有时这个信息非常复杂。而且，在一种文化或者语言中存在的概念可能在另一种语言中并不存在。有效的跨文化沟通会尽可能有效地弥合语言鸿沟，使工作场所里的每个人都能达成共识。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 4 Preventing misunderstandings防止误解"},{"lang":"en","text":"Given the inexactitude of language, misunderstandings can frequently arise between people from different cultures when they exchange information. Idioms often become lost in translation. For example, the English expression “to shoulder responsibility” translates into Swedish as “be a man for your hat”. Intercultural communication does not rely on expressions native to a particular language that could lead to confusion; rather, it relies on clear messages that all parties understand."},{"lang":"zh","text":"鉴于语言的不精确性，不同文化背景的人们之间进行信息交换时常常会产生误解。习语在翻译时常常会使人迷惑。例如，英语“承担责任”翻译成瑞典语就成了“自己的帽子自己戴”。跨文化交际依赖的不是某一种语言所固有的表达方式，那样做会引起困惑。相反地，它依赖的是各方都能理解的清晰的信息。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para 5 Fostering respect培养尊重"},{"lang":"en","text":"Communication happens differently in various cultures. What one society finds acceptable may be unacceptable to another. When coworkers from different cultures do not take these differences into account, not only does communication suffer but conflicts come to the fore. Effective intercultural communication does not try to ignore societal differences; rather, it respects the variations among the human race and enables people to transmit information clearly."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不同文化中的交流方式是不同的。一个社会所能接受的表达或许是另一个社会所不能接受的。如果不同文化背景的同事们不考虑这些差异，他们之间不仅交流会受到影响，而且还会发生冲突。有效的跨文化交际不是要尝试忽视社会差异，而是要尊重人类之间的差异，使人们能够清楚地传递信息。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":305},{"id":"r-人文英语4-6-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"Social Worker Cover Letter","subtitle":"社会工作者求职信","paragraphs":[{"lang":"zh","text":"James Bush詹姆斯·布什"},{"lang":"zh","text":"35 West 9 Avenue第九大道西35号"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Pensacola, FL23506彭萨科拉，佛罗里达州23506"},{"lang":"zh","text":"P: (03) 86661234电话：(03) 86661234"},{"lang":"zh","text":"M: 0651 222555手机：0651 222555"},{"lang":"en","text":"E: james.bush@hotmail.com.us.电子邮箱:james.bush@hotmail.com.us."},{"lang":"zh","text":"[Date][日期]"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Nick C. Brown尼克·C.ˑ布朗"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Hiring Manger人事部经理"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Saint Louis Mental Health Service圣路易斯精神健康服务中心"},{"lang":"zh","text":"16 Mary Street玛丽街16号"},{"lang":"zh","text":"River Dale, IL 566077河谷区，伊利诺伊州566077"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Dear Mr. Brown,尊敬的布朗先生，"},{"lang":"en","text":"I wish to apply for the position of Social Worker as advertised on seek.com.au. Please find my résumé attached ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我想应聘在seek.com.au 网上刊登的社工职位。随信附上我的简历。"},{"lang":"en","text":"For almost two years I have worked as Mental Health Case Manager for TrueCare and their Housing and Accommodation Support Initiative . During the time I have proven my ability to work with an interdisciplinary team, and also developed interpersonal skills and strong professional relationships with clients, including individuals, families and community groups. In my work I have acquired a thorough understanding of the Mental Health Act of 2014 in relation to social work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为精神健康项目经理，我在真爱中心及他们的住房住宿支援委员会工作了近两年。在此期间，我证明了自己同跨学科团队协作的能力，并且提高了人际交往技能，与个人、家庭和社区群体等客户建立了良好的业务关系。在工作中，我对涉及社会工作的2014《心理健康法》有了一个深刻的理解。"},{"lang":"en","text":"My duties have included providing psychosocial support to clients, in the form of one-onone counseling as well as group therapy; developing and overseeing treatment plans for clients; advising family caregivers; and consulting with doctors, therapists and medical professionals. I was awarded with the New Employee Achievement Award for my work on a difficult case in 2015. My strong verbal and written communication skills have been well utilized in this role and I have also demonstrated solid organizational skills in my case management."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我的工作职责包括为顾客提供社会心理支持，有一对一专业咨询，也有集体心理治疗；设计和监督顾客的治疗方案；为家庭关爱者提供建议；向医生、治疗专家及医疗专业人士进行咨询。2015年，我处理了一件棘手的案子，被授予新员工成就奖。在工作中，我的较强的口头和书面沟通技能得到了发挥，在案件的处理过程中，我也展示了很好的组织能力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"I have a strong desire to make a positive difference in people's lives and I believe I would be an asset to Saint Louis Mental Health Service if given the opportunity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我非常渴望能在人们的生活中发挥积极的作用。如果能给我机会的话，对于圣路易斯精神健康服务中心来说，我将会是一个有用之人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If you require more information please contact me at the phone numbers above. I am available for interviews and hope to hear from you soon."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果您需要更多信息，请通过上面的电话号码与我联系。我可以随时面试，期待会很快收到您的回复。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Yours sincerely您真诚的，"},{"lang":"zh","text":"James Bush[签名] 詹姆斯·布什"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":245},{"id":"r-人文英语4-6-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"History of Social Work","subtitle":"社会工作的历史","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Charity is a concept which dates back to Biblical times, when helping the poor was something that rich people basically did to make themselves feel good. Social work has its roots in charity, as it originally began around the time of the industrial revolution when there were many poor people and society was seeking a way of dealing with the poor and social problems. Although social work began as charity work, it has expanded a lot and needs to be seen from a completely different perspective."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“慈善”这一概念可以追溯到圣经时代，那时帮助穷人是富人基本上都做的事情，以此来使他们自己有成就感。社会工作起源于慈善，它最初开始于工业革命时期，那时有许多穷人，社会寻求一种解决穷人和社会问题的途径。尽管社会工作源于慈善工作，然而它的意义已经有了很大的扩展，需要以一个全新的视角来看待。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Modern-day social work deals not only with poverty and the subsequent problems, but also with the problems arising from various types of “social fear” (“social phobias ”) and discrimination such as sexism , racism , and discrimination against an individual due to his age, or mental or physical disabilities. Social workers deal with the consequences of these discriminations as well as consequences that arise from sexual abuse, drug abuse, and various other problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"现代的社会工作不仅要处理贫穷及其引发的问题，还要应对由社会恐惧和歧视导致的各种问题，诸如由性别、种族以及个体的年龄、精神或身体疾病导致的种种歧视问题。社会工作者需要处理这些歧视导致的结果及性虐待、吸毒及各种其他问题导致的结果。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Social work provides an important service to society. Individuals and families in need of help are the focus of it, and are referred to as clients. Social workers help clients live a productive life in their own community. In order to reach this goal, they often enlist the assistance of family members, relatives, local religious leaders, and other influential members of the community.Although institutionalization may be necessary at times, it is a temporary solution. Social workers usually serve in the front line, and reach out to the clients soon after problems occur. The goal is to help clients return to normal life in a natural setting."},{"lang":"zh","text":"社会工作为社会提供重要的服务，主要帮助那些需要帮助的家庭和个人，他们被称为当事人。社会工作者帮助当事人在他们自己的社区过上富有成效的生活。为达到这一目的，他们常常寻求家庭成员、亲戚、地方宗教领袖及社区其他有影响力成员的援助。尽管有时制度化或许是必要的，但这只是暂时的解决办法。社会工作者常常服务在一线，在问题发生后能很快帮助当事人。其目的就是帮助当事人回归自然环境中的正常生活。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":264},{"id":"r-人文英语4-7-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"A Civil Complaint","subtitle":"民事起诉状","paragraphs":[{"lang":"zh","text":"To: Guangzhou People's Court呈送：广州人民法院"},{"lang":"en","text":"Plaintiff : Handcup Marketing原告：Handcup销售部"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Domicile : No. 33, 4th Road, New York住址：纽约第四大道33号"},{"lang":"en","text":"Legal Representative : Qing Su法定代表人：秦苏"},{"lang":"en","text":"Position : Manager of Handcup Marketing职务：Handcup销售部经理"},{"lang":"en","text":"Defendant : South China Corporation被告：中国南方合作公司"},{"lang":"en","text":"Domicile: No. 21 Binjiang Nan Road, Guangzhou住址：广州滨江南路21号"},{"lang":"en","text":"Legal Representative: Bai Mei法定代表人：白梅"},{"lang":"en","text":"Position: manager of the South China Corporation职务：中国南方合作公司经理"},{"lang":"zh","text":"CLAIMS :请求事项："},{"lang":"en","text":"1．To order the Defendant to pay to the Plaintiff 18,000,000 RMB, including 15,000,000 RMB for the dispatched products and 3,000,000 RMB for the interest .1．判令被告向原告支付人民币18 000 000元，包括15 000 000元人民币的货款以及3 000 000元人民币的利息；"},{"lang":"en","text":"2．To order the Defendant to pay for the court fees .2．判令由被告承担诉讼费用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"FACTS AND REASONS:事实和理由："},{"lang":"en","text":"The defendant is the plaintiff's distributor in Southern China. From September 2010 to October 2011, the plaintiff issued all kinds of products worth 15,000,000 RMB to the defendant.(see Exhibit I)"},{"lang":"zh","text":"被告是原告在中国东南区的批发商。从2010年9月至2011年10月，原告向被告发放价值15 000 000元人民币的各种货物。（见证据1）"},{"lang":"en","text":"Each of the said transactions was signed and received by the defendant (see Exhibit II). Although the plaintiff had repeatedly requested, the defendant failed to pay the debt on time.每笔交易均由被告正式签署和接受（见证据2）。尽管原告多次要求，但被告仍然没有按时付款。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The indebtedness arising out of the transactions between the plaintiff and the defendant shall be under the legal power of Chinese laws. The defendant refused to accept mediation .The plaintiff is now facing huge economic loss (see Exhibit III). Therefore, in accordance with relevant Chinese laws and regulations, the defendant should bear corresponding civil responsibility ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"原告与被告之间的债务纠纷应该适用中国法律。被告拒绝接受调解。原告现在面临着巨大的经济损失（见证据3）。因此，依据中国有关法律法规，被告应承担相应的民事责任。"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to Articles 106 and 112 in General Principles of the Civil Law of the PRC , Article 108 in Civil Procedure Law of the PRC and other related laws and regulations, the plaintiff hereby files this case with the court for your adjudication ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据《中华人民共和国民法通则》第106条和第112条，以及《中华人民共和国民事诉讼法》第108条和其他相关法律和规章，原告向法院提起诉讼，要求判决。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Plaintiff: Handcup Marketing原告： Handcup销售部"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Date: May 14, 2012日期：2012年5月14日"},{"lang":"en","text":"ATTACHMENTS:附件："},{"lang":"en","text":"1．One copy of the plaintiff's business license; 1．附件1 原告营业执照复印件"},{"lang":"en","text":"2．One copy of the original Certificate of the Legal Representative; 2．附件2 法定代表人资格原件复印件"},{"lang":"zh","text":"3．One copy of the original Power of Attorney; 3．附件3 授权委托书原件复印件"},{"lang":"en","text":"4．Exhibit I: Invoices for each transaction; 4．附件4 交易发票"},{"lang":"en","text":"5．Exhibit II: Receipts for each transaction; 5．附件5 交易收据"},{"lang":"en","text":"6．Exhibit III: List of losses. 6．附件6 损失明细单"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":261},{"id":"r-人文英语4-7-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"An Answer to a Civil Complaint","subtitle":"民事答辩状","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Respondent : People's Hospital答辩人：人民医院"},{"lang":"en","text":"Address: No. 1, Binhai Road, Binhai City地址：滨海市滨海路1号"},{"lang":"en","text":"The following answer is given to Zhang Hua's claim for personal-injury compensation by the People's Hospital:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"就张华要求人民医院人身损害赔偿一案，现提出如下答辩意见："},{"lang":"en","text":"1．The respondent does not have a direct contractual relationship with Zhang Hua. Zhang Hua had an oral contract to remove the high-voltage meter cabinet with Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company on June 10, 2008. He was assigned by Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company and therefore has no direct contractual relationship with the respondent."},{"lang":"zh","text":"答辩人与张华不存在直接的合同关系。张华与滨海第二建筑安装公司在2008年6月10日就移动高压仪表箱达成口头协议。他受雇于滨海第二建筑安装公司，因此与被告没有直接的合同关系。"},{"lang":"en","text":"2．Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company should be responsible for compensating Zhang Hua for the following reasons. Firstly, according to PRC laws and relevant judicial interpretations , Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company shall be responsible for any injury employees suffered in the contract performance . Secondly, Zhang Hua seriously violated the overtime procedure in removing the high-voltage meter cabinet and failed to pay due attention thereto ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"滨海第二建筑安装公司应该负责对张华的伤害赔偿，具体理由如下：首先，根据中华人民共和国法律和相关司法解释，滨海第二建筑安装公司应对其职工在履行合同的范围内所受到的伤害承担责任；其次，张华在移动高压仪表箱的时候严重违反了操作程序，没有给予应有的注意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"3．The respondent shall not be responsible for compensating the injuries of Zhang Hua. According to the General Principles of the Civil Law, any person engaged in highly dangerous operations shall be responsible for compensation. In this case, the respondent entered into a contract with Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company, whereby the source of high danger shifted to Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company. Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company became the subject of the dangerous operation, and therefore any damages caused in the contract performance by Binhai No. 2 Construction and Installation Company have no connection with the respondent."},{"lang":"zh","text":"答辩人对张华的伤害赔偿不应承担责任。根据《中华人民共和国民法通则》的规定，任何从事高度危险作业的单位，对其员工的人身损害应负赔偿责任。在这种情况下，答辩人与滨海第二建筑安装公司达成合约，这样，高危险源就转移到了滨海第二建筑安装公司。滨海第二建筑安装公司成为该危险作业物的责任主体，因此任何与滨海第二建筑安装公司履行合同中所造成的伤害都与答辩人无关。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Therefore, People's Hospital is not liable for compensating the defendant. We hereby request the court to reject the plaintiff's action according to law. 因此，滨海人民医院不应承担赔偿。请贵院依法驳回原告起诉。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"To:此致"},{"lang":"en","text":"Binhai City Intermediate People's Court滨海市中级人民法庭"},{"lang":"en","text":"Respondent: Binhai People's Court答辩人：人民医院"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Date: May 10, 2011 2011年5月10日"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":277},{"id":"r-人文英语4-8-1","book":"人文英语4","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Terrorist Suspects in the 911 Attacks 9·11”","subtitle":"恐怖袭击案嫌犯","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"NEW YORK — The five men facing trial in the Sept. 11 attacks will plead not guilty. They would state their criticisms of US foreign policy, the lawyer for one of the defendants said Sunday."},{"lang":"zh","text":"纽约——涉嫌“9·11”袭击案中的5名男子在审判中将做无罪辩护。周日，其中一名被告的辩护律师说，他们将陈述他们对美国外交政策的谴责。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Scott Fenstermaker, the lawyer for accused terrorist Ali Abd al-Aziz Ali, said the men would not deny their role in the 2001 attacks but “would explain what happened and why they did it.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为其中一名被指控的恐怖主义者——阿济兹阿里的律师，史科特•范斯德梅克尔表示，这些男子不会否认他们在2001年袭击中扮演的角色，但是他们会解释具体发生了什么以及他们为何要这样做。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ali and four other men are accused of killing nearly 3,000 people in the nation's deadliest terrorist attack. The US Justice Department announced earlier this month that they will face a civilian federal trial just blocks from the World Trade Center site."},{"lang":"zh","text":"阿里和其他四个人被指控在美国的致命恐怖袭击中杀害了近3000人。美国司法部在本月初宣布这五名男子将在位于世贸中心遗址的街区上接受联邦审判。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ali is also known as Ammar al-Baluchi. He is a nephew of the claimed 9/11 planner, Khalid Sheikh Mohammed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"阿里又名阿马尔•奥尔巴鲁奇。他是“9·11”事件的策划者哈立德·谢赫·穆罕默德的侄儿。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Mohammed, Ali and the others will explain “their assessment of American foreign policy,” Fenstermaker said."},{"lang":"zh","text":"范斯德梅克尔表示，穆罕默德、阿里以及其他男子将阐述他们对美国外交政策的评价。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Their assessment is negative,” he said."},{"lang":"zh","text":"他说：“他们的评价是否定的。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fenstermaker met with Ali last week at the US prison at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba. He has not spoken with the others. But he said the men have discussed the trial among themselves."},{"lang":"zh","text":"上周，范斯德梅克尔在古巴关塔那摩湾的美国监狱里与阿里相见。他没有与其他四人交谈。但是，他说，这些男子已经讨论了这次审判。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fenstermaker was first quoted in The New York Times in Sunday's editions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"《纽约时报》在周日的版面上第一时间引述了范斯德梅克尔的话。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Critics of Attorney General Eric Holder decided to try the men in a New York City civilian courthouse . It has warned that the trial would provide the defendants with a propaganda platform ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"对美国司法部长埃里克·霍尔德在纽约民事法庭审判这些男子的决定，批评者警告审判将会给被告提供一个鼓动宣传的平台。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Dean Boyd, a spokesman for the Department of Justice, said Sunday that while the men may attempt to use the trial to express their views, “we believe the courts and the federal judge may govern the trial. The course of justice will be led appropriately and with minimal break, as federal courts have done in the past.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"美国司法部发言人迪安·博伊德称，尽管这些男子试图利用审判来表达他们的观点，但“我们相信法庭和联邦法官会控制审判。像过去一样，联邦法院会合理引导法庭进程，尽量减少中断”。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":281},{"id":"r-人文英语4-8-2","book":"人文英语4","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"Alternative Legal Billing — Win Strategies","subtitle":"可供选择的律师付费方式——取胜策略","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Hourly billing is the best way to be charged for legal services. About 95 percent of lawyers still perform their legal work on an hourly basis. If you want something better than the old “ bill by the hour ” deal, try presenting one of these billing structures."},{"lang":"zh","text":"按时计费是法律服务的最佳收费方式。大约95%的律师仍采用这种方式为自己的法律工作收费。如果你想找比传统的“按时计费”更好的方法，可以尝试下面的某种计费方式。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Project billing for routine issues常规项目计费"},{"lang":"en","text":"If your legal needs include large but repetitive tasks, consider a flat-fee approach. Once you get a project billing estimate, don't hesitate to shop around to compare prices and services with other law firms . A firm may provide a better deal if it expects future work from your company."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你的法律业务，包括数量大并且重复性的任务，可以考虑固定收费的方式。一旦得到项目大致报价，就抓紧时间了解情况，与其他法律事务所的报价和服务进行比较。如果事务所期望与你进行未来的合作，它会提供一个合理的报价。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Results-oriented options结果导向选择"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Pay-according-to-success” is one choice. It considers fees based on the outcome of the case and the performance of your counsel . Contingency fees turn the matter into a shared risk or shared encouragement, making the law firm your business partner, not just representation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据胜诉来付费也是一种选择，它将根据事情结果和法律顾问的表现来考虑费用。胜诉费将事情变成共同风险或共同激励，让法律事务所成为你的合作伙伴，而不仅仅是代理身份。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Multi-layered tasks多层次任务"},{"lang":"en","text":"If you're shopping for a firm for actual legal work involving a number of legal specialties , consider using blended hourly fees. The firm calculates in advance an “average” rate based on the anticipated time each lawyer spends on the matter."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你打算挑选一个事务所，并要邀请几位法律专家进行工作，那么需要考虑使用混合计时费率。法律事务所根据每个律师处理案件的预期时间，提前测算出一个“基准”费率。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This arrangement helps the client to avoid paying a senior partner's hourly rate for research that should be conducted by a junior associate."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果工作是由初级律师完成的，这种方式就使你不必按照一个资深合伙人的计时标准来付费。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Legal “Insurance”法律“保险”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The contract fee allows the client to pick up the phone and talk to the lawyer without needing to eye the clock. This approach works like a legal insurance policy. It encourages companies to contact their counsel on non-litigation , non-crisis matters, and to save money in the long run by engaging in more preventive legal action."},{"lang":"zh","text":"合同付费的方式可以允许客户与律师随时交流而不用担心通话时间。这种方式好似购买法律保险。它鼓励公司在非法律业务和非紧急事务方面与法务咨询人员沟通，并且通过采取更具预防性质的合法行动，从长远来说以节约经费。"}],"source":"人文英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":274},{"id":"r-商务英语3-1-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Five Ways to Stay Energized with Colleagues","subtitle":"和同事一起保持充沛精力","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"We all have those days when all we want is to crawl back in bed for a few more hours. Unfortunately, few of us have that luxury . The following hints may help you stay energize , or at least get you going until you can make the time for rest."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们都有那么几天，最想做的事儿就是可以多在床上赖上几个小时。遗憾的是，很少有人能拥有这样的奢侈。下面几个提示可以帮助您保持精力充沛，或至少可以让你在找到时间休息之前有精力继续工作。"},{"lang":"en","text":"● engage in a quick conversation with high-energy colleagues. Their positive energy may refresh you. Just be careful not to drag them down!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 和精力充沛的同事进行快节奏的交谈。他们的积极能量可以让您振作精神。要当心，别让他们招架不住哦！"},{"lang":"en","text":"● Snack more! Having a healthy snack on hand, like a granola bar or fruit can help your blood sugar levels and may provide a healthy boost of energy. However, moderation is key! Overeating will do the opposite and drag you down!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 多准备些零食。手头备点儿健康的零食，如格兰诺拉麦棒或水果可以帮助稳定您的血糖水平，提供健康能量。注意，适量是关键！过量食用会适得其反，令人萎靡不振！"},{"lang":"en","text":"● Exercise. If you know that your schedule does not allow for a visit to the gym today, find a way to move around during your day. Instead of sending an email to your co-worker, walk to her desk or just take the stairs today, even though you're tired. People who exercise get more restful sleep and often feel more energized than those who don't."},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 适度运动。如果你知道当天的时间安排满到没有时间去健身房，那就换种方法，起来走走，比如走到同事的办公室找她谈工作，而不是发电子邮件，或者即使累了也走楼梯上下楼。经常锻炼的人比不运动的人睡眠更安稳，更富有活力。尽管你很累，但与其发电子邮件给同事，不如今天就走到她的办公桌前或者就走走楼梯吧。"},{"lang":"en","text":"● Drink water. “ Hydration is critical ,” says Steven Masley, medical director of the Pritikin Longevity Center in Aventura, Florida. The majority of your body is made of water. “If you don't hydrate , you're going to feel tired.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 多喝水。“水是至关重要的，”位于弗罗里达州阿文特拉的普里蒂金长寿中心的医学主任史蒂芬•马斯利认为。人身体的大部分是由水构成的。“如果不喝水，人就会感觉很疲惫。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"● Plan a vacation. Whether you leave town for a day or for a week, having something fun you've been looking forward to will excite you and stimulate energy."},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 计划休假。不管出游一天还是一个星期，做些一直期待的事情，开心得游玩会令人兴奋，并激发潜能。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":242},{"id":"r-商务英语3-1-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Dealing with People in Business","subtitle":"商务活动中的待人之道","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In business, you have to deal in person with all kinds of people.1．When talking to people within your company who don't speak your language, you may have to use English; these people may be colleagues or co-workers — who may work with you in your own department, in another part of the building or in another branch. And you may also have to deal with people from outside the organization: clients, suppliers, visitors and members of the public. Moreover, these people may be friends or strangers — people of your own age, or people who are younger or older than you."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在商务活动中，人们不得不亲自与各种各样的人打交道。与公司内不会讲你的母语的人交谈时，你可能不得不使用英语；这些人可能是同事，也可能是合作者，他们也许与你同属一个部门，也许就职于同一公司的其他部门，也许来自其他分部。你还必须与单位以外的人打交道：客户、访客或社会公众。还有，他们可能是朋友，也可能是陌生人，他们当中有你的同龄人，也有比你年轻或年长的人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The relationship you have with a person determines the kind of language you use.2．For example, it's not appropriate to say “Hi, how are you!” when meeting the Managing Director of a large company or to say “Good morning, it's a great pleasure to meet you.” when being introduced to a person you'll be working closely with in the same team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"与他人的关系决定了你选择使用什么样的语言。例如，在与大公司的总经理会面时说“嗨，你好吗？”，或者当被介绍给即将密切合作的团队成员时说 “早上好，见到您荣幸之至”这样的话，都是不合时宜的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"People usually form an impression of you from the way you speak and behave.3．People in different countries have different ideas of what sounds friendly, polite or sincere — and of what sounds rude or unfriendly! Good manners in your culture may be considered bad manners in another. Sometimes your body language, gestures and expressions may tell people more about you than the words you use."},{"lang":"zh","text":"通常，人们会通过你的言谈举止对你形成印象。不同国家的人们对如何讲话才是友好的、礼貌的或真诚的看法各不相同，对什么样的语言是粗鲁的或不友好的标准也不尽相同！一种文化中的良好举止可能在另一种文化中会是陋习。有时，人们的身体语言、手势和表情可能会比话语传达的信息更加丰富。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":227},{"id":"r-商务英语3-2-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Learning Business Skills through Junior Achievement","subtitle":"通过“青年成就”学习商务技能","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Junior Achievement is an international movement to educate young people about business and economics for the purpose of helping them prepare to succeed in world economy . The organization is the largest of its kind."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“青年成就”是为年轻人提供商务和经济学教育的国际运动，目的是帮助他们为在世界经济领域取得成功做好准备。这个组织是同类组织中规模最大的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Junior Achievement has gone through different stages a period in the course of a process or set of events; state reached at a particular time in its development. It was started by two business leaders, Horace Moses and Theodore Vail, and Senator Murray Crane in 1919 in Springfield, Massachusetts. The organization started with a small number of children aged ten to twelve. For more than 50 years, Junior Achievement programs met after school as a group of business clubs. But in 1975, Junior Achievement began to offer classes during school hours. Many more young people joined the organization once it began to teach business skills as part of the school day. In 2004, Junior Achievement Worldwide was formed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“青年成就”经历了不同的发展阶段。早在1919年，它由两个商业领袖贺瑞斯·摩西和西奥多·维尔以及参议员莫里·克兰在美国马萨诸塞州的斯普林菲尔德建立。刚开始，这个组织只有为数不多的10到12岁的孩子参加。有50余年的时间里，“青年成就”项目以课后商业俱乐部的形式开展。但是，在1975年，“青年成就”开始在正式的上课时间安排课时。自从在课上教授商务技能以后，越来越多的年轻人加入了进来。在2004年，“国际青年成就组织”成立。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The Junior Achievement programs teach about businesses, how they are organized, and how products are made and sold. The programs also teach about the American and world economies and business operations. Young people can learn how Entrepreneurship the state of being an entrepreneur, or the activities associated with being an entrepreneur works by operating their own companies. For instance, the students develop a product and sell shares any of the equal portions into which its ownership is divided and evidenced by a stock certificate in their company. They use the money to buy the materials they need to make their product, which they then sell. Finally, they return the proﬁt to the people who bought shares in the company. It's reported that in the United States alone, there are more than 22, 000 places that hold Junior Achievement events currently. According to Junior Achievement, about 287, 000 volunteers a person who performs voluntary work support its programs around the world."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“国际青年成就组织”项目教授的内容包括商业、商业组织形式、产品生产与销售。项目还教授美国经济和世界经济知识商务运作方式。年轻人可以通过运营自己的公司来了解创业之路。例如：学生研发产品，在公司发行股票。他们用钱购买生产产品所需的原材料，然后再销售。最终，他们把钱返还给在公司里购买他们股票的投资人。据报道，仅在美国，就有22000处开展“国际青年成就组织”项目的地方。根据“国际青年成就组织”提供的数据，在全世界有近287000志愿者在支持这个项目。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":305},{"id":"r-商务英语3-2-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Three Effective Management Styles","subtitle":"三种有效的管理方式","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Being an effective manager means knowing when to use the right management style. Some styles, for instance, are more people- oriented , while others tend to focus on a project or product. The management style you select will depend on your people's skills and knowledge, available resources (like time and money), desired results, and, of course, the task before you. The common management styles can be summarized into three category ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为一名高效的主管，必须清楚何时使用恰当的管理方式。例如，一些方式更加以人为本, 而有些则专注于项目或产品本身。你选择的管理风格将取决于你的成员的技能和知识、可支配的资源（如时间和资金）、预期的结果，当然还有你面临的任务。常见管理方式分三大类。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The participatory style is the first of its kind. Here, it is critical to give each employee an entire task to complete. If that's not possible, make sure the individual knows and understands his or her part as it relates to the project or task. When people in your team know where they fit in the big picture, they're more likely to be motivated to complete the task."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第一类是参与式管理。这种方式的关键是让每个员工完成一个完整的项目。如果做不到这样，每个人也必须了解他们作为项目一部分所要承担的任务。当你的团队成员知道他们在公司里所处的位置时, 他们才更有可能有动力去完成这个任务。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Following that, we have the directing style. Sometimes a situation will call for a direct style of management."},{"lang":"en","text":"Perhaps a tight deadline loom , or the project involve numerous employees and requires a top-down management approach. Here, a manager answers five questions for the employees: What? Where? How? Why? and When? Let employees know what they need to do, how they're going to do it, and when the questions must be dealt with."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第二类是主导式管理。有时，某种情境中需要采取直接管理的风格。也许任务的截止日期迫近，或者是项目的参与成员众多，需要采取自上而下的管理方式。主管需要回答员工5个问题，做什么、在哪儿、怎么做、为什么、何时做。要让员工知道他们需要做什么，如何去做，以及何时解决这些问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The last one is the teamwork style. If you want to speed up a project and choose the best process for completing that project, managing by teamwork is the way to go. When you motivate people to pool their knowledge, the results may exceed your expectation . Often, teams can tackle problems more quickly than what you can accomplish on your own. The give-and-take can create a process that you can repeat in other projects."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第三类是团队协作式管理。如果你想要加快项目进度并选择完成它的最佳途径，通过团队式管理方可实现。当你激发的员工集思广益时，结果可能远超你的预期。团队协作往往可以比单枪匹马更快地解决问题。这种相互让步的合作过程可以沿用到其他项目中。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":286},{"id":"r-商务英语3-3-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"Three Advantages of Online Banking","subtitle":"网上银行的三个优势","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Online banking refers to banking activities that are carried out over the Internet on a secure website. It developed in the late 1990s and grew more popular over the years since it can make one's financial life much easier to manage."},{"lang":"zh","text":"网上银行是指通过互联网在安全的网站上进行的银行业务活动。网上银行起源于上世纪90年代末，因为它使得人们的金融活动更加容易管理，这些年来网上银行变得越来越普及起来。"},{"lang":"en","text":"First, you can use online banking to pay your bills. Most banks have a section in which you set up payees . Fill out the information once, you can simply choose that profile every time you pay a bill online."},{"lang":"zh","text":"首先，你能够使用网上银行支付账单。大多数银行都有一个可以让您设立收款人的栏目。一旦填好这些信息，每次您都可以简便地选择那个人，在线支付账单。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Second, online banking allows you to access your account history and transactions from anywhere. It is the quickest way to check and see if a transaction has cleared your account. It also enables you to find out about unauthorized transactions more quickly."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 网上银行使得您可以在任何地方查看您的账户历史以及交易记录。它是最为快捷的查看交易是否结清的方式。网上银行还能使您更迅速地发现是否有未授权的交易。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Thirdly, online banking also allows you to transfer money between accounts effectively. It is more convenient than using the automated phone service. When you set up your online banking, be sure that all of your accounts at the bank are listed. This will make it easier to transfer money and make loan payments online."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第三，网上银行还允许您在账户之间有效地转账。它比使用电话服务更方便。当您建立自己的网上银行账户时，要保证银行所有开设的账户都要包含在内。这使得转账和贷款支付更加容易。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Obviously , you need to pay special attention to your safety or privacy using online banking. It is important to clear your cookies after each banking session , especially at a public computer. Additionally, make sure that your password is long enough to prevent it from easily being hacked. Never give your online account information to anyone else. Check your credit report regularly. Thus you can protect yourself from identity theft."},{"lang":"zh","text":"显而易见，使用网上银行时，您需要特别注意您的安全或隐私。很重要的一点是，每次银行交易结束后，要清除信息记录文件，尤其是在公共电脑上。此外，确保您的密码足够长，以防止轻易受黑客攻击。不要把您的网上账户信息告诉其他任何人。定期查看您的信用报告。这样，您就可以保护自己，避免身份被盗。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":245},{"id":"r-商务英语3-3-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"RMB Business for Personal Account in the United States","subtitle":"在美国个人账户的人民币业务","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"With economic development, Chinese banks are extending services in more and more countries. The following is a brief introduction to RMB business for personal customers offered by the Bank of China in the United States."},{"lang":"zh","text":"随着经济的发展，中国的银行的业务正在扩展到越来越多的国家。下面简单的介绍中国银行在美国为个人客户提供的人民币业务。"},{"lang":"en","text":"To open a RMB account with the Bank of China in the United States, you must first open a USD account. Of course, a minimum deposit requirement is needed for both the USD and the RMB accounts. Then you must complete the Bank's Account Application Form and an Internal Revenue Service (IRS) Form on your status . In addition, you are required to provide the Bank with your Social Security Number and two valid identification documents . One is your Passport or Driver's License , the other is your major credit card, employee identification card or health insurance card."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为了在美国开立中国银行人民币账户，您必须首先开立一个美元账户。当然，对于美元和人民币两种账户，都需要按照银行规定存入最低金额。然后根据您的状况，您必须完成填写该银行的账户申请表格和国税局（IRS）表格。此外，您需要向银行提供您的社会安全号码和两个有效的身份文件。一个是护照或驾驶执照，另外一个是您最主要的信用卡、员工识别卡或健康保险卡。"},{"lang":"en","text":"With the RMB account you can withdraw and deposit RMB cash directly. The daily limit is 20, 000 yuan on each transaction. Usually a service fee is charged for withdrawals above 3, 000 yuan. You can also exchange USD for RMB or exchange RMB for USD. The daily limit is USD $4, 000 worth of RMB. Be careful about the exchange rates. They might not be the same as the exchange rates offered in China."},{"lang":"zh","text":"用人民币账户，您可以直接提取和存入人民币现金。每日每笔交易限额为20000元。通常，提现3000元以上会被收取服务费。您也可以把美元换成人民币，或者把人民币兑换成美元。每天限额美元4000或等值人民币。注意有关汇率。它们可能和在中国提供的汇率不尽相同。"},{"lang":"en","text":"For further information, you can call at the bank's customer service hotline at 123456789 to the extension 9578, or pay a visit to www.bocusa.com."},{"lang":"zh","text":"要了解更多信息，您可以拨打银行客服热线123456789 转分机9578，或者访问www.bocusa.com 网站。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":224},{"id":"r-商务英语3-4-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Preparations for Negotiation","subtitle":"谈判准备","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Before you go to visit a new customer to negotiate a sale, you should find out as much as you can about them."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在你去拜访新客户洽谈业务之前，你应该尽可能多地了解他们的情况。"},{"lang":"en","text":"At the beginning of the negotiation you should draw up an agenda together with your customer."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在谈判开始前你应该与你的客户一起制定一个议程。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Then both sides should put forward their proposals before you get down to trading."},{"lang":"zh","text":"双方都提出各自的方案，然后进行讨价还价。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ideally a negotiation should be a win-win situation so both you and your customer will probably have to give in on some points, and you should be prepared in case your customer turns down your proposals by having a second plan to fall back on."},{"lang":"zh","text":"理想的谈判应该是一个双赢的局面，因此，你和客户可能在某些方面都应做出一些让步，你应该做好准备，以防客户转而依靠另一方案来否决你的提议。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Before closing the sale it's a good idea to run through the main points you have agreed on again."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在达成交易前，将你认可的要点再过一遍，这是个好主意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As the salesperson, you should write up the agreement as soon as possible after the negotiation and send a copy to your customer."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为销售人员，你应该在谈判结束后尽快拟定协议，并把副本发送给你的客户。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":141},{"id":"r-商务英语3-4-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"Hard Sell vs. Soft Sell","subtitle":"硬推销和软推销","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Hard sell and soft sell are important business terms and useful strategies for sales staff to know and understand. Both of them can work. The effect depends on the type of customers and the type of products."},{"lang":"zh","text":"硬推销和软推销是销售人员需要了解和理解的重要商务术语和实用策略。二者都很奏效，其效果取决于客户的类型和产品的类型。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Hard sell is a kind of more direct and forceful sales tactics . The sales person just keeps explaining how good the product is, why people should buy it and even how the prices might increase if the customer walks off."},{"lang":"zh","text":"硬推销是一种更加直接和有力的销售策略。销售人员坚持不断地解释这个产品有多好，为什么人们应该买它，甚至如果客户不买，价格会如何上涨。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Soft sell is a different approach. The sales person tries to build trust with consumers. He doesn't put pressure on them to buy things, just recommending a product and letting the consumers make their own decisions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"软推销是一种不同的方法。销售人员竭力与消费者建立信任，并不给他们施加压力去买东西，只是推荐产品，让消费者自己决定。"},{"lang":"en","text":"An example of soft sell is to distribute free samples to which customers often respond favorably. Businesses can use free samples to build rapport and engage customers in products or services. Recommending products between friends is a little bit like doing soft selling. People don't really care if someone else buys the product. They are just giving their honest opinions and trying to be helpful."},{"lang":"zh","text":"软推销的一个例子是分发免费样品,客户通常积极回应。企业可以使用免费样品和客户建立融洽的关系，并以此吸引他们对产品或服务的兴趣。朋友间推荐产品有点像做软式销售，人们实际上不关心别人是否会购买该产品，他们只是想给出诚实的看法，做点有益他人的事。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Humor in advertising is also used to attract the customers' attention and get them interested in the products or services. Customers often resist hard sales tactics, thus making soft-selling much more effective for success."},{"lang":"zh","text":"诙谐的广告也被会用来吸引顾客的注意力，引起他们对产品或服务的兴趣。顾客往往抵制那些硬推销策略，从而使得软推销能更有效地获得成功。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Dear Mr. Shepherd,"},{"lang":"zh","text":"亲爱的谢泼德先生："},{"lang":"en","text":"Thank you for your recent inquiry."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谢谢您最近的询盘。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Please find below our quotation . It is valid for the next two months:请查阅下面我们的报价。未来两个月内有效。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Room size / m2面积/每平方米"},{"lang":"en","text":"Monthly rate月租金"},{"lang":"en","text":"25% off monthly offer rate月租金25%优惠"},{"lang":"en","text":"$80"},{"lang":"en","text":"$60"},{"lang":"en","text":"$100"},{"lang":"en","text":"$75"},{"lang":"en","text":"$120"},{"lang":"en","text":"$90"},{"lang":"zh","text":"We are now running a promotion, offering you a 25% discount off your first two months' storage. Besides, we can offer you a further discount of 5% if you pay in advance for twelve weeks, or 8% for sixteen weeks.我们现在正在搞促销活动，对您前两个月的仓储费我们可以给您25%的折扣。除此之外,如果您提前十二周支付费用，再给予5%的折扣，或者提前十六周支付，再给予8%的折扣。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Moreover, reservations by credit card four weeks in advance guarantee availability of the room size required. Our terms of storage require a security deposit and minimum of four weeks' rent also payable in advance. Both the security deposit and any unused rent will be refunded when you move out. We sell insurance coverage; the charge you pay will depend on the cover you require. 另外，用信用卡提前四个星期预定，可以确保您所需的空间。我们的仓储条款要求预交押金（保证金）和最少四周的房租。当您搬走时，押金和任何未使用的租金都将退还给您。我们出售保险，费用取决于您想要投保的险别。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It is obvious that we would be delighted if you would like to visit our store to see in person what we have to offer. You'll find everything you need to make your self storage experience as easy as possible.当然，我们也欢迎您亲自来参观我们的仓库，来看看我们所提供的服务。您定会感受到无比便捷的仓储体验。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Please find enclosed our brochure and other leaﬂets outlining our range of services. If you require any further information or would like to make a reservation, please do not hesitate to call us at 0800-123-7265, or visit www.superspace.com.请查阅附件中我们的宣传册和宣传单，里面概述了我们服务的范畴。如果您想进一步了解详情，请致电0800-123-7265，或者访问ww.superspace.com。"},{"lang":"en","text":"We are looking forward to receiving your reply.我们期待收到您的回复。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Yours sincerely,您真诚的"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Adam Lambert亚当•兰伯特"},{"lang":"en","text":"P.S.: Don't forget to use the enclosed special $15-off voucher for all packing materials.注: 别忘了使用附赠的价值$15的包装材料特别优惠券。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":413},{"id":"r-商务英语3-5-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Functions of Marketing","subtitle":"市场营销的功能","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"There are eight traditional functions of marketing:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"市场营销有八个传统功能："},{"lang":"en","text":"A. Buying: A marketer focuses on buyers' needs and desires in order to decide what products to make available. Understanding buyers' behavior is of great importance."},{"lang":"zh","text":"A．购买：营销人员需要聚焦买方的需求和意愿，来决定提供哪些产品。了解买方的行为很重要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"B. selling: Marketers usually view selling as a persuasive activity that is completed through promotion."},{"lang":"en","text":"Selling includes personal selling, advertising, and other selling methods. It is probably the function of marketing that we most often see in our daily life."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 推销：营销人员通常将推销视为通过促销可以实现的游说行为。推销包括个人销售、广告以及其他销售方法。这就是在我们在日常生活中最常见的市场营销功能。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•"},{"lang":"en","text":"C. transporting: It is physically moving the product from the seller to the buyer. Marketers focus on transporting costs and services."},{"lang":"zh","text":"C．运输：产品从买方到卖方的物资移动就是运输。市场营销主要关注运输成本和服务。"},{"lang":"en","text":"D. Storing: Like transporting, storing is an aspect of the physical distribution of products. Storing includes warehousing activities. Warehouses hold products for long periods sometimes in order to create time utility."},{"lang":"zh","text":"D．储存：像运输一样，储存也是产品物资调运的一个方面。储存包括了仓储活动。有时候在仓库里长时间的保存产品是为了增加时间效用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"E.grading: It involves sorting products according to size and quality. This makes buying and selling easier because it reduces the need for inspection and sampling."},{"lang":"zh","text":"E．分级：根据产品的尺寸和质量给产品分级。这使得买卖双方都更加便利，因为这样可以减少检查和抽样的需要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"F. Financing: For many products, such as automobiles, fridges, and new homes, the purchase is facilitated when the marketer provides credit that makes the purchasing of the product possible."},{"lang":"zh","text":"F．金融支持：对于像汽车、冰箱和新的房产这些大宗产品，营销人员提供贷款等金融服务可以促进顾客购买产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"G. Marketing research: Through research, marketers may find out the need for new products and services. By gathering information on a regular basis, they can better plan, carry out and control marketing activities."},{"lang":"zh","text":"G．市场调研：通过调研，营销人员可以发现市场对新产品和新服务的需求。通过定期收集数据，他们能更好地策划、实施以及控制营销行为。"},{"lang":"en","text":"H. Risk taking: It involves bearing the uncertainties that are part of the marketing process. Most marketing decisions result in either success or failure that is associated with risk."},{"lang":"zh","text":"H．风险承担：承担不确定的风险是市场营销过程中的不可或缺的一个部分。大多数营销决策会导致与风险相关的成功或失败。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":242},{"id":"r-商务英语3-5-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"Secret of Sales","subtitle":"销售的秘诀","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"You don't have to be a special kind of person to sell a product. Although successful salespeople often have special talents and an outgoing personality , the skills they employ are used by us all: we build and maintain relationships with different kinds of people, we listen to and take note of what they tell us and don't just enjoy the sound of our own voices, and we explain things to them or discuss ideas with them."},{"lang":"zh","text":"推销一个产品，你不一定做个特殊的人。虽然成功的销售人员通常拥有特别的天赋和开朗的性格，但是，他们所运用的技巧我们也经常使用，我们和不同的人建立并保持关系，我们聆听并注意他们所讲的内容，而不只是欣赏我们自己的声音，我们跟他们解释一些事情，或者讨论一些观点。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Keeping salespeople “on the road” is much more expensive than employing them to work in the office because much of their time is spent in traveling. Telephone selling may use this time more productively , but a face-to-face meeting is much more effective. Export companies often have a separate export sales force, whose travel and accommodation expenses may be very high. So serving overseas customers may often be done by phone, fax, letter or email without so many personal visits. Many firms employ an overseas agent who is responsible for selling their products in another country."},{"lang":"zh","text":"让销售人员“在路上”比让他们待在办公室里工作更加昂贵，因为他们的大量时间花在旅途中。虽然电话推销能有效地利用时间，但是面对面交流却更加让人印象深刻。外贸公司通常拥有独立的出口销售团队，他们的差旅和食宿花销会非常高。所以对于国外客户，通常会通过电话、传真、信件或电子邮件等手段进行服务，而不是亲自拜访。很多公司雇佣海外代理商，这些代理商负责在其他国家销售他们的产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A sales department consists of many people who are based in different parts of the country or the world, and who don't have day-to-day contact or chances for communicating with each other. For this reason, firms hold regular sales conferences where their entire sales force can meet, receive information and ask questions about new products and receive training."},{"lang":"zh","text":"销售部由在全国乃至世界各地工作的很多人员组成，销售人员之间缺乏日常接触或互相交流的机会。鉴于此，公司会定期召开营销会议，全体营销人员可以碰面，接受新产品相关信息并提出有关问题，接受培训。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":233},{"id":"r-商务英语3-6-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"The Importance of Information in the Supply Chain","subtitle":"供应链中信息的重要性","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Information is important because it provides the facts that supply chain managers use to make decisions.1．Without information, a manager will not know what consumers want, how much inventory is in stock and when more products should be produced and shipped. In short, without information, a manager can only make decisions blindly ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"信息很重要，因为它提供了供应链管理者用于决策的事实。如果没有信息，管理者就无法知道消费者的需求是什么，无法确定需要多少库存，也无法确定什么时候生产或运输更多的产品。总之，没有信息，管理者只能盲目决策。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Managers must understand how information is gathered and analyzed.2．This is where information technology comes into play. Information technology serves as the eyes and ears of management in a supply chain , capturing and delivering the information necessary to make a good decision. For instance, an IT system at a personal computer manufacturer may help a manager analyze the information and recommend an action. The manager can use the remaining chips first, then look at demand forecast, and determine whether to order more chips."},{"lang":"zh","text":"管理者必须清楚如何收集和分析信息，这就要求信息技术发挥作用了。信息技术在供应链上充当管理的耳目，获取并传递做出正确决策所需要的信息。例如，个人电脑制造商的信息技术系统可以帮助管理者分析信息，并对行动提出建议。管理者可以先使用现有芯片，然后查看需求预测，再决定是否订购更多的芯片。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are four reasons why timely and accurate information has become more important for effective logistics system design and operations.3．First, customers recognize information about order status, product availability , delivery schedule, and shipment tracking as necessary elements of total customer service. Then, managers realize that information can be used to reduce human resource requirements. What's more, information increases flexibility with regard to how, when, and where resources may be used to gain strategic advantage."},{"lang":"en","text":"And finally, enhanced information transfer and exchange capability of using the Internet is changing relationships between buyers and sellers and refining channel relationships."},{"lang":"zh","text":"及时、准确的信息对于高效的物流系统的设计与运行发挥着更加重要的作用，有如下四个原因。首先，客户认为，订单状况、产品现货供应状况、送货日期、货物跟踪这些信息是全面客户服务的应有内容。其次，管理者认识到，信息可以降低对人力资源的需求。此外，信息能够提高何时何地如何利用资源赢取战略优势的灵活性。最后，互联网的使用增强了信息传递和交互能力，使买卖双方之间的关系发生着变化，也使渠道关系更趋完善。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":232},{"id":"r-商务英语3-6-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Functions of Logistics","subtitle":"物流的功能","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Logistics is the physical ﬂow process of goods from the point of origin to the point of consumption concerning transportation, warehousing and storage, loading and unloading, goods handling, packing, distribution processing delivery and information management. For example, after a commercial transaction is done, logistics will carry out the transfer of goods from the seller to the buyer at the lowest cost and in the most effective manner. During the transfer process,"},{"lang":"en","text":"logistics facilities, equipment (carriers), administration of information and standardization are needed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"物流指的是物品从产品生产地向消费点的实物流转过程，其中包括运输、仓储、装卸、物品搬运、包装、配送以及信息管理。例如，商品交易完成之后，物流会以最低成本和最高效率将物品从卖方运送给买方。运输过程中，既需要物流设施和设备（运输工具），也需要进行信息管理和标准化管理。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Logistics has three major functions. Firstly, it creates time value. The same goods can be valued differently at different times. Goods are often in stagnation during the transfer process, which is called the storage of logistics. Secondly, it creates"},{"lang":"en","text":"location value. The same goods can be valued differently at different locations. The value added distribution processing value during the transfer process is the location value of logistics. Thirdly, it creates. Sometimes the distribution processing changes the packages of the goods. That is, during this stage, it cuts large packages of goods into smaller parts, which creates added value for goods."},{"lang":"zh","text":"物流有三大主要功能。 第一，物流创造时间价值。相同的物品在不同时间会有不同的价值。在商品传送过程中，物品通常会处于停滞状态，这被称为物流储存。第二，物流创造场所价值。相同的物品在不同场所会有不同的价值。这种因商品流转过程中而产生的附加增值被称为物流的场所价值。第三，物流创造配送加工价值。有时候，配送过程改变物品的包装形式。也就是说，在这个阶段，配送加工把大包装的货物拆分成较小的部分，这样可以创造商品的附加价值。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":182},{"id":"r-商务英语3-7-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Top Eight Accounting Mistakes","subtitle":"八大常见会计错误","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Accounting errors will happen from time to time, but many common accounting mistakes can be avoided with proper planning and preparation. Here are the top eight accounting mistakes that can ruin your accounting career."},{"lang":"zh","text":"会计错误时有发生, 但是如果规划准备合理，很多常见的错误都可以避免。下列错误就是可以毁掉你前程的八大常见会计错误。"},{"lang":"en","text":"1．Not knowing your true cash balance : Due to things like automatic payments and bank charges, money that appears in your cash drawer and your checking account may already be spent."},{"lang":"zh","text":"1．不了解真实的现金余额：例如除去自动给付、银行收费，你的现金抽屉和活期存款中的钱可能已经被花掉了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"2．Mistaking profits for cash: When you have a lot of credit sales, your company can post big profits without seeing any cash."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2．错把利润当成现金: 当公司存在很多赊销的时候，可能会宣布获得很大利润，却看不到任何现金。"},{"lang":"en","text":"3．Paying bills too soon: If your vendors give you thirty days to pay them, take it. Unless you get a discount for paying early, paying your bills only when they're due improves your company's cash ﬂow."},{"lang":"zh","text":"3．急于付款: 如果供应商容许30天时间的付费期限，那就好好利用这个期限。除非有提前付费的折扣，当期限快到时再付费可以增加公司的现金流。"},{"lang":"en","text":"4．Avoiding book-keeping tasks: Not recording and posting transactions regularly leaves you with a mountain of book-keeping to deal with in the end."},{"lang":"zh","text":"4．不及时记账: 不按时记录和过账，到头来会使记账工作堆积如山。"},{"lang":"en","text":"5．Paying accidental dividends: Every time a corporation owner takes money out of his business, it counts as a dividend."},{"lang":"en","text":"That can lead to a bigger personal income-tax bill."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 不按计划支付分红: 公司所有者每次从经营所得中提取的资金，都被视为分红。这会导致个人所得税的增加。"},{"lang":"en","text":"6．Not keeping personal finances separate from business: Mixing up business and personal money can cause book-keeping and legal problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"6．把个人和公司的财务状况混为一谈: 把公司和个人的财务混在一起会产生记账和法律问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"7．Setting prices too low: Know your costs before you set product or service prices, or you can run the risk of losing money on every sale. A simple break-even analysis can help you set prices at a profitable level."},{"lang":"zh","text":"7.定价过低: 在为产品或服务定价之前需要了解成本，否则会有销售亏本的风险。简单的盈亏平衡分析法就可以帮助你把价格定在可盈利的范围内。"},{"lang":"en","text":"8．Turning over all the financial issues to someone else: Without a good knowledge of your company's finances, you can't make successful decisions. Even if you don't want to deal with the daily book-keeping tasks, look at your financial statements every month to help you plan for profits and prevent potential problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"8．把所有财务问题交给他人处理: 对公司财务状况缺乏很好的了解，你就不可能做出正确的决策。即使你不想处理日常的记账工作，每月定期了解自己的财务状况可以帮助你规划收益和防范风险。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":287},{"id":"r-商务英语3-7-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Every Business Has Assets","subtitle":"每个企业都有资产","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"No matter how small your business is and what industry you are in, your company has assets. From a computer to a processing plant, every single thing your company owns is an asset."},{"lang":"zh","text":"无论你的企业有多小，无论从事哪个行业，你的公司都有资产。从一台电脑到一家工厂，你公司拥有的每个零件都视同资产。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Assets can be in different forms. Some assets are physical, such as computers, filing cabinets , and delivery vans . Others are legally binding promises, such as accounts receivable, the money owed to your company. Still others seem to exist more on paper, for example, a year's worth of insurance paid in advance. No matter what form it takes, anything with monetary value that your company owns counts as an asset."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产分成不同的形式。有些资产是实物，例如电脑、储物柜和运货车。有些是具有法律约束力的承诺，如应收账款、公司所拥有的款项。还有一些更多是呈现在文件中的数据，例如每年预付的保险费用。无论何种形式，你公司拥有的任何有价值的东西都视同资产。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Assets appear on your balance sheet, reporting the key financial statements at the end of each accounting period. Your assets will be split into different types to make analysis easier. The order in which you list them on the balance sheet typically matches the way they appear in your chart of accounts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产体现在资产负债表当中, 记录每个会计周期的主要财务数据。为了让分析简单化，你的资产会划分成不同的形式。在资产负债表中列举资产的典型顺序和会计图表中的顺序应该是一致的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Assets do more than just show up on reports, though. They are the resources your company uses to produce revenue. Your business cannot bring in sales without assets.For product-based businesses, you can't produce anything without proper assets. It's true for service companies as well. At least, you have to have cash to pay your expenses and to help get the word out that your company exists. Service companies also need basic tools to provide service to customers: a hair stylist needs a chair, scissors , and styling tools; an accountant needs a computer and a lot of filing cabinets. Assets are key factors for any business."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不过，资产的价值不只是在报告中出现，还是公司籍以盈利的资源。没有资产，就不能产生销售。例如做产品的企业，没有资产就不可能生产任何产品。这也同样适用于服务业。至少，你需要有现金支付开销以及宣传你的公司。服务型公司也需要为消费者服务的基本的工具，如理发师需要座椅、剪刀以及美发工具；会计需要电脑和许多档案柜。资产对任何企业都具有重要的作用。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":261},{"id":"r-商务英语3-8-1","book":"商务英语3","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"What Is International Trade?","subtitle":"什么是国际贸易？","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"International trade is the exchange of goods and services between countries.It gives consumers and countries the opportunity to be exposed to goods and services not available in their own countries. Almost every kind of product can be found on the international market: food, clothes, spare parts, oil, jewelry , wine, stocks, currencies and water. Services are also traded: tourism , banking, consulting and transportation. A product that is sold to the global market is an export , and a product that is bought from the global market is an import ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"国际贸易是国家之间商品和服务的交换，为这些国家和消费者们提供了机会，使其能够接触本国没有的商品和服务。在国际市场上，几乎可以找到各种商品，如食物、衣服、备用零件、油、珠宝、酒、证券、货币和水。服务也可以进行交易，如旅游业、银行业务、咨询行业和运输。在全球市场上出售的商品是出口商品，从全球市场买入的商品是进口商品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"International trade can benefit us a lot.Trading globally allows us to expand our markets for both goods and services that otherwise may not have been available to us. If you walk into a supermarket and are able to buy Indonesian bananas, Brazilian coffee and a bottle of French wine, you are experiencing the effects of international trade."},{"lang":"zh","text":"国际贸易能使我们获益良多。全球贸易使得我们的商品和服务市场得以扩大，否则我们不可能得到这些商品和服务。如果你走进一家大型超市，能够买到印度尼西亚香蕉、巴西咖啡或者法国红酒，你正体验国际贸易带给我们的影响。"},{"lang":"en","text":"International trade brings us both advantages and disadvantages. For instance, international trade may also make the world economy easily affected by factors like prices, supply and demand, as well as global events. Political change in Asia, for example, could result in an increase in the cost of headlaborhunters , thereby increasing the manufacturing costs for an American sneaker company based in Malaysia , which would then result in an increase in the price that you have to pay to buy the tennis shoes at your local mall . A decrease in the cost of labor, on the other hand, would result in you having to pay less for your new shoes."},{"lang":"zh","text":"国际贸易既有它的优势，也有它的劣势。例如，国际贸易也可能使世界经济容易受到一些因素的影响，如价格、供需关系，以及全球性事件。例如，亚洲的政治变动会引起劳动力成本的增加，进而增加位于马来西亚的美国运动鞋工厂的制造成本，这个又导致你在本地商场购买网球鞋的花费上涨。而另一方面，劳动力成本的降低会降低你买一双新鞋的花费。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":254},{"id":"r-商务英语3-8-2","book":"商务英语3","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"The Basics of Import and Export","subtitle":"进出口的基本要素","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Importing and exporting is transferring goods from one country to another while paying attention to the laws and requirements of bringing goods out or into that country. If you want to import in large quantities for commercial purposes, you'll need to have the consent of the local customs department and the right paperwork. Import and export are the basics of international trade. If you are looking forward to starting your own business in the field of importing and exporting business, then here are some tips for starters."},{"lang":"zh","text":"进出口是指在遵循有关进口和出口的法律和要求的情况下，将一国的商品转移到另一国。如果你想从事大量的商业进口业务，你需要获得当地海关部门的许可，并持有相关文件。进口和出口是国际贸易的基本要素。如果你计划在进出口业务领域开创业务，请注意下面这些给创业者的建议。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Foreign embassies provide nice programs and a great deal of information about their goods to promote exporting. You can find out exactly what it is you are looking to buy. If you are exporting, you can approach your local department of trade and see what plans they have on offer to promote exports. Besides, you should consult the tax department to find out if there is a particular process to setting up an importing and exporting company and what documentation you will require. It is also necessary that you find out about any licensing requirements for importing and exporting of goods. Some countries do not allow their goods to go to a certain country and vice versa, this is known as an embargo. In this way, you can make sure that there are no embargoes with the country you are looking to trade with."},{"lang":"zh","text":"外国大使馆会提供一些优秀的项目及大量信息来促进商品出口。你可以找到想要进口的商品。如果你在做出口业务，你可以同当地贸易部门接洽，了解他们促进出口业务的相关计划。此外，你还可以咨询税务部门，了解是否有开办进出口公司的特别程序，以及需要准备什么文件。了解进出口货物的相关执照要求也是非常必要的。有些国家不允许本国的商品出口到某些国家，反之亦然，这就是禁运令。这样一来，你就可以确定你所进行贸易的国家没有相关的贸易禁运令。"}],"source":"商务英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":231},{"id":"r-商务英语4-1-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Traveler's Checks","subtitle":"旅行支票","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Many of the banks and travel services in western countries provide a convenience for travelers by issuing traveler's checks. Travelers, when buying the checks, have to sign the checks in the presence of the bank or service clerks. During the trip, travelers can cash the checks at the agencies of the bank or the travel service whenever they need after their counter-signatures are recognized. A lot of travelers like to buy these checks as they don't have to take along much cash and worry about counterfeit signatures. The agencies will get back the money they have paid by sending the checks to the issuing offices."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在西方国家，很多银行和旅行社都发行旅行支票，为旅客提供便利。购买旅行支票时，旅客必须当着银行或旅行社职员的面，在支票上签名。在旅行途中，当旅客需要时，可以在复签得到确认后，向银行或旅行社的代理机构兑现旅行支票。很多旅客喜欢购买旅行支票，因为这样就无须携带大量现金，也不用担心伪造签名。代理机构寄送旅行支票给发行机构，就可以获得其已经支付的数额。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Traveler's checks are generally of small face value, such as ten or twenty dollars, or five or ten pounds, for miscellaneous payments. There is no time limit for their circulation period. It is very profitable for the issuing offices to finance the funds they collect by issuing traveler's checks because they not only receive a service charge from the check buyers, but they also don't need to pay any interest no matter how long the checks remain in circulation before clearing. This is why banks and travel services are willing to provide this convenience."},{"lang":"zh","text":"旅行支票通常是小面额，例如10美元或20美元、5英镑或10英镑，用于小额支出。旅行支票的流通没有期限。对发行机构来说，通过发行旅行支票来提供融资便利是有利可图的，因为发行机构不但可以向支票购买者收取费用，而且，这些支票无论在外流通多久，在清算之前，发行机构都可以无息占用（支票上的资金）。这正是银行和旅行社愿意提供便利的原因所在。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":200},{"id":"r-商务英语4-1-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Schengen Visa Application Steps","subtitle":"申根签证申请步骤","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Identify the country or countries you will be traveling to.It is particularly important to know which countries you are traveling to because it determines where and how you are going to send your application."},{"lang":"zh","text":"确定你要去旅行的一个或几个国家。确定你要去旅行的国家，这非常重要，因为这决定了你寄送申请的地点和方式。"},{"lang":"en","text":"● If you are intending to visit just one Schengen country, you will need to apply for the Schengen visa directly with the embassy or consulate of that particular country."},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 如果你打算只去一个申根国家旅行，那么，你需要直接向这个国家的大使馆或领事馆申请申根签证。"},{"lang":"en","text":"● If you are intending to visit two or more Schengen countries, your application must be sent to the embassy or consulate of the country that shall be your main destination."},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 如果你打算去两个或更多的申根国家旅行，那么，你的申请必须寄送到主要目的地国家的大使馆或领事馆。"},{"lang":"en","text":"● If you are intending to visit several Schengen countries, but do not have a main destination, you should apply for the visa at the embassy or consulate of the first Schengen country on your travel itinerary."},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 如果你打算去多个申根国家旅行，但没有主要目的地，那么，你应该向旅行计划中的第一个申根国家申请签证。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A Fill out an application form beforehand to obtain a Schengen visa.You can download and print off the form online."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在获得申根签证前，你要填写申请表格。你可以从网上下载并打印申请表格。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Prepare all the requirements for your Schengen visa application.Depending on the consulate or embassy, you are required to show the following documents:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"准备申根签证申请所需要的所有资料。大使馆或领事馆一般要求提交以下资料："},{"lang":"en","text":"● a valid national passport;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 有效的公民护照；"},{"lang":"en","text":"● Evidence showing the purpose of your trip (e.g. international conference);"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 旅行目的证明材料（例如，参加国际会议）；"},{"lang":"en","text":"● proof of medical insurance;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 医疗保险证明；"},{"lang":"en","text":"● a round-trip travel ticket;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 往返机票；"},{"lang":"en","text":"● proof of funds"},{"lang":"zh","text":"● 资金证明。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Check the processing time to ensure you get your Schengen visa on time.The processing time varies per embassy, so it is important to take the processing time into account when planning your trip."},{"lang":"zh","text":"核实（签证）处理时间，以确保你按时获得申根签证。各个使馆（对签证的）处理时间不同，因此，在计划出行时，要将（签证）处理时间考虑在内。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":235},{"id":"r-商务英语4-2-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Customer Service","subtitle":"客户服务","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The American idea of customer service is to make each customer the center of attention. And wherever you go, good customer service means making customers feel special."},{"lang":"zh","text":"美式客服理念认为每位客户都是关注的焦点。无论你到哪儿，良好的客户服务就是让客户感觉与众不同。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When customers get to a store, they are treated as honor guests. Customers don't usually find store clerks sitting around watching TV or playing cards. Instead, the clerks greet them warmly and offer to help them find what they want. Customers usually don't have to ask how much items cost, since prices are clearly marked."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当客户走进商店，他们会被当作贵宾对待。客户不会看到商店职员围坐在一起看电视或打牌。相反，职员热情问候，提供帮助，找到客户之所需。客户通常也不用询问产品价格，因为价格已经明确标出。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When customers are ready to check out, they can go to the nearest and shortest checkout lane. Good stores open new checkout lanes when the lineups get too long.Some even offer express lanes for customers with 10 items or less. After they pay for their purchases, customers receive a smile and a warm \"thank you and have a nice day\" from the clerk."},{"lang":"zh","text":"结账之时，客户可以走向最近、最短的付款通道。当排队人数太多时，好的商店会开启新的付款通道。一些商家甚至为购买10件或10件以下商品的客户提供快速付款通道。客户结账付款之后，职员会送上微笑和温暖的祝福：“感谢您的光临，祝您度过美好的一天。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"In America, customer service continues long after the sale.Many products come with a money-back guarantee. Expensive items like cars, computers or stereo often have a warranty that ensures trouble-free use for a period of a year or more. Advertisements regularly include the motto, \"Your satisfaction is guaranteed.\" So if there is a problem with the product, customers can take it back.The customer service representative will often allow them to exchange the item or return it for a full refund."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在美国，（商品）售出之后，客户服务会延续很长时间。许多产品都有退款承诺。汽车、电脑、音响等高价位的商品通常有质保期，保证一年或更久的时间内使用该产品没有任何问题。广告一般有“包您满意”之类的标语。所以，如果产品有问题，客户可以把它送回去。客服代表往往会允许客户更换其所购商品或者全额退款。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Customer service in America grows out of the belief that \"the customer is always right\". If a person receives poor service from a store, he probably will avoid shopping there in the future.On the other hand, customers often remain loyal to a business that has excellent service even if their prices are higher."},{"lang":"zh","text":"美式客户服务相信“客户永远是正确的”。如果商家的客户服务差强人意，客户可能不再在此购物。另一方面，如果商家的服务上乘，即使其价格高一些，客户也会对其很忠诚。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":282},{"id":"r-商务英语4-2-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"The \"Feel Good Factor\" in Customer Service","subtitle":"顾客服务中的“感觉良好因素”","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Para.1 Challenge in customer service"},{"lang":"en","text":"A challenge in working in customer service is to ensure that you have focused your attention on the right key areas, measure by the right Key Performance indicator(KPI). One of the most important aspect of a customer service KPI is what is often referred to as the \"Feel Good factor\". basically the goal is not only to help the customer have a good experience, but to offer an experience that exceeds expectations. Several key points are listed as follows:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"客户服务部门工作的一大挑战，是保证聚焦于正确的关键领域，这可以用关键绩效指标（KPI）来衡量。客户服务关键绩效指标中最重要的一方面，是我们通常所说的“利好因素”。从根本上说，目标是不但要帮助客户获得良好的体验，而且要提供超出客户预期的体验。以下为主要几点："},{"lang":"en","text":"Para.2 Know your products"},{"lang":"en","text":"Know what products / services you are offering from back to front. In other words, be an information expert. It is okay to say “I don't know”, but it should always be followed up by “but let me find out” or possibly “but this person will be able to assist you”. Whatever the situation may be, make sure that you don't leave your customer with an unanswered question."},{"lang":"zh","text":"全面了解你所提供的产品或服务。换句话说，要成为信息专家。说“我不知道”没问题，但是，一定还要说“让我找找”或“这位能够帮助到您”。不管什么情况，一定要确保客户的问题得到答复。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para.3 Body language"},{"lang":"en","text":"Most of the communication that you relay to others is done through body language. If you have negative body language when you communicate with others, it shows that you don't care.Two of the most important aspects of positive body language are smiling and eye contact. Make sure to look your customers in the eye. It shows that you are listening to them and hearing what they are saying.And of course smiling is more inviting than a blank look or frown."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你与他人的大多数沟通交流，是通过肢体语言完成的。如果你与他人交流时，你的肢体语言不积极，就说明你不关心。积极的肢体语言拥有两大关键点：微笑和眼神交流。确保要直视客户的眼睛。这表明，你正在聆听他们，听到了他们所言。当然，微笑会比茫然的表情或眉头紧皱更加友好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Para.4 Anticipate guest needs"},{"lang":"en","text":"Nothing surprises your customers more than an employee going the extra mile to help them. Always look for ways to go above and beyond the expectations of your customers. In doing so, it helps them to know that you care and it will leave them with the \"Feel Good Factor\" that you are searching for."},{"lang":"zh","text":"没有什么能比员工加倍努力去解决问题更让客户惊喜的了。一定要想方设法，超越客户的期望。这么做有助于客户感受到你的关心，你一直追寻的“利好因素”也就传递给了客户。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":300},{"id":"r-商务英语4-3-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"Non-Verbal Communication in Negotiation","subtitle":"谈判中的非言语交际","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Communication plays an important role in a negotiation. Participants communicate information not only verbally but non-verbally through body language and gestures. By understanding how non-verbal communication works, a negotiator is able to understand the information the other participants are giving out non-verbally. At the same time, the negotiator keeps things secret that would limit his /her ability to negotiate."},{"lang":"zh","text":"沟通交流在商务谈判中起着非常重要的作用。谈判人员不仅通过言语交流信息，还可以通过肢体语言和手势等进行非言语交际。通过理解非言语交际如何发挥作用，谈判者能够理解其他谈判人员透露的非言语信息。同时，谈判者对会限制他（她）谈判能力的事情只字不提。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Take “non-verbal anchoring” as an example. In a negotiation, a person can gain the advantage by verbally expressing his / her position first. He / she also can “ anchor” and gain advantage with non-verbal cues like the following. First, personal space: the person at the head of the table is the obvious symbol of power. Negotiators may be unhappy with this strategic advantage. Second, first impression: begin the negotiation with positive gestures and enthusiasm. Look the person in the eye with honesty and respect. If you cannot maintain eye contact, the other person might think you are hiding something or you are dishonest."},{"lang":"zh","text":"举“非言语定位”一例进行说明。在一场谈判中，一个人可以先通过言语表明他（她）的身份地位，从而获得优势。他（她）也可以采取“定位”的方法，通过下列非言语线索获得优势。首先，个人空间。位于桌子前端的人明显是权力的象征。谈判者一般不喜欢这种战略优势。其次，第一印象。以积极的手势热情饱满地开始谈判，诚实而尊重地看着对方的眼睛。如果你不能保持目光接触，那么谈判的另一方可能会认为你有所隐藏或者你并不诚实。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another example is reading non-verbal communication. Being able to read the non-verbal communication of another person can be a great asset in the communication process. By being aware of different signs and expressions that a person gives verbally and non-verbally, a negotiator can adjust his / her approach and the negotiation can go smoothly. If possible, it may be helpful for negotiation partners to spend time together in a comfortable atmosphere outside of the negotiation room. Being familiar with another person helps you to sense the differences between verbal and non-verbal communication within the negotiation atmosphere."},{"lang":"zh","text":"另外一个例子是读懂非言语交际。能够读懂对方的非言语交际是交流过程中非常有用的能力。通过理解对方利用言语和非言语所表达出的不同信号和态度，谈判者可以调整谈判方法，使谈判顺利进行。如果可能的话，谈判双方在谈判室之外的轻松氛围中共度一段时间，会有很大帮助。熟悉对方可以帮助你感觉出在谈判环境中言语交际和非言语交际的不同。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":264},{"id":"r-商务英语4-3-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"The Golden Rules of Negotiating","subtitle":"谈判的黄金法则","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The art of negotiating is a difficult skill for most of us, even good salespeople. Here are three golden rules for you to follow:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"对于我们大多数人，甚至是优秀的销售人员来说，谈判艺术是一种很难掌握的技能。在此给大家提供三条黄金法则："},{"lang":"en","text":"1. Always Start the Negotiations"},{"lang":"zh","text":"总是发起谈判"},{"lang":"en","text":"You must initiate the process. This is because whoever controls the start of the negotiations tends to control where they end. If you let the other party start negotiations, you will be Constantly giving up control, often without even realizing it. For instance, when you ask someone what his project budget is, you are allowing him to start the negotiations. You will then spend your time chasing his number rather than finding the best solution. So, never let the other party control the negotiations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你必须启动谈判程序，这是因为，谁控制了谈判的开始，谁就会控制谈判在哪里结束。如果是对方发起谈判的话，你会不断地放弃对谈判的控制，甚至通常连你自己都意识不到。例如，当你问某人，他的项目预算是多少时，你就让对方发起了谈判。于是，你就会花时间跟着他的数字跑，而不是寻找最佳解决方案。所以，永远也不要让对方控制谈判。"},{"lang":"en","text":"2. Always Negotiate in Writing"},{"lang":"zh","text":"总是以书面形式谈判"},{"lang":"en","text":"The purpose of negotiations is to arrive at a formal written agreement, not tell a story or spend time talking. From the first moment you begin a proposal, you should Create a document and take it to the client. It will include all the points of agreement and become real to the prospective customer. Negotiating first and then having to create a document adds unnecessary time to a transaction. But if you build your written agreement as you negotiate, you are prepared to ask for a signature the moment the decision to buy is made."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谈判的目的是为了达成正式的书面协议，而不是讲故事或者聊天。你从一开始提出建议，就应该拟定文件并带给客户。文件应包括协议的所有要点，并且潜在客户能够实现。先谈判再拟定文件会为交易的达成增加不必要的时间。但是，如果你在谈判时就建立书面协议的话，一旦你决定购买，你就可以准备要求对方签字了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"3. Always Stay Cool"},{"lang":"zh","text":"总是保持冷静"},{"lang":"en","text":"The negotiation table can be loaded with agendas, egos and emotions. Great negotiators know how to stay cool, providing leadership and solutions, while the rest of the room becomes insanely invested in personal agendas and useless emotions. Crying, getting angry and blowing off steam may make you feel good, but such behavior will not benefit you while negotiating. When the rest of the room gets emotional, stay cool and use logic to negotiate and close."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谈判桌承载着议事日程、自我意识和各种情绪。当谈判室里的其他人失去理智，被个人议程和无用的情绪所左右时，伟大的谈判者知道如何保持冷静，如何领导他人并提出解决办法。哭喊、愤怒、发脾气可能会使你感觉好一些，但是，这样的行为在谈判时对你而言没有一点好处。当谈判室里的其他人变得情绪化时，你一定要保持冷静，有逻辑地谈判并结束谈判。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":289},{"id":"r-商务英语4-4-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Franchise","subtitle":"特许经营权","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Franchising is the practice of using another firm's successful business model. The word “franchise” comes from French meaning free, and is used both as a noun and as a verb. For the franchisor, the franchise is another way to build “chain stores” to distribute goods that avoids the investments and debts of a chain. The franchisor's success depends on the success of the franchisees. The franchisee can get more money than a direct employee because he or she has a vital interest in the business."},{"lang":"zh","text":"特许经营是一种使用其他公司的成功经营模式的做法。“特许经营权”在法语中的意思是“免费”，既可用作名词，也可用作动词。对于特许权拥有人来说，特许经营是建立“连锁店”的另一种方式，这样可以分销商品，避免连锁店的投资和债务。特许权拥有人的成功依赖特许经营者的成功。由于在公司中的切身利益，特许经营者能够比直属雇员赚更多的钱。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It should be recognized that franchising is one of the means available for getting investment money without giving up control of the chain operation and building a distribution system for servicing it. After the brand and the action plans are carefully designed and properly operated, franchisors are able to sell franchises and expand rapidly across the globe. It is said about 4% of all businesses in the United States are franchisee-worked. But franchisor rules are usually very strict in the US as well as in most other countries. Trademarks, proprietary service marks and regulations need to be observed carefully."},{"lang":"zh","text":"应该认识到的是，特许经营是获得投资的有效手段之一，同时不用放弃连锁经营权，还能建立一套分配制度为之服务。在认真设计品牌和行动方案、合理运营之后，特许权拥有人就可以销售特许经营权并在全球迅速扩张。据说，美国4%的商业都是特许经营的工作模式。但是，特许经营权的授予规则在美国与在其他大多数国家一样，非常严格。要认真遵守商标权、专属服务标志权和规章制度。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's important to know that there is risk for people buying the franchises. There are a lot of myths"},{"lang":"en","text":"Surrounding the success and failure rates of franchise businesses. One of the more popular myths states that franchise businesses have lower risk than independent business start-ups. Another one suggests that it's almost impossible to fail. Both are untrue and it's important for today's franchise-seekers to be aware of this fact."},{"lang":"zh","text":"特许经营是一种使用其他公司的成功经营模式的做法。“特许经营权”在法语中的意思是“免费”，既可用作名词，也可用作动词。对于特许权拥有人来说，特许经营是建立“连锁店”的另一种方式，这样可以分销商品，避免连锁店的投资和债务。特许权拥有人的成功依赖特许经营者的成功。由于在公司中的切身利益，特许经营者能够比直属雇员赚更多的。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":255},{"id":"r-商务英语4-4-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"Four Tips for Becoming a Franchisee","subtitle":"成为特许经营人的四个窍门","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"If you want to become a franchisee, the tips below can help you to find the perfect opportunity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你想成为特许经营人，下面的窍门能帮助你找到最好的机会。"},{"lang":"en","text":"1. Be focused on your preference"},{"lang":"zh","text":"关注你的偏好"},{"lang":"en","text":"On the stage of decision-making, the bottom line is: Don't rule out a business without learning or seeing what the day-to-day will look like. For instance, think about a mom returning to the work force who knows she wants to interact with children on a daily basis. Among the hundreds of options there, she needs to decide if she would like to be hands-on as a teacher or if she would rather manage a facility that tutors children in math. Deciding between the two is easy if she considers which day-to-day position she would prefer and how that will impact her other goals."},{"lang":"zh","text":"决策阶段的底线是，不了解公司的日常情况，就不要排除这个公司。比如说，试想一位重返工作岗位的母亲，她知道自己想要天天与孩子进行交流。在众多选择中，她需要做决定，是亲自做老师，还是经营一个场所来辅导孩子们的数学。如果她考虑一下，自己更喜欢哪种日常状态，这将如何影响她的其他目标，那么，在这两个选择中做决定就很容易了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Be proactive with your research"},{"lang":"zh","text":"主动研究"},{"lang":"en","text":"After you've determined what role you want in a franchise, it's important to start researching different options. Physically visit many different franchise locations and Browse the web and then determine what will be a good fit in your community."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当你确定在特许经营中的角色后，开始研究不同的选择是非常重要的。亲自参观一些不同的特许经营场所，浏览网站，然后决定什么最合适你的社区。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Make sure the franchisor has experience"},{"lang":"zh","text":"确定特许权拥有人具备经验"},{"lang":"en","text":"Before signing on to a franchise, it is essential to ask the franchisor about the executive team and its past industry experience. Find out if the company leaders have had significant experience at another franchise and are now applying that knowledge successfully."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在签订特许经营合同之前，务必要向特许权拥有人了解其管理团队的情况及其过去的产业经历。要搞清楚公司领导人是否有在其他特许经营中积累的有益经验，是否现在成功地应用了这些知识。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Read the franchise disclosure document carefully"},{"lang":"zh","text":"仔细阅读特许经营的公开文件"},{"lang":"en","text":"The first thing to look at is how much a franchise would cost to purchase. Make sure you have a financial advisor who can look at that item with you and see the type of profit a franchisee can make on average. It's also important to take a look at the post-termination clause in the agreement to make sure that when you want to leave the business, you know the terms well and your interests are properly protected."},{"lang":"zh","text":"首先要做的事是看一看特许经营的费用。一定要有一位财务顾问和你一起审阅条款，判断特许经营人能够赚取的平均利润。还有一点很重要，就是看一看协议中的后终止条款，以确定当你不做这个业务时，你非常了解这个条款，并且你的利益得到了适当保护。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":309},{"id":"r-商务英语4-5-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"(2021","subtitle":"年5月英语第三篇阅读理解","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Successful Team Work and Team Building"},{"lang":"zh","text":"成功的团队合作和团队建设"},{"lang":"en","text":"Team building skills are critical for your effectiveness as a manager or entrepreneur. And even if you are not in a management or leadership role yet, better understanding of team work can make you a more effective employee and give you an extra edge in your corporate office."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队建设技能对于经理或企业家的高效性而言至关重要。即使你并未担任管理或领导职位，较好地理解团队合作也能让你成为一名更有效率的员工，从而赋予你在办公场所的额外优势。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Team building success is when your team can accomplish something much bigger and work more effectively than a group of the same individuals working on their own. There are two critical factors in building a high performance team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队建设的成功是指相比同样一群各自行事的个体，你的团队能够取得更大的成就和更高的效率。在建设高效能团队的过程中有两个关键要素。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The first factor in team effectiveness is the diversity of skills and personalities. It means people use their strengths in full, but can compensate for each other's weaknesses. Or, different personality types balance and complement each other."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队有效性的第一个要素是技能和性格的多样性。这意味着人们在充分发挥才能的情况下，可以弥补彼此的短处。不同的性格类型可以相互平衡和补充。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The other critical element of team work success is that all the team efforts are directed towards the same clear goals, the team goals. This relies heavily on good communication in the team and harmony in member relationships."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队合作成功的另一个要素是所有团队成员要朝着同一个明确的团队目标共同努力。这主要靠团队成员之间良好的沟通和团队成员关系的融洽。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In real life, team work success rarely happens by itself if there are no focused team building efforts or activities. There is simply too much room for problems. For example, different personalities may build up conflicts. Or even worse, some people with similar personalities may start fighting for authority and dominance in certain areas of expertise . Even if the team goals are clear and accepted by everyone, there may be no team commitment to the group goals, or no consensus on the means of achieving those goals. There may be a lack of trust and openness, which may block critical communication and lead to loss of coordination in the individual efforts. This is why every team needs a good leader who is able to deal with all team work issues."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在现实生活中，如果没有致力于团队建设的努力和活动，团队合作成功的概率就几乎为零。可能出现问题的地方太多了。例如，不同的性格有时可能造成矛盾。更为甚者，为了获取在某些专业领域的权威地位和支配优势，相似性格的人可能会开始争斗。即使团队目标明确，并得到大家的一致认可，也可能会有这样的情况：团队没有努力朝着团队目标（奋斗），没有形成实现目标的共识。团队中可能会缺乏信任和坦诚，从而导致重要沟通受阻，团队里的每个人自行其是，无法协作。所以，每个团队都需要一个能够处理此类团队合作问题的好领队。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":297},{"id":"r-商务英语4-5-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"Team Spirit","subtitle":"团队精神","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Team spirit can make or break a team. Teammates who have team spirit are better able to work together and achieve team goals. They are also more satisfied with their team activities. John Wooden, a former basketball coach at UCLA, said, “Team spirit means you are willing to sacrifice personal considerations for the welfare of all. That defines a team player.” There are certain skills team members develop that serve as good examples of team spirit."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队精神既能成就一个团队，也能击垮一个团队。具备团队精神的成员能够更好地合作并实现团队的目标。他们对团队活动也更满意。加州大学洛杉矶分校的篮球队前教练约翰·伍登说：“团队精神意味着，你愿意为了大家的利益，牺牲个人的考虑。这才是团队成员的定义。”团队成员所具备的一些技能是团队精神的良好体现。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Cooperation"},{"lang":"zh","text":"合作"},{"lang":"en","text":"Cooperating is simply working together as teammates for the good of the team. Cooperation is a skill that team members can sharpen during practice. For example,basketball players must practice passing the ball in different plays and situations.Team efficiency is directly related to the cooperation of its members. Acting cooperatively is a good way to show team spirit because doing so contributes to the overall success of the team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"合作就是团队成员为了团队利益共同努力。合作是团队成员在实践中能够提高的一种技能。例如，篮球队员们必须练习技能，能够在不同的比赛和不同的情况下传球。团队效率与团队成员之间的合作直接相关。合作行为是一种展现合作精神的很好的方式，因为这样做有助于整个团队的成功。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Motivation"},{"lang":"zh","text":"动机"},{"lang":"en","text":"Team members must fulfil their duties with their full efforts. Staying motivated shows team spirit because it shows that you want the team to do well. This includes being motivated to give your best in practice and in competition, as well as outside of team activities. For example, a baseball player can show team spirit by being motivated to practice his swing outside of practice."},{"lang":"zh","text":"团队成员必须尽职尽责。工作积极主动是团队精神的体现，因为这表明你希望整个团队有上乘的表现。这意味着成员在实践中、在竞争中以及在团队活动之外的情形下都竭尽全力。例如，篮球运动员在非训练时间还积极主动地练习，就是团队精神的体现。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Respect"},{"lang":"zh","text":"尊重"},{"lang":"en","text":"Respect for your fellow team members is a must. You can show respect to your teammates by treating everyone fairly and equally. Teammates also respect each other by allowing everyone to participate. Respecting fellow teammates keeps everyone in a good mood and encourages overall team spirit. For example,people cane show team spirit through respect by encouraging other team members who might be struggling."},{"lang":"zh","text":"必须尊重团队成员。公正公平地对待每位团队成员，就是尊重的表现。让每位成员参加团队活动，团队成员之间也会彼此尊重。尊重队友会让团队中的每个人都保持好心情，还能振奋团队精神。例如，人们可以通过鼓励正在努力奋斗的队友以示对其的尊重，这也是团队精神的表现。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":278},{"id":"r-商务英语4-6-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"The Balance Sheet","subtitle":"资产负债表","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The balance sheet is produced at the end of a company's financial year, and is a snapshot"},{"lang":"en","text":"of its financial situation. It shows the company's assets and liabilities at that point in time."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产负债表是公司在一个财政年度中，对公司的财政状况进行记录的报表。该表及时记录了公司的资产和负债状况。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are two halves to a balance sheet. The top half shows where the money is being used in the business (the net assets), and the bottom half shows where this money came from (the capital employed). The total of each half should be the same, hence the expression balance sheet."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产负债表由上、下两部分组成。上半部分显示了钱的用途（净资产），下半部分显示了钱的来源（负债）。每部分的总和应该是相等的，因此称之为资产负债表。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are two kinds of assets—long-term and short-term. The long-term assets are known as fixed assets, and include the land, buildings, machinery and vehicles that are used in connection with the business. All fixed assets except land are depreciated as they wear out over time. The total fixed assets are the value of the fixed assets, less the accumulated depreciation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产分为长期资产和短期资产。长期资产又称固定资产，包括土地、房产、与经营相关的机器和车辆。随着时间的推移，除土地之外的所有固定资产都会折损。固定资产总额等于固定资产的价值减去累积折旧。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The short-term assets are known as current assets, and include cash, stocks and receivables that are due within one year."},{"lang":"zh","text":"短期资产又称流动资产，包括现金、股票和一年内到期的应收款项。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The top half of the balance sheet also includes liabilities, that is, all debts and"},{"lang":"en","text":"obligations owed by the business to creditors. Current liabilities are those debts that must be paid within the year, such as wages earned but not yet paid. Long-term liabilities may include mortgages and other loans that will not have been paid off within the year."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产负债表的上半部分还包括负债，即企业对债权人承担的一切债务。流动负债是指年内必须要支付的债务，如应付职工薪酬。长期负债包括偿还期超过一年的抵押贷款和其他贷款。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The top half of the balance sheet therefore consists of the total of fixed and current assets, less the current and long-term liabilities, giving the net assets."},{"lang":"zh","text":"因此，资产负债表的上半部分就是固定资产与流动资产的总和，减去流动负债和长期负债，由此得出的净资产值。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The bottom half of the balance sheet shows where this money came from. For a limited company, this will include the money raised by issuing shares, and is known as the share capital. The business may also have"},{"lang":"en","text":"Plowed some of the money back into building up the business. This is called retained profit."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产负债表的下半部分显示了资金的来源。对于有限公司而言，这包括通过发行股票筹集的资金，即股本。公司可以将部分资金投资于公司业务，这就是留存收益。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The bottom half of the balance sheet therefore consists of the total of share capital and retained profits, giving the capital employed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"资产负债表的下半部分就是股本金与留存收益的总额，即动用资本。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":334},{"id":"r-商务英语4-6-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Benefits of Electronic Accounting Software in Organizations","subtitle":"会计电算化给企业带来的有利之处","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Data management"},{"lang":"zh","text":"数据管理"},{"lang":"en","text":"The manual handling of data, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, payrolls , debt collection"},{"lang":"en","text":"and other accounting tasks, is time-consuming. Large organizations will find it impossible to manage all these data if manual accounting is used. Electronic accounting software facilitates purchase-order control, invoice processing, payment selection and handling. Because the systems are automated, tasks are managed simultaneously. These systems also enhance data accuracy by double-checking a vendor's invoice against the purchase order and the inventory module."},{"lang":"zh","text":"人工处理数据，包括应收账款、应付账款、工资核算、债务清算和其他会计业务，十分耗时。大型公司发现，如果采用手工记账，则不可能进行有效的数据管理。会计电算化软件可以辅助管理采购订单、处理发票、选择支付方式和进行支付。因为系统是自动的，所以记账任务可以自动完成。对照采购订单和存货清单，该系统仔细检查供应商发票，从而提高数据的准确性。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Faster and more efficient in processing information"},{"lang":"zh","text":"信息处理更加快捷、高效"},{"lang":"en","text":"Software enables the generation of many types of useful reports and documents for customers and government agencies and also for management to make decisions. These include invoices, checks and account statements as well as tax-return forms. With modules such as point of sale, the system automatically generates sales slips or sales invoices, reports on items and produces reports on customer and salesperson activities. The payroll module generates and prints payroll checks and can be attached to the general ledger to automatically facilitate the setting aside of the correct amount for the Federal Insurance Contribution Act tax."},{"lang":"zh","text":"该软件可以生成各种有用的报告和文件，方便客户、政府部门和管理层进行决策。这些包括发票、账簿、账目报表和退税表格。该系统拥有诸如销售点之类的模块，可以自动生成销售单或销售发票、商品报告、客户及销售人员活动报告。工资单模块生成和打印工资单，附至总分类账之上，自动生成《联邦保险捐税法》所要求缴纳税种的正确数额。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Cost benefits"},{"lang":"zh","text":"成本效益"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are more and more manufacturers of software for accounting; this has made the different types of software more accessible in terms of costs and variety. In the long term, there is a remarkable return on investment for organizations that Install accounting software. Manual accounting is time-consuming and therefore is invariably costly to the organization. In the absence of automated systems, plenty of labor is required to perform core and non-core accounting functions. But electronic accounting only requires one or two people for accounting, as most data is managed by the system."},{"lang":"zh","text":"由于会计软件生产商越来越多，在成本和种类上，有很多不同类型的软件可供选择。从长远来看，使用会计软件的公司，其投资回报率可观。人工记账十分耗时，所以公司担负的成本很高。在没有自动化系统的情况下，需要大量的人力来完成核心的和非核心的会计职能。但是会计电算化仅需要1~2名员工来负责会计工作，因为大多数的数据都是由系统来处理的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Communication and decision-making benefits"},{"lang":"zh","text":"沟通和决策效益"},{"lang":"en","text":"The efficient and timely generation of important documents facilitates communication in an organization, especially a large one. Accounting software essentially connects all other functions and departments in an organization. Decision-makers can easily access inquiries, memos, payrolls, invoices and reports. Unlike manual accounting, data is stored, duplicated and backed up for future reference and to enhance accountability in the organization."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有效和及时生成重要文件有助于公司内部的沟通，对于大型公司而言更是如此。会计电算化软件从根本上将公司内部的所有其他功能和部门都联系起来。决策者可以很容易进行查询，获取备忘录、工资、发票和报告等信息。与人工记账不同，电子记账可以存储、复制、备份数据以备将来参照，还可以增强组织的责任。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":345},{"id":"r-商务英语4-7-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Online Shopping Spree Sets Record","subtitle":"疯狂网购创纪录","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Chinese shoppers spent billions online yesterday as they took advantage of discounts offered on Singles' Day (November 11). It is a festival for young single people to celebrate by eating together, sending gifts or going shopping, thus seized on by online retailers to increase sales."},{"lang":"zh","text":"中国购物者昨天趁光棍节（11月11日）打折的机会，在线花费数十亿元。这本是单身年轻人通过一起吃饭、赠送礼物或购物来庆祝的一个节日，结果被网上零售商利用来增加销售量。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It took only 13 hours for sales on just two online sites, Taobao and Tmall, to fly past last year's overall total of 19.1 billion yuan (US$3.1 billion). The final figure of Singles' Day reached an astonishing 35.02 billion yuan as hundreds of thousands of consumers rushed to buy clothes, furniture, and home decoration items at discount prices. What friends and colleagues greeted each other with that day was “Bought anything today?” as they exchanged tales of bargains or disappointing news of popular items sold out minutes after the spree began at midnight."},{"lang":"zh","text":"淘宝和天猫两个网站只花了13个小时，就超越了去年全年的销售总额191亿元（31亿美元）。因上千万的消费者争相以折扣价格购买衣服、家具和家居装饰品，光棍节当天最终的销售额达到惊人的350.2亿元。“今天买什么了?”是朋友和同事们那天的彼此问候语，同时，他们分享便宜货的故事或畅销商品在午夜购物狂欢开始几分钟后便被卖光的失望消息。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In under nine hours, turnover at the Alibaba Group's Tmall and Taobao sites had exceeded that of last year's"},{"lang":"en","text":"Cyber Monday, a similar event in the United States."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不到9个小时，阿里巴巴旗下的淘宝和天猫两个网站的销售额就超越了去年美国的类似事件“网购星期一”的销售额。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“We hope other e-commerce sites also did a good job as we want Singles' Day to be a holiday for consumers and a good chance for retailers to discover the unmet needs of shoppers,” Jack Ma, founder and chairman of Alibaba Group, told reporters."},{"lang":"zh","text":"阿里巴巴集团创始人兼董事长马云告诉记者：“我们希望其他电子商务网站也能做得很好，因为我们希望光棍节成为消费者的节日，也成为零售商发现消费者尚未得到满足的需求的好机会。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"“It's not a difficult thing to bring our total transaction size to 100 billion yuan in a couple of years but we hope to do more to help vendors and manufacturers to upgrade their products and service to reach more clients,” Ma said at a news briefing ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"马云在一次新闻发布会上说：“在几年内把我们的总交易额提高到1 000亿元并不难，但我们希望能做更多的工作，来帮助供应商和制造商提升产品质量和服务质量，以此吸引更多的客户。”"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":253},{"id":"r-商务英语4-7-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Cyber Monday Clicks in with Record Sales","subtitle":"“网购星期一”网上销售创纪录","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Cyber Monday rocked while mobile sales roared ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当移动销售火爆时，“网购星期一”震撼无比。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The day widely regarded as the Super Bowl of online sales created a record day for retailers, including Walmart, and marked a shift in shopping preferences as smartphones and tablets drove nearly a third of traffic — and for some retailers, more than half."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这一天被视为超级在线购物日，为包括沃尔玛在内的零售商打造了创纪录的一天。这标志着人们的购物偏好发生了变化，因为智能手机和平板电脑驱动了近三分之一的销售量，而对有的零售商而言，已超过一半的销售量。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Walmart.com expects to register its biggest Cyber Monday yet, coming off a record Black Friday weekend online. Heading into the afternoon Monday, the website had already sold out of PlayStation 4 and Xbox One"},{"lang":"en","text":"consoles, which weren't even discounted . Significant savings on TVs and tablets also encouraged shopping, says Joel Anderson, CEO of Walmart.com."},{"lang":"zh","text":"沃尔玛公司希望能够注册迄今为止其最大的“网络星期一”，创造了“黑色星期五”的周末在线狂销的新纪录。进行到周一下午时，网站已经卖光了第4代家用游戏机和Xbox One游戏机，这些甚至都没有折扣。沃尔玛首席执行官乔尔·安德森说，电视和平板电脑的大幅度让利也刺激了购物。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Retailers from Target to Sears are fast evolving Cyber Monday into something more akin to Cyber Week, as online deals stretch well beyond Monday."},{"lang":"zh","text":"从塔吉特到西尔斯的零售商们正迅速把“网购星期一”发展成为更似“网购一星期”的促销，因为在线交易在星期一之后依然很好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As of 6 p.m. ET, sales on Amazon were up 44.3% over last year, while sales at eBay were up 32.1%, according to Channel Advisor , which tracks third-party sellers on eBay and Amazon. The online marketplaces are doing well in part because shoppers are heading to those sites to find popular products that are selling out at regular retailers, says Scot Wingo, CEO of ChannelAdvisor."},{"lang":"zh","text":"电子商务平台畅路销追踪eBay和亚马逊上的第三方卖家，根据畅路销提供的数据，截至美国东部时间下午6点，亚马逊的销售额比去年同期增长了44.3%，eBay的销售额增长了32.1%。畅路销的首席执行官斯科特·温格说，在线市场销售状况良好的部分原因是，消费者去这些网站购买普通零售商店在售的畅销产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Flash-sale site Rue La La started Cyber Monday deals on Sunday with a “Cyberthon” that drew more than 350,000 people to the site. The sale promoted as much as 80% off on more than 150 brands. On Monday, sales of Cole Haan and Pandora Jewelry merchandise were strongest, CEO Steve Davis says."},{"lang":"zh","text":"限时抢购网站Rue La La在周日就以“网购马拉松”开始了“网购星期一”的交易，吸引了超过35万人到网站购物。此次促销活动中，150多个品牌的最高折扣达2折。首席执行官史蒂夫·戴维斯说，在周一，可汗品牌和潘多拉珠宝品牌的商品销售情况最为强劲。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":243},{"id":"r-商务英语4-8-1","book":"商务英语4","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Organizing a Business in Different Ways","subtitle":"以不同的方式组织企业","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Businesses are structured in different ways to meet different needs. The simplest form of business is called an individual or sole proprietorship . The proprietor owns all of the property of the business and is responsible for everything."},{"lang":"zh","text":"企业是以不同的方式组建的，这是为了满足不同的需求。最简单的企业形式叫作个人独资或独资经营。企业的经营者拥有企业的所有财产，并对一切负责。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another kind of business is a partnership. Two or more people go into business together. An agreement is usually needed to decide how much of the partnership each person controls. One kind of partnership is called a"},{"lang":"en","text":"limited liability partnership. There are full partners and limited partners. Limited partners may not share as much in the profits, but they also have less responsibility for the business. Doctors, lawyers and accountants often form partnerships to share their risks and profits. A husband and wife can form a business partnership together. Partnerships exist only for as long as the owners remain alive.The same is true of individual proprietorships."},{"lang":"zh","text":"另一种企业形式是合伙经营，即两个或多个人一起合伙经营。这样做通常需要一个协议来决定每个人控制的合伙企业的份额有多少。合伙关系中有一种称为有限责任合伙，有完全责任合伙人和有限责任合伙人之分。有限责任合伙人可能不会分到太多利润，但他们对企业的责任也较小。医生、律师和会计师经常结成合伙关系来共同分担风险和利润。丈夫和妻子也能一起建立企业合伙关系。只要所有者还在世，这种合伙关系就存在。个人独资企业也是这样。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But corporations are designed to have an unlimited lifetime . A corporation is the most complex kind of business organization. Corporations can sell stock as a way to raise money. Stocks represent shares of ownership in a company. Investors who buy stock can trade their shares or keep them as long as the company is in business."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但是，公司被设计成没有经营期限的限制，它是最复杂的一种企业形式。公司可以通过出售股票来筹集资金。股票代表着一个公司的所有权。只要公司还在经营，购买股票的投资者就可以进行股票交易或保留他们的股份。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A corporation is recognized as an entity — its own legal being , separate from its owners. A board of directors controls corporate policies. The directors appoint top company officers. The directors might or might not hold shares in the corporation. Corporations can have a few major shareholders, or ownership can be spread among the general public. But not all corporations are traditional businesses that sell stock. Some non-profit groups are also organized as corporations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"股份公司被认为是一个实体——法人，独立于公司所有人而存在。董事会控制着公司的政策，董事任命公司高层管理人员。董事们可能持有公司股份，也可能不持有公司股份。公司可以有几个大股东，或者所有权可以分布在普通公众中。但并非所有公司都是出售股票的传统企业，一些非营利组织也采用公司的组织形式。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":274},{"id":"r-商务英语4-8-2","book":"商务英语4","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"Three Americans Win Nobel Economics Prize in 2013","subtitle":"三名美国人获2013年度诺贝尔经济学奖","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The Royal Swedish academy of Sciences awarded the Nobel Prize in economics to three Americans, Eugene Fama, Lars Peter Hansen and Robert Shiller on Oct. 14, 2013. Eugene Fama and Lars Peter Hansen are both professors at the University of Chicago. Robert Shiller is a professor at Yale University.They will share the prize worth about 1.2 million dollars."},{"lang":"zh","text":"瑞典皇家科学院于2013年10月14日向三名美国人尤金·法玛、拉尔斯·彼得·汉森和罗伯特·希勒授予诺贝尔经济学奖。尤金·法玛和拉尔斯·彼得·汉森都是芝加哥大学的教授。罗伯特·希勒是耶鲁大学的教授。他们将分享价值约120万美元的奖金。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“This year's prize in economic sciences is about predictions .” All three of this year's prize winners are mainly known for their research and explanations of pricing forces in financial markets. They have had a big influence on the way people look at and talk about financial markets."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“今年的经济科学奖是关于预测的。”今年的三个获奖者都主要是因对金融市场上定价力的研究和解释而闻名的。他们对于人们看待和讨论金融市场的方式有很大影响。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Eugene Fama's research on financial markets in the 1960s led market watchers to change their ideas about investing. His ideas are linked to the theory that markets are efficient, which means market actors taking all available information to create the correct price for things at any given time. This also means that over short periods of time, it is not possible to predict prices."},{"lang":"zh","text":"尤金·法玛在20世纪60年代对金融市场的研究引导了市场观察者，改变了他们对投资的看法。他的思想与市场有效理论相关，这个理论意味着市场参与者在任何给定的时间内利用所有可用信息来确定合适的价格。这也意味着在短时间内不可能预测价格。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Robert Shiller found, however, that over long periods, the opposite is true. It is possible to predict the movement of prices and that price changes are linked to human behavior."},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而，罗伯特·希勒发现，从长期来看，情况恰好相反。价格变动是可能预测的，而且价格变化与人类的行为有联系。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The findings of both economists have led to the growth of index funds, investing many different securities as a way to reduce risk. Mr. Shiller also helped to create the Standard & Poor's Case-Shiller home prices index. That index follows home prices across the United States."},{"lang":"zh","text":"两位经济学家的研究结果引起了指数基金的增长，这些基金投资不同证券，作为降低风险的方式。希勒先生还帮助创立了标准普尔/凯斯-希勒房价指数。该指数追踪美国各地的房价。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Lars Peter Hansen developed a method for studying historical pricing information. His method supports Mr. Shiller's findings and has influenced efforts to predict prices in the financial industry."},{"lang":"zh","text":"拉尔斯·彼得·汉森开发了一种研究历史定价信息的方法。他的方法支持希勒先生的发现，并影响了金融业的价格预测。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The Nobel Prize in economics was not created by Alfred Nobel, but was established in his memory by Sweden 's central bank in 1968."},{"lang":"zh","text":"诺贝尔经济学奖不是由艾尔弗雷德 • 诺贝尔创立的，而是为了纪念他，由瑞典中央银行于1968年建立的。"}],"source":"商务英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":294},{"id":"r-理工英语3-1-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Top Three Green Home Innovations","subtitle":"三大重要绿色家居创新","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In the last decade a growing number of people have become interested in conserving energy and preserving the environment by living “green”. There are many things you can do to reduce your carbon emissions and help to make the earth a better place for future generations. Here are a few suggestions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在过去的十年里，越来越多的人对采取绿色生活方式来节约能源、保护环境产生了兴趣（在过去的十年，越来越多的人对采取绿色生活方式来节能环保产生了兴趣）。你可以做很多事情来降低二氧化碳排放量，使我们的地球更适合后代生存。以下有几点建议。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Although LED lamps initially cost more than standard incandescent or compact fluorescent bulbs, these long-lasting LED lamps will eventually be worth the money because of energy saved. LED lamps also produce a cleaner, more natural light."},{"lang":"zh","text":"尽管刚开始LED 灯比标准白炽灯或（节能灯）价钱都贵，但耐用的LED 灯因为节能最终是值这个钱的。而且，LED灯光更干净、更自然。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Water” is a hot topic, especially in the Southwest. Whole-house water filters are now available for cleaning and reusing water from showers and baths. Gray water systems redirect the used water from washing machines to lawns or gardens."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“水”是一个热门话题，尤其是在西南部。现在全屋水过滤器可以对淋浴和浴缸水清洁再利用。灰水系统可以把洗衣机排出的废水引到草坪或花园。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In recent years indoor air pollution has gotten a lot of attention. Building materials and embellishments like paint and carpets can “shed” chemical compounds into the atmosphere, and because a home is an enclosed space, those compounds can sometimes accumulate to dangerous levels. 10 Installing a whole-house air purification system is one way to keep indoor air clean and circulating."},{"lang":"zh","text":"近年来，室内空气污染引起了广泛的关注。建筑材料和油漆、地毯之类的装饰材料会向空气中释放化合物，由于家是一个封闭的空间，这些化合物有时可积聚到危险水平。安装一个全屋空气净化系统是保持室内空气清洁和循环的一种方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Going “green” doesn't have to be a challenge. A home is a long-term investment, and you don't have to start from scratch. 11 You can make small changes like choosing environmentally friendly paint or LED bulbs. Chances are your home will need improvements eventually. 12 Whenever possible, choose upgrades that will reduce your carbon footprint. It's good for the planet, and it's good for you."},{"lang":"zh","text":"过“绿色”生活不一定是一个挑战。家是一种长期投资，你没有必要从头做起。你可以做一些小的改变，如选择环保涂料或LED灯泡。你的家终究还是需要改进，只要有可能就选择升级换代，这将减少你的碳排放。这对地球有好处，对你也有好处。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":251},{"id":"r-理工英语3-1-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Five Tips for Making Your House Greener","subtitle":"使房子更环保的5个建议","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"There are plenty of ways to make your house greener. It doesn't matter how many people reside in your home. It doesn't even matter about the size of your home. What matters is how your house looks and how it affects you and others residing in it."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有许多方法使你的房子变得更环保，不管有多少人住在你的房子里，也不管你的房子有多大，要紧的是你的房子看起来如何以及它怎样影响你和住在房子里的其他人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It is very important to make your house greener because it has a direct impact on your health. If you keep your house green, you avoid the risk of many dangerous diseases. Here are some ways to keep your house greener."},{"lang":"zh","text":"把房子变得更环保十分重要，因为这直接关系到你的健康。如果房子环保，你就避免了罹患许多危险疾病的风险。以下是使房子更环保的几种方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Indoor material must be of good quality for windows, doors, cupboards etc. These things play an important role in keeping the house green. Doors and cupboards must be of high quality wood. Aluminum windows should be used. You should use high-quality paints for walls, doors, windows and cupboards."},{"lang":"zh","text":"室内窗、门和橱柜等一定要用优质材料，这些对于保持房子环保起着重要的作用。门和橱柜必须是高质量的木材，要用铝质窗，要用高质量的涂料来刷墙、门、窗和橱柜。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Oxygen is a necessary element for life. For a healthy life, windows and doors should be wide and usually they should be kept open for at least 15 hours a day, as fresh air is good for your health."},{"lang":"zh","text":"氧气是生命中不可或缺的元素。若想健康，门窗每天至少应敞开15小时，因为新鲜空气对健康有益。"},{"lang":"en","text":"No one wants an empty house, and plants definitely play an air-freshening role. First, plants provide you with oxygen necessary for survival. Second, plants and especially flowers spread an attractive fragrance. All unhealthy odors are eradicated from your home and you feel fresh whenever you are inside it. Flowers also make your home interior look more appealing."},{"lang":"zh","text":"没有人想要一栋空房，植物显然起着着净化空气的作用。首先，植物提供了生存必需的氧气。其次，植物，尤其是花儿会散发出迷人的香味，所有不健康的气味都会被清除掉，无论何时你身处室内都能感到很清新。花儿也使家里看起来更令人心旷神怡。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's very important to dispose of waste far away from your home every day. When waste is kept untouched for many days, it attracts bacteria and viruses. Flies and mosquitoes are attracted to garbage and start multiplying in such places. As a result, diseases are caused."},{"lang":"zh","text":"每天将你家里的垃圾远远地处理掉也很重要。几天不处理，垃圾就会滋生细菌和病毒，引来苍蝇和蚊子并开始在这些地方繁殖，从而造成疾病。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Usually unclean fans, floors and walls breed bacteria and viruses, which are then carried by flies and mosquitoes. These carriers then infect humans through contaminated food or by direct contact with the body. It's always recommended to use anti-bacterial or anti-viral cleaners to clean fans, walls, floors, laptops, and TVs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"通常，不干净的风扇、地板和墙壁滋生细菌和病毒，然后由苍蝇和蚊子携带，通过污染食物或与直接的身体接触使人类被感染。要使用抗菌或抗病毒清洁剂来清洁风扇、墙壁、地板、手提电脑和电视机。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":331},{"id":"r-理工英语3-2-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"I. M. Pei and the Louvre Pyramid","subtitle":"贝聿铭和卢浮宫金字塔","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Ieoh Ming Pei is definitely one of the biggest names in architecture. Born in China in 1917, Pei was the son of a prominent banker. He grew up mostly in Hong Kong and Shanghai. At the age of 17, Pei left for the United States to study architecture at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology and then Harvard University."},{"lang":"zh","text":"贝聿铭无疑是建筑界史上最响亮的名字之一。贝1917年出生于中国，他父亲是一位杰出银行家。他大部分时间在香港和上海长大，17岁时，贝前往美国马萨诸塞理工学院学习建筑，接着又到哈佛大学求学。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Pei attracted great attention in the U.S. for the John F. Kennedy Library in Boston, but it was the Louvre Pyramid that brought him worldwide fame. In 1981, the newly elected President of France came up with an ambitious plan for a variety of construction projects, including the renovation of the Louvre Museum. Pei was invited to join the renovating team. Pei finally agreed to take on the project after three secretive trips to Paris."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在美国，贝因为设计波士顿的肯尼迪图书馆而受到广泛关注，但是让他享誉世界的却是卢浮宫金字塔。1981年，新当选的法国总统制定了一个雄心勃勃的计划，要大兴土木，其中就包括对卢浮宫博物馆的改造。贝被邀请加入改造团队。先后三次秘访巴黎后，他最终同意接手这个项目。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Pei designed not only a glass and steel pyramid to serve as the entrance to the Louvre, but also a transformation of the interiors. The public reacted harshly to the design, mostly because of the proposed pyramid. In an attempt to soothe public anger, Pei took a suggestion from then-mayor of Paris and placed a full-sized model of the pyramid in the courtyard of the Louvre. During the four days of its exhibition, an estimated 60,000 people visited the site. Critics eased their opposition after witnessing the proposed scale of the pyramid."},{"lang":"zh","text":"贝不仅设计了一个玻璃和钢结构的金字塔作为卢浮宫的入口，还进行了内部改造。人们当时并不喜欢这个设计，主要是因为这个金字塔的设计。为了平息公众的愤怒，贝采纳了当时巴黎市长的建议，将一个真实大小的金字塔模型放在卢浮宫大厅里。在为期四天的展览里，约六万人前来参观。在看到金字塔的拟建规格后，批评者的抵触情绪有所缓和。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The new entrance was opened to the public in March, 1989. By that time, public opinion had softened on the Pyramid; a poll found a 56 percent approval rating for the pyramid. “The much-feared pyramid has become adorable,” wrote a French writer. The experience was exhausting for Pei, but also rewarding. “After the Louvre,” Pei said later, “I thought no project would be too difficult.” Now the Louvre Pyramid is Pei's most famous structure."},{"lang":"zh","text":"新入口于1989年3月正式对外开放。当时，公众对金字塔的态度已经缓和了。一项民意调查发现民众对金字塔的满意度高达56％。一位法国作家写到：“令人相当担心的金字塔变得令人喜欢了”。对于贝，虽然这个经历令他疲惫，但也有回报。“经历了对卢浮宫的改造，”贝说，“没有一个项目会叫我觉得太难”。现在卢浮宫金字塔是贝最具代表性的建筑作品。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":297},{"id":"r-理工英语3-2-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Amphibious Architecture: Flood-Proof Home Designs","subtitle":"水陆两用建筑：防洪房屋的设计","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Instead of trying to beat back the rising flood, innovative amphibious buildings can adapt to the rising flood. These buildings are ready for whatever Mother Nature might throw at them-even 10-foot floodwaters. Let's take a look at just two of them."},{"lang":"zh","text":"极具创新的水陆两用建筑可以适应不断上涨的洪水，而不是试图去阻止它。这些建筑可以应对大自然所发生的一切，哪怕是十英尺高的洪水。我们一起来看看其中两种建筑。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The UK's first amphibious house is located on the Thames River. And the first amphibious building in Britain will be completed soon. Baca Architects designed this home for a couple who wanted to live on a flood-prone island in the Thames River, an island easily attacked by floods. This building is equipped with a terraced landscape. And this terraced landscape acts as an early warning system when the waters are rising. The terraces will be filled with water before the “wet dock” under the house is, and then the home itself will slowly rise to stay above the water."},{"lang":"zh","text":"英国第一栋水陆两用房位于泰晤士河旁，而且这栋房子马上就要竣工了。泰晤士河上的一个岛屿常发生洪水，一对夫妇却想定居于此，巴卡建筑事务所为他们设计了这座房子。房子装上了台阶，当水位不断上升的时候，台阶可以当作一个早期预警系统。台阶将比房子下面的“湿坞”先充满水，然后房子本身会缓慢上升，并保持在水面以上。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Residents of Makoko in Nigeria have been building houses on stilts for generations. People there go from one house to another by canoe. As sea levels are rising, officials threaten to tear down the entire community. If these houses are torn down, 250,000 people will be homeless and have to look for a new place to live. Architects found a solution in floating structures with improved sanitation conditions. The first completed example is a three-story solar-powered school."},{"lang":"zh","text":"尼日利亚的马卡卡居民世世代代都在建吊脚楼。人们依靠独木舟在吊脚楼中来往。因为海平面不断上升，官员们声称要拆除整个社区。房子一旦被拆除，25万人将无家可归，他们只能寻找一个新的地方去生活。建筑师找到了解决办法——带有改善的公共卫生条件的浮体结构。第一个已完成的样板房屋是一所利用太阳能的三层学校。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This amazing floating school addresses social, physical and ecological needs. Built on top of 256 recycled blue barrels, the school buildings are made of triangular bamboo and wood. Makoko's residents made full use of their skills when building these structures. With three levels, the solar-powered high school has room for 100 local kids and recycles rainwater to flush the toilets. And the cost for the whole school structures was under $7,000."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这种神奇的浮体学校满足了社会需求、物质需求和生态需求。浮体学校建在了256个蓝色回收桶上面，校舍是由竹质和木质三角做成的。在搭建这些结构的时候，马卡卡居民充分利用了他们的技能。太阳能中学一共有三层，能同时容纳当地100名孩子，还可以回收雨水来冲洗厕所。整个学校的建造成本还不到7000美金。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":289},{"id":"r-理工英语3-3-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"Vegolution","subtitle":"素食行动","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The Belgian city of Ghent has declared Thursdays meat-free days. Should cities around the world join in the vegolution?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"比利时根特市已经声明把星期四定为无肉日。世界上其他城市是否也应该加入素食运动呢？"},{"lang":"en","text":"By encouraging people to eat no meat one day a week, Ghent hopes to improve public health and reduce our impact on the environment. In fact, according to the UN's Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO): “The livestock sector has become one of the top two or three most significant contributors to the most serious environmental problems.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"根特市鼓励人们一星期有一天不吃肉，希望藉此增进公众的健康，减少对环境的影响。事实上，联合国粮食及农业组织（FAO）指出:畜牧业已经成为导致严重环境问题的首要原因之一。"},{"lang":"en","text":"And if the idea can be accepted among people, the impact will be enormous. If everyone in Flanders (population: six million) does not eat meat one day a week, it will save as much CO 2 in a year as taking half a million cars off the road. Imagine if every city in the world followed suit!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果这个想法能被人们接受，其影响将会是巨大的。如果佛兰德斯（人口：六百万）每个人每周都有一天不吃肉，一年减排的二氧化碳相当于马路上五十万辆汽车的排放量。试想一下：如果世界上各个城市都效仿的话会怎么样！所以就算我昨天在布鲁塞尔外出吃饭，我也选择了素食。"},{"lang":"en","text":"So even though I ate out in Brussels yesterday, I chose a veggie meal. Don't get me wrong. I'm by no means vegetarian. In fact, I love flesh very much. But for the past couple of years, my wife and I have changed our diet and try to eat meat or fish only a couple of times a week. After a period of adjustment, we both feel healthier."},{"lang":"zh","text":"别误会，我可绝不是一个素食主义者。事实上，我非常喜欢吃肉。但过去几年，我的妻子和我已经改变了饮食习惯，我们一个星期只吃几次肉或鱼。经过一段时间的调整，我们俩都感到更健康了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“There has been a great increase in demand for vegetarian dishes at my restaurant over the past few years,” a Ghent restaurant said. “The selection of vegetarian dishes we offer has also grown considerably.” He adds that his clients are eating veggie mainly for their own well-being, and then, the environment."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根特一家餐厅说：“过去几年，餐厅对素食餐点的需求量大增，我们提供的可选择素食餐点也比以前增加了很多”，他补充说，客人吃素食主要是为了自己的健康，然后才是为了环境。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The idea has been picked up by media around the world and captured the attention of ordinary people. One meatless day a week is a great idea, and no loss for those who want a tasty diet. Let the vegolution begin!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"世界各地的媒体都报道了这个想法，并受到很多普通民众的关注。一个星期一天无肉是一个伟大的想法，对那些想要美味饮食的人来说也没有任何损失。让素食运动行动起来吧！"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":293},{"id":"r-理工英语3-3-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Earth Hour","subtitle":"地球一小时","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"More than 134 countries across the world, including the UK, turned off their lights for an hour on Sunday. The event is in hopes of creating a sustainable future for the planet. Environmental charity World Wildlife Fund (WWF) has organized the Earth Hour event."},{"lang":"zh","text":"包括英国在内，世界上超过134个国家，在周日熄灯一小时。这个活动旨在为我们居住的星球创造一个可持续的未来。环保慈善组织世界自然基金会组织策划了地球一小时活动。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The event saw iconic buildings such as Big Ben, the BT Tower, Buckingham Palace, Windsor Castle and Edinburgh Castle blacking out for an hour. The event took place at 8:30 p.m. Sunday around the world and it started in Fiji, New Zealand and Australia. The aim is to call on governments, organizations and individuals to take actions to tackle climate change."},{"lang":"zh","text":"大本钟、英国电信塔、白金汉宫、温莎古堡、爱丁堡城堡等世界标志性建筑都参与了这次熄灯一小时活动。该活动始于斐济、新西兰和澳大利亚，并在周日晚上8点半席卷全球，其目的在于呼吁政府、组织和个人行动起来应对气候变化。"},{"lang":"en","text":"At the Royal Albert Hall in London, television presenter Kirsty Gallacher led a team of 60 cyclists from the UK-World Wildlife Fund. They aimed to appeal for the public to pay attention to endangered species including dolphins and tigers. Colin Butfield, head of campaigns, WWF-UK, said: “Our event at the Royal Albert Hall, alongside the hundreds of thousands of events across the world, shows global support for the need to tackle climate change and protect the natural world. The challenge for our future well-being could not be greater. WWF's Earth Hour is about to create a message so powerful that governments and individuals cannot fail to take notice.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"在伦敦的皇家阿尔伯特音乐厅里，电视节目主持人Kirsty Gallacher带领来自世界自然基金会的60名自行车手组成的团队。他们旨在呼吁公众关注包括海豚和老虎在内的濒危物种。活动的领导人是来自世界自然基金会英国分会的Colin Butfield，他说：“我们在皇家阿尔伯特音乐厅的活动，以及世界各地的众多活动，都显示了全世界应对气候变化、保护自然的需求和支持。阻碍我们未来幸福的困难不会增加。世界自然基金会发起的“地球一小时”活动，必将发出一个强有力的信息，引发所有政府和个人的关注。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Earth Hour started in 2007 in Sydney, Australia, when 2.2 million individuals and more than 2,000 businesses turned their lights off for one hour to take a stand against climate change. The following year, Earth Hour had become a global sustainability movement with more than 50 million people across 35 countries participating. Four of the world's five tallest buildings turned off their lights with the tallest, the 828-metre Burg Khalifa in Dubai, switching off about half a million lights. Also darkening for the occasion were floodlights at natural wonders such as Niagara and Victoria Falls."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2007年，地球一小时在澳大利亚的悉尼发起，当时220万个人和超过2000家企业熄灯一小时以表明对抗气候变化的立场。第二年，“地球一小时”已经发展成为一个全球性的可持续运动，共有35个国家5000多万人参与。全世界最高的5幢建筑物有4幢熄灯，其中最高的是828米的迪拜哈利发塔，关闭了约50万盏灯。尼亚加拉大瀑布和维多利亚大瀑布等自然景观的投光灯也为这一活动熄灯一小时。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":304},{"id":"r-理工英语3-4-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Parents Use TV as an Electronic Babysitter","subtitle":"电视被父母用作电子保姆","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Television has become such a major part of life that many American parents use it as a babysitter. A new study shows that almost one-third of families have TVs in children's bedrooms, and the number of television programs geared toward infants is growing."},{"lang":"zh","text":"电视现在变成了生活中如此重要的一部分，许多美国的父母使用电视来照看孩子。一项新的研究表明在几乎三分之一的家庭里，孩子的卧室里都有电视，面向婴儿的电视节目在不断增加。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Katie Weaver has her hands full. Four children in her kitchen, and two of them are hers. All of them are under the age of six, and thirsty at the same time. It's enough to get on the nerves of any adult. Like many of the 1,000 parents surveyed in a Kaiser Family Foundation study, Katie admits she sometimes uses TV as a pacifier when her children are overly- excited and it usually works."},{"lang":"zh","text":"凯蒂忙得不可开交。厨房里有四个孩子，其中两个是她的。这些孩子都在六岁以下，都在同一时间口渴，这足以让任何成人感到烦躁。凯撒家庭基金会曾经对1000个父母进行了调查，像里面的许多人一样，凯蒂承认，有时候当孩子过于吵闹时，她会用电视来安抚孩子，通常这个办法还很管用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“I don't use it as a babysitter because they don't watch enough or long enough for that, but if they are very hyped up, sometimes I'll use TV to calm them down, ” she said. While there has been some concern that watching too much television fosters obesity in children, the long-term effects of parking a very young child in front of the “tube” are not clear."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“我没有使用电视来照看小孩，因为他们不会长时间看电视，但如果他们过于兴奋，有时我会用电视让他们平静下来”， 她说。尽管有人担心，看电视时间太长会导致儿童肥胖，但长期影响尚不明确。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“A lot of them are two-parent working families, so we're talking about having very little time with the children. If that time is used in front of a screen, rather than interactively, it's compromising the way these children are learning to pay attention, the way they're learning to problem-solve, and most importantly, the way they're learning to think and use language, ” said Greenspan, who is the expert of the Kaiser Family Foundation study."},{"lang":"zh","text":"格林斯潘是凯撒家庭基金会的研究专家， 他说：“这么做的家庭通常是父母俩人都工作，也就是父母和孩子可以共处的时间很少。如果这些时间被用来看电视，而不是与孩子进行互动，这影响着孩子集中注意力的能力、解决问题的能力，更重要的是，影响着他们的思维和语言表达能力。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"In the survey, parents of children much younger, up to a year old, report viewing averages of an hour per day. For kids one to two years, it's close to an hour and a half. Greenspan believes babies and children under the age of two should not be watching at all and he's worried that some parents are concealing the real truth. “If anything, it's an underestimation, because if a kid's watching two hours, they might say an hour. So I think what we're getting is a minimal estimate, ” he said."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在调查中，不到一岁孩子的父母们报告说他们的孩子每天平均看一个小时电视。对于一到两岁的孩子，看电视时间接近一个半小时。格林斯潘认为两岁以下的孩子根本不应该看电视，他担心其中一些父母没说实话，“或者是他们估计不足，如果孩子看两个小时的电视，他们会说只看了一个小时。所以我认为，我们得到的只是最低估算”，他说。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Television programming for very young children has been increasing. Yet one researcher involved in the Kaiser study says there is still no evidence that children up to the age of two learn anything of value from television."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为年幼孩子开设的电视节目一直在增加，但是凯撒家庭基金会的一位研究专家说没有证据证明不到两岁的孩子能从电视中学到有价值的东西。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":387},{"id":"r-理工英语3-4-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"Smart Lock","subtitle":"智能锁","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In the home of the future, you can skip the keys. Just tap your phone, your door swings open."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在未来的家中，你不再需要钥匙，只需轻点手机，家门马上被打开。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A new company with a high-powered designer is hoping to take that vision to the masses. That company, August, introduced its version of the so-called smart-lock to the public last week. The lock is the brainchild of CEO Jason Johnson and renowned designer Yves Béhar."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一家名叫August，拥有超强设计师的新公司正希望把这幅愿景带给大众。上周，该公司向公众推出了自己的智能锁产品。这种智能锁是首席执行官杰森•约翰逊和知名设计师伊夫•贝哈尔的杰作。"},{"lang":"en","text":"While people may like the idea of smart homes, according to research firm IHS, only 5.6 million smart platforms have been installed globally. But the number is expected to rise to 44.6 million by 2018."},{"lang":"zh","text":"研究公司IHS表示，尽管人们可能喜欢智能家居这个理念，但全球目前只安装了560万套智能平台。不过到2018年，这个数字有望升至4460万。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Smooth and round, August's lock allows users to unlock their doors by using their phones. Customers can also let in a babysitter or a maid by issuing them a temporary wireless key. “We're approaching it as a consumer product rather than a piece of technology, ” says Béhar."},{"lang":"zh","text":"August智能锁光滑圆润，用户可以通过手机开门，还能给保姆或家政人员一把临时的无线钥匙。贝哈尔称：“我们将其作为消费产品而不是一项技术来开发的。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The lock, which uses Bluetooth, fits smoothly over an old-fashioned door with the help of two screws and some wing flaps so customers can retrofit their doors without altering the appearance. Users open the door by holding their phone app up to the lock or tapping a button on their phone screen."},{"lang":"zh","text":"无需改变房门外观，只需两颗螺丝和几个合页，就能轻松地这把使用蓝牙技术的锁安装在老式门上。用户把手机上的应用软件对准这把锁，或是按一下屏幕上的按键就能开门。"},{"lang":"en","text":"August has raised over $10 million in venture capital funding for their lock. It faces a lot of competition from both well-established brands and start-ups. Yale has its own line of smart locks while Kwikset released its smart-lock, Kevo, last year. Meanwhile, start-up Goji plans to release a sleekly designed smart-lock that will take pictures of people who knock on your door and send the pictures to your phone."},{"lang":"zh","text":"August公司已为这款智能锁募集了超过1000万美元风投。不过它正面临来自知名品牌和初创企业的激烈竞争。耶鲁公司（Yale）就有自己的智能锁产品线，Kwikset公司去年也推出了自己的智能锁Kevo。同时，初创公司Goji正计划推出一款设计时尚的智能锁，它能拍下敲门人的照片再发到用户手机上。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This lock is August's first product, but they don't seem too worried about the competition. “We'd love to see other people enter this market,” says Johnson. “It helps us if more people start using smart locks.” He adds: “We're about changing the way you interact with your home. We have keyless cars, why not keyless homes?”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"这款锁是August公司的首款产品，但该公司似乎并不太担心激烈的市场竞争态势。约翰逊称：“我们很乐意看到其它公司进入这个市场。如果更多人开始用智能锁，这对我们来说是件好事。”他说：“我们会改变你和家互动的方式。已经有无钥匙汽车了，为什么不能有无钥匙之家呢？”"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":330},{"id":"r-理工英语3-5-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Tips for Online Shopping on Singles'Day","subtitle":"光棍节网上购物的技巧","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"For those who just love to shop online, now is the best time of the year, because Nov. 11th, China's Singles'Day, will see some seemingly irrational discounts, in line with the tradition that was started in 2010."},{"lang":"zh","text":"对于喜欢网购的人来说，现在是一年中最佳时机，因为11月11日（中国的光棍节）这天，很多网店疯狂打折，这都源于2010年的传统。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Last year, Taobao, a major online shopping website, set a record of 1 billion yuan in sales on that day alone, with a whopping 19.1 billion yuan exchanging hands on the website. The number of sold items paralyzed the delivery services due to overloading. On the verge of yet another annual spending spree, it's worth reading up on the tricks and tips to make the most of the shopping carnival."},{"lang":"zh","text":"去年，最大的在线购物网站——淘宝，仅光棍节一天就创造了10 亿元的销售纪录，整个网络的销售总额更是达到了惊人的191 亿元。售出的商品使快递服务陷于瘫痪。在一年一度又一个消费热潮即将来临之际，为了更好地把握购物狂欢节，了解一些购物攻略很有必要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Put everything you want in the “shopping cart” to make a list of potential purchases. Then go through it carefully, removing anything you selected on impulse."},{"lang":"zh","text":"将你需要的一切东西放进“购物车”，形成一张预购的商品清单。然后，认真地浏览该清单，删除由于冲动而挑选的商品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Talk to service staff as early as possible. They may have already decided on a discount policy for Nov. 11th and may even ship the product to you in advance, which is a good way to avoid the heavy online traffic on that day."},{"lang":"zh","text":"尽早与客服谈好。他们可能已经制定好了“双十一”的打折方案，并且可能将货品提早寄送给你。这是避免节日那天网络阻塞的好方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Popular items will be in strong demand, so make sure you're ready to pay with the least number of procedures. It's best to deposit a reasonable amount of money in your Alipay account so that you can pay without going through any lengthy verification. If you're planning on using a credit card, you can call the bank to apply for more credit, but only spend as much as you can afford to repay"},{"lang":"zh","text":"受欢迎的商品将会很抢手，所以要确保先准备好最便捷的支付方式。最好提前往支付宝账户里存入一笔数额合适的资金，这样你支付的时候就不需要经过烦琐的身份核实程序了。如果你打算使用信用卡，可以先致电银行申请临时调高信用额度，不过要控制在你能够偿还的额度内。"},{"lang":"en","text":"With many products, such as shoes and clothes, it's better to look at them first to check their quality, size and appearance and insure you're buying the right one."},{"lang":"zh","text":"购买了大量的商品，例如，鞋子和衣服，你最好先看看，检查它们的质量、尺寸和外观，保证购买无误。"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to Alipay, there are several peak hours when online traffic is heavy and there is a higher risk of failed transactions. Try to avoid the following time spans: 12:00 p.m.-1:30 a.m., 10:00-11:00 a.m., 3:00-5:00 p.m., and 8:00-10:00 p.m."},{"lang":"zh","text":"按照阿里巴巴的说法，有几个网络阻塞和交易失败风险较高的时间段。要避开以下时间段：夜晚12：00-凌晨1：30，上午10：00-11：00，下午3：00-5：00和晚上8：00-10：00。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Because of the huge demand, delivery mistakes are inevitable, so try to track the package. If the product is perishable, keep the tracking record in case of a dispute. When the package arrives, check the item carefully before signing for it. Now you can go ahead and enjoy all your new stuff!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"由于需求量巨大，快递误差不可避免，因此，尽量跟踪你的包裹。如果你购买的是容易坏的东西，记得保留记录，以防出现纠纷。包裹到了的时候，签收前要仔细检查。现在你可以前往选购新东西了！"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":368},{"id":"r-理工英语3-5-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"E-Commerce Challenges Traditional Shops","subtitle":"电子商务挑战传统商店","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Lynne Shaner used the Internet to buy everything she needed for her wedding and holiday gifts for her husband and step-daughter. Other than food, 90 percent of her purchases are made on the computer in her Washington apartment."},{"lang":"zh","text":"林恩﹒沙纳在网上购买婚礼所需的一切东西，也上网给她丈夫和继女购买节日礼物。除了食品，90%的购物都是她在华盛顿公寓的家里上网买的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“I find that, by being able to go online and choose the things that I need to choose, and have them delivered to me right at my doorstep, I eliminate all the driving, all the crowds, all the noise of that, and I usually get a better selection,” Shaner explained."},{"lang":"zh","text":"沙纳解释说“我发现在网上就能够挑选到我需要的东西，这些东西通过快递直接送到我家门口，省去我了开车外出的麻烦，免去了在熙熙攘攘的人群中挤来挤去的烦恼。而且，通常我买到的东西也更好”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Analysts say US online shopping has hit records in November and December. Fifty-seven percent of Americans have made at least one online purchase. Traditional merchants worry that the growing e-commerce will shrink their share of the market. Cornell University Marketing Professor Ed McLaughlin says they have reason for concern."},{"lang":"zh","text":"分析员说，美国的网上购物在11月和12 月创造了新纪录。57%的美国人至少上网购物一次。传统的生意人担心不断发展的电子商务会使他们占有的市场份额收缩。康乃尔大学市场学教授埃德•麦克劳克林说他们的担心不无道理。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Anything that can move online will go. It is just a matter of time,” he stated. McLaughlin says traditional stores can keep their customers by offering The overall volume of B2B transactions is much higher than the volume of B2C transactions. The primary reason for this is that in a typical supply chain there will be many B2B transactions，such as selling components (零部件) and materials; however, there will be only one B2C transaction, that is, the sale of the finished product to the end customer. For example, an automobile manufacturer makes several B2B transactions such as buying tires, glass for windscreens, and rubber hoses for its vehicles. The final transaction, a finished vehicle sold to the consumer, is a single (B2C) transaction.goods like clothing, which customers may want to see and try on before purchasing — as well as items that are difficult to ship. He says some bricks and mortar stores are also pleasing customers with services that set up or repair computers and electronics.7 Traditional stores also offer a social experience that some shoppers enjoy."},{"lang":"zh","text":"麦克劳克林教授说：“任何交易，只要能够在网上进行，都会向着网络发展，只是个时间问题”。他说一些传统的实体店可以通过售卖某些商品留住顾客，比如服装，顾客在购买之前想看好并试穿，还比如一些商品长途装运有困难。他还说实体店也会通过一些特别的服务来吸引顾客，比如，电脑和电子产品的安装和维修。传统的实体店还可以为顾客提供一种社会生活体验，这是一些购物者喜欢的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Oftentimes, you need that last sense of ‘this is exactly what I want' before you part with your money,” he said. “And you can't always get that online. It's a rather cold process. Traditional stores can also deliver goods more quickly than online retailers,” Martin says. And smart merchants are using stores to guide customers to websites and using their websites to encourage customers to visit their stores."},{"lang":"zh","text":"他说：“很多时候，在钱花出去之前，你需要慎重考虑‘这真的就是我想要的”。马丁说：“你在网上购物时不是总是能做到这一点，网上购物少了一些人情味儿。还有，传统的实体店比网上的零售店送货快”。一些聪明的商家正在通过店铺引导顾客访问网站，也通过网站吸引顾客光顾自己的店铺。"},{"lang":"en","text":"While e-commerce worries some merchants, it's a huge boost for delivery services like FedEx and UPS. UPS Manager Dana Kline says e-commerce means her company is even busier than usual this time of year. “We are expecting 28 million pieces on their peak day, which is December．which is up about a million from last year,” she noted. UPS is so busy that it's hiring 55,000 temporary workers during the holiday season to deliver gifts. Those packages are headed for homes, including Lynne Shaner's purchase."},{"lang":"zh","text":"电子商务让一些商人忧心忡忡，却为物流服务带来了巨大的发展，比如FedEx快递和UPS快递。UPS快递公司的达纳·克莱恩经理说，电子商务对她的公司来说意味着一年中的这段时间比平常忙得多。她提到，“12月20日是高峰日，我们要处理两千八百万快递，这比去年增加了大约一百万件”。节日期间，UPS 非常忙碌，雇用了55，000 名临时工来派送网购礼物。这些包裹被送往千家万户，林恩的网购也在其中。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":475},{"id":"r-理工英语3-6-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"Poker Shark","subtitle":"扑克老手","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A computer program, “Cepheus”, has solved the game of poker. The Computer Poker Research Group (CPRG) created Cepheus. It claims Cepheus can not only play poker, but also beat human opponents."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一个名为“Cepheus”（仙王座）得计算机程序已经解决了扑克游戏的问题。计算机扑克研究小组（简称CPRG）创建了Cepheus程序。它声称，Cepheus不仅可以打扑克牌，还可以打败人类对手。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Games, such as poker and chess, have been used as test beds. New concepts in artificial intelligence are being developed. Past successes in this field include IBM's Deep Blue. It defeated world champion Garry Kasparov in chess."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不同的游戏，比如说扑克和国际象棋，已经被用作试验品。人工智能方面的新概念在不断发展。过去在这一领域的成功例子包括IBM（美国国际商用机器公司）的“深蓝”超级电脑。它打败了国际象棋世界冠军加里·卡斯帕罗夫。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Poker brings special challenges to artificial intelligence researchers. The players — human or computer — don't know about the past events. They can't see the cards in the hands of their opponents."},{"lang":"zh","text":"扑克给人工智能的研究者带来特殊挑战。玩家—人类或电脑---对过去的比赛项目不太了解。他们看不见对手手中的牌。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The CPRG determined that any game could be solved. Over the course of a lifetime, it could be played with 95 percent confidence. To test Cepheus with poker, the computer was trained for two months with more than 4,000 CPUs in use. Each CPU considered more than 6 billion hands of poker. That amounted to more poker than has been played by the entire human race. From each hand, Cepheus was able to improve its play. It can refine its choices to get closer to finding the best possible solution."},{"lang":"zh","text":"CPRG确定任何游戏问题都能被解决。在游戏有效期内，你可以带着95%的信心进行游戏。为了用扑克来测试Cepheus，计算机接受了两个月的培训，使用4000多个CPU（中央处理器）。每个CPU要考虑超过60亿手的扑克。那比全人类玩的扑克还要多。从每一手牌中，Cepheus能够提高它的牌艺。它能调整自身选项以尽可能找到最佳解决方案。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In developing Cepheus, the CPRG's goal was not to beat all human players and win the World Series of Poker. This technology is just one way to make a computer actually “think”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在发展Cepheus的过程中，CPRG的目标不是要打败所有的人类玩家并赢得世界扑克大赛冠军。这项技术只是让计算机真正“思考”的一种方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The next step for Cepheus will likely involve more hands of poker. More players are added. That will add more computation problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"Cepheus的下一步将可能涉及更多的扑克牌。更多的玩家会被增加。那样将增加更多的计算问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Cepheus thus far has proved its prowess with cards. But what it does next will be limited by today's computational capabilities. Computational power within the CPU/GPU, storage and RAM has continued to evolve. It allows for more complex supercomputing, software programming and problem solving. This allows the computer to learn. In the case of an unbeatable poker program, the computer would have to learn every possible move in every possible given situation.Then it would draw on its database to know the possible best move to make to win."},{"lang":"zh","text":"到目前为止，Cepheus已证明其纸牌实力。但下一步它要怎么做，将受到今天的计算能力限制。CPU（中央处理器）/GPU（图形处理器）内部的计算能力、存储器和RAM(随机存储器)不断进化。它允许更复杂的超级计算、软件编程和问题解决。这让电脑学习。在这个不可匹敌的扑克程序里，计算机必须学会在所有既定情境中的各种可能步骤。然后，它会利用数据库获取赢得游戏的最佳可行策略。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":329},{"id":"r-理工英语3-6-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Story-Mode Minecraft","subtitle":"我的世界：剧情版","paragraphs":[{"lang":"zh","text":"A brand new Minecraft game will be story-driven.（新版本的《我的世界》是有故事情节的。）"},{"lang":"en","text":"The new series of Minecraft: Story Mode will be set in the world of Minecraft, but it will feature an original story that combines new characters with familiar themes. It is driven by player choice. It will be a separate standalone product."},{"lang":"zh","text":"新的《我的世界：剧情版》仍然设定在《我的世界》的原有世界里，但故事是全新的，结合了新角色和熟悉的主题。故事按玩家的选择发展。这是一款独立的单机游戏产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The decision to make the new game community-driven is potentially brilliant. It's interesting that feedback from the community is going to be brought into Minecraft: Story Mode. In a way, it echoes what Minecraft is. It is a user-generated world."},{"lang":"zh","text":"让新游戏成为社区驱动模式很可能是个绝佳的主意。有趣的是社区的反馈将会被带进《我的世界：剧情版》。这在某种程度上反映出《我的世界》的实质，它就是一个用户创建的世界。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's likely that there already have been gamers on Minecraft fan blogs. They have come up with theories as to how the universe was created. There could be lots of contradictory things there. But from a marketing standpoint, it makes all the sense in the world for the community of “you guys are going to write this”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"《我的世界》的粉丝博客中很可能已经有一些玩家提出了一些诸如如何创造宇宙的理论。这些理论中可能有很多矛盾的地方。但从市场的角度出发，这对于相信“你们即将书写这里的历史”的群体来说，一切都很有意义。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Minecraft first came out in 2009 and is probably due for an evolution of some sort. Story Mode seems like a natural next step. A dedicated fan base has very high expectations. It will be satisfied with the story it is developing."},{"lang":"zh","text":"《我的世界》第一版是2009年发布的，现在也许是到了该升级的时候了。《剧情版》似乎是顺其自然的一步，骨灰级粉丝团对此抱有极高期望，他们会对由自己推动发展的故事感到十分满意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There will be challenges, however. Minecraft does not follow what the game industry is used to working with. It will be a completely different development scenario. It is a world with no story and starting from the beginning. As long as the Minecraft story is popular and successful, that might be OK."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但是，挑战仍然存在。《我的世界》并没有遵循游戏产业一贯的规律。它将面对完全不同的发展情景。这是个从零开始没有故事的世界。只要《我的世界》的故事受到大家欢迎取得成功，就没问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Driverless Cars Will Soon Hit Our Streets"},{"lang":"zh","text":"无人驾驶汽车将很快风靡街头"},{"lang":"en","text":"You jump into a car, tell it where you want to go, then sit back and let a computer take control. It seems like a dream in the future. It isn't."},{"lang":"zh","text":"跳进汽车，告诉它你的目的地，然后，你就可以往后一坐，让计算机操控车辆。这听起来像一场未来的梦。然而，这并非梦。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In many ways such driverless cars are already with us. There is partial automation in many cars，such as intelligent braking, lane departure warning and automatic parking. The systems are there so that cars can pretty much drive themselves. No one noticed the introduction of cruise control. We've got collision avoidance, and we'll soon have automatic lane change."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在许多方面，这种无人驾驶的汽车已经存在。许多车已经有了部分自动功能，比如智能刹车系统、车道偏离警报系统、自动泊车系统。安装了这些系统，车辆完全可以自行驾驶。安装的定速巡航常被人们忽视不用。我们已经有了防撞系统，很快，我们还将会有自动换道控制系统。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Improving this technology should make the roads safer. Machines are much better at following rules than humans. Road signs ad vise drivers to slow down to avoid creating jams. They are often ignored by drivers. But it won't happen to a computer. Driverless cars could also choose the best route to avoid traffic jams."},{"lang":"zh","text":"改善这种技术能够让道路更安全。机器比人类更擅长遵守规则。路标建议司机减速以避免导致堵塞，但常常被司机视而不见。但对于计算机来说这是不可能发生的。无人驾驶汽车还可以选择最佳路线以避免交通堵塞。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fewer jams will mean less stop-start driving. Maintaining smooth and constant speeds will improve fuel efficiency. Computers could also be programmed to take the greenest route, rather than the fastest one. Under computer control, cars could also travel much closer together."},{"lang":"zh","text":"更少的堵塞意味着驾车时更少的启停。保持匀速行驶可以提高燃油效能。电脑可以设定程序，选择最绿色环保、而不是最快捷的路线。通过计算机控制，车间距可以更短。"},{"lang":"en","text":"They can effectively “slipstream” one another and use less fuel to move themselves forward. They can even form multi-car “trains” going at high speeds. However, with driverless cars on the roads, there will be potential trust issues between people and machines. We could therefore see guard rails back on the sides of roads. This would be a backward step."},{"lang":"zh","text":"它们可以有效地在前面车辆形成的滑流里行驶，这样可以使用更少的燃料驱动车辆自身前进。他们甚至可以像火车一样，多车连在一起，高速行驶。然而，在道路上使用无人驾驶汽车，人和机器的信任问题需要解决。因此，可能在路的两边需要安装护栏，这无疑是一种倒退。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":486},{"id":"r-理工英语3-7-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Driverless Cars Will Soon Hit Our Streets","subtitle":"无人驾驶汽车将很快风靡街头","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"You jump into a car, tell it where you want to go, then sit back and let a computer take control. It seems like a dream in the future. It isn't."},{"lang":"zh","text":"跳进汽车，告诉它你的目的地，然后，你就可以往后一坐，让计算机操控车辆。这听起来像一场未来的梦。然而，这并非梦。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In many ways such driverless cars are already with us. There is partial automation in many cars，such as intelligent braking, lane departure warning and automatic parking. The systems are there so that cars can pretty much drive themselves. No one noticed the introduction of cruise control. We've got collision avoidance, and we'll soon have automatic lane change."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在许多方面，这种无人驾驶的汽车已经存在。许多车已经有了部分自动功能，比如智能刹车系统、车道偏离警报系统、自动泊车系统。安装了这些系统，车辆完全可以自行驾驶。安装的定速巡航常被人们忽视不用。我们已经有了防撞系统，很快，我们还将会有自动换道控制系统。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Improving this technology should make the roads safer. Machines are much better at following rules than humans. Road signs ad vise drivers to slow down to avoid creating jams. They are often ignored by drivers. But it won't happen to a computer. Driverless cars could also choose the best route to avoid traffic jams."},{"lang":"zh","text":"改善这种技术能够让道路更安全。机器比人类更擅长遵守规则。路标建议司机减速以避免导致堵塞，但常常被司机视而不见。但对于计算机来说这是不可能发生的。无人驾驶汽车还可以选择最佳路线以避免交通堵塞。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fewer jams will mean less stop-start driving. Maintaining smooth and constant speeds will improve fuel efficiency. Computers could also be programmed to take the greenest route, rather than the fastest one. Under computer control, cars could also travel much closer together."},{"lang":"zh","text":"更少的堵塞意味着驾车时更少的启停。保持匀速行驶可以提高燃油效能。电脑可以设定程序，选择最绿色环保、而不是最快捷的路线。通过计算机控制，车间距可以更短。"},{"lang":"en","text":"They can effectively “slipstream” one another and use less fuel to move themselves forward. They can even form multi-car “trains” going at high speeds. However, with driverless cars on the roads, there will be potential trust issues between people and machines. We could therefore see guard rails back on the sides of roads. This would be a backward step."},{"lang":"zh","text":"它们可以有效地在前面车辆形成的滑流里行驶，这样可以使用更少的燃料驱动车辆自身前进。他们甚至可以像火车一样，多车连在一起，高速行驶。然而，在道路上使用无人驾驶汽车，人和机器的信任问题需要解决。因此，可能在路的两边需要安装护栏，这无疑是一种倒退。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":245},{"id":"r-理工英语3-7-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Google's Fully Functional Driverless Car Is Adorable","subtitle":"受人青睐的谷歌全功能无人驾驶汽车","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Google unveiled its latest self-driving vehicle on Monday. It looks like a cartoon koala wearing a fez."},{"lang":"zh","text":"周一，谷歌推出了其最新款的自动驾驶汽车。车外形看起来像一只戴着土耳其毡帽的卡通考拉。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This self-driving car is fully functional. It even has real headlights. The round, white and gray car is designed without a gas pedal or wheel. However, because of California state law, a real person needs to be in the car and ready to take over in an emergency. The goal is to finally remove any controls inside the car. If so, passengers can take a nap or knit while the car does all the work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这辆自动驾驶汽车是全功能的，甚至拥有真正的车前灯。圆形车身，白灰相间，没有油门踏板系统和方向盘。然而，因为根据加利福尼亚州法律规定，汽车里需要有真人来应对紧急情况。目标是最终移除车子内部的任何控制装置，这样的话，乘客可以让车辆自行驾驶而自己可以打个瞌睡或织毛衣。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Google's self-driving car team will continue to test the vehicle on a private track in California. There it works its way around traffic lights. Google has said it's interested in launching a pilot program for the cars in the coming years."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谷歌的自动驾驶汽车团队将继续在加利福尼亚的一条私家道路上进行汽车测试。在那里，将进行车辆识别交通信号灯测试。谷歌表示有兴趣在未来几年推出一个汽车试点项目。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When the tech company first started experimenting with self-driving technology, it modified existing cars, like a Toyota. It added multiple cameras and sensors and an onboard computer. Now Google has moved on to making its own car. The car's dome-like shape is for giving sensors the widest field of view."},{"lang":"zh","text":"科技公司首次开始尝试自主驾驶技术时，是对现有车辆（如丰田车）进行改装，车上增加多个摄像头、传感器和一部车载电脑。如今，谷歌已经转向研制自己的汽车。汽车的圆顶形状是为了给传感器最广泛的视角。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A car could help put people's minds at ease about the technology. Before self-driving cars can start taking us to work, companies need to figure out issues like hitting a deer and improve basic driving functions. Companies also need to work with governments on legislation to allow driverless cars on all roads."},{"lang":"zh","text":"汽车能让人对科技放下心来。在无人驾驶汽车开始可以送人们去上班之前，公司需要解决诸如开车时候撞到鹿的问题，并改进基本的驾驶功能。公司也需要与政府磋商，立法允许无人驾驶汽车在所有道路上行驶。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Google is just one of many companies developing driverless car technology. Universities and major auto manufacturers such as BMW are working on similar vehicles. Google hopes to have its own car on the road by the end of the decade."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谷歌只是研发无人驾驶汽车的众多公司里的一个。许多大学还有宝马之类大的汽车制造商都在研发类似的交通工具。谷歌希望在这个十年后期能够有自己的汽车行驶在路上。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":281},{"id":"r-理工英语3-8-1","book":"理工英语3","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Fabric Charger","subtitle":"织物充电","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Imagine having jeans that charge your phone just by putting it in your pocket. That's what this material does. It was developed for the British Army. The fabric is made of yarn. The yarn can conduct electricity from a battery pack to anywhere in your clothing. It can charge your gadgets on contact."},{"lang":"zh","text":"试想一下这个场景：手机放到牛仔裤的口袋里就能充电。这种织物就可以做到。该材料是为英国军队研制的，它由特殊纱线编织而成。电池组通过纱线将电流传到衣服上面。这样就可以给接触衣服的手机充电了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The fabric has been developed by Intelligent Textiles. It can carry either power or data through a soldier's clothes, helmet, or backpack. It can charge gear that otherwise needs separate power sources. The materials have been field tested. But they still need to be weather-proofed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"Intelligent Textiles公司改进了这种织物，使其能将电流或数据传输到士兵的服装、头盔或背包上，还可以给其它需单独供电的装备充电。这些材料已进行了现场实验，但还需要进行耐风雨测试。"},{"lang":"en","text":"And that's all great, but could this ever make it into your home, and charge your phone or laptop someday? Right now, charging a battery still involves wires, chargers, and sockets. Inductive charging is developing. But you cannot just put your phone down on any surface and start powering up."},{"lang":"zh","text":"取得这样的成绩已经不错了。但是，将来能不能应用到我们家里面，给手机、笔记本充电？目前，给电池充电还需要充电线、充电器和插座。感应式充电仍在研制当中。但还不能做到把手机放在任何材料上就能充电。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But what if your pants or jacket or bag could charge your phone, or laptop or anything else? And what if that could be combined with some kind of inductive charging? You'd be able to almost totally cut the cord with your gadgets. Yes, you'd need to charge up whatever power source you're using now and then, but keep a pair of khakis plugged in while they hang in the closet. It would be a lot different from having to remember to plug in your phone."},{"lang":"zh","text":"假设你的裤子、夹克或包包能够给手机、笔记本或其它东西充电怎么办？假设能跟感应式充电结合起来会怎么样？那样的话，你就可以摆脱对传统充电器的依赖。是的，你可能需要给时常用到的电源充电。但只要给衣柜里的卡其裤连接上电源就可以了。这与过去要记得给手机充电大不一样了。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":235},{"id":"r-理工英语3-8-2","book":"理工英语3","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"Pedestrian Power on Tiles","subtitle":"行人发电地砖","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"This summer at the largest urban mall in London, visitors may notice something different at their feet. Twenty bright green rubber tiles will decorate one of the outdoor walkways at the mall. Next to it lies the new Olympic stadium in east London."},{"lang":"zh","text":"今年夏天，逛伦敦最大的城市购物商场的游客们可能会发现脚下跟以往有些不一样。其中一条户外人行道将会用20块翠绿色橡皮地砖来装饰。商场旁边坐落着伦敦东部的新奥林匹克体育馆。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The squares aren't just ornamental. They are designed to collect the energy created by pedestrians. It is estimated that 40 million pedestrians will use that walkway in a year. It will generate several hundred kilowatt-hours of electricity from the footsteps. That's enough to power half the mall's outdoor lighting."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这些地砖不仅仅具有装饰功能，还能用来收集行人产生的能量。预计一年有4000万行人走过那条人行道。行人的脚步可以产生几百千瓦时的电量。足以给商场户外一半的灯光设备供电。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The tiles were developed and produced in 2009 by a 26-year-old Londoner. The 17.7-by-23.6-inch tiles are designed to be used wherever pedestrians gather en masse: transportation hubs such as train, subway, and bus stations, airports, schools, malls. The power is generated from millions of footfalls. It can be used to power a range of lightings, signs, digital ads, etc."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2009年，26岁的伦敦人研制和生产出了这种地砖。17.7*23.6英寸的地砖可以应用到任何一个行人聚集的交通枢纽，如火车站、地铁站、汽车站、机场、学校和商场。数百万计脚步产生的能量可以用来给照明灯、指示牌、电子广告等供电。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Nearly 30 such projects have been installed in Europe. For two years now, four of its tiles have lined a hallway at a school near London. They collect energy from footfalls of its 1,100 students to keep the corridor lit. Music festival attendees' footfalls have also been controlled to charge cell phones and power lights."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在欧洲，这样的工程安装了近30个。目前，伦敦附近一所学校的走廊安装4块这样的地砖已经两年了。它们从1100名学生的脚步中收集能量，用来为走廊照明。音乐会上，人们的脚步产生的能量也被收集起来，用于给手机和照明灯供电。"}],"source":"理工英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":205},{"id":"r-理工英语4-1-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Time on Its Side: Apple Watch Said to Be Raising Bar","subtitle":"苹果手表：时间为之倾倒","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Apple Inc's “next big thing” is coming — finally."},{"lang":"zh","text":"苹果公司的下一个大事件，终于，到来了！"},{"lang":"en","text":"Apple Watch, a wearable device, is set to challenge the players in the Chinese market, much like what iPhone has done in the smartphone market."},{"lang":"zh","text":"正如苹果手机在智能手机市场上的表现一样，苹果手表这种可穿戴设备也旨在挑战中国市场上的竞争者。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Though local companies move earlier in the wearable devices market, the U.S. tech giant's watch is set to dominate the market after its launch next year, analysts said. “There will be a great change in the coming months,” said Daniel Matte, an analyst. “Smart wearable bands should not imitate but instead insist on their own unique design.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"分析师指出，尽管本地企业在可穿戴设备领域行动更早，但是，这个美国技术巨头的手表旨在明年推出并占领市场。“下个月将会有巨大变化发生，”分析师丹尼尔·梅特指出，“智能手环不应模仿，而应坚持自己独特的设计。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Chinese companies have released a number of wearable devices over the past few months. A week before the Apple Watch launch, Bai du Inc, the biggest online search provider in China, announced its first wearable device — Baidu Eye smart glasses. Lenovo Group Ltd, the world's largest personal computer maker, also launched its own smart glasses that can take photos. Xiaomi Corp, a Beijing-based smartphone brand, also introduced a 79 yuan ($13) bracelet which can track basic movements."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在过去的几个月里，中国企业推出了不少可穿戴设备。就在苹果手表发布前一周，百度公司，中国最大的网络搜索供应商，发布了其第一个可穿戴设备——百度智能眼镜。联想集团，全球最大的个人电脑制造商，也发布了可以拍照的智能眼镜。小米公司，一个北京的智能手机品牌的生产商，也推出了一款79元（13美元）的可追踪基本运动轨迹的手环。"},{"lang":"en","text":"With a sale price of about $350, the Apple Watch is expected to hit the market in early 2015 with more than a dozen accessory designs. After the smart watch release, Apple will dominate the wearable gadget market in 2015, threatening other players'positions, according to a report published by Forrester Research Inc."},{"lang":"zh","text":"将在2015年年初面世的苹果手表有一系列附件的设计，预计售价约350美元。弗雷斯特研究公司发布的一份报告称，苹果智能手表面世后，将占领可穿戴产品市场并给其他竞争者带来威胁"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":216},{"id":"r-理工英语4-1-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Google Glass? Baidu Eye!","subtitle":"谷歌眼镜？百度眼！","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Baidu, China's leading search engine company, has unveiled its own eyewear called Baidu Eye. It is said to be a different product from Google Glass in terms of functionality."},{"lang":"zh","text":"百度，中国搜索引擎的领导者，发布了自己的头部穿戴设备——“百度眼”。据说，从功能上来讲，这是一款不同于谷歌眼镜的产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The company demonstrated a working prototype on September 3 at its annual Technology Innovation Conference in Beijing. It bears a similarity to Google Glass, but it has no screen. Instead, the device uses a camera to scan objects, and focuses on analyzing information around its user and beaming that to a smartphone."},{"lang":"zh","text":"9月3日，百度在北京举行了公司年度技术创新大会，并在会上演示了一种工作模型。这款产品与谷歌眼镜相似，但没有屏幕，而是用摄像头来扫描物体，专注于分析使用者周围的信息，并将信息传输到手机上。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Baidu says the device is designed to support image search. The company's CEO Robin Li believes in five years' time, people will get used to searching by image and audio rather than text. Li has given an example of how one can take advantage of Baidu Eye, “If you are in a shopping mall and come across a woman whose skirt looks really attractive, you take a photo of her skirt using Baidu Eye, and you'll get to know where to buy one for yourself.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"百度表示，这款产品被设计来支持图片搜索。公司总裁李彦宏认为，五年后，人们将习惯于用图片和音频而不是文字来进行搜索。李彦宏还举例说明人们可以怎样使用“百度眼”：“如果你在购物中心偶遇一位女士穿着一件漂亮的裙子，你可以用“百度眼”拍下照片，然后就可以知道在哪儿为自己买一件了。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to Kaiser Kuo , Baidu's director of international communications, Baidu Eye can also recognize voice and gesture, “You can use voice commands, or gesture commands — like expanding to zoom, or circling an object in your field of view with your finger.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"据百度国际媒体公关总监郭怡广说，“百度眼”还可以识别声音和手势，“你可以发出语音或手势指令，就像在视线范围内用手指放大或圈住物体”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Baidu is yet to announce a release date or marketing plans for Baidu Eye."},{"lang":"zh","text":"百度还没有发布“百度眼”的上市时间或营销计划。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":220},{"id":"r-理工英语4-2-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Trust Me, I'm a Robot","subtitle":"我是机器人，值得你信任","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Surgery in the future will look very different. Where now there may be up to a dozen medical professionals present in the operating theater, soon there may be only two or three, with robots having taken over many of the jobs done by nurses and support staff. Even the surgeon may be elsewhere."},{"lang":"zh","text":"未来的外科手术将会和现在有很大的不同。现在的手术室里面也许会有十多个医护人员，而将来或许就只有两三个了。护士和支持人员现在所做的大量工作将由机器人接管。医生甚至都会不在手术室里。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Telerobotics enables a doctor to do surgery at a distance. “It's easy to imagine a future where, if I need a medical specialist from afar, a robot could remotely become his or her eyes, hands, and ears,” says Joanne Pransky, an expert on robot psychiatry."},{"lang":"zh","text":"医生能够使用遥控机器人进行远程手术。机器人精神病学专家乔安妮·普兰斯基说：“不难想象，在未来，如果我需要一位身处远方的医学专家，机器人可以远程成为这位专家的眼睛、双手和耳朵。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The first medical robots are already being used in hospitals now — the da Vinci Surgical System was approved for use by the U.S. government in 2000, and more will follow."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第一个医疗机器人已经在医院投入使用——达·芬奇外科手术系统已在2000年由美国政府批准使用，后期将会有更多的机器人投入使用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“These robots work on the ‘master slave' concept, with the surgeon as the master,” says Dr. Ara Darzi. “The da Vinci system has three arms, and you can add a fourth, with 3D stereo imagery available during surgery. It also has a motion scaling concept, which can be scaled down to five- to-one, so you can be much more precise than a human hand could. The surgeon feels very similar sensations if he or she was working with their hands.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"“这些机器人在‘主从’概念下进行工作，外科医生就是主人，”阿拉·达兹医生说，“达·芬奇系统有三只手臂，你可以再增加第四只。手术中有三维立体图像。该系统还有动作尺度概念，可以从五级到一级，这样就比人手操作更加精确。医生操作起来会和他们用双手进行手术的感觉相似。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The robots act as an extension of a practitioner's skills, which allows them to perform better by helping improve control and precision. Already robots are being used to position endoscopes, and even perform gallbladder surgery. The hope is that soon they will be able to perform major operations such as heart surgery, perhaps using nanotech tools — microscopic robots — that would make the need to crack open a patient's chest a thing of the past."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为医师技能的延伸，机器人可以通过提高控制力和精确度让手术实施得更好。机器人已经被用于放置内窥镜，甚至进行胆囊手术。在不久的将来，机器人将有望能够实施心脏手术这样的大手术，或许能够通过纳米技术工具——显微机器人，让打开病人胸腔的需要成为历史。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Robots will also help surgeons cope with the exhaustion of long procedures, and the da Vinci system's mechanics have been programmed to compensate for the hand tremors tired surgeons sometimes suffer from."},{"lang":"zh","text":"机器人还可以帮助外科医生应对长时间进行手术产生的疲乏。科学家对达·芬奇系统进行了设计，以弥补外科医生在疲惫时出现的手颤问题。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":315},{"id":"r-理工英语4-2-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Robot Revolution? Scientists Teach Robots to Learn","subtitle":"机器人革命？科学家教机器人学习","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Would a robot serving you coffee in bed make waking up easier on weekday mornings? Could a household robot help an elderly relative who is living alone? How would you like to climb into a robotic car and eat breakfast with the kids while you're all driven to school and work?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果在清晨有一个机器人将咖啡送到你床边，起床上班是不是要容易一点？家用机器人是否能照顾独居老人？钻进一辆机器人轿车，和孩子们一起边享用早餐边开车去上学和上班，你感觉如何？"},{"lang":"en","text":"These scenarios may sound like science fiction, but experts say they're a lot closer to becoming reality than you probably think."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这些场景听起来像是科幻小说。不过，据专家们说，这些会比你想象的更快成为现实。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Brown University roboticist Chad Jenkins expects a near-term robot revolution that will echo the computing revolution of recent decades. And he says it will be driven by enabling robots to learn more like humans do — by watching others demonstrate behaviors and by asking questions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"布朗大学的机器人学家查德·詹金斯预计，随着近几十年电脑革命的发生，一场机器人革命即将到来。这场革命的驱动理念将是让机器人能够通过观察其他人的示范行为和提问，像人类一样学习。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“The robots you're seeing now mostly are analogous to the mainframe computers of the 1970s.”Jenkins said. “But you're starting to see things develop. The vacuum cleaners, the drones, those are the initial steps.” he said, referring to iRobot's Roomba vacuum cleaner, which has autonomously cleaned millions of homes since its 2002 debut."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“现在我们所看到的机器人大部分还类似于20世纪70年代的大型主机”，詹金斯说道，“但是，你会发现，改变正在发生。扫地机器人、无人机，这些都是变革的初步尝试。”他指出，iRobot公司生产的扫地机器人自2002年首次推出后，已经清洁了上百万的住家。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“And these platforms are going to get cheaper while becoming more capable and more compact.” he added."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“而且，在未来这些平台会更加便宜，同时这些平台还会有更强大的功能以及更紧凑的设计。”他补充说。"},{"lang":"en","text":"And entrepreneurs like Dmitry Grishin, founder of a major Russian investment firm dedicated to personal robotics, have taken notice. He says the industry could be worth $18 billion by 2015."},{"lang":"zh","text":"德米特里·格里申是俄罗斯的一家致力于个人机器人技术的大型投资公司的创始人，像他这样的企业家已经注意到这点。他认为这个产业到2015年的时候将会价值180亿美元。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But to really transform, roboticists say, robots will have to evolve from machines that can perform only the tasks they're programmed to do into automatons that can truly learn. That's because it's impossible to pre-program a robot for everything it will encounter in the ever-changing real world."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但是，机器人学家认为，要做到真正的改变，机器人必须要从只能完成预设任务的机器转变成为能够真正学习的自动机器。因为我们不可能对机器人在这不断变化的真实世界里会遇到的所有事情都预先进行编程。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“If you look at where robots are successful right now, it's primarily in applications where the environment is very controlled, like an assembly line where everything is the same, or in the hands of experts with PhDs, where we see them on Mars.” said Chernova."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“如果你留意一下那些成功使用了机器人的地方，就会发现，它们主要都是在环境完全受控的情况下的应用，例如，在所有东西都一样的设备流水线上，或者在我们看到的火星上的博士专家们的手里。”切洛娃说。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“To really get them to handle the complexities of our real world,” she said, “they are going to have to be customized onsite. It's not going to happen tomorrow, but it's very close.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"她说：“要想让机器人能真正应对我们这个复杂的真实世界，它们就得就地定制。这当然不是明天就能做到的事情，但是我们也非常接近了。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Such a leap could help bring robots into the mainstream."},{"lang":"zh","text":"而这一飞跃将会使机器人成为主流。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":351},{"id":"r-理工英语4-3-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"The Real-Life Barbie Doll","subtitle":"现实中的芭比娃娃","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"With a teeny waist, exaggerated breasts, icy-blue eyes, 21-year-old Valeria says she is the real natural deal. A real-life Barbie, that is."},{"lang":"zh","text":"腰部纤细，胸部夸张，眼睛冰蓝，21岁的维拉利亚说，她是真实自然的芭比。也就是说，她是生活中真实的芭比娃娃。"},{"lang":"en","text":"That's what she claims anyway, but many people doubt her claims. Whether she underwent plastic surgery or uses Photoshop remains unclear. On her blog, the model notes that she is the most famous woman on the Russian Internet because of her doll-like appeal. Hundreds of photos on her Facebook page show a wide-eyed, nearly fake-looking Valeria posing in a variety of outfits."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不管怎样，那是她自己的说法，很多人对此说法表示怀疑。她是做了整形手术还是使用了PS软件，我们不得而知。在她的博客上，这位模特说，因为她具有芭比娃娃一样的魅力，所以她是俄罗斯互联网上最出名的人物。在维拉利亚的脸谱网网页上有上千幅图片，图片上的她眼睛大大的，脸像假的一样，展示着各种服装。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The model did not return requests for comment. If Photoshop is not a factor in getting Valeria's look, she likely underwent a barrage of plastic surgery. The president of the American Society of Plastic Surgeons（ASPS）said, plastic surgery should never be used to transform oneself into a favorite celebrity or, in this case, a play toy. He also warns patients to keep in mind that plastic surgery is real surgery with real risks, just as with any operation, so the decision should not be taken lightly."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这位模特没有对评论做出回应。如果不是PS软件帮助她获得现在的容貌的话，那她可能做了一系列的整形手术。美国整形医师协会主席说，整形手术绝不应该用于把一个人整成自己喜欢的名人的样子，或者像这个案例，整成玩具的样子。他还告诫人们要牢记，整形手术也是手术，也有着实实在在的风险，因此做决定时要慎重。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Whether Valeria is real or fake, photoshopped or a product of plastic surgery, the mystery of her existence is not the issue. The problem is that her unnatural image exemplifies the issue of objectification of women in today's society."},{"lang":"zh","text":"不管维拉利亚的芭比形象是真是假，是软件处理的还是整形手术的产物，她是否存在已经不是争议的重点。重点是她那不自然的形象是当今社会把女性物化的例证。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Barbie has always been controversial and really changed the discussion on how girls play. When Barbie came into existence, play suddenly became about dressing up and looking right and it eventually played a role in how women wanted to look in real life."},{"lang":"zh","text":"芭比娃娃形象本身一直存有争议，它也确实改变了女孩们的妆扮方式。当芭比形象渐入人心时，化妆突然等同于妆扮得体和赏心悦目，这对女性在现实生活中的妆扮产生了很大的影响。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Valeria is an extreme example of societal expectations of perfect beauty. If society expects women to look like that, it is harder for almost any woman to totally resist it."},{"lang":"zh","text":"维拉利亚是社会对极致美丽期望的终极代表。如果社会期望女人们那样妆扮，那么任何一个女人都很难坚持不去那样妆扮。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":289},{"id":"r-理工英语4-3-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Angelina Jolie: My Medical Choice","subtitle":"安吉利娜·朱莉：我的医疗选择","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"My mother fought breast cancer for almost a decade and died at 56 . My children never have the chance to know her and experience how loving and gracious she was. We often speak of “ Mommy's mommy ”, and they asked if the same could happen to me. I have always told them not to worry, but the truth is I carry a “faulty ”gene, BRCA 1 , which sharply increases my risk of developing breast cancer and ovarian cancer."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我母亲和乳腺癌战斗了近10年，56岁时去世。我的孩子们从未有机会感受她的慈爱和优雅。我们通常称她为“妈咪的妈咪”。孩子们经常问我，我是否会经历同样的事情，我总是告诉他们不用担心。但事实是，我携带了“有问题”的基因——BRCA1。它极大地增加了我患乳腺癌和卵巢癌的风险。"},{"lang":"en","text":"My doctors estimated that I had an 87 percent risk of breast cancer and a 50 percent risk of ovarian cancer. Once I knew that this was my reality, I decided to be proactive and to minimize the risk as much as I could."},{"lang":"zh","text":"医生估计我有87%的概率患乳腺癌，50%的概率患卵巢癌。一得知这是我要面对的现实，我便立刻决定主动出击，以最大限度地降低患癌的风险。"},{"lang":"en","text":"My own process began on Feb. 2 with a procedure known as a “ nipple delay ”, which rules out disease in the breast ducts behind the nipple and draws extra blood flow to the area. This causes some pain and a lot of bruises, but it increases the chance of saving the nipple."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第一步是2月2日的“乳头保留”手术，这个手术切除了乳头后方乳腺导管中的病变，并将更多的血液导入这个部位。这会导致疼痛和大量瘀伤，不过能增加留住乳头的概率。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Two weeks later I had the major surgery, where the breast tissue is removed and temporary fillers are put in place. The operation took eight hours."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2周后，我接受了主要的手术，切除了乳腺组织并填充了一些临时填充物。这个手术用了8个小时。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Nine weeks later, the final surgery is completed with the reconstruction of the breasts with an implant. On April 27 , I finished the three months of medical procedures that the mastectomies involved."},{"lang":"zh","text":"9周后，我接受了最后一次手术，用植入物重塑了乳房。4月27日，我结束了针对乳腺切除手术的三个月疗程。"},{"lang":"en","text":"I wanted to write this to tell other women that the decision to have a mastectomy was not easy. But it is one I am very happy that I made. My chances of developing breast cancer have dropped from 87 percent to under 5 percent. I can tell my children that they don't need to fear they will lose me to breast cancer."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我记录下这些，是想告诉其他女性，下决心做乳房切除手术很难。不过，我非常高兴我做了这样一个决定。我患上乳腺癌的概率从87%下降到5%以下。我可以告诉我的孩子，他们不必害怕乳腺癌会带走我了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The cost of testing for BRCA 1 and BRCA 2 , at more than $ 3 , 000 in the United States, remains an obstacle for many women. Life comes with many challenges. The ones that should not scare us are the ones we can take on and take control of."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在美国，检测BRCA1和BRCA2的费用要3 000多美元，这成为很多女性的障碍。虽然生活中充满挑战，但有些挑战吓不倒我们，因为我们能应对和掌握这些挑战。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":330},{"id":"r-理工英语4-4-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"3D Print Canal House","subtitle":"3D打印的“运河之家”","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"If you think 3D printing is only good for making flimsy paperweights, then you're pretty much right. However, a group of audacious Dutch architects have already begun 3D printing an entire canal house in Amsterdam. Is the first 3D printed house a gimmick? Definitely! Is it an experiment that pushes the possibilities for 3D printing technology and architecture? Maybe!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你认为3D打印只擅长打印轻薄的镇纸，那你是非常正确的。但是，一群大胆的荷兰建筑师已经在阿姆斯特丹开始打印一座完整的“运河之家”了。这第一座3D打印的小屋有趣吗？肯定的！这是一项推进3D技术和建筑学发展的实验吗？或许吧！"},{"lang":"en","text":"3D Print Canal House is the brainchild of DUS Architects. “KamerMaker”, Dutch for “room maker”, is their giant printer built inside a shipping container. Just a few weeks ago, KamerMaker began printing plastic furniture and walls at an empty canal-side lot in northern Amsterdam. Smaller versions of the unusual honeycomb walls have been tested on normal desktop printers, and everyone just needed to scale it up. Well, if only it were that easy."},{"lang":"zh","text":"用3D技术打印“运河之家”是DUS Architects工作室的构想。KamerMaker在荷兰语中表示“房屋建造者”的意思，是他们建造在集装箱中的巨大打印机的名字。就在几周前，KamerMaker在阿姆斯特丹北部的运河边的空地上开始打印塑料家具和墙壁。这种不同寻常的蜂窝墙的缩小版已经在普通台式打印机上被测试打印过，大家要做的是把它放大。哦，要是那么简单多好！"},{"lang":"en","text":"“The printer did not always manage to spread the plastic evenly, making some of the ribs of the honeycomb structure of the block uneven,” reported ARN (Australian Radio Network), to the surprise of no one who has used a 3D printer. But the architects remain optimistic. The first few printed blocks are meant to be test pieces as they improve the process."},{"lang":"zh","text":"澳大利亚广播网报道：“这台打印机不能一直均匀地喷出塑料，这使得蜂窝结构的某些骨架不那么平滑。”对于使用过3D打印机的人而言，这没有什么值得大惊小怪的。但是，建筑师们一直很乐观。在他们改进的过程中，首先被打印出的一些块状物只是测试品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It takes about a week to print a 3-meter high block right now. The project's leader hopes to eventually get that down to two hours and finish the first of 12 rooms in a year, and the entire house in less than 3 years."},{"lang":"zh","text":"目前，打印一个3米高的块状物大概需要一周。该项目负责人希望最终把时间减少到2小时，1年内完成12个房间中第1个房间的建造，整个房子的建造时间不超过3年。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ultimately, 3D Print Canal House is an architectural research project, one that is very much being conducted in the public eye: you can actually buy tickets to visit the construction site for 2.50 Euros."},{"lang":"zh","text":"总的来说，3D打印的“运河之家”是一项建筑研究项目，它基本上是在人们的视野中公开进行的——你可以花2.5欧元买票参观。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The top floors will become more ornate, for example, as newer techniques are incorporated. They'll explore the possibilities of 3D printing, like the honeycomb walls or an entire room recycled, redesigned, and built anew. Nobody's going to move into a 3D printed house soon, but, if anyone ever does, something might be learned from this experiment by the canal."},{"lang":"zh","text":"随着新技术的不断引入，上面几层会变得相对更华丽。他们将探索3D打印的各种可能性，比如蜂窝墙或者整个房屋的回收利用、重新设计和重新建造。没有人会在短期内搬入这个3D打印的房屋居住，但是，如果有人这样做的话，我们可以从这个运河旁的实验项目中学到一些东西。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":329},{"id":"r-理工英语4-4-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"A 3D, Talking Map for the Blind (and Everyone Else)","subtitle":"一幅给盲人（和所有人）的会说话的3D地图","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"These maps are made for talking and touching. And they're beautiful, too. Touch-responsive maps bring interactive way-finding to a new level, providing independence to the visually impaired."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这种地图可以说话和触摸，它们也很漂亮。触摸响应式地图把互动问路方式提升到一个新的层次，增强了盲人的独立性。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Center for Inclusive Design and Environmental Access (IDEA Center) tested a new kind of interactive way-finder: 3D maps that vocalize building information and directions when touched."},{"lang":"zh","text":"包容性设计和环境无障碍中心（IDEA中心）测试了一种新的互动式寻路器：3D地图。触摸时，这种地图可以说出建筑物的信息和方位。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The technology is designed with an important mission in mind: to help visually impaired visitors navigate public spaces like museums and college campuses."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这个技术产品的设计开发肩负着一项重要的使命：为视力受损的人在诸如博物馆、大学校园之类的公共场所行走提供帮助。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's really about giving this audience, this population, a way to understand their environment.We're providing a level of information that allows them to navigate their environment easily, without help, which gives them a sense of independence."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这种地图确实能给用户提供一种理解周围环境的方式。我们为他们提供的信息，足以让他们在毫无帮助的情况下自由探索周遭环境，给他们一种独立自主的感觉。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As guests explore the model with their hands, the map announces building names and directions for getting to destinations. A menu controlled by just three buttons lets users browse a verbal index of all points of interest."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当用户用双手探索使用样品的时候，地图会播报建筑物的名称和去往目的地的方向。仅由三个按钮控制的菜单就能让使用者通过有声索引浏览他们感兴趣的地方。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Sound effects embedded in the landscape serve as auditory landmarks for people who are visually impaired: a fountain gurgles when tapped, and a bell tower chimes."},{"lang":"zh","text":"音响效果嵌入地貌之中，给视力受损的人充当听觉路标。敲击地图时，喷泉汩汩作响，钟楼也会打钟报时。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The touch-responsive models solve the “last mile problem” for blind pedestrians, who can often navigate to a building or campus address using GPS, but then need help to get to the classroom building or doctor's office where they need to be."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这款触摸响应式寻路器会为有视觉障碍的行人解决“最后一英里”问题。他们经常使用GPS走到建筑物或者校园的某个地方，但要到达教室或者医生办公室这种具体的地方却需要帮助。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Though the technology has been designed for people with visual impairments, the multisensory models make way for a better experience for everyone."},{"lang":"zh","text":"虽然这项技术是为有视觉障碍的人士设计的，但多感官操作的3D寻路器可以为每个人带来更好的寻路体验。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":243},{"id":"r-理工英语4-5-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Turning Cigarette Butts into Batteries","subtitle":"将烟头变成电池","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"If you see a person carelessly throwing a cigarette to the ground,what are you likely to think? That depends. If you hate people throwing things on the ground, you might think,“That person should not litter. ” If you are a smoker, you might think, “ I would sure like a cigarette right now. ” Most likely, though, you are not thinking, “ You know, that unused cigarette butt could be used to make something, something amazing! ”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你看到一个人不经意地扔了一个烟头，你会怎么想呢？那可真是仁者见仁，智者见智。如果你讨厌随地乱扔东西，你可能会想：那个人不应该乱丢垃圾。但如果你是烟民，你可能会想：我现在真想来一根。不过，大多数情况下，你可能不会想：你要知道，这没用的烟头很有可能被用来制成某种非常神奇的东西。"},{"lang":"en","text":"That is, unless you are a creative scientist. If you are, you may see a possibility where others simply see trash. That is just what has happened in South Korea. The spirit of invention can hit at the strangest times and in the most unusual places. In South Korea, it happened near a trash can."},{"lang":"zh","text":"事实是这样的，除非你是一个有创造力的科学家。如果你是，你就可能从别人眼里的垃圾中看出可能性。这正是在韩国发生的情况。发明创造的灵光常常出现在最奇异的时刻以及最不寻常的地方。在韩国，它就出现在垃圾桶旁边。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Kim Gil-Pyo is with Seoul National University. Mr. Kim says he saw people throwing away cigarette butts. And that got him thinking. He began wondering if something useful could be made from them. The result? Mr.Kim and other researchers found a way to turn cigarette butts into the materials required for high-performance batteries. We often say, “ One person's trash is another person's treasure. ” And in this example, this is unquestionably true."},{"lang":"zh","text":"金吉彪就职于首尔国立大学。金先生表示，他看到人们扔烟头，这给了他灵感。他开始设想，如果一些有用的东西可以从烟头里获得的话，会是什么样的结果呢？金先生和其他研究人员发现了一种能将烟头转化成高性能电池所需材料的方法。我们常说：“一个人的垃圾是另一个人的财富。”在这个例子中，这无疑是正确的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Kim Gil-Pyo says he and his fellow researchers looked closely at used cigarette filters. The filter is the part of the cigarette that smokers put into their mouths. Mr. Kim explains that the filters can be made into another material: carbon. He says the filters are changed through a one-step burning process. After this, he says, they are turned into an energy storage material."},{"lang":"zh","text":"据金吉彪说，他和研究团队的成员们仔细观察了已抽过的香烟过滤嘴。过滤嘴是吸烟者放进嘴里的部分。金先生解释说，过滤嘴可变成另一种材料：碳。他说，过滤嘴只需通过燃烧这一个步骤就可发生改变，并被转换为储能材料。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Carbon has many qualities that seem to make it the perfect material. Carbon can easily carry an electrical current. It also stays stable, unlikely to change, for a long time. And carbon does not cost a lot. All these qualities make it the most popular material for making super-capacitors."},{"lang":"zh","text":"碳的许多优点似乎能使其成为最完美的材料。碳可以轻松地传导电流，同时也很稳定，在很长的一段时间内不会发生改变，而且成本极低。所有的这些优点使碳成为制造超级电容器最常用的材料。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Super-capacitors are good at storing energy. They have high-powered mass. They require only a short time for re-charging. And they have a long lifecycle. Super-capacitors are used in products such as laptop computers and cell phones. They are also used in industrial energy converters, like wind turbine machines. Combining carbon and super-capacitors seems like a perfect marriage."},{"lang":"zh","text":"超级电容器能极好地储存能量。它们有很高的功率密度，仅需极短的时间充电，有很长的使用寿命。超级电容器可用在笔记本电脑和手机这样的产品中，还可用在风力发电机这样的工业能源转换器中。碳和超级电容器的结合似乎非常完美。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Mr. Kim says that cigarette butts could affect the economy in a huge way. They could prove to be a low-cost source of carbon material. They are so cheap that smokers throw them on the ground, and you don't get much cheaper than that."},{"lang":"zh","text":"金先生表示，烟头可能会对经济产生极大的影响。它们有可能被证明是一种低成本的碳源物质。它们如此便宜，以至于被吸烟者扔到地上，而你再也找不到比这更便宜的东西了。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":426},{"id":"r-理工英语4-5-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"Growing Vegetables in Sea Water","subtitle":"海水种菜","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Climate change has caused a rise in sea levels. This has increased the amount of salt in fresh water used on coastal farms. As a result, farmers are increasingly unable to use fields close to the sea."},{"lang":"zh","text":"气候变化会导致海平面上升，这就导致沿海农场使用的淡水的含盐量增加，结果农户们越发难以利用沿海农田。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Scientists call this process “ salinization ” which means the mixing of salt and water. Salinization is reducing the world's irrigated lands by 1 to 2 percent every year."},{"lang":"zh","text":"科学家称这一过程为“盐碱化”，也就是盐和水的混合。盐碱化使得全世界可灌溉土地每年减少1%~2%。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But a farmer in the Netherlands is now using a mixture of sea and fresh water to grow healthy and tasty vegetables. Marc Van started with an experiment."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但荷兰的一个农民现在使用海水和淡水的混合物来种植健康美味的蔬菜。马克·范开始了这个试验。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“We put in a lot of plants in the fields and then we put them in fresh water and in sea water and all the varieties between them, and then we see which variety is surviving and which variety is dying. ”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"“我们把很多作物种在田里，然后把它们分别放到海水、淡水以及各种比例的淡水和海水的混合物当中，看哪种能存活下来，哪种会死掉。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Mr. Van worked on the project with scientists from the Free University of Amsterdam. He divided a farm into eight areas. Separate pipes pumped fresh and sea water, and a computer program created water with eight levels of salinity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"范先生和阿姆斯特丹自由大学的几位科学家一起进行这个项目的研究，他把农场分为 8个区域，用不同的管道来输送淡水和海水，并用电脑程序生成8 种不同浓度的盐水。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Computerized measuring devices called “ sensors ” controlled the water levels and the levels of salinity. Mr. Van says he was able to harvest vegetables from most of the eight test areas. He says the vegetables were smaller than those grown in fresh water. But he says they also have more sugar and salt, so they taste better."},{"lang":"zh","text":"名为“传感器”的电脑测量装置控制水位和盐度。范先生表示，8个实验区域大都能收获蔬菜，这样种植出的蔬菜比在淡水中种植出的蔬菜个头要小些。不过，他也说，因为这种蔬菜含有更多的糖分和盐分，所以口感更好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The farmer grew carrots, cabbage and onions. But he found that potatoes grew better than the other vegetables in the combination of sea and fresh water. Mr. Van says four kinds of these potatoes were recently sent to Pakistan, where thousands of hectares of land have been damaged by salinization. Farmers in Pakistan will test these potatoes to see if they can be grown in those fields."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这位农民种植胡萝卜、大白菜、洋葱。不过，他发现，在海水和淡水的混合物中，土豆比其他蔬菜长得更好。范先生说，其中的4种土豆最近被送到巴基斯坦，那里有数千公顷土地被盐碱化，巴基斯坦的农民将用这些土豆来做实验，看它们是否能在本国土地上生长。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":293},{"id":"r-理工英语4-6-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"Young Technology Expert Works to Stop Car Thefts","subtitle":"年轻的技术专家致力于阻止汽车失窃","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Cars were stolen in the capital. Kenya has east Africa's largest economy. Its capital city is growing quickly, but so is the city's crime rate. Thieves in the capital steal an average of 10 cars each day."},{"lang":"zh","text":"肯尼亚是东非最大的经济体，首都内罗毕发展很快，但是城市犯罪率增长得也快。平均每天有十辆汽车在首都失窃。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A young inventor. Kelvin Macharia has invented a tracking device that uses computers and wireless technology to help owners know where their cars are, and find them if they are stolen. Mr. Macharia is just 24 years old. He is the CEO of Sunrise Tracking."},{"lang":"zh","text":"凯文·玛卡里亚发明的汽车追踪设备能通过电脑和无线技术帮助车主定位他们的车辆，并在车辆被盗后将车辆找回。年仅 24 岁的玛卡里亚已是朝阳追踪公司（Sunrise Tracking）的总裁了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The smart anti-theft system. He began working on his invention in 2012 . Using $ 300 from his savings, he improved a system that was already being used to find stolen cars. His smart anti-theft system uses a computer or a mobile phone to tell owners where their cars are. Mr. Macharia says if a car is stolen, the owner can find it using his tracking device. The owner is able to send a command signal to the vehicle through a text message. It immediately stops the car from moving. Experts say this shows the power of security solutions that involve mobile technology."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2012 年他便开始致力于这项发明。他从积蓄中拿出300美元，用以改进一套用于追踪失窃车辆的系统。他的智能防盗系统使用电脑和手机告诉车主其车辆的位置。玛卡里亚说，如果汽车被盗，失主使用他的追踪设备就能找到车辆。车主可以通过短信向汽车发送命令，然后汽车就会立即熄火停车。专家说，这显示了移动技术在安全方案中所起的强大作用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The new product helps its client. Mr. Macharia used material available in Kenya to make his first tracker device. When he was satisfied with the design, he outsourced the making of the device to a factory in China. 5 He says his company is now worth more than $ 100 , 000 and has more than 100 companies as clients. Tony Wanga is one of those clients. He owns three minibus taxis. Car thieves in the capital have targeted these vehicles. Mr. Wanga bought trackers for each of his vehicles. The trackers cost $ 250 each. He says the trackers tell him where his vehicles are. He says when the tracker is placed in one of his vehicles, he can follow its travels as he sits in his office."},{"lang":"zh","text":"玛卡里亚使用现有的材料在肯尼亚制造出他的第一台追踪设备。他对自己的设计满意之后，就把这种设备的制造外包给一家中国工厂。他表示，现在其公司的市值已超过 100 万美元，同时拥有超过 100 家的公司客户。托尼·王就是其中的一位客户，他拥有三辆小型巴士出租车。在内罗毕，偷车贼常以这些机动车为目标，因此，王先生为每辆车都买了追踪设备，每个跟踪设备花费 250 美元。他说，追踪设备能显示汽车的位置。而且，在安装了追踪设备以后，他坐在办公室里便可掌握汽车的运行路线。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Other security products. Mr. Macharia continues to develop other security products. His other security products include car alarms and a camera hidden inside a pen. And he says he is building a wireless security camera that will be able to store video information for long periods of time. Mr. Macharia hopes his technological innovations give his clients the security and safety they want and need."},{"lang":"zh","text":"玛卡里亚还在继续研发其他的安保产品，包括汽车警报器以及隐藏在钢笔里的摄像头。他介绍说，他正在开发一款能够长时间地储存影像信息的无线安保摄像头。玛卡里亚希望他的技术创新能够为客户带去他们想要的保障和安全。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":367},{"id":"r-理工英语4-6-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Talking Cars: The Vehicle of the Future","subtitle":"“会说话”的汽车：未来的交通工具","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Something else could be coming soon to a vehicle near you: more technology, the kind that could help your car talk to others around it. Unlike some proposed cars of the future, it would not actually do the driving for you. But it could warn you about what other drivers are doing. The U.S. government may require this feature in the future, but it would add to the cost of the car."},{"lang":"zh","text":"很快，在你的周围，会有其他类型的车辆出现。会有更多的科技应用到汽车领域，让你的汽车能与周围的车说话。不同于某些未来概念车型，它不会实际为你驾驶汽车，而是会告诉你周围其他驾驶者在干什么。美国政府可能在不久的将来会要求汽车具备这个特征，但这会增加汽车的成本。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Vehicles of the future could be cars that talk to the driver and each other. The U.S. government wants them on the road soon, pushing for technology that would warn drivers of danger coming from any direction."},{"lang":"zh","text":"未来的新型汽车可以和驾驶员以及其他人交流。美国政府想让这种车尽快投入生产，用先进科技提醒驾驶员来自各个方向的危险。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's called vehicle-to-vehicle technology. Cars would send wireless messages to each other within about 300 yards, communicating information like speed, direction and GPS position ten times per second. When cars share this information, they can account for all the vehicles around them, which means they are able to identify possible crashes."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这是被称为“车车交互”的科技，即在 300 码的范围内，汽车之间可以互相发送无线信息，诸如速度、方向、GPS 定位等信息会每秒交互 10 次。当车辆间分享这些信息时，它们就会照顾到周围车辆，也就意味着，它们可以警觉到可能发生的事故。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The technology sees around corners, over hills and through other vehicles. For example, my car will tell me that there are five cars just ahead of me, and I can slow down beforehand while the vehicle ahead sends my car a message giving me enough time to react."},{"lang":"zh","text":"这种科技可以知晓被角落、丘陵以及其他车辆阻挡的车辆的运行状态。例如，我的车前有 5 辆车，前面的车辆会给我的车发来信息，使我获得足够的反应时间，我就能够提前减速。"},{"lang":"en","text":"33 , 000 Americans are killed and 2.3 million injured in car crashes every year. The Department of Transportation (DoT) predicts, talking cars could prevent up to 80 percent of crashes involving sober drivers."},{"lang":"zh","text":"每年有 33 000 美国人死于车祸，230 万美国人在车祸中受伤。据交通部预测，这种“会说话”的汽车可以预防高达 80%的不涉酒驾的汽车交通事故。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Five major car companies have been working with DoT on developing and testing the technology. 3 , 000 cars are already using it as part of a government pilot test. Sometime after 2016 , the U.S. government hopes your car will be able to communicate with you."},{"lang":"zh","text":"交通部与五大汽车生产商一直在对该项技术进行研发和测试。目前，作为政府试点的一部分，已有 3 000 辆汽车投入使用。到 2016 年之后的某个时候，美国政府希望你的车将能与你进行交互。"},{"lang":"en","text":"While DoT hopes to make this technology the rule by 2016 , it will still need the public to weigh in before anything is finalized. Now, as for privacy, the government says that data sent between cars doesn't record personal information, so your privacy should not be compromised."},{"lang":"zh","text":"交通部希望，到 2016 年，这个技术能够成为普遍规则，但规则出台前需要公众广泛参与讨论。至于隐私的问题，目前，政府部门表示，车辆之间所传输的数据并不会记录个人信息，因此你的个人信息不会被泄露出去。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":329},{"id":"r-理工英语4-7-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"The Company Leading the Future of Farming","subtitle":"畜牧不再靠农场","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Here's a crazy idea: Combine bioprinting and tissue engineering to “print” animal products and tackle some of the planet's biggest problems. Animal farming, after all, accounts for about half of all human-caused greenhouse gases, taking place on one-third of the available, non-frozen land on Earth, all to feed people's appetites for 300 million tons of meat a year."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有这样一个疯狂的想法：将生物打印技术和组织工程结合在一起，来“打印”畜产品，解决这个星球上最大的问题。毕竟，畜牧业只发生在地球上 1/3 的可用非冰冻土地上，而它释放的温室气体占人类活动产生的温室气体总量的一半。这些都是为了满足人类每年消耗 3亿吨肉制品的需求。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Modern Meadow is a Missouri-based startup that engineers tissues to create lab-grown edible meat, in a process that eliminates many of the negative environmental effects associated with traditional livestock practices."},{"lang":"zh","text":"Modern Meadow 是美国密苏里州的一个新兴公司，他们通过改变组织结构，生产实验室培育的可食用肉。这种肉类生产过程能够消除传统畜牧业对环境产生的许多负面影响。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The company claims that by carefully layering mixtures of cells of different types in a specific structure, in vitro meat production becomes feasible. It's set a short-term goal of printing a sliver of meat around two centimeters by one centimeter, and less than half a millimeter thick, which is edible."},{"lang":"zh","text":"该公司声称，通过在某一特殊结构中将不同类型细胞的混合体按片层状整合到一起，体外肉类培植有望实现。它定下短期目标：通过实验室打印出长 2 厘米、宽 1 厘米的可食用肉片，厚度不超过 0.5 毫米。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The company explains in a submission to the United States Department of Agriculture: “The technology has several advantages in comparison to earlier attempts to engineer meat in vitro. The bio-ink particles can be reproducibly prepared with mixtures of cells of different types. Printing ensures consistent shape, while post-printing structure formation and maturation in the bioreactor facilitates conditioning.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"该公司在呈交给美国农业部的一份报告中解释：“与早期体外培植肉类的尝试相比，此技术有一些优势。不同类型细胞的混合体确保生物墨水颗粒能够源源不断地被生产出来。打印可以保证肉类形状一致，打印好后，在生物反应器中进行的结构成型和成熟能够促进肉类的形成。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"However, it admits that the road ahead is strewn with difficulties. “The consumer acceptance of such products may not be without challenges. We expect it will first appeal to culinary early-adopter consumers and the segment of the vegetarian community that rejects meat for ethical reasons. With reduction in price, it can reach the masses with religious restrictions on meat consumption (people restricted to Hindu, Kosher, Halal diets) and finally populations with limited access to safe meat production.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而，该公司也承认，前路困难重重。“该类产品的市场接受度可能是个挑战。我们期待它能够吸引一批喜好烹饪的早期消费者和那些出于伦理道德原因拒绝肉食的素食主义者。随着价格的降低，在肉类消费上有宗教禁忌的大众（如食用印度、犹太、清真食物的人们）将接受该产品，较难吃到放心肉产品的群体最终也将接纳它。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Whatever the final outcome, lab-grown edible meat is no longer in the realm of science fiction. It is coming."},{"lang":"zh","text":"无论最终结果如何，实验室培育的可食用肉不再只存在于科幻小说中。它的时代即将来临。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":300},{"id":"r-理工英语4-7-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Can GM Food Help Combat World Hunger?","subtitle":"转基因食品能否对抗世界饥饿？","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"By 2050, the world's population is projected to rise to 9 billion from just over 7 billion currently. Proponents of genetically modified foods say they are safe and can boost harvests even in bad conditions by protecting against pests, weeds and drought. This, they argue, will be essential to meeting the needs of a booming population in decades to come and avoiding starvation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"到 2050 年，预计世界人口数量将由现在的 70 多亿增至 90 亿。转基因食品的拥护者声称，转基因食品非常安全，且抗虫、抗杂草、抗旱，即使在恶劣的条件下仍能提高产量。他们辨称，转基因食品至关重要，能够满足未来几十年迅猛增长的人口需求，避免饥荒。"},{"lang":"en","text":"However, Doug Gu rian-Sherman, senior scientist for the food and environment program at the Union of Concerned Scientists, an advocacy group, said genetic engineering for insect resistance has provided only a modest increase in yields since the 1990s and drought-resistant strains have only modestly reduced losses from drought."},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而，美国忧思科学家联盟（一个支持转基因食品的团体）食品与环境项目的资深科学家 Doug Gurian-Sherman 先生说，自从 20 世纪 90 年代以来，旨在抵御病虫灾害的基因工程只是少量提高了农作物产量，旨在抵御干旱的植物品系仅仅稍微降低了干旱损失。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Moreover, he said conventional crossbreeding or cross-pollinating of different varieties for desirable traits, along with improved farming, is getting better results, boosting yields at a lower cost. In fact, much of the food Americans eat has been genetically modified by those conventional methods over thousands of years, before genetic engineering came into practice."},{"lang":"zh","text":"他还说道，（为了获得某种特性而进行的不同种类间的）传统的杂交和交叉授粉，加上先进的耕种方式，正以较低的成本获得较好的收成。事实上，在基因工程进入实践之前，美国人吃的大部分食物已经在数千年的传统种植中发生了基因变化。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“Overall, genetic engineering does not get nearly the bang for the buck as conventional breeding and improve agricultural practices,” Gu rian-Sherman said. His organization advises caution on GM foods and favors labeling, though it acknowledges the risks of genetic engineering have sometimes been exaggerated."},{"lang":"zh","text":"Doug Gurian-Sherman 先生说：“总体上，相对传统育种，基因工程并不划算，在提高农产品产量上，也并不突出。”他所在的组织建议对转基因食物保持警惕，并赞成标记此类食物，尽管它也承认，转基因食物的威胁有时候被夸大了。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Andrea Roberto Sonnino, chief of research at the U.N. food agency, said total food production at present is enough to feed the entire global population. The problem is uneven distribution, leaving870 million suffering from hunger. He said world food production will need to increase by 60 percent to meet the demands of 9 billion by 2050. This must be achieved by increasing yields, he added, because there is little room to expand cultivated land used for agriculture."},{"lang":"zh","text":"联合国粮农组织研究员 Andrea Roberto Sonnino 说，目前粮食产量足够养活全球人类。问题是分布不均，导致 8.7 亿人遭受饥饿。粮食产量需要提高 60%，以满足 2050 年时 9 亿人口的需要。他继续补充道，这一目标只有通过增加产量才能达到，因为农业耕地扩充的空间非常小。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Genetically modified foods, in some instances, can help if the individual product has been assessed as safe, he said. “It's an opportunity that we cannot just miss.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果单个食品能被评估为安全的，那么，在某些情况下，转基因食品是可行的。AndreaRoberto Sonnino 说道，“我们不能错失这样的机会。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":311},{"id":"r-理工英语4-8-1","book":"理工英语4","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Diary of a Space Zucchini","subtitle":"太空西葫芦的日记","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"June 17"},{"lang":"zh","text":"6月17日"},{"lang":"en","text":"Excitement is in the air. Gardener said we will soon be returning to Earth. Our part of the mission is nearly complete and the new crew will take over for us. I am a bit worried about Broccoli,Sunflower, and me. If Gardener leaves, who will take care of us? And what about little Zuc? He is now a big sprout and ready to branch out on his own. Gardener talked about pressing us. I am not sure what that means; this does not sound good."},{"lang":"zh","text":"空气中弥漫着激动人心的气息。园丁说我们马上就要返回地球了。本段任务已接近尾声，新的宇航员将会接管过去。我有点担心西兰花、太阳花，还有我自己。如果园丁离开了，谁将照顾我们呢？小西葫芦怎么办？他已经发芽了，快要长出枝叶了。园丁说要压一压我们。我不知道那是什么意思，但听起来感觉不太好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"June 21"},{"lang":"zh","text":"6月21日"},{"lang":"en","text":"Gardener and crew wore their spacesuits today. This is something Broccoli, Sunflower, little Zuc and I do not have. They spent time in the part of the spaceship that breaks off and falls back to Earth.It is very cramped inside. It must be their version of a seed pod."},{"lang":"zh","text":"园丁和宇航员们今天穿上了太空服。这是西兰花、太阳花、小西葫芦还有我所没有的。宇航员们待在分离后返回地球的飞船里。里面空间非常狭小，那一定是他们的种荚。"},{"lang":"en","text":"June 24"},{"lang":"zh","text":"6月24日"},{"lang":"en","text":"Sunflower is going to seed! His blossom is wilted-brown and has a few lopsided packed seeds.This is not quite normal, but then, we are living on the frontier and things are different here. They are not ready now; I wonder if they will be by the time Gardener is with his seed pod."},{"lang":"zh","text":"太阳花已经开始结籽了。它的花因枯萎而呈现褐色，并挂着些许分布不均的荚果。这并不太正常，但我们正生活在宇宙的边界，这里一切都不一样。他们现在还没准备好，我在想，不知他们在园丁进入种子荚的时候是否能准备好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"June 26"},{"lang":"zh","text":"6月26日"},{"lang":"en","text":"Gardener has this big book. He called it an atlas, a map of Earth. It is normally kept by the big window but now it is stuck to the wall right next to Broccoli, Sunflower, little Zuc, and me. He also transplanted us into new bags. This time the bags are very small, just enough to contain our root ball and a splash of water. He told us that he will soon be leaving and that we will return later in the belly of a Dragon."},{"lang":"zh","text":"园丁有一本大书，他叫它地图集，是地球的图册。通常它被放在大窗户旁边，但现在它挨着西兰花、向日葵、小西葫芦和我，贴墙放着。他还把我们移植到新的培育袋中。这次的袋子非常小，刚好能容纳根茎和一点水。他告诉我们，他很快就要离开，我们很快也将回到宇宙飞船Dragon的舱内。"},{"lang":"en","text":"July 1"},{"lang":"zh","text":"7月1日"},{"lang":"en","text":"Today Gardener and his crew will depart in their seed pod; the replacement crew is ready to carry on in their place. He is wearing his spacesuit undergarments. Not too stylish but functional. He gave all of us an extra long smell. His nose twitched with the slightest tickle from the leaf hairs on little Zuc. He said that what will be is for the best. It has been a wonderful journey; one chapter is closing, another is opening. He had tears in his eyes, not just a small drop at the corners but a pool that was making him blink. He reached up and turned out the light. In the frontier you should not be afraid of the dark."},{"lang":"zh","text":"今天园丁和宇航员们将乘他们的种荚离开了，替代他们的船员也准备就位了。园丁贴身穿着太空服，虽不时髦但却实用。他意味深长地嗅了嗅我们，用鼻子轻挠着小西葫芦叶子上的茸毛。他说，即将到来的，就是最好的。这是一段精彩的旅程，旧的篇章结束，新的篇章开启。园丁的眼里含着泪，不是眼角的泪滴，而是像一汪水，让他不由自主地眨眼。他伸手去关灯。在宇宙的边界，你不应该害怕黑暗。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":402},{"id":"r-理工英语4-8-2","book":"理工英语4","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"Space Elevator: Expert Q&A","subtitle":"太空电梯：专家问答","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Why build a space elevator?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"为什么要建造太空电梯？"},{"lang":"en","text":"The space elevator will reduce the cost of getting from Earth to space. It will also allow us to take very large payloads into space very easily, very safely. Because of that, we can build cities on the moon. We can build space stations. We can build large solar arrays in space to collect energy from the sun and beam it down to Earth."},{"lang":"zh","text":"太空电梯将降低从地球到太空的费用。太空电梯能够让我们运送巨大载荷进入太空，既轻松又安全。这样，我们就可以在月球上建城市，可以建空间站，可以在太空修建大型太阳能帆板来收集太阳能量，然后将它发射回地球。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Why not just use rockets instead?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"为什么不使用火箭？"},{"lang":"en","text":"Rockets are very expensive. The shuttle costs $10,000 a pound to put a payload into low-Earth orbit, and if you want to go to the moon or Mars, it's hundreds of thousands of dollars per pound or more. Rockets are also very limited in the amount of payload they can carry, and they're risky. With a space elevator, the cost is a fraction of that — it may go down to 100th or 1,000th of current costs — and there are no rocket engines that might explode."},{"lang":"zh","text":"火箭费用太昂贵了。将载荷送往低地球轨道，每磅得花1万美元；若要运往月球或火星，每磅的花费更高。在运送数量上，火箭也受到限制，且充满风险。但太空电梯就不一样了，费用仅为火箭运输的一小部分，只有其百分之一或千分之一，且不会像火箭引擎那样面临爆炸的风险。"},{"lang":"en","text":"What would it be like to ride the elevator?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"登上太空电梯是什么感觉？"},{"lang":"en","text":"You'd go to an ocean platform, you'd climb into a module, and you'd feel it start moving. You'd see the Earth fall away. In just a half hour or so, you'd pass up through the clouds, and you'd start to see the curve of the horizon. Another half an hour to an hour later, you'd basically be in space. You'd see stars, even in the middle of the day. Eventually you'd be weightless. It'd be a very smooth ride;there wouldn't be any shaking."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你得登上海洋发射台，爬进舱体，你会感觉它开始移动。你可以看到，地球离你越来越远。大约半小时之后，你会穿越云层，渐渐能够看到地平线了。再过半小时或一小时，你基本就进入太空了。你会看到星星，即使是在大白天。最终你会处于失重的状态。那将是一次非常平稳的旅行，感觉不到任何摇晃。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Are there potential drawbacks to opening space this way?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"通过太空电梯开发太空有什么潜在弊端吗？"},{"lang":"en","text":"Everything we do has the potential for creating some bad. If we mine an asteroid, the asteroid's going to look ugly, just like a mine here. But I think the benefits of opening up space far outweigh the damage that we can see — benefits in terms of gaining energy from space to replace oil,additional capabilities in telecommunications, manufacturing in space, additional real estate and exploration."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们做的任何事情都可能产生潜在的负面影响。若我们开采小行星，它可能会变得破败不堪，就像地球上的矿井一样。但我认为，开发太空的益处远远大于我们能预见的弊端，这些益处可能涉及：从太空获取替代石油的能源，在电信、太空制造、额外地产以及探索方面的附加能力。"}],"source":"理工英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.docx","words":328},{"id":"r-管理英语3-1-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Managing Oneself","subtitle":"自我管理","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"We live in an age full of opportunities: If you are smart enough, and have got ambition and keep pushing forward, you can rise to the top of your chosen profession, no matter where you started out."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们生活在一个充满机遇的时代︰无论你从哪里开始，如果你既聪明过人，又有远大抱负，并且勇往直前，那么你就可以在自己所选的职业领域中出类拔萃。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But with opportunity comes responsibility. Companies today aren't managing their employees'careers. Professional workers must be their own chief executive officers (CEO). It's up to you to strive or your place, to keep yourself engaged and Productive during a working life that may last around 50 years. To do those things well, you'll need to have a deep understanding of yourself —not only what your strengths and weaknesses are, but also how you learn, how you work with others what your values are, and where you can make the greatest contribution because only when you operate from strength can you achieve true excellence."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但是，随着机遇而来的便是责任。现在的公司已经不管理员工的职业生涯，自由职业者必须成为自己的首席执行官(CEO)。在大约五十年的职业生涯中，能否积极上进、勤奋工作、取得成效取决于你自己。要把事情做好，你需要对自己有一个深刻的了解，不仅仅是你的优缺点，还有你的学习方式，你与人共事的方式，你的价值观，以及你能作出最大贡献的领域。因为只有当你充分发挥自己的长处时，你才能做到真正优秀。"},{"lang":"en","text":"History's great achievers —Napoléon, da Vinci, and Mozart —have always managed themselves. But they are so unusual both in their talents and in their accomplishments as to be considered rare exceptions Now, most of us, even those of us with modest talents, will have to learn to manage ourselves. We will have to learn to develop ourselves. We will have to place ourselves where we can make the greatest contribution. And we will have to stay mentally alert and engaged during a 50-year working life, which means knowing how and when to change the work we do."},{"lang":"zh","text":"历史上那些取得伟大成就的人——拿破仑，达·芬奇和莫扎特，他们一直在管理自己。正因为他们既才智过人，又成就非凡，所以人们把他们视为少之又少的例外。现在，我们中的大多数人，即使智力平平，也都得学会自我管理。我们不得不学会发展自己。我们应该把自己放到能作出最大贡献的位置。在将近五十年的工作生涯中，我们必须让自己时刻头脑清醒，全神贯注，这意味着我们该了解转变我们现有工作的方式和时机"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":236},{"id":"r-管理英语3-1-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Organization Structure in Hoogle Engineering Hoogle","subtitle":"工程公司的组织结构","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"I'm Michael Bush, Managing Director of Hoogle Engineering. I am pleased to welcome you here to our website and I'd like to tell you a little about the company and its organization. Hoogle Engineering was set up in 1960. It was divided into several departments at that time, such as the sales department, marketing department, and production department. Lots of managers were employed to manage it all."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我是Hoogle工程公司的主管麦克· 布什。欢迎你来到我们的网站，请允许我为你介绍一下公司及其结构的情况。Hoogle工程始建于1960年，当时被分为几个部门，如销售部、营销部和生产部。我们要聘请许多管理人员来管理各个部门。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fortunately things are different now. Sixty people are employed by Hoogle and communication between departments is considered to be one of the most important aspects of the business. The market is global so we need to make contact with customers worldwide, not just locally."},{"lang":"zh","text":"幸运的是现在的情况不一样了。Hoogle雇佣了六十个人，而部门之间的沟通被认为是业务中最重要的一个方面。市场是全球性的，所以我们需要与全球的客户密切联系,而不仅仅是本地客户。"},{"lang":"en","text":"But in the old days we were all in different departments and never spoke to each other. We had a tall structure. Traditionally we had people at the first level on the shop floor manufacturing products according to the instructions which they were given. Then you had a supervisory level of people who supervised them every day. Then you moved up to the middle management, who were doing the tasks of getting new business, and then you had the senior anagement team, and then you had the board, who decided the business strategy. So there were a lot of levels in the company in the old days actually."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但在过去，我们在不同的部门,也没有互相沟通。以前，我们是直线式结构，车间里的一线员工按照指令生产产品，会有一个管理层人员每天监督他们。当你上升到要处理新业务的中层管理时,你就会有高级管理团队,你上面有董事会来决定业务策略。因此，在过去的年代，一个公司有很多层级管理。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The structure today is that we form teams within teams to place people who can manufacture a product. Each team has members that can manufacture different products. The actual teams now are self-managing, so we don't even have team leaders. You've got the teams, and then you've got two people, only two people, who are what you think of as management. This is generally called flat structure."},{"lang":"zh","text":"现在的结构是，我们在团队内组建小团队，安排能够生产同一产品的人员在其中。每个团队都有可以制造不同产品的成员。 现在的团队是自我管理的，所以我们甚至不需要团队领袖。你有团队，然后你有两个人，只有两个人，这就是你认为的管理。这通常被称为扁平式结构。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":286},{"id":"r-管理英语3-2-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"“War for Talent” Goes on in Job Market","subtitle":"","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The “war for talent”reads like headlines from many years ago, but it has never gone away, says Eleanor Nickerson, director of UK operations for Top Employers.Many companies they have researched on are short of talents. Though the companies may receive many"},{"lang":"en","text":"Applications ,they cannot find the people they want."},{"lang":"zh","text":"顶尖雇主的英国业务主管Eleanor Nickerson说，“人才争夺战”看起来像许多年前的头条新闻，但它从未离开过我们的眼球。他们调查的许多公司都缺乏人才。虽然那些公司可能会收到很多应聘申请，但他们找不到他们想要的人才。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Top Employers' research shows that offering good career chances is the key to attracting and keeping the talent. Smart employees know their own value and will want to know what their employers can offer them after 5 or 10 years' career development. So, keeping staff is the biggest challenge employers face in the long run."},{"lang":"zh","text":"顶尖雇主的研究表明，提供优厚的事业发展前景是吸引和留住人才的关键。聪明的员工知道自身价值，并希望知道雇主在他们5-10年的职业发展后可以给他们提供什么。所以，从长远来看，留住员工是雇主面临的最大挑战。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Yet not every employee feels that they can better their career chances. Some are still nervous about losing their jobs, despite a recent fall in unemployment, says the Trades Union Congress (TUC). TUC points out that some four-fifths of new jobs created have been in part of the economy where average pay rates are less than £8 an hour since the"},{"lang":"en","text":"recession began. Many of these jobs are on temporary or zero-hours contracts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"但是，并不是每位员工都觉得他们能够获得更好的事业发展机会。贸易联盟大会（TUC）表示，虽然近期失业率有所下降，但有些人仍然担心失去工作。 TUC指出，自经济衰退开始以来，约有五分之四的新就业机会是来自于平均工资水平低于时薪8英镑的工业，其中许多工作是临时或零时工合同。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A report from the Office for National Statistics published in February showed that real wages have been falling consistently since 2010.It's the longest period since at least 1964. “We're still in the hardest living standards squeeze for over a century and those who are already working have had years of real-terms pay cuts, ” says TUC spokesperson Liz Chinchen. “Understanding the pressures that staff face is a good starting point for any employer. If employers want to show concern for their staff, they should be paying them well and understand that zero-hours contracts bring Insecurity and extreme money worries.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"2月份发布的国家统计局的报告显示，自2010年以来，实际工资一直在持续下降。这是自1964年以来最长的时期。TUC发言人Liz Chinchen说：“一个多世纪以来，我们的生活水平一直处于最艰难的状况，而且，多年来员工的收入实际上一直在减少。” “了解员工面临的压力是每一位雇主的良好起点。如果雇主想要关心他们的员工，他们应该很好地支付他们，并理解零时工合同给员工带来不安全感和极大的金钱忧虑。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":277},{"id":"r-管理英语3-2-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Human Resources Management","subtitle":"人力资源管理","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Human Resources Management (HRM) is the process of managing people and their relationships in an organization. These two processes are important in the success and growth of a business."},{"lang":"zh","text":"人力资源管理（HRM）是在一个组织里管理人员和他们之间的关系的过程，这两个过程对于企业的成功和发展至关重要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In managing people, staffing is the most important Component of HRM. It needs to make guideline and procedures for hiring and placement. Staffing also involves the management of employees on matters like monitoring of holidays, absences , health and safety, disciplinary action, and dismissal ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在管理人员方面，人事工作是人力资源管理最重要的内容，得制定招聘和安置的指导方针和章程。人事工作也包含对员工的管理，如休假、缺勤、健康与安全、纪律处分和解雇等事项。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another important element of HRM in managing people is keeping the employees in the company. The training of employees to enable them to improve their career development is very important. Good HRM policies ensure that there are clear regulations which show the pay levels for the different positions in an organization. It is important for the staff to know the career path, pay, training and other opportunities that are available to them. Performance management is another important component of HRM. The reason for this is that many employers use it to evaluate career improvement and to determine pay increases."},{"lang":"zh","text":"人力资源管理在人员管理上另一个重要作用是留住员工在公司。提升员工职业发展能力的培训十分重要。优质的人力资源管理能够保证公司有明确的制度实行以岗定薪，重要的是让员工了解他们可能得到的职业前景，薪资，培训和其他机会。绩效管理是人力资源管理的另一个主要内容，这样做的原因是，许多雇主用它来评估职业提升和确定加薪。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The secondary role of HRM is the management of the relationships among people in an organization. This includes staff within departments as well as across the whole organization. The relationship between staff and management is an important factor in the success of an organization. It decides how fast an organization will realize their goals."},{"lang":"zh","text":"人力资源管理的另一个内容是管理员工之间的关系，这包括部门内以及整个机构的人员。员工与管理层之间的关系是一个机构成功的重要因素之一。它决定了机构实现其企业目标的快慢。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The focus of HRM is the people within an organization. Regular planning, monitoring and evaluation are important for the success of HRM. Successful management ensures that all employees know their role, career development and also feel part of an organization."},{"lang":"zh","text":"人力资源管理的重点是机构内部的人。常规规划、记录和评价对人力资源管理的成功非常重要。成功的管理确保所有员工都知道他们的角色、职业发展以及归属感。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":265},{"id":"r-管理英语3-3-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"Save Money by Understanding Why You Spend It","subtitle":"知道为何花钱才知道如何省钱","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"To save money, you simply need to spend less than you earn. It is easy to say, but why is it so difficult to do? To answer this question, you need to study the factors that keep you spending all the time."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为了省钱，你的花费只要不超过你挣得的钱就行。但为什么说得容易做的难呢？ 回答这个问题，你需要研究一下是哪几个因素让你一直不停的花钱。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Easy access to credit容易获得信贷"},{"lang":"en","text":"For most people, this is the biggest reason for overspending. People can easily get a credit card, simply by filling out a short form in a bank or jumping on their website. They can borrow money from banks to go shopping, even buy cars or houses. When you aren't physically handing someone money or a check for a purchase, you will feel you are spending free money or you aren't pending money at all. Try using cash to get your spending under control."},{"lang":"zh","text":"对大多数人来说，这是超支最大的原因。信用卡获取方便，人们只需要在银行或在其网站上填写一个简易表格就行。有了信用卡，人们就可以从银行借钱去购物，甚至去买汽车或房子。当你在购物时不是实实在在用现金或支票付款，你会觉得你在免费消费或者完全没有花钱。试着用现金付款来控制你的消费。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Misusing credit cards滥用信用卡"},{"lang":"en","text":"A credit card is an interest free short-term loan. When used as planned, this can be a powerful financial tool. The problem is when you begin to let the balance continue from month to month. If you make a $200purchase on your credit card and find out that at the end of the month you can't afford to repay the full amount, this is when the high interest rates on the cards really begin to hurt you. That is no way of saving money."},{"lang":"zh","text":"信用卡是短期的无息贷款。如果有计划的使用，信用卡是一个强有力的金融工具。问题是你何时开始可以保持每月的收支平衡。如果你用信用卡支付了200美元后，发现在这个月底你不能全额偿还，这时高利率可能真的开始伤害你了。那当然更不是省钱的办法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Giving in to temptation屈服于诱惑"},{"lang":"en","text":"We all need to enjoy life, but don't waste your financial future for a few guilty pleasures today if they aren't in your budget. When you know that you can't afford an activity, don't give in. Instead, invite your friends over for a home dinner party, game night, or some other activities where you can still enjoy time together, but without breaking your budget."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们都需要享受生活,但是如果有些消费不在你的预算内，就不要让今天的一些负罪享乐影响你的未来财务状况。当你知道自己负担不起有些开销时，就别被诱惑了。不如邀请你的朋友来家里聚餐,设计家庭游戏夜,或一些其他的活动,这样你既没有超出预算，也可以和朋友们一起享受时光。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Spending to feel good支出感觉良好"},{"lang":"en","text":"Everyone enjoys getting something new —buying yourself something feels good. There is absolutely nothing wrong with this, as long as you don't go overboard . You'll feel good about your purchase whether you make it with cash or by credit card, but you'll feel even better when you don't have to spend the next two years trying to pay it off with 20% interest."},{"lang":"zh","text":"每个人都喜欢得到一些新的东西——给自己买东西的感觉总是很好的。只要不过火，这件事就没有任何错。无论你用现金还是用信用卡支付，你都会感觉良好，不过，当你随后两年不用被迫还清附加20% 高利息的债务时，感觉会更好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"To save money, you simply need to spend less than you earn. It is easy to say, but why is it so difficult to do? To answer this question, you need to study the factors that keep you spending all the time."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为了省钱，你的花费只要不超过你挣得的钱就行。但为什么说得容易做的难呢？ 回答这个问题，你需要研究一下是哪几个因素让你一直不停的花钱。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Easy access to credit容易获得信贷"},{"lang":"en","text":"For most people, this is the biggest reason for overspending. People can easily get a credit card, simply by filling out a short form in a bank or jumping on their website. They can borrow money from banks to go shopping, even buy cars or houses. When you aren't physically handing someone money or a check for a purchase, you will feel you are spending free money or you aren't pending money at all. Try using cash to get your spending under control."},{"lang":"zh","text":"对大多数人来说，这是超支最大的原因。信用卡获取方便，人们只需要在银行或在其网站上填写一个简易表格就行。有了信用卡，人们就可以从银行借钱去购物，甚至去买汽车或房子。当你在购物时不是实实在在用现金或支票付款，你会觉得你在免费消费或者完全没有花钱。试着用现金付款来控制你的消费。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Misusing credit cards滥用信用卡"},{"lang":"en","text":"A credit card is an interest free short-term loan. When used as planned, this can be a powerful financial tool. The problem is when you begin to let the balance continue from month to month. If you make a $200purchase on your credit card and find out that at the end of the month you can't afford to repay the full amount, this is when the high interest rates on the cards really begin to hurt you. That is no way of saving money."},{"lang":"zh","text":"信用卡是短期的无息贷款。如果有计划的使用，信用卡是一个强有力的金融工具。问题是你何时开始可以保持每月的收支平衡。如果你用信用卡支付了200美元后，发现在这个月底你不能全额偿还，这时高利率可能真的开始伤害你了。那当然更不是省钱的办法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Giving in to temptation屈服于诱惑"},{"lang":"en","text":"We all need to enjoy life, but don't waste your financial future for a few guilty pleasures today if they aren't in your budget. When you know that you can't afford an activity, don't give in. Instead, invite your friends over for a home dinner party, game night, or some other activities where you can still enjoy time together, but without breaking your budget."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们都需要享受生活,但是如果有些消费不在你的预算内，就不要让今天的一些负罪享乐影响你的未来财务状况。当你知道自己负担不起有些开销时，就别被诱惑了。不如邀请你的朋友来家里聚餐,设计家庭游戏夜,或一些其他的活动,这样你既没有超出预算，也可以和朋友们一起享受时光。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Spending to feel good支出感觉良好"},{"lang":"en","text":"Everyone enjoys getting something new —buying yourself something feels good. There is absolutely nothing wrong with this, as long as you don't go overboard . You'll feel good about your purchase whether you make it with cash or by credit card, but you'll feel even better when you don't have to spend the next two years trying to pay it off with 20% interest."},{"lang":"zh","text":"每个人都喜欢得到一些新的东西——给自己买东西的感觉总是很好的。只要不过火，这件事就没有任何错。无论你用现金还是用信用卡支付，你都会感觉良好，不过，当你随后两年不用被迫还清附加20% 高利息的债务时，感觉会更好。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":702},{"id":"r-管理英语3-3-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Three Steps to a Good Marketing Budget","subtitle":"三个步骤做好营销预算","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Without good budget management, you are likely to overspend on marketing accidentally. Here are three steps that help to make a good marketing budget."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你不做好预算管理，可能在做营销时不小心就超支了。这里介绍三个步骤帮助你做好营销预算。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Step 1: Organize financial information（步骤1:整理财务信息）"},{"lang":"en","text":"The first step is to be clear of your current financial situation. You need to know how much money your company makes monthly and the changes that might arise in the future. Although income flows change throughout the year, you must organize the information based on"},{"lang":"en","text":"Reliable revenue —the minimum amount of money your company makes each month."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第一步是要弄清楚你当前的财务状况。你要知道公司每月的收入和未来可能出现的变化。虽然全年收入量在变化,你必须基于可靠的收入数据——公司每月的最低收入额来整理信息。"},{"lang":"en","text":"A realistic budget plan will always focus on the income that"},{"lang":"en","text":"Exceeds the expenses, not the total revenue that comes in. When you have determined the amount of disposable income available for the company, you should determine where the money will go."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一个切实可行的预算方案永远关注的是大于支出的收入，而不是总收入。一旦确定了公司现有的可支配收入，你就应该确定如何花这些钱。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Step 2: Determine where you want to spend marketing funds"},{"lang":"zh","text":"（步骤2:确定如何支配营销资金）"},{"lang":"en","text":"After you know the total amount available to spend on marketing, the next step is how you plan to spend that money. Three main factors decide how you spend marketing funds: the budget amount, your past experiences, and where you can reach the right audience."},{"lang":"zh","text":"下一步就是当你知道可用于营销的资金总额后，你就应该计划如何花这些钱。三个因素决定如何使用营销资金：预算额度、以往经验和寻找目标客户。"},{"lang":"en","text":"You will start organizing how to spend the funds based on the amount. Besides, you need to consider the strategies that have worked in the past. Also, you need to consider which marketing channels will allow you to reach the right audience."},{"lang":"zh","text":"基于已有额度你要开始策划如何使用这些资金。除此之外,你需要考虑以往工作中的营销策略，还要考虑寻找目标客户的营销渠道。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Step 3:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Assess data and make appropriate changes（第三步:评估数据和适当调整）"},{"lang":"en","text":"The final step in building a good marketing budget is the analysis of the plan and any changes that may improve revenue. ultimately , marketing is designed to bring in extra revenue. If the activity does not bring in any additional revenue over its cost, then it is better to change strategy and try something else."},{"lang":"zh","text":"做好一个营销预算的最后一步是分析，即对可提高收入的计划和可能产生的变化进行分析。市场营销的最终目的是带来额外收益。如果营销活动不带来任何额外的收入，那么最好是改变战略,尝试别的方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Assessing the data is a vital part of creating an effective marketing strategy.Evaluation begins with comparing past performance to the performance after marketing the product or services."},{"lang":"zh","text":"数据评估是制定有效市场营销策略的重要一环。评估始于对产品销售和服务的过去的业绩与现状进行比较。"},{"lang":"en","text":"However, a good budget alone is not enough. You have to take action and remain committed to following through your plan. By keeping the budget in mind when you make decisions, you will have the opportunity to work out different strategies to find the best solutions for your business goals and prevent overspending on marketing."},{"lang":"zh","text":"然而,仅仅有一个好的预算方案是不够的。你必须付诸行动,继续致力于实施你的计划。在你决策时，只有不忘预算，你才有机会找到多种策略和相应措施，达到商业目标，并防止营销超支。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":363},{"id":"r-管理英语3-4-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"Road Closure Procedures in Sydney","subtitle":"悉尼道路封闭程序","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"To minimize traffic jams in the city center and on Major roads out of Sydney, the City's highway department will not agree to road closures schedule for weekdays or Saturdays. On minor roads outside the city center, weekdays and Saturdays may be considered. You must apply for approval to do roadwork and other road-related activities , tree cutting and use of very large construction machinery , ladder, etc. Please note that approval is needed if you plan to block the road or footpath ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为了减少悉尼市中心和主要道路的交通堵塞，市公路局不会同意工作日或周六的道路封闭，不过可考虑市中心外的次要道路的封闭。道路施工或实施与道路有关的活动，如砍树、使用大型筑路机械、云梯等，必须提交申请。请注意，如果计划封锁道路或人行道，是需要获得批准才能进行的。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Applications to have a road closed to traffic must be completed and sent to the Department's Traffic Calming Committee at least a month before the scheduled date."},{"lang":"zh","text":"道路交通封闭申请必须在离预定日期至少一个月之前提交给政府交通稳静化委员会。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Roads can be closed partially or fully , depend on your requirements. Partial road closures are only allowed in light traffic areas where there will be at least 1lane for traffic with extra traffic control Measures to make sure 2-way traffic can continue to run for the duration of the work. Any change of traffic flow will require the proposal to be treated as a full road closure. For further information about a partial road closure, please refer to Contacts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据要求，道路可实行全封闭或部分封闭。部分道路封闭只允许在交通不繁忙的地段进行，封闭期间至少得有一条车道用于通行，辅以交通管制措施保证双向交通顺畅通行。以任何方式改变交通流量都被视为全面封路，需要提交申请。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If you are organizing a parade , march or other type of street-based"},{"lang":"en","text":"event, approval is also required and we recommend you choose one of our 4 preferred route. Choosing an existingroutereduce the amount of planning you will need to do."},{"lang":"zh","text":"组织示威游行或其他需要占用道路的活动也须得到批准。建议从四条预定的路线中选择一条。选择一条现有的线路，需要做的准备工作会少很多。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":228},{"id":"r-管理英语3-4-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"Beijing's Roads for the Future","subtitle":"北京未来的道路系统","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The road system in Beijing's central business district (CBD) is being"},{"lang":"en","text":"re-design to make public transportation easy and improve efficiency."},{"lang":"zh","text":"北京中心商务区（CBD）的道路系统正在被重新设计，以便让公共交通更加便捷。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Plans for 45 roads within the CBD have been approved, measuring 41.5 kilometers in total. In addition to public buses, free or low price shuttle buses from residence areas to subway stations will also be provided for commuters."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在CBD内新建四十五条道路的规划已获批准，总长度为41.5公里。除公交车外，还将向上班族提供免费或廉价的班车往返于居住地与地铁站之间。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This is just over four times the number of roads opened in 2007, and will add another 15.5 km to the existing road network."},{"lang":"zh","text":"规划中的道路略高于2007年开通道路的四倍，将在现有道路网的基础上增加15.5公里。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Besides roads, an underground traffic system has also been operating, which includes four new subway lines beneath the CBD."},{"lang":"zh","text":"除了道路，一套地下交通系统也一直在运行，包括在CBD下运行的四条地铁线。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The underground connection system is made up of two levels. The first underground floor is set aside mainly for pedestrians and commercial facilities, while the second underground floor is planned for parking."},{"lang":"zh","text":"地下互联系统有两层，地下一层主要用于行人和商业设施，而地下二层计划为停车场。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The city has also invested 140 million yuan to set up a traffic inquiry system, through which the public can check traffic conditions online and see the most convenient routes on their GPS system.In the future, the CBD will be fully covered by an intelligent traffic control system."},{"lang":"zh","text":"北京市还投资了一亿四千万元建立一个交通查询系统，通过这个系统，市民可以在网上查询交通状况，在GPS系统上查到最方便的路线。今后，CBD将全面覆盖智能交通控制系统。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The road system in Beijing's central business district (CBD) is being"},{"lang":"en","text":"re-design to make public transportation easy and improve efficiency."},{"lang":"zh","text":"北京中心商务区（CBD）的道路系统正在被重新设计，以便让公共交通更加便捷。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Plans for 45 roads within the CBD have been approved, measuring 41.5 kilometers in total. In addition to public buses, free or low price shuttle buses from residence areas to subway stations will also be provided for commuters."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在CBD内新建四十五条道路的规划已获批准，总长度为41.5公里。除公交车外，还将向上班族提供免费或廉价的班车往返于居住地与地铁站之间。"},{"lang":"en","text":"This is just over four times the number of roads opened in 2007, and will add another 15.5 km to the existing road network."},{"lang":"zh","text":"规划中的道路略高于2007年开通道路的四倍，将在现有道路网的基础上增加15.5公里。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Besides roads, an underground traffic system has also been operating, which includes four new subway lines beneath the CBD."},{"lang":"zh","text":"除了道路，一套地下交通系统也一直在运行，包括在CBD下运行的四条地铁线。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The underground connection system is made up of two levels. The first underground floor is set aside mainly for pedestrians and commercial facilities, while the second underground floor is planned for parking."},{"lang":"zh","text":"地下互联系统有两层，地下一层主要用于行人和商业设施，而地下二层计划为停车场。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The city has also invested 140 million yuan to set up a traffic inquiry system, through which the public can check traffic conditions online and see the most convenient routes on their GPS system.In the future, the CBD will be fully covered by an intelligent traffic control system."},{"lang":"zh","text":"北京市还投资了一亿四千万元建立一个交通查询系统，通过这个系统，市民可以在网上查询交通状况，在GPS系统上查到最方便的路线。今后，CBD将全面覆盖智能交通控制系统。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":356},{"id":"r-管理英语3-5-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Food Safety","subtitle":"食品安全","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A question that often troubles food companies is how to control problems like rats and insect without harming the food. Pest control experts say poison should never be used where they may enter food. They say the first line of defense against pests is to clean the places where the food is handled or stored."},{"lang":"zh","text":"经常困扰食品公司的一个问题是,如何控制老鼠和昆虫，同时又不会对食物造成破坏。鼠害控制专家说，凡是在毒药有可能污染食物的地方决不能使用毒药。他们说，防止鼠害的第一道防线就是将加工和储存食品的地方弄干净。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Floors, food preparation surfaces and tools can be disinfect with chemicals like chlorine iodine or bromine. Food containers should be stored about half a meter off the ground and about half a meter away from any walls. Storage areas should be kept dry and clean."},{"lang":"zh","text":"地板、食品加工场地和工具可以用氯、碘、溴等化学物进行消毒。装食品的容器的设置应高出地面半米，且离墙半米。存储区域应保持干燥和清洁。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Containers for raw materials such as rice, wheat, etc. should be kept closed and clean. Any foodstuff split during delivery or handling should be cleared up both inside and outside the building. Pests enter a building from the outside, so pay attention to outer walls. Small stones can be used to cover the ground and block the growth of plants and the grass should be kept short to deny pests a place to live."},{"lang":"zh","text":"装原材料如大米、小麦等的容器应加盖严实，保持干净。在食品运输或加工过程中，任何洒落在室内外的食物都要清理干净。老鼠是从室外进入屋内的，因此要注意检查外墙。可用小石子铺上地面以阻止草木生长，长出的草要剪短，使老鼠无藏身之处。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Check that doors and windows are completely closed. Also any hole that might allow pests to enter a building should be filled. Rats can enter through a hole the size of a coin. A mouse can pass through a hole half that size."},{"lang":"zh","text":"门窗要经常检查，确保严实无缝，任何老鼠可能钻进来的洞都要堵上。田鼠可从一个硬币大小的洞钻进屋内，而半个硬币大小的洞则可让家鼠钻进来。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Supervisors should make a list of pest control measures to be taken by employees. This will aid the efforts and also help prepare for any inspections . In most countries, there is a food and administration"},{"lang":"en","text":"bureau ,or some agency with a similar name, which enforces rules nationwide, responsible for rules about the use of pesticides , etc. However, businesses where food is stored, prepared or sold must also follow state and local health laws. Most of these governmental departments or bureaus have their websites with information about food safety policies and other issues. People can easily access the information."},{"lang":"zh","text":"管理者应当给员工列出需要采取的鼠害防治措施。这将有助于鼠害防治工作，也便于员工做好随时检查的准备。大多数国家都有食品药品管理局或类似的机构，其职责是在全国范围内加强执法，负责制定毒鼠药和杀虫剂的使用条例。食品储存、加工或销售单位也必须遵循国家和当地制定的健康法规。大多数相关政府部门或食品药品局都建有网站，提供有关食品安全政策等信息，人们可以便捷地获取这些信息。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":315},{"id":"r-管理英语3-5-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"The International Food Safety Authorities Network (INFOSAN)","subtitle":"国际食品安全当局网络","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"With the rapid globalization of food production and trade, international issues related to food safety are likely to increase. Food safety authorities all over the world have realized that food safety problems should be carried out at both national and international levels. ("},{"lang":"zh","text":"随着食品生产和贸易的迅速全球化，国家食品安全问题有可能会增加。世界各地的食品安全部门意识到，解决食品安全问题应在国家和国际这两个层面进行。发生重大食品安全问题时，迫切需要交换常规的食品安全信息，快速分享经验和信息。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"This global network includes 181 Member States. Each has a designated INFOSAN Emergency Contact Point which manages communication between national food safety authorities.国际食品安全当局网络（INFOSAN）由世界卫生组织（WHO）和联合国粮食及农业组织（FAO）共同承担。这一全球性网络包括181个成员国。每个成员国都有一个指定的国际食品安全当局网络紧急联络点，负责各国食品安全部门之间的联系。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The network aims to: 该网络旨在："},{"lang":"en","text":"●Promote the rapid exchange of information during food safety related events;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"促进食品安全事件发生期间的信息快速交换；"},{"lang":"en","text":"●Share information on important food safety related issues of global interest;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"分享全球共同关心的重要食品安全问题的信息；"},{"lang":"en","text":"●Promote partnership and cooperation between countries;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"促进各国之间的协同合作；"},{"lang":"en","text":"●Help countries strengthen their capacity to manage food safety risks."},{"lang":"zh","text":"帮助各国提高管理食品风险的能力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"As part of its routine activities, the INFOSAN Secretariat publishes reports in six languages and provides members with summaries and guidance on relevant food safety issues."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为日常生活的一部分，国际食品安全当局网络秘书处用六种语言发布报告，为成员国提供相关的食品安全问题总结和指导。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It is also a useful resource for other public health organizations which recognize INFOSAN as an organization through which findings of investigations and strategies for improving food safety may be shared."},{"lang":"zh","text":"国际食品安全当局网络促进各成员国之间食品安全信息和经验的交换。对于其他公共卫生组织来说，这也是一个有用的资源。其他公共卫生组织认为国际食品安全当局网络是一个可以分享食品安全问题调查结果和改善食品安全策略的组织。"},{"lang":"en","text":"INFOSAN can work with other international organizations to provide assistance to the countries or regions with emerging food safety events of possible international concern."},{"lang":"zh","text":"国际食品安全当局网络与世界卫生组织预警和应对活动项目密切合作，监控可能发生的国际食品安全事件。国际食品安全当局网络可以与其他国际组织一道，共同为发生可能引发国际关切的食品安全事件的国家和地区提供帮助。"},{"lang":"en","text":"With the rapid globalization of food production and trade, international issues related to food safety are likely to increase. Food safety authorities all over the world have realized that food safety problems should be carried out at both national and international levels."},{"lang":"zh","text":"随着食品生产和贸易的迅速全球化，国家食品安全问题有可能会增加。世界各地的食品安全部门意识到，解决食品安全问题应在国家和国际这两个层面进行。发生重大食品安全问题时，迫切需要交换常规的."}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":207},{"id":"r-管理英语3-6-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"Door-Knocking","subtitle":"上门探访","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Door-knocking is the most effective way of making face-to-face community contact, but it has become a lost art.8 With the recent focus on customer privacy , door-knocking seems like an intrusion into other people's lives. But those who try it for the first time are usually surprised by the pleasant reception they receive. Here are some suggestions that will help you promote your services face-to-face."},{"lang":"zh","text":"上门探访是进行社区面对面交流的最有效的方法，但它已经成为了一门失传的艺术。随着近来对客户隐私的重视，上门探访似乎是对他人生活的侵扰。但是第一次尝试上门探访的人通常会为自己受到的友好接待而感到惊喜。接下来是几条能帮助你提高面对面服务效果的建议。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"BEFORE YOU GO OUT在你出动之前"},{"lang":"zh","text":"◆—先挂上门牌"},{"lang":"en","text":"Try leaving a door hanger two days before you go door-knocking. It should briefly describe the project and say that someone will be around in person."},{"lang":"zh","text":"尝试在你去上门探访的前两天留一个门牌。门牌上应该简要的描述你的来意，并说明最近会有人亲自上门拜访。"},{"lang":"en","text":"◆ Wear an official name tag戴上正式的名牌"},{"lang":"en","text":"Door-knockers should wear name tags with the logo of their organization. The best name tags will also include a color photo and the name of the caller."},{"lang":"zh","text":"上门探访者应该戴上有你们组织标识的名牌，好的名牌上会有彩色证件照和探访者的姓名。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"◆让当地人敲开自己街区的门"},{"lang":"en","text":"The easiest way to do door-knocking is to try your local area first. Being a neighbor creates an immediate connection with the person answering the door; after that, everything else is easy. But those who try it for the first time are usually surprised by the pleasant reception they receive."},{"lang":"zh","text":"上门探访最容易的还是先从自己所在的社区开始。作为邻居能即刻与开门的人产生联结感，之后其他事情都好办了."},{"lang":"zh","text":"◆找个上门探访的好理由"},{"lang":"en","text":"A short survey about local concerns or a current project is a good excuse. Figure out responses for various situations. What if the person who answers the door cannot speak English? What if a child answers the door?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"做个关于社区关注问题或流行项目的简短调查是个好理由。要做好应对不同情况的准备：应门的人不会说英语怎么办？要是应门的是个孩子呢？"},{"lang":"zh","text":"WHEN YOU GO OUT当你出动时"},{"lang":"zh","text":"◆选好时机和要做的事"},{"lang":"en","text":"The best times to knock are usually Saturdays. On other days, after dinner is ideal. When someone answers the door, smile and introduce yourself; say you are a volunteer and, if it helps, state where you live. Give the name of your organization and, briefly, the reason for the visit."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最好的敲门时间通常是星期六。其他日子里，晚饭后的时间最理想。当有人应门时，微笑并且介绍自己，然后说明你是一个志愿者，如果有用的话，说出你所居住的地方，介绍你的组织名称，并且简要地说明来意。"},{"lang":"en","text":"◆ State what action the other person should take and the benefits"},{"lang":"zh","text":"说明他人需要采取的行动和可以获得的利益"},{"lang":"en","text":"Tell the person what they need to do and how their actions will benefit themselves and others. If a person hesitates , emphasize benefits you've already mentioned and then, if necessary, add further benefits. If a person agrees, follow up immediately. If possible, get a donation , a signature , or a promise."},{"lang":"zh","text":"告诉他人他们需要做什么，他们的所作所为会给自己和别人带来什么好处。如果对方犹豫了，就再次强调你所提到的利益，必要时可以补充说明长远利益。如果对方同意了，就立即进行下一步。如果可能，就争取获得捐款、签名或者承诺。"},{"lang":"en","text":"◆现场记下联系方式 Record names, addresses, e-mail addresses, phone numbers, and responses to questions on the spot. You won't remember them later!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"当场记下对方姓名、地址、电子邮箱、电话号码，问题答案等。否则过一会儿你就忘记了！"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":350},{"id":"r-管理英语3-6-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Community Service","subtitle":"社区服务","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Community service is a service or activity which is performed by someone or a group of people for the benefit of the public or public organizations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"社区服务是由个人或者群体为了社会或者社会组织的利益而进行的服务或者活动。"},{"lang":"en","text":"While volunteers may provide community service, not everyone taking part in a community service program is a volunteer, because not everyone is doing it through their own choice. Sometimes people are asked to do it by:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"虽然志愿者会提供社区服务，但并不是每一位参与社区服务的人都是志愿者，因为有些人并不是自愿的，他们会被以下机构要求做社区服务"},{"lang":"en","text":"• their government, as part of a citizenship requirement instead of military service;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"政府；代替服兵役，尽到公民的义务；"},{"lang":"en","text":"• the courts and other criminal justice punishments;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"法庭；作为刑事处罚；"},{"lang":"en","text":"• their school, to meet the requirements of a class, or to meet the requirements of graduation, or, in the case of parents, required to provide a certain number of hours of service in order for their child to be enrolled in a school or sports team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"学校；为了达到学业或者毕业要求，还有在为了让孩子能被学校或者运动队录取的情况下，家长也会被要求完成数小时的服务。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are also people providing community service, but they receive some form of payment in return for their work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"还有些提供社区服务的人会得到某种形式的报酬。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Youth community service 青年社区服务"},{"lang":"en","text":"Community service performed by young people, also known as youth service, is intended to strengthen young peoples' senses of civic engagement and community, and to help them achieve their educational, developmental and social goals."},{"lang":"zh","text":"由年轻人完成的社区服务，也就是青年服务，旨在增强年轻人的公民参与意识与社区参与感，同时也帮助他们实现接受教育、自我发展和参与社会活动等目标"},{"lang":"en","text":"High school graduation 高中毕业"},{"lang":"en","text":"Many educational institutions in the United States require students to perform community service hours to graduate from high school. In some high schools in Washington State, for example, students must complete 60 hours of community service to receive a diploma"},{"lang":"zh","text":"在美国，很多教育机构要求学生高中毕业前要达到一定的社区服务时数。比如，在华盛顿州的某些高中，学生在取得毕业证前必须完成60小时的社区服务。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Conditions of participation 参与条件"},{"lang":"en","text":"Contribution of service is a condition of enrollment in some programs. Most commonly, parents may be required to serve for their child to be enrolled in a school or sports team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"奉献服务是有些项目的录取条件之一。通常，为了孩子能被某所学校或某个运动队录取，家长可能会被要求进行社区服务。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"Colleges高等院校"},{"lang":"en","text":"Though technically not a requirement, many colleges make community service an unofficial requirement for acceptance . However, some colleges prefer work experience over communityservice, and some require that their students also participate in community service in order to graduate."},{"lang":"zh","text":"虽然严格来说，社区服务不是所招学生的必备条件，但是很多院校将它视为非官方的录取要求。然而，有的院校更看重学生的工作经验而不是社区服务，有的院校则要求学生参与社区服务才能毕业。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":297},{"id":"r-管理英语3-7-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Notable Quality Management Failures","subtitle":"著名质量管理失误案例","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A Quality Management System (QMS) should clearly understand customer's requirements, and to provide good design, qualified production in an effective and efficient way."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一个质量管理体系应该以有效和高效的方式清楚地了解客户的需求，并提供设计优良和合格的产品。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When the quality management system fails to fulfil its function and customer requirements are not met, customers might be upset; management and employees both might be unhappy, but its negative influence is not so wide-spread. Unluckily, some quality management system failures do make headlines."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当某个质量管理体系不能实现其功能和未满足客户需求时，顾客可能会生气；管理层和员工都可能不满意，但其负面影响并没有那么广泛地传播。不幸的是，一些质量管理系统的失败确实成了头条新闻。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Here are three cases of famous quality management failures:"},{"lang":"en","text":"3 Mile Island"},{"lang":"en","text":"The worst nuclear disaster in US history broke out at the 3 Mile Island reactor facility in eastern Pennsylvania in March 1979. Proper controls that should have been developed as part of routine safety procedures were not in place. Then the situation was made worse by human error because of the lack of proper training. The only new nuclear power stations built since that day were the ones already under construction."},{"lang":"zh","text":"1979年3月，美国历史上最严重的核灾难在宾夕法尼亚东部的三哩岛核电厂反应堆爆发。本该制定的作为部分日常安全程序的正确管控措施没有到位。由于缺乏正确的培训，事故状况被人为的错误弄得更糟。事故之后新建的核电站都是当时已经开工建设的核电站。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ford Pinto"},{"lang":"en","text":"The Ford Pinto is the most well-known and the worst disaster in the whole US automobile idustry in the 1970s. Apparently the entire US auto industry decided to spend the 1970s resting on their laurels after building great cars that sold well during the sixties. Not only were many cars built in the 1970s ugly and poorly designed, they also became very unreliable after 40- 50 thousand miles. The Pinto tops the list of QMS failures because of its dangerous design faults and the Questionable ethical decisions made by top management."},{"lang":"zh","text":"福特平托是1970年代整个美国汽车工业最出名和最严重的灾难。很显然，在六十年代制造出质量过硬且销售良好的汽车后，七十年代美国整个汽车工业打定了主意吃老本了。七十年代制造的很多汽车不仅外观设计难看，性能也较差，而且这些汽车在行驶了四、五万英里后性能还会变得相当不稳定。由于它危险的设计缺陷，以及最高管理层令人质疑的道德决策，平托事件名列质量管理体系失误案例的榜首。"},{"lang":"en","text":"iPhone 4"},{"lang":"en","text":"Apple almost lost its dominance in the smart phone market when it became clear that it was difficult to make a call using the much expected iPhone 4. Calls were dropped suddenly and frequently causing wide spread dissatisfaction among loyal customers who had upgraded to the new model early on. Independent tests showed that touching the left side of the case at a certain spot interrupted the signal and dropped the call — not a great feature for a handheld device mainly used to make calls. Meanwhile Apple continued to deny or minimize the problem. As the problem continued to make news headlines, Apple eventually agreed to a “voluntary” recall to correct the problem."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当发现使用期待已久的iPhone 4打电话是那么困难时，苹果几乎失去了在智能手机市场的主导地位。通话会频繁地突然断掉，造成了刚刚升级到新款手机的忠实客户们的广泛不满情绪。独立检测显示触碰话机左侧一个特定的点会中断电话信号并挂断电话——对于一个主要用于打电话的手持设备来说并不是一个优点。与此同时苹果公司不断否认或者淡化这个问题。由于这个问题连续成为新闻头条，苹果公司终于同意“自愿”召回并维修问题手机。"},{"lang":"en","text":"All of the above famous quality management failures could probably have been prevented if the principles of a fully functioning quality management system had been in place."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果一套功能完备的质量管理体系的各项准则都落实到位，那么上述这些耸人听闻的质量管理事故就不会发生。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":380},{"id":"r-管理英语3-7-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"The History of Quality Control","subtitle":"质量控制的历史","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Quality control is a series of activities that ensure and improve the quality of products and services."},{"lang":"zh","text":"质量控制是一系列确保和提高产品质量及服务的行为。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If strong leadership is the term for managers in a quality environment, then empowerment is the key concept for workers in Deming's system. Improved education and training are key factors in reaching employees and making them believe that their increased participation in the work process is an essential part of improving quality. Involvement participation, and teamwork are seen as absolute “must haves” if a quality workplace is to be created."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果在质量语境中强有力的领导是对经理们来说重要的字眼,那么在戴明的体系中赋权就是对员工来说最核心的概念。不断升级的教育与培训是凝聚员工的关键因素，可以使使员工们坚信自己的积极参与是提高产品质量的重要环节。如果要创造高质量的工作环境，员工介入、员工参与、以及团队合作是绝对的“必要条件”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another important principle of Deming's beliefs was that upper management should be responsible for quality failures. He strongly believed that it was possible for the workers to work hard to produce the highest quality products if they were given the right tools and working environment. In Deming's own words, “ the basic cause of sickness in American industry and the resulting unemployment is a failure of top management to manage.” He believed that strong leadership led to a motivated work force."},{"lang":"zh","text":"另一个戴明理论中的重要原则是高层管理应该对质量失误负责。他深信工人们如果拥有恰当的工具和工作环境，他们能够努力工作制造出高质量的产品。用戴明的原话来说就是“导致美国工业弊病以及由此带来的失业的首要原因是顶层管理的失败”。他坚信强有力的领导会形成有活力的工作团队。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The Japanese were the first to use Deming's Fourteen Points, and made great success. As an example, one Japanese factory doubled production in just one year and was expecting to gain an additional 25 percent improvement the following year, with no increase in the amount of working hours. All this happened as a result of simply improving quality. It was in the late 1970s that American manufacturing factories realized that quality control was a significant issue. By that time, Japanese firms such as Honda and Sony were taking over large portions of the American consumer market while it took most American firms until the 1990s to put quality control practices in place."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最早实践戴明十四要点的是日本人，并且他们取得了巨大的成功。举一个例子，一个日本工厂在一年内将产量翻了一番，并且下一年在不增加工作时间的情况下将获得额外25%的产能增加。所有这些得以实现不过是由于提高了质量而已。1970年代晚期美国的制造业工厂才意识到质量控制是一个重大问题。在那时，像本田和索尼这样的日本公司已经占领了大部分的美国消费者市场，而大多数美国公司直到1990年代才开始实行质量控制。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The term “quality control” came into common use in the 1950s because of W. Edward Deming. His “Fourteen Points” have become the bible for quality control specialists. When the post-war world returned to regular manufacturing , Deming said that inspecting product quality after they were made was unacceptable .Instead, he proposed a process known as “ statistical quality control”. It would use closely monitored performance measures to control quality while a product was being made. The goal of statistical quality control was to gather data that would allow for the constant improvement of manufacturing processes. This would in turn improve quality control."},{"lang":"zh","text":"由于威廉·爱德华兹·戴明，“质量控制”这个术语在1950年代开始广泛使用。他的“十四要点”已经成为了质量控制专业人士的宝典。当战后世界恢复正常生产时，戴明提出在制造完成后再检查产品质量是不可接受的。相反，他提出了被称为“统计质量管理”的一个流程。它会在产品生产过程中严密监控绩效指标从而控制质量。统计质量控制的目标在于收集数据以利于不断地改进制造工艺。这将反过来提高质量控制。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":379},{"id":"r-管理英语3-8-1","book":"管理英语3","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Ebola Surge","subtitle":"埃博拉袭来——2014","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The 2014 Ebola outbreak is the largest in history and the first Ebola outbreak in West Africa. Although the current epidemic does not cause a significant risk to other nations, many countries, including China and the United States of America, have actually been working closely with the Ebola hit states. For example, the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) is taking precautions at home besides its activities abroad."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2014年埃博拉疫情的爆发是历史上规模最大的一次，也是埃博拉在西非的第一次爆发。尽管目前疫情仍未对其他国家带来很大的风险，但是包括中国和美国在内的许多国家，已与遭受埃博拉病毒袭击的国家切实开展了密切合作。例如，美国疾病预防控制中心（以下简称“疾控中心”）不仅在国外采取行动，在国内也是如此。"},{"lang":"en","text":"CDC's team of “ virus hunters” is supported by Specialized public health teams both in West Africa and at the CDC Atlanta headquarters. Together, they offer continuous support to save lives and protect people. CDC works closely with a number of US government agencies, national and international partners. CDC's experience of working with Ebola is important to the World Health Organization's growing West Africa Ebola response ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"疾控中心的“病毒猎人”小组受到了在西非和疾控中心亚特兰大总部的专业公共健康团队的支持。他们一起为挽救生命与保护民众提供持续不断的援助。疾控中心与许多美国政府机构与国内外伙伴密切合作。美国疾病预防控制中心应对埃博拉的经验对世界卫生组织在西非地区日益展开的抗击埃博拉疫情而言至关重要。"},{"lang":"en","text":"On Sept. 2, 2014, CDC Director, Tom Frieden called for more international partners to join this effort. “The sooner the world comes together to help West Africa, the safer we all will be. We know how to stop this outbreak. There is a window of opportunity to do so — the challenge is to scale up the massive response needed to stop this outbreak.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"2014年9月2日，疾控中心主任汤姆.弗利登倡议更多国际伙伴加入这次行动。“世界越早团结一致帮助西非，我们就越安全。我们知道如何阻止这次爆发。现在已经打开了这样做的机遇之窗，而挑战在于大幅扩大应急响应规模以阻止疫情。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"CDC's response to Ebola is the largest international outbreak response in CDC's history with over 100 disease specialists on the ground in West Africa, supported by hundreds of public health emergency response experts stateside ，activated at Level 1, its highest level, because of the significance of this outbreak."},{"lang":"zh","text":"美国疾病预防控制中心对埃博拉疫情采取的应对是其历史上规模最大的国际疫情爆发响应，超过100名疾病专家在西非进行实地工作，数百名突发公共卫生事件应对专家在美国本土后援支持。因为疫情爆发的影响力，应急响应为最高级别——一级。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The CDC supports affected countries to establish Emergency Operations Centers at national and local levels and helps countries"},{"lang":"en","text":"track the epidemic including using real-time data to improve real-time response."},{"lang":"zh","text":"疾病预防控制中心支持疫情蔓延的国家建立国家级与地方级的紧急行动中心，运用实时数据以提高实时应急能力，帮助这些国家监控疫情。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Efforts in West Africa to identify those infected and track people who have come into contact with them are improving. The CDC is operating and supporting labs in the region to improve diagnosis and testing samples from people with suspected Ebola from around the world."},{"lang":"zh","text":"西非在确认感染人群和追踪与他们有过接触人群方面的努力成果正在彰显。美国疾病预防控制中心在这些地区运行并支持实验室加强诊断能力，检测全球携带疑似埃博拉病毒人群样本。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Local health care systems are strengthened through communication,"},{"lang":"en","text":"coordination with partners and training on infection control for health care workers and safe patient treatment."},{"lang":"zh","text":"地方医护体系通过与合作方进行沟通与协作，以及培训卫生工作者的感染控制能力与安全病患治疗技术，得到进一步加强。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":341},{"id":"r-管理英语3-8-2","book":"管理英语3","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"How to Prepare an Emergency Response Plan for Your Workplace","subtitle":"如何在您的工作场所准备应急预案","paragraphs":[{"lang":"zh","text":"1.指定应急计划的必要性"},{"lang":"en","text":"Emergencies and disasters can occur any time without warning. The more you are prepared for them, the better you will be able to act, reducing panic and confusion when an emergency occurs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"紧急事件与灾难随时会在没有预警的情况下发生。准备越充分，应对就越自如，事件突发时的恐慌与混乱也会随之减少。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Emergency response plans (ERPs) are intended to provide clear and effective steps for managing an emergency. An ERP should deal with a variety of issues including evacuation of buildings, communication with local emergency services and the general public, individual roles and responsibilities during an emergency, and supplies and materials that may be needed."},{"lang":"zh","text":"应急响应预案将为突发事件的处理提供清晰有效的应对步骤。一套完善的应急预案应该能够应对各种各样情况，包括楼房疏散，与本地应急服务机构和大众的沟通，紧急情况中个人的角色和责任，以及应急所需补给与物资等。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Follow these basic guidelines to develop an effective ERP for your workplace:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"在为您的工作场所制定有效的应急预案时，请遵照以下的基本指导原则"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Determine when an evacuation would be necessary."},{"lang":"zh","text":"决定何时进行必要的人群疏散。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"2.指定应急撤退线路，并进行明确表示。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Choose primary and secondary evacuation routes and emergency exits. Make sure they are clearly marked and well lit. Post signs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"选择首选和备用的疏散路线与紧急出口。保证它们指示清晰，照明良好。贴上"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Install emergency lighting in case a power cut occurs during an evacuation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"安装应急照明系统以防在疏散过程中出现断电情况。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"3.保持应急通道宽敞、畅通，避免次生灾害。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Ensure that evacuation routes and emergency exits are wide enough for people to be evacuated, clear at all times, and unlikely to expose evacuating people to additional hazards."},{"lang":"zh","text":"确保疏散路线和紧急出口足够宽敞并随时保持通畅，避免将疏散人群置于其他危险境况。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Coordinate your plan with the local emergency management office."},{"lang":"zh","text":"与当地应急管理部门一起协调你们的预案。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Choose “evacuation wardens ” who will help others during an evacuation and account for employees."},{"lang":"zh","text":"挑选“疏散监管人员”，在紧急疏散中帮助他人并对员工的安全负责。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"4.指定具体应急步骤"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Establish specific evacuation procedures. This includes a sample ERP to give you a better idea of what your procedures should include."},{"lang":"zh","text":"颁布具体的疏散程序，这里有一个应急预案样本能给你更清晰的思路，让你知道应该有哪些步骤。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Establish a system for accounting for evacuated employees."},{"lang":"zh","text":"建立一套确保员工疏散安全的体系。"},{"lang":"zh","text":"5.进行应急预演"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Hold emergency drills at least once a year to ensure that employees know what to do in an emergency and to test the effectiveness of emergency exit routes and procedures. Keep records of such drills."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一年至少举行一次应急演练，以确保员工们清楚在紧急情况下要如何行动，同时检验应急出口通道以及相关程序的有效性。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Consider the transportation needs of employees."},{"lang":"zh","text":"考虑员工的交通需求。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Post evacuation procedures where employees can read them."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在员工可以阅读的地方粘贴疏散程序。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Establish procedures for helping people with disabilities and people who do not speak your local language."},{"lang":"zh","text":"制定帮助残疾人与不使用当地语言的员工的相关程序。"},{"lang":"en","text":"•Consider how you could quickly get important personal information about employees in an emergency (for example, contact numbers for their home, next-of-kin , or special medical conditions)."},{"lang":"zh","text":"考虑你如何才能快速收集到在应急中需要的员工个人信息（比如，家庭联系电话号码，近亲情况，或者特殊的病史等）。"}],"source":"管理英语3（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":309},{"id":"r-管理英语4-1-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":1,"reading":1,"title":"Five Basic Functions That Make up the Management Process","subtitle":"构成管理过程的五个基本功能","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In 1916, a French coal mine director named Henri Fayol wrote a book entitled Administration Industrielle et Generale, which set forth five distinct functions of managing that Fayol insisted were applicable in any industry."},{"lang":"en","text":"In the 1950's, management textbooks began to incorporate some of Fayol's ideas into their content, and today, management courses still use many of his ideas to teach management to business students."},{"lang":"zh","text":"1916年，法国煤矿公司总经理亨利·法约尔写了一本名为《工业管理与一般管理》的书，书中提出了五种独特的管理职能，并强调这些管理职能适用于任何行业。20世纪50年代，管理学教科书开始编入法约尔的理念，时至今日，管理学课程依然向商科学生传授他的思想。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Planning"},{"lang":"zh","text":"规划"},{"lang":"en","text":"Planning involves deciding where to take a company and selecting steps to get there."},{"lang":"en","text":"It first requires managers to be aware of challenges facing their businesses, and then it requires managers to forecast future business and economic conditions. They then formulate objectives to reach by certain deadlines and decide on steps to reach them. They re-evaluate their plans as conditions change and make adjustments as necessary."},{"lang":"zh","text":"规划包括确定公司的发展方向，并选择实现目标的各个步骤。首先它要求管理者意识到企业面临的挑战，然后要求管理者预测未来的业务和经济状况。接着，他们制定在一定期限前要达到的目标，并决定实现它们的步骤。随着情况的变化，他们重新评估他们的计划，必要时进行调整。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Organizing"},{"lang":"zh","text":"组织"},{"lang":"en","text":"Managers organize by bringing together physical , human and financial resources to achieve objectives. They identify activities to be accomplished, classify activities, assign activities to groups or individuals, create responsibilities and delegate authority. They then coordinate everything so operations run smoothly."},{"lang":"zh","text":"管理者集中物力、人力和财力，建立组织来实现目标。他们确定要完成的活动、进行活动分类、将活动分配给团体或个人、明确责任和分配权力。然后他们协调一切，保证项目顺利运行。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Leading"},{"lang":"zh","text":"领导"},{"lang":"en","text":"Leading requires managers to motivate employees to achieve business objectives and goals. It requires the use of authority to achieve those ends as well as the ability to communicate effectively. Effective leaders can influence their personnel to view situations from their perspectives . Leading also involves supervision of employees and their work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"领导要求管理者激励员工去实现业务的大小目标。这些目标的实现既需要权力的运用也需要有效沟通的能力。有效率的领导者可以从员工的角度看待问题，从而对他们产生影响力。领导还包括对员工及其工作进行监督。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Controlling"},{"lang":"zh","text":"控制"},{"lang":"en","text":"Controlling involves measuring achievement against established objectives and goals. It also requires managers to be able to identify sources of deviation from successful accomplishment and to provide a corrective course of action."},{"lang":"en","text":"Managers first establish objectives and goals, then measure achievements, identify anything that is keeping the company from achieving their objectives and goals, and provide means of correction if necessary."},{"lang":"zh","text":"控制涉及根据既定目标来衡量成果。它还要求管理者明确偏离成功目标的根源，并采取纠正措施。管理者首先确定大小目标，然后衡量成果，确定会使公司不能实现其目标的任何事项，并在必要时提供纠正方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Staffing"},{"lang":"zh","text":"人员配备"},{"lang":"en","text":"Without human resources, no organization can get off the ground , let alone do business and make profits."},{"lang":"en","text":"Some distinct features of the staffing function are:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"没有人力资源，任何公司都不能顺利起步，更别说经营获利了。人员配备功能的一些明显特点是："},{"lang":"en","text":"• It puts the right man in the right job."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 把正确的人放在正确的工作岗位上。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• It is an ongoing activity. As employees keep leaving and joining the company, they also retire from time to time leaving empty places in various positions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 这是一个持续的活动，因为随时有员工进出公司，也不时有员工退休，一些岗位会出现缺员现象。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Efficiency is a prime focus of this function. As managing people is the toughest job, everything must be accounted for , leaves, payments, benefits, medical allowances , social security accounting and much more."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 效率是此功能的重中之重，因为做管理是一份艰巨的工作，事事都需要有人负责，如请假、工资、福利、医疗津贴、社会保险等等。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":379},{"id":"r-管理英语4-1-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":1,"reading":2,"title":"Who Killed Nokia?","subtitle":"","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Nokia executives attempted to explain its fall from the top of the smartphone pyramid with three factors: 1) that Nokia was technically inferior to Apple, 2) that the company was complacent and 3) that its leaders didn't see the disruptive iPhone coming."},{"lang":"zh","text":"诺基亚的执行官们试图用三个因素解释诺基亚为何从智能手机的金字塔顶端跌落至谷底：1）诺基亚的技术比苹果公司逊色；2）诺基亚公司自以为是；3）诺基亚的领导者没能预见苹果手机的入市会给他们带来毁灭性的冲击。"},{"lang":"en","text":"It has also been argued that it was none of the above. Nokia lost the smartphone battle because of divergent shared fears among the company's middle and top managers which led to company-wide inertia that left it powerless to respond to Apple's game."},{"lang":"zh","text":"也有人认为不是上述原因。诺基亚输掉智能手机战，完全是因为公司里中高层管理者中普遍存在的不同的恐惧，它导致全公司的不作为，致使诺基亚在与苹果的较量中无力回击。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Based on the findings of an in-depth investigation and 76 interviews with top and middle managers, engineers and external experts, the researchers discovered a culture of fear due to temperamental leaders and that frightened middle managers were scared of telling the truth."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据深入的调查结果和对76名中高层管理人员、工程师和外部专家的采访，研究人员发现了易怒的领导者引起了恐惧文化，使中层管理人员害怕说实话。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The fear that froze the company came from two places. First, the company's top managers had a terrifying reputation. Some members of Nokia's board and top management were described as “extremely temperamental and they regularly shouted at people “at the top of their lungs”. It was very difficult to tell them things they didn't want to hear. Second, top managers were afraid of the external environment and not meeting their quarterly targets, which also impacted how they treated middle managers."},{"lang":"zh","text":"僵化公司里的恐惧来自两个地方。首先，公司的高层管理人员有着骇人的声誉。诺基亚董事会和高层管理人员的一些成员被描述为“暴脾气”，他们经常“顶着肺”地朝人喊叫。告诉他们那些他们不想听的东西是非常困难的。其次，高层管理人员恐惧外部环境，也担心达不到季度目标，这也影响了他们对待中层管理人员的方式。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Top managers thus made middle managers afraid of disappointing them. Middle managers were told that they were not ambitious enough to meet top managers' goals."},{"lang":"zh","text":"因此，高层管理人员使得中层管理人员害怕令他们失望。中层管理人员被告知，他们没有足够的壮志雄心去达成高层管理人员的目标。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Fearing the reactions of top managers, middle managers remained silent or provided optimistic, filtered information."},{"lang":"en","text":"Thus, middle managers directly lied to top management."},{"lang":"zh","text":"中层管理人员害怕刺激高层管理人员，只好保持沉默，或者报喜不报忧。"},{"lang":"en","text":"What was worse, a culture of status inside Nokia made everyone want to hold onto inside Nokia made everyone want to vested power for fear of resources being allocated elsewhere if they delivered bad news or showed that they were not bold or ambitious enough to undertake challenging assignments."},{"lang":"zh","text":"更糟糕的是，诺基亚内部的等级观念致使每个人都想守住既得利益，害怕如果自己传达了坏消息，或者表现出不够勇敢或缺乏雄心壮志去承担挑战性的任务，那么自己手中的资源就会被分配到其他地方。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Beyond verbal pressure, top managers also applied pressure for faster performance in personnel selection. This led middle managers to over promise and under deliver. One middle manager told us that “you can get resources by promising something earlier, or promising a lot. It's sales work”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"除了言语压力之外，高层管理人员在人事选择方面，通过施加压力来更快地见到成效。。这导致了中层管理者过度承诺和行动不足。一位中层管理人员告诉我们：“你可以通过早做承诺或者夸下海口来获得资源。这是销售工作。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"While modest fear might be healthy for motivation, abusing it can be like overusing a drug, which risks generating harmful side effects ."},{"lang":"en","text":"To reduce this risk, leaders should coordinate with the varied emotions of the staff. Nokia's top managers should have encouraged safe dialog, Internal coordination and feedback to understand the true emotion in the organization."},{"lang":"zh","text":"虽然适度的畏惧有益于内部激励，但是，对其滥用就像用药过度一样，会有产生有害的副作用的风险。为了减少这种风险，领导应该协调工作人员的不同情绪。诺基亚的高层管理人员应该鼓励安全对话、内部协调和反馈，以了解组织中的真实情感。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":403},{"id":"r-管理英语4-2-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":2,"reading":1,"title":"Habits of Highly Effective Communicators","subtitle":"善于沟通者的习惯","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"It's no secret that good leaders are also good communicators. Indeed, communication and leadership are inextricably tied. How can you inspire or guide others if you don't communicate in a clear, credible and authentic way? Here are 5 essential communication practices of effective leaders:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"优秀的领导者总是善于沟通，这并不是什么秘密。确实，沟通力和领导力总是形影不离。如果你不能用清楚、可信、可靠的方式来进行交流，你如何激励和领导其他人？下面是出色的领导者必做的五件事："},{"lang":"en","text":"1. Mind the say-do gap"},{"lang":"zh","text":"1. 注意说和做之间的差距"},{"lang":"en","text":"Trust is the bedrock of effective leadership – your behavior is your single greatest mode of communication, and it must be congruent with what you say."},{"lang":"en","text":"If your actions don't align with your words, you are storing up trouble for the future."},{"lang":"zh","text":"信任是有效领导的基石，你的行为是你唯一的最佳沟通方式，它必须与要表达的内容一致。如果你言行不一，你是在为将来埋藏隐患。"},{"lang":"en","text":"2. Make the complex simple"},{"lang":"zh","text":"2. 让复杂的事情变得简单"},{"lang":"en","text":"Effective leaders distill complex thoughts and strategies into simple, memorable terms that colleagues and customers can grasp and act upon."},{"lang":"en","text":"he most important thing is to clarify what you want to say, look out for technical jargon and avoid business speak, which add complexity. Say what you mean in as few words as possible."},{"lang":"zh","text":"善于沟通的领导者能够把复杂的思想和策略提炼成简单易记的语句，便于同事和顾客领会执行。最重要的是把你想说的东西说清楚，谨慎使用技术行话、避免打官腔，那只会增加事情的复杂性。把你要表达的用最精简的语句说出来。"},{"lang":"en","text":"3. Find your own voice"},{"lang":"zh","text":"3. 找到自己的语言"},{"lang":"en","text":"Use language that's distinctly your own; let your values come through in your communication. Correct use of language and grammar is important, of course, but don't become overly fixated on eloquence for eloquence's sake; concentrate on being distinct and real."},{"lang":"en","text":"People want real, people respect real, people follow real."},{"lang":"zh","text":"运用自己特色鲜明的语言，通过交流传递价值观。正确运用语言和语法当然很重要，但是，不要过于执着于口才至上，而要将精力集中在鲜明的特色和事实真相方面。人们渴望真实，人们尊重真实，人们追随真实。"},{"lang":"en","text":"4. Be visible"},{"lang":"zh","text":"4. 让别人看见自己"},{"lang":"en","text":"Visibility is about letting your key stakeholders get a feel for who you are and what you care about. Don't hide behind a computer and only interact with people electronically – see them face to face and voice to voice, and interact with them in a real, substantial way. In today's environment, where people are often burned out, it's important for employees to have a personal connection with you and the work you believe in."},{"lang":"en","text":"Show the people who work for you that you're engaged and you care about them and their work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"让别人注意到你的存在是让你的重要利害关系人对你是谁和你关心什么有所感受。切忌躲在电脑背后，只通过电子方式跟人交流；要面对面互相倾听，进行大量切实的互动。在如今的工作环境中，人们常常精疲力竭，让雇员与你及你所倚重的工作建立起切身的联系尤为重要。让那些为你工作的人看到你的投入、你对他们和他们工作的关心。"},{"lang":"en","text":"5. Listen with your eyes as well as your ears"},{"lang":"zh","text":"5. 用你的眼睛和耳朵一起倾听"},{"lang":"en","text":"Effective communication is a two-way process, and good leaders know how to ask good questions, and then listen with both their eyes and their ears. Because you are in a position of authority, others may be reluctant to express their real opinions to you directly. You won't always get direct feedback, so you also need to be able to read between the lines and look for the non-verbal cues."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有效的沟通是一个双向过程，优秀的领导者知道如何提出有价值的问题，然后用他们的眼睛和耳朵一起倾听。因为你处在权力位置上，其他人可能不愿意把他们真实的想法直接告诉你。你不会总是得到直接的反馈，所以你需要能够体会言外之意，同时发现一些非言语的暗示。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":374},{"id":"r-管理英语4-2-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":2,"reading":2,"title":"Communication Failure","subtitle":"沟通失败","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"The meaning of “communication” goes a lot deeper than people often think. Communication is about conceiving, sending, receiving, and interpreting messages as well as confirming reception of these messages. A failure at any point in this chain can result in ineffective communication."},{"lang":"zh","text":"沟通的含义比人们通常理解的要更深刻。沟通是关于信息的构思、传输、接收和理解，以及确认这些信息的送达。在这个链条上的任何一个环节出现失误都会导致沟通无效。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ineffective communication can be disastrous. There is a famous story of a British Army Commander who sent the message “Send reinforcements, we're going to advance. ” back to his Command Center, through a long chain of subordinates. When the message finally reached the Command Center, it had become “Send three and four-pence, we're going to a dance. ”"},{"lang":"en","text":"The reinforcements never arrived."},{"lang":"zh","text":"无效沟通可能带来严重的损失。有个很著名的关于一位英国陆军司令的故事，他通过多级下属向他的指挥中心发出消息“请派援军，我们的部队要往前推进”。当这条消息最终传到指挥中心的时候，变成了“送三四便士来，我们要去跳舞”。援军始终没有到达。"},{"lang":"en","text":"You can demonstrate this same principle, albeit on a less dramatic scale, by trying to play Chinese Whispers with more than 20 people."},{"lang":"en","text":"It is highly unlikely the same message you started with will be the one you end with."},{"lang":"zh","text":"通过和20多人玩中国耳语游戏，你可以证明同样的道理，尽管后果没有那么严重。游戏开始时传递的信息几乎不可能和游戏结束时得到的信息相同。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In a business, there are three main types of communication failure. Each has its own indicative signs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在商业活动中，有三类主要的沟通失败。每一类都有独特的指示标志。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The first type is known as allocative failure. This occurs when a firm is not gathering enough intelligence about its market or (most often), the information is not reaching the right points. The firm will not be allocating resources in step with the shifts in demand."},{"lang":"en","text":"If demand is rising but the firm is suffering from allocative communication failure, then stocks will fall and there will be understaffing. If the inverse happens, there will be a surplus of stocks and overstaffing."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第一类被称作资源配置失败。当一个公司没有得到足够的市场情报（大多数情况下是这样），或者这些情报没有被送到正确的地方时，这种失败就会发生。公司在配置资源时，跟不上需求的变化。如果需求持续增加而公司正经历资源配置沟通方面的失误，那么库存将下降并且出现人手不足的状况。如果相反的情况发生，将会出现库存增加和人员过剩的情况。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The second type is executive failure, where communication to trigger specific events/actions is either late, lacking or in error."},{"lang":"en","text":"The symptoms of this are a general loss of direction in the company or departments, a loss of co-ordination and an increase in complaints from customers as things happen late or not at all."},{"lang":"zh","text":"第二种类型是执行层面的失败。这种失败是指激励具体事项或行动的沟通要么来得太迟，要么缺失，要么是错误的。出现这类失败的情形表现为，公司或多个部门普遍失去了发展方向和缺少合作，由于反应迟缓或完全没有反应，造成越来越多的客户投诉。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The final type is human failure. This occurs when the general culture of a business or the relationships between particular individuals or departments do not foster effective communication. This leads to alienated staff, an increase in staff turnover, an increase in absenteeism and general frustration among staff."},{"lang":"en","text":"Creativity, especially that which takes place across departmental boundaries, is likely to suffer hugely as team synergy slips."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最后一种类型是人事层面的失败。当一个企业的总体文化，或是特定个人或部门之间的关系不能增进有效沟通的时候，这种失败就会发生。这会导致员工离心离德，增加员工更替率，助长旷工现象，也会在员工中造成普遍的挫败感。创造力，尤其是跨越部门界限体现出的创造力，可能由于团队协作能力的下降而受到很大冲击。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":360},{"id":"r-管理英语4-3-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":3,"reading":1,"title":"A Teamwork Game","subtitle":"团队游戏","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A team of about 35 employees had come together for a team building event. They were a young, bright and enthusiastic team. However, one of their chief problems was the fact that they wouldn't share information or solutions with each other, and the team leader thought they were too focused on themselves and not on the team. As a result, she brought them all into the cafeteria. All of the tables and chairs had been stored away, and fun decorations and hundreds of different colored balloons had been placed around the room."},{"lang":"zh","text":"一个约35名员工的团队聚集在一起进行团队建设活动。他们是一个年轻、聪明和热情的团队。但是，他们的一个主要问题就是他们不会彼此分享信息或解决方案，团队领导也认为他们太关注自己，而不是整个团队。结果，她把他们全都带进了自助餐厅。所有的桌椅都被收了起来，房间内布满了有趣的装饰和数百个五颜六色的气球。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In the center of the room was a big box of balloons that hadn't been blown up yet."},{"lang":"en","text":"The team leader instructed everybody to pick a balloon, blow it up, and write their name on it, but they had to be careful not to burst the balloon. Although they were given a second chance if their first balloon popped , they were out of the game the second time round. In the end, about 30 team members wrote their names without their balloons popping. They were then asked to leave the room and, after five minutes, the team leader brought them back in and asked them to find the balloon with their name on it amongst the hundreds of other balloons in the room. After 15 minutes of searching, no one had found their balloon, and the team were told that they were then going to move on to the third round of the activity."},{"lang":"zh","text":"房子中间放着一大箱尚未充气的气球。队长指示大家挑一个气球，吹起来，写下他们的名字，但是他们必须小心，不要弄炸气球。尽管第一次他们的气球炸掉了，他们还有一次机会，但是如果他们的气球再爆掉，他们就得出局。最后，大约有30名队员写了他们的名字，气球也没有炸掉。随后，他们被要求离开房间，五分钟后，团队领导带他们回来，并要求他们在房间里的数百个气球中找到写着自己名字的气球。经过15分钟的寻找，没有人找到自己的气球，接下来团队被告知，他们将进入第三轮活动。"},{"lang":"en","text":"In this round, each team member was instructed to find any balloon with a name on it and then give that balloon to the person whose name was on it. Within two minutes, everybody had their own balloon. The team leader summarized the activity thus: “We are much more efficient when we are willing to share with each other and much better at problem solving when we are working together, not individually.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"在这轮中，每个队员被指示寻找任何一个写有名字的气球，然后把这个气球送给相应的人。两分钟后，每个人都拿到了自己的气球。团队领导这样总结活动的意义：“当我们愿意相互分享时，我们的工作效率会更高；当我们一起工作而不是单打独斗时，问题也会解决得更加顺利。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Sometimes, members of teams create obstacles by focusing solely on their own pursuits and goals."},{"lang":"en","text":"Every member of the team should ask themselves on a regular basis what they are doing and what they can do for the team."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有时，当团队成员只关注自己的追求与目标时，反而会给自己制造障碍。团队的每个成员都应该定期问自己在做什么，以及他们能为团队做些什么。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":354},{"id":"r-管理英语4-3-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":3,"reading":2,"title":"Tips for Team Building","subtitle":"团队建设的忠告","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"When you think of team building, do you immediately picture your group off at a resort playing games or hanging from ropes?"},{"lang":"en","text":"Traditionally, many organizations approach team building in this way but, then, they wonder why that wonderful sense of teamwork that had been displayed at the retreat or the seminar fails to impact long term beliefs and actions back at work."},{"lang":"zh","text":"想到团队建设，你是否会马上想到你的团体在度假场所玩游戏或者荡秋千的场景？很多机构通常用这种方式进行团队建设，但是，他们也在思考：为什么在度假胜地或者研讨会上展现出的良好的团队意识，在回到工作中之后就难以持续影响员工的信念与行动呢？"},{"lang":"en","text":"I'm not averse to retreats, planning sessions, seminars and team building activities — in fact I lead them — but they have to form part of a much larger teamwork effort. You will not build teamwork by “retreating” as a group for a couple of days each year, instead you need to think of team building as something you do every single day."},{"lang":"zh","text":"我不反对休养、规划会议、研讨会和团队建设活动——事实上，我牵头进行这些活动——但是它们必须成为一个更大的团队合作活动的一部分。团队建设不可能通过每年几天的“休养”达成，相反，你需要把团队建设当成每天的“必修课”。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Form teams to solve real work issues and to improve real work processes. Provide training in systematic methods so the team expends its energy on the project, not on trying to work out how to work together as a team to approach the problem."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·组建团队去解决真实的工作难题，推进工作进程。提供系统训练方法，让团队把精力花到项目上，而不是探索以团队的形式解决问题的方式方法本身。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Hold department meetings to review projects and progress, to obtain broad input, and to coordinate shared work processes. If there is friction between team members, examine the work processes they mutually own — the problem is not usually their personalities;"},{"lang":"en","text":"instead, it is often the fact that the team members haven't agreed on how they will deliver a product or service, or the steps required to get something done."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·召开部门会议审查项目进展情况，争取广泛投入，协调共同的工作流程。假如团队成员间出现了摩擦，就需要审视他们共享的工作程序，因为问题通常不源自他们的不同个性；然而，事实往往是，组员没有在如何提供产品或服务上达成共识，或者在完成任务所需步骤上意见不合。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Build fun and shared occasions into the organization's agenda — hold pot luck lunches, take the team to a sporting event, sponsor dinners at a local restaurant, go hiking or go to an amusement park."},{"lang":"en","text":"Hold a monthly company meeting, sponsor sports teams and encourage cheering team fans."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·公司日程中应有趣味活动、快乐分享等活动安排，如举行百乐午餐，带领团队参加运动会，在当地餐厅举办赞助晚餐，组织远足或者游园活动。举行每月一次的公司会议，赞助运动队，鼓励拉拉队的球迷。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Use ice breakers and teamwork exercises at meetings — these help team members get to know each other, share details about each others lives, and have a laugh together."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·在会议中开展破冰活动和团队练习——这些能帮助团队成员彼此认识，分享彼此的生活细节，共同欢笑。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Celebrate team successes publicly. There are many ways you could do this, for instance by buying everyone the same T-shirt or hat, putting team member names in a draw for company merchandise and gift certificate ."},{"lang":"en","text":"The only thing limiting you is your imagination."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·公开庆祝团队的成功。做这件事可以有很多方式，例如，给每人都买相同的T恤衫或者帽子，或者用团队成员姓名抽奖，赢取公司产品和礼券。限制你的唯一的东西就是你的想象力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"If you do the types of teamwork building listed above, you'll be amazed at the progress you will make in creating a teamwork culture,"},{"lang":"en","text":"a culture that enables individuals to contribute more than they ever thought possible — together."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果你按照上面列举的方式去建设团队，你会为你在构建团队文化中所取得的进步而感到震惊，这种文化能使个人做出多于过去的贡献。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":392},{"id":"r-管理英语4-4-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":4,"reading":1,"title":"How Google Continues to Keep Employees Happy","subtitle":"谷歌如何一直让员工开心","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Working for Google is a dream of many, not just because of what this company has achieved in the last 15 years, but because of its enviable work culture."},{"lang":"en","text":"With about 37,000 employees in 40 countries, you might wonder how Google maintains a motivating work experience throughout its entire company."},{"lang":"zh","text":"到谷歌工作是很多人的梦想，不仅仅是因为这个公司在过去15年所取得的成就，还因为那里有令人羡慕的企业文化。谷歌在40个国家拥有约3.7万名员工，您可能会想知道它如何在整个公司维持积极的工作体验。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Working for Google comes with perks that most other organizations can't provide — bowling alleys , free haircuts, gym memberships, and shuttles to and from work. The company's secret to success is putting the same amount of time and effort into keeping employees happy as it does into innovating products."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在谷歌工作有大多数其他机构不能提供的待遇——保龄球馆、免费理发、健身房会员和往返于公司的班车。谷歌公司成功的秘诀在于，在保持员工幸福感和产品创新方面，它投入了同样多的时间与精力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Back when the company was just a start-up , co-founders Larry Page and Sergey Brin had the goal of making Google a place the most talented people wanted to work at."},{"lang":"en","text":"Their idea was simple: creating a work culture that keeps employees happy, will motivate them to do their best, and will keep them loyal to the company."},{"lang":"zh","text":"公司刚创立的时候，共同创始人拉里·佩奇和赛吉·布林就设定了一个目标：要让谷歌成为最杰出的人才想为之效力的地方。他们的想法很简单：创造一种可以让员工保持快乐的工作文化，激励他们尽最大努力保持对公司的忠诚度。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“It's less about the aspiration to be No. 1 in the world, and more that we want our employees and future ones to love it here, because that's what's going to make us successful,” said Karen May, the Vice President of People Development at Google."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谷歌人力发展副总裁凯伦·梅说：“与其说我们想力争成为世界第一强，不如说我们想让我们现在和未来的员工都爱上这里。因为只有这样，才能使我们成功。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Google also makes its employees want to work because managers provide tasks that are inspiring and challenging. Every employee at Google has the opportunity to spend 20% of his or her working time on a project they choose."},{"lang":"en","text":"This freedom takes employees out of their routine and away from the mundane tasks that often make workers feel uninspired about their jobs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谷歌员工有热情，因为管理人员提供了令人振奋和充满挑战的任务。谷歌的每个员工都有机会把20%的工作时间花费到自选项目上。这样的自由可以使员工不用循规蹈矩，从单调乏味、毫无工作激情的任务中解脱出来。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Lastly, Google shows each employee just how important he or she is to the company. Each employee, regardless of his / her spot on the totem pole , has an influence on how Google performs."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最后，谷歌向每位员工表明，他（她）对公司很重要。每一个人，无论他（她）在什么岗位，都对谷歌的运营产生影响。"},{"lang":"en","text":"“If you value people, and care about them as whole people, one thing you do is give them a voice, and you really listen,” May said."},{"lang":"zh","text":"“如果你重视人才，把他们当作一个健全的人格来关心，你所要做的事就是给他们一个发声的机会，而你要认真地听”，梅说。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Google does just that by hosting employee forums every Friday, where they discuss the 20 most-asked questions."},{"lang":"en","text":"Employees have access to all company information, adding a sense of trust, and employees and leaders work together to solve problems."},{"lang":"zh","text":"谷歌是通过每周五都举办员工论坛做到这点的，论坛上大家会讨论最常问的20个问题。员工可以获悉公司的所有信息，从而增加对公司的信任，使员工和领导能携手解决问题。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":355},{"id":"r-管理英语4-4-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":4,"reading":2,"title":"The Right Way to Motivate Employees","subtitle":"激励员工的正确方法","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"It's important for a CEO to be passionate and enthusiastic, but there's a line of professionalism that must always be maintained."},{"lang":"zh","text":"作为一名首席执行官，有激情与热忱固然重要，但必须坚守职业操守。"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to a report from the technology website VentureBeat, PayPal CEO David Marcus wrote a critical letter to his employees blaming them for not using PayPal products and encouraging them to leave if they didn't have the passion to use the products they work for."},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据美国科技网站VentureBeat的报道，贝宝（PayPal）首席执行官大卫·马库斯给员工写了一封批评信，谴责他们不用贝宝的产品，并规劝他们，如果他们不热衷使用公司产品，可以辞职。"},{"lang":"en","text":"According to the website, part of the leaked letter reads:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"根据这一网站显示，一部分泄露的信件内容是："},{"lang":"en","text":"“It's been brought to my attention that when testing paying with mobile at Cafe 17 last week, some of you refused to install the PayPal app, and others didn't even remember their PayPal passwords."},{"lang":"en","text":"That's unacceptable to me, and the rest of my team; everyone at PayPal should use our products when available. That's the only way we can make them better, and better.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"“有件事引起了我的注意：上周在Cafe 17餐厅测试移动支付的时候，你们中的部分人拒绝安装应用软件贝宝，还有些人甚至忘了自己的贝宝密码。这对我来说是不能接受的，每个在贝宝工作的人都应该在可以用的地方使用我们的产品。这是我们可以更好地使它们的唯一途径。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"“In closing, if you are one of the folks who refused to install the PayPal app or if you can't remember your PayPal password, do yourself a favor, go and find something that will connect with your heart and mind elsewhere.”"},{"lang":"zh","text":"“最后，如果你是拒绝安装贝宝应用程序的人之一，或者如果你不记得你的贝宝密码，请帮自己一个忙，去别处寻找一些可以与你的心产生共鸣的东西。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"While not obvious at first, the letter reveals a problem of morale and culture at PayPal. As an executive, you certainly want your employees to use and promote your products. However, when faced with a situation where staff aren't embracing what they make, you need to investigate the root of the problem — not threaten."},{"lang":"zh","text":"虽然开始并不明显，这封信揭示了贝宝有关士气和文化的问题。作为执行官，您当然希望员工使用和宣传自己公司的产品。但是，当面对员工不欢迎自己所做的东西的情况时，您需要调查问题的根源——而不是威胁。"},{"lang":"en","text":"When faced with internal problems, good executives start by asking “why”. They reach out to their executive team first and then to the entire staff to find the root of a problem and how to fix it."},{"lang":"en","text":"Sending out a one-sided note about the problem is not leading; it's retreating."},{"lang":"zh","text":"面对内部问题时，好的高管首先要问“为什么”。他们首先会要求执行团队，接着发动全体员工找出问题根源，寻求解决办法。就存在的问题发出片面的书面告示，这种做法不是在引导解决问题，而是在逃避责任。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Leadership starts by listening. Good executives need to get out among the staff and ask questions and listen without judgment or reaction. The fact that company employees are not embracing and using its products is a failure of leadership that Marcus needs to address by self-reflection ."},{"lang":"en","text":"At the end of the day, if his employees have to be forced to use the app, how can he expect consumers to want to willingly pay to use it?"},{"lang":"en","text":"Marcus should have focused on three questions:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"领导从聆听开始。好的执行官要到员工中去，问问题，倾听他们的意见，而不需要作出判断或反应。公司员工不喜欢也不使用自己的产品这一事实体现了领导力的失败，为此马库斯应该自我反省。如果到了最后，他的员工必须被强制使用这个应用软件，那么他如何奢望顾客会愿意花钱去使用它呢？马库斯应该将注意力集中到三个问题上："},{"lang":"en","text":"• Why are you not using the app?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"为什么不使用这个应用程序？"},{"lang":"en","text":"• What is it that we can do to ensure you use our app?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"我们可以做什么来确保你使用我们的应用程序？"},{"lang":"en","text":"• What do you need from me?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"你需要我做些什么？"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":395},{"id":"r-管理英语4-5-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":5,"reading":1,"title":"Performance Management and Performance Appraisal","subtitle":"绩效管理和绩效评估","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Performance management aims to acknowledge the employees' achievements, support their personal and professional development, and motivate and empower them to perform their work effectively."},{"lang":"en","text":"Performance management helps employees to develop their understanding, knowledge and skills so that they can contribute to the achievement of the enterprise's goals and gain personal and job satisfaction."},{"lang":"en","text":"It is a vital part of any quality human resource system."},{"lang":"zh","text":"绩效管理的目的在于：肯定雇员的成绩，帮助他们实现个人成长及职业发展，激励他们并使他们能够更加有效地完成工作。绩效管理旨在帮助员工提高认知水平、专业知识和技能，以便他们在努力实现企业目标的同时，增强对自身和职业的满意度。这是任何有效的人力资源管理制度的重要组成部分。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Every enterprise wants and should expect high performance from each employee. The elements of a competency-based performance management system will, if implemented well, enable high performance which will define enterprise and personal success."},{"lang":"en","text":"Using performance management processes, an enterprise can be better placed to meet competitive challenges. This is done by:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"每个企业都需要也期待每一个员工有优异的表现。如果基于能力评定的绩效管理制度的各项指标得以有效实施，就可以确保高效能，这意味着企业和员工共同获得成功。通过绩效管理手段，企业将更能应付有竞争力的挑战。这可以通过以下措施得以实现："},{"lang":"en","text":"• identifying the critical positions;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 找出核心岗位；"},{"lang":"en","text":"• determining the most important competencies for these positions;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 确定这些岗位所需的关键能力；"},{"lang":"en","text":"• providing the education, training and feedback required by employees;"},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 提供员工要求的教育、培训和反馈；"},{"lang":"en","text":"• holding each person accountable for their results."},{"lang":"zh","text":"• 使每个人各尽其责。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The key to the performance management process is “performance appraisal”. Performance appraisal is simply an evaluation of how well an employee performs his or her job compared to a set of predetermined standards."},{"lang":"en","text":"It is a systematic process of feedback on an employee's work performance, and agreement to future training plans, job goals and job aspirations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"绩效管理过程的关键是“绩效评估”。绩效评估，简单地说，就是对照一系列既定的标准来评价员工的工作表现。它是对员工工作表现的系统反馈，也是确定未来培训安排、工作目标和工作预期的依据。"},{"lang":"en","text":"To be effective, a performance appraisal needs to have a set of agreed criteria that will be the basis of feedback as well as of setting future goals."},{"lang":"en","text":"Units of competency provide a very effective tool for setting benchmarks or criteria for work performance. The performance criteria within units of competency can be used as measures to assess against in a performance appraisal or review."},{"lang":"zh","text":"为了更加有效，绩效评估需要设定一套一致的标准，作为确定评价反馈和工作目标的依据。工作绩效的标准或要求是按人的各项能力来设定的。这样的业绩标准可以在绩效评估和评议时作为标尺来衡量。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":265},{"id":"r-管理英语4-5-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":5,"reading":2,"title":"How to Handle a Bad Performance Review?","subtitle":"如何面对不佳的绩效考核结果？","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Getting a bad performance review can make you feel angry, unappreciated, defeated, and hopeless. But it's not the end of the world. Remember that the way you respond to this appraisal can make all the difference in the next one. Even if you believe that the review is inaccurate and that your boss is completely wrong, you will benefit by reacting in a mature, adult manner. Here are some suggestions:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"绩效考核的成绩欠佳可能会让你感到愤怒、不被认可、挫败和丧失希望。但这并不是世界末日。要记住，你对这次绩效考核结果的反应，会大大影响你下次的考核结果。即使你认定考评结果不准确，或者你的老板完全错了，如果你通过成熟的、成年人的方式去应对，你将受益匪浅。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Stay calm. Relax. Breathe. Do not overreact and be objective. Especially, do not say things that will likely be regretted later. Besides, the person giving the performance review may or may not be the one who has written the bad review."},{"lang":"zh","text":"镇定下来，放松，深呼吸。持客观态度，不要反应过度。特别是，不要说你之后会后悔的话。另外，拿给你这份考评结果的人可能并不是写下这份考评的人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"What to Do When Receiving a Bad Performance Review"},{"lang":"zh","text":"收到成绩欠佳的考评结果时该怎么做"},{"lang":"en","text":"It's best to listen attentively. And make comments or remarks only when asked for them. Besides, during the performance review, you will be given the chance to respond and may disagree."},{"lang":"zh","text":"最好的做法是认真聆听。只在需要你回应时，你才反馈你的看法和意见。另外，在进行绩效考评时，你会有机会回应，甚至提出异议。"},{"lang":"en","text":"What to Do After Receiving a Bad Performance Review"},{"lang":"zh","text":"收到成绩欠佳的考评结果以后该怎么做"},{"lang":"en","text":"Don't be intimidated by the bad performance review and want to quit the job; instead, learn from it. Also, if the organization allows their employees to make a written statement on their own behalf, do make one. It is important for the worker to show why she does not agree with the bad performance review; for instance, an employee may express their different understanding and, at the same time, a willingness to comply with any constructive suggestions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果绩效考核结果不佳，不要过于担心，甚至想辞去工作，而应该从中吸取教训。同时，如果公司允许员工自己提供一份书面说明，一定要写一份。对于被考核者来说，表达出不认同不良评定的原因是很重要的。例如，被考核者可在表达不同看法的同时，表示愿意接受有益建议。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Ways to Improve a Bad Performance Review"},{"lang":"zh","text":"改善绩效考核不良成绩的方法"},{"lang":"en","text":"A way to improve a bad performance review is to set self-reviews, that is, establish performance standards. Another way to improve a bad review is to learn more about what the manager, supervisor, or boss wants or expects from his / her employees. Learning what it was that caused a bad performance review helps improve professional growth and encourages as well as motivates the worker to do better in order to receive a good review next time."},{"lang":"zh","text":"改善绩效考核不良成绩的一个有效方法是建立自我评价体系，也就是设定业绩标准。另一个办法是更多地去了解你的经理、上司或老板对员工的期望。让员工了解自己绩效评价结果不佳的原因可以帮助促进其专业发展，鼓励并激励其在下次考核时取得好的成绩。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":321},{"id":"r-管理英语4-6-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":6,"reading":1,"title":"How to adapt to Change in the Workplace?","subtitle":"如何适应职场变化","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"If there's one word that captures the essence of what is occurring in the world today, it's “change”."},{"lang":"en","text":"Downsizing , reorganizing, and cutting costs, are now the norm for survival."},{"lang":"en","text":"No industry is exempt . Even the most conservative institutions are undergoing significant changes just to survive."},{"lang":"zh","text":"如果用一个词来捕捉当今世界的本质特征，那非“变化”莫属。裁员、重组、降低成本如今已经成了生存的常态，无一行业可以幸免。为了生存，哪怕最保守的机构也要进行改革。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Change management has always been an issue of debate amongst scholars : how can employers create suitable conditions for a successful change process? And what can employees do to get through it?"},{"lang":"zh","text":"应对变化是学者们经常争论的一个话题：雇主如何才能为成功推进改革进程创造合适的条件？员工们又该如何应对？"},{"lang":"en","text":"Tips for dealing with change in the workplace:"},{"lang":"zh","text":"小贴士：如何应对职场变化"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Make yourself aware that change happens: it happens in personal life; it happens in your professional life. You cannot live in the past, so denying that change could occur only makes things more complicated for you."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·让自己认识到，变化总是会发生的，生活在变，工作也在变。你不能生活在过去，因此，否认变化的发生只能使事情变得对你来说更加复杂。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Stay alert in the workplace: know what is happening around you. When you come across clues that hint change is on the way, acknowledge them!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"·时刻保持清醒的头脑：注意身边发生的一切。当你看到有迹象表明变化即将发生时，要敢于面对。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Maintain open communication channels. Don't lay back and expect things to pass you by smoothly. You need to get acquainted with the occurring changes. Seek more details from your management and peers to form an accurate understanding of the matter. Be transparent and honest about your fears: dealing with the unknown is often resented and daunting . Make the picture as clear as you can."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·保持沟通渠道畅通。不要只是退缩等待，希望凡事都会顺利过去。你需要了解正在发生的变化，从领导和同事那儿了解更多的详情，形成对事情的正确认识。坦诚面对自己的担忧，应对未知之事往往会令人不快，令人畏惧。尽可能把情况弄清楚。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Assess yourself. Change is a time when one's confidence about one's skills and capabilities gets shaky ."},{"lang":"en","text":"Recognize your strengths and where you could bring them into play. At the same time, stay aware of your developmental areas and work on improving those."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·自我评估。变革的时候，人们往往对自己的技能和能力产生怀疑。清楚自己的优势，并知道在什么地方能发挥出来。同时，明白自己的发展领域，并努力改进完善。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Don't be stiff. It will make the change process much harder if you are rigid. Be fl exible enough to look at the different angles of the change and see where you could apply your “existing” skills and knowledge, and what new skills you need to acquire."},{"lang":"zh","text":"·不要固执死板。顽固不化只会使进程的改变变得更难。要足够灵活，从各个不同的角度看待改变，发现自己在哪些地方可以运用“现有”的技能和知识，有哪些新技能有待掌握。"},{"lang":"en","text":"• Stay optimistic. Keep a positive attitude and don't let yourself drown in uncertainty . Involve yourself in the new process; locate yourself properly in the new scenario . Adjust!"},{"lang":"zh","text":"·保持乐观。保持积极心态，不要让自己犹豫不决。参与到新的变化进程中去，在新的环境下重新定位、调整自我、迅速适应！"},{"lang":"en","text":"“You can't get to the top of Everest by jumping up the mountain."},{"lang":"en","text":"You get to the mountaintop by taking incremental steps. Step by step, you get to the goal,” says Robin Sharma, one of the world's most sought-after leadership and personal success experts."},{"lang":"zh","text":"世界上最受推崇的一位领导学和个人成功领域的专家罗宾·夏玛说：“没人可以一步跨上珠穆朗玛峰峰顶。只有踏着坚实的脚步才能到达山顶。一步一步地，你就可以达到目的地。”"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":370},{"id":"r-管理英语4-6-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":6,"reading":2,"title":"Jack Welch Leading Organizational Change at GE","subtitle":"杰克·韦尔奇领导通用电气的机构改革","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"When Jack Welch, the Chairman and CEO at General Electric (GE) retired in 2001, he could look back at a very successful career."},{"lang":"en","text":"He became CEO in 1981 at the age of 45. At that time, GE had a very complex organizational structure with considerably bureaucratic rules."},{"lang":"zh","text":"2001年，通用电气公司董事长兼首席执行官杰克·韦尔奇退休，回顾他的职业生涯，可谓事业有成。1981年他45岁时成为首席执行官。当时的通用电气机构臃肿，官僚主义盛行。"},{"lang":"en","text":"One of his first changes was to initiate a strategy formulation process with the guideline that each of the businesses should be number 1 or 2 in their respective areas. If this was not the case, managers had the options of fixing the problem, selling their particular business, or closing it. In an effort to streamline the organization, Welch removed the sector level and eliminated thousands of salaried and hourly employee positions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"他的首要变革就是，启动战略制定程序，其原则是：每项业务在各自领域都要做到数一数二。否则，其业务经理面临三种选择：一是解决问题，二是出售业务，三是关门大吉。为了精简机构，韦尔奇取消了科级部门，裁掉了成千上万的计时付酬的工人。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The restructuring was followed by changing the organizational culture and the managerial styles of GE’s managers. One such program was the Work-Out. Groups of managers were assembled to share their views openly in three-day sessions. At the beginning of the meetings, the superior presented the challenges for his or her organizational unit. Then the superior had to leave, requesting the groups to find solutions to the problems. Facilitators helped these discussions. On the last day, the superior was presented with proposed solutions. He or she then had three choices: to accept the proposal, not to accept it, or to collect more information. This process put great pressure on the superior to make decisions."},{"lang":"zh","text":"机构重组之后，他便着手改革企业文化和整顿经理们的管理作风。他采用一种被称为“群策群力”的解决方案。具体做法是，部门经理们用三天时间分组开会，公开交流意见。会议伊始，主管领导向下属单位经理提出问题，随后便离开会场，让这些经理研究出解决方案，小组主持人组织讨论。会议最后一天，主管领导会收到经理们提交的解决方案。主管领导可以有以下三种选择：接受方案、不接受方案或者收集更多信息。这种做法给主管领导的决策增加了压力。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another program to improve effectiveness and efficiency was Best Practices. The aim was to learn from other companies how they obtained customer satisfaction, how they related to their suppliers, and in what ways they developed new products. This helped the GE people to focus on the processes in their operations that would improve the company’s performance."},{"lang":"zh","text":"另一种提高效率的做法叫“最佳实践”,其目的是向其他公司学习怎样赢得客户满意，学习怎样与供应商打交道，学习怎样开发新产品。这样做有助于通用人将他们的生产活动集中在改进公司的业绩方面。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Jack Welch was personally involved in developing managers at GE’s training center in Crotonville. Leaders, Welch suggested, are not only those who achieve results but also those who share the values of the company."},{"lang":"zh","text":"杰克·韦尔奇还亲自到克罗顿维尔的通用培训中心参与对经理的培训。他认为，领导者不仅要能够达成既定目标，还要能够分享公司的价值观。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":322},{"id":"r-管理英语4-7-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":7,"reading":1,"title":"Organizational Culture and Its Functions","subtitle":"企业文化及其功能","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Just as individuals have personalities , so, too, do organizations."},{"lang":"en","text":"Individuals have relatively enduring and stable traits that help us predict their attitudes and behaviors. Organizations, like people, can be characterized as, for example, rigid, friendly, warm, innovative , or conservative."},{"lang":"en","text":"These traits, in turn , can be used to predict attitudes and behaviors of the people within these organizations."},{"lang":"zh","text":"正如每个人都有个性一样，企业也有个性。每个人所具有的相对持久稳定的特质有助于我们预测他们的态度和行为。企业就像人一样，具有诸如严厉、友好、热情、创新或保守的特征。这些特质反过来又可以用来预测这些企业内人员的态度和行为。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The culture of any organization, although it may be hard to measure precisely, nevertheless exists and is generally recognized by its employees. Organizations have cultures that govern how members behave. Organizational culture refers to a system of shared meaning held by members that distinguishes the organization from other organizations. It is a set of key characteristics that the organization values. There are seven primary characteristics that capture the essence of an organization's culture. They are: innovation and risk taking, attention to details, outcome orientation , people orientation, team orientation, aggressiveness and stability . Appraising the organization on these seven characteristics gives a composite picture of the organization's culture. This picture becomes the basis for feelings of shared understanding that members have about the organization, how things are done in it, and the way members are supposed to behave."},{"lang":"zh","text":"任何企业的文化，尽管很难准确度量，但确实存在，并被组织内员工所认同。组织文化规范员工的行为举止。企业文化指的是所有员工认同的思想体系，可以用来区别于其他企业，是企业非常珍惜的一系列重要特征。体现企业文化的本质主要有以下七大特征：大胆创新并敢于冒险、看重细节、注重结果、以人为本、团队精神、积极进取、稳定发展。从这七个方面对某一组织进行评估，勾画出这一组织文化的全貌。这一画面成为员工对企业共同理解的情感基础：工作应该怎么完成，需要员工怎么做。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Culture performs a number of functions within an organization. First, it creates distinctions between one organization and others. Second, it conveys a sense of identity for organization members. Third, culture facilitates the generation of commitment to something larger than one's individual self interest."},{"lang":"en","text":"Fourth, it enhances the stability of the social system. Finally, culture serves as a sensemaking and control mechanism that guides and shapes the attitudes and behaviors of employees."},{"lang":"zh","text":"企业文化具备如下功能。第一，用于区别其他组织；第二，体现企业内员工的认同感；第三，有助于产生对企业的承诺，这种承诺超越了员工自身的利益；第四，加强社会体系的稳定。最后，文化还可作为一个思想意识形成和组织管理机制，指导和养成员工的态度和行为。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The role of culture in influencing employee behaviors appears to be increasingly important in today's workplace. Who receives a job offer to join the organization, who is appraised as a high performer, and who gets a promotion are strongly influenced by the individual-organization “fit”."},{"lang":"en","text":"It is not a coincidence that employees at Disney theme parks appear to be almost universally attractive, clean, and wholesome looking, with bright smiles. And once on the job, a strong culture, supported by formal rules and regulations, ensures that Disney theme park employees will act in a relatively uniform and predictable way."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在当今的职场环境中，企业文化在影响员工行为举止方面所起的作用显得越来越重要。个人与企业的融合度极大地影响着个人是否被录用，是否作为优秀员工受到表彰，是否得到晋升。迪斯尼主题乐园的员工们似乎都富有魅力、干净健康、笑容灿烂，这绝非偶然。一旦上岗，强大的以严格规章制度为支撑的迪士尼文化，确保所有员工操作规范一致，符合人们的预期。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":362},{"id":"r-管理英语4-7-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":7,"reading":2,"title":"Create a Positive Workplace Culture","subtitle":"创建积极的企业文化","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"In competitive markets, leaders are under increased pressure to maintain a positive work culture. A positive work culture cultivates greater employee satisfaction; greater employee satisfaction contributes to higher performance; higher performance impacts improved client outcomes; improved client outcomes contribute to service excellence."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在竞争激烈的市场中，领导者为保持积极的企业文化而备受压力。积极的企业文化提升员工满意度，员工满意度越高，工作就越出色；工作越出色，顾客就越多；顾客越多，服务质量就越好。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Positive work cultures are built over time and need constant attention. Such cultures are dependent on leadership vision and values."},{"lang":"zh","text":"积极的企业文化是经过较长时间建立的，需要不断呵护。工作文化的形成靠的是领导者的见识和价值观。"},{"lang":"en","text":"An effective leader sets the tone for the team, encourages a positive workplace culture and is able to bring about cultural change."},{"lang":"zh","text":"卓有成效的领导者为团队定下基调，鼓励积极文化的培养，大胆进行文化改革。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Workplace culture is made up of the shared attitudes, beliefs, behaviors, values and expectations that influence the way people work in the workplace. It is “the way we do things around here”. Workplace culture is made up of the shared attitudes, beliefs, behaviors, values and expectations that influence the way people work in the workplace. It is “the way we do things around here”."},{"lang":"zh","text":"企业文化由共同的态度、观念、行为、价值观和期待构成，影响着职场员工的工作方式。“这事在我们这里就得这么办。”"},{"lang":"en","text":"Some cultural aspects are understood by all and are obvious such as turning up for work on time, while others may be “unwritten rules” that are not so obvious, for example, how personal issues are resolved with work colleagues."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有些文化现象显而易见，人人皆知，如按时上班；有些则是不成文的规矩，不是很明显，如怎样处理同事间的关系。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Many factors that influence whether a workplace has a positive outlook are within the control of people who work in the workplace. There are also factors out of their control, such as slumps in global prices or a change in demand and supply. The company can, however, control how they respond to these factors."},{"lang":"zh","text":"影响企业文化是否积极的诸多因素掌控在企业员工手中。但有些因素是他们无法掌控的，如全球价格下滑或者供需改变等。然而，企业可以掌控的是对这些因素的应对方法。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Those companies that do create positive workplace environments develop a reputation in their community as being “good to work for” and have a competitive edge . Not only are these companies more able to attract and retain people, they tend to be more stable as they proactively deal with issues and adapt to change."},{"lang":"zh","text":"那些真正创造了积极向上工作环境的企业在业界享有“最佳工作场所”的声誉，具有竞争优势。这些企业不但能够更加吸引和留住人才，而且能够更加积极主动地处理问题，更加稳妥地应对变革。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Teams work best when they are clear about what is expected of them. They are more able to deal with difficult issues if they feel the values of the organization are supportive of them."},{"lang":"zh","text":"当一个团队清楚人们对他们的期望时，他们的工作会做得最好。一旦感受到企业价值观的支持，他们就更有能力处理棘手的问题。"},{"lang":"en","text":"For a workplace culture to be positive, the direction and actions of the business must be consistent with the core values of the people in the workplace."},{"lang":"en","text":"The people must trust each other and be able to openly express and exchange ideas."},{"lang":"zh","text":"若想要企业文化积极向上，企业的定位和运作机制必须与企业员工的核心价值观一致。员工们必须相互信任，并能够公开表达和交换意见。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Working through these steps will help with developing a positive business culture."},{"lang":"zh","text":"以上步骤有助于形成积极的企业文化。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":382},{"id":"r-管理英语4-8-1","book":"管理英语4","unit":8,"reading":1,"title":"Vision and Execution: Two Sides of a Successful Strategy","subtitle":"愿景和执行：成功战略的两个方面","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"A strategic plan is not the end goal of the strategic planning process — it is the framework for successfully implementing a strategy. Until a strategic plan is put into effect, it has no real value."},{"lang":"zh","text":"在战略规划过程中，战略规划不是最终目标，而是成功执行战略的一个框架。一个规划只有被付诸实施时才具有重要价值。"},{"lang":"en","text":"There are several keys to successful implementation. First, people directly involved in executing the strategy must be included in the planning process. Strategic planning is no longer a top-down directive."},{"lang":"en","text":"Without the input and feedback of the people responsible for executing the strategy, a seemingly solid strategy is likely to fall apart when implementation is attempted ."},{"lang":"zh","text":"有几个关键因素会影响成功实施。首先，在规划过程中必须把直接参与执行策略的人考虑在内。战略规划不再是一个自上而下的指令。如果缺乏负责实施计划的人员的投入与反馈，一个看似可靠的计划也可能在实施过程中功亏一篑。"},{"lang":"en","text":"The next key to successful implementation is clearly communicating the strategy to the whole company. The communication should ensure that everyone in the company understands and accepts the strategy as the best path forward, and not simply the leadership's latest idea. Without clear communication, employees lack a sense of ownership and clarity of purpose. When a strategy is not understood or embraced, it usually results in misunderstanding and uneven commitments to implementation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"成功实施的下一个关键因素是将战略清晰传达给整个公司。上下沟通应该确保公司内每个人都理解这个战略，并把它当作前进的最佳路径，而不是把它当作领导层的最新想法。没有明确的沟通，员工缺乏归属感和清晰的目标。当一个企业战略不被员工理解或接受时，通常会导致误解，甚至造成实施过程中努力程度的差异。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Another key to the successful execution of a strategic plan is the clear and straightforward description of the plan and its operations. Even the most brilliant strategy faces failure if it cannot be explained clearly and flourish."},{"lang":"zh","text":"另一个关键是对战略规划及其运作作出清晰和直接的描述。即使是最无懈可击的战略，如果不解释简洁、清晰、到位，也会面临失败。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":201},{"id":"r-管理英语4-8-2","book":"管理英语4","unit":8,"reading":2,"title":"How Do You Create a Culture of Innovation?","subtitle":"企业的创新文化源于何处？","paragraphs":[{"lang":"en","text":"Have you noticed the courage buried in the word “encourage”? To create a culture in which innovation flourishes takes courage."},{"lang":"en","text":"Determined innovators are always courageous enough to establish a culture in which innovation is greatly encouraged and rewarded. Here are three ways to do that."},{"lang":"zh","text":"你有没有注意到在“encourage”（鼓励）中含有“courage”（勇气）？建立一种鼓励创新的企业文化是需要勇气的。坚定的革新者总是有足够的勇气去建立一种激励和奖励创新的企业文化。要做到这一点，可以从三个方面着手。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Put innovation at the heart of strategy, and persist it in every message. Think of innovation strategy as a pyramid: big bets at the top, a few projects in development in the middle, and a broad base of continuous improvements, lasting contributions, and early-stage new ideas at the bottom."},{"lang":"zh","text":"把创新放在战略的核心，并把它体现在方方面面。把创新战略看成是一个金字塔：顶部是大目标，中间是在研项目，底部是不断的改进、持续的贡献，以及新想法雏形。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Define jobs around innovation. Make it a job prerequisite . Consider 3M's move to become one of the first companies to tell professionals that they could spend 15 percent of their time on projects of their own choice."},{"lang":"en","text":"Now many high-tech companies know that they can't get the best talent without providing this kind of flexibility. And some of those self-selected, self-organized projects might even result in a blockbuster product or line of business."},{"lang":"en","text":"For 3M, it was the Post-it note."},{"lang":"zh","text":"用创新定义工作。把创新看成是工作的先决条件。想当初，3M公司率先容许员工们可以使用15%的工作时间，自主选择参与工作项目。现在很多高科技公司都知道，如果他们不能给人才提供这种创新的便利条件，就没法吸引优秀的人才。一些个人自主选择、自我安排的项目甚至会成为轰动一时的产品或业务链条。对于3M而言，这种企业文化就是自己的身份标签。"},{"lang":"en","text":"Recognize innovation in every part of the company. To build a culture of creativity and innovation, Gillette developed an innovation fair in which every unit could show off its most promising new concepts."},{"lang":"en","text":"It shows that everyone has a role to play in a culture of innovation."},{"lang":"zh","text":"肯定公司里无处不在的创新。为了建立一个善于创新的文化，吉列公司组织了创意展览会，在那里，每个部门都能展示他们大有可为的理念。这表明每个人在创新文化中都能发挥自己的作用。"},{"lang":"en","text":"To go from idea to successful innovation requires a great deal of support and collaboration. When people are surrounded by constant communication and encouragement, they can find the courage to try, fail, redo, and try again."},{"lang":"zh","text":"从理念到创新成功需要大力支持与通力协作。当人们在工作中能不断沟通、不断受到鼓励时，他们就有勇气去尝试、去失败、重头再来并继续尝试。"}],"source":"管理英语4（阅读文章中英文对照）.doc","words":261}],"stats":{"rawQuestions":1294,"uniqueQuestions":887,"mergedDuplicates":407,"articles":128,"dailyQuestions":900,"essentialQuestions":394,"categories":{"交际用语":161,"词汇与语法":311,"汉译英":119,"英译汉":61,"虚拟语气":235},"answerConflicts":[],"questionSources":31,"readingSources":8},"questionAliases":{"q-425f77f52c485638":{"id":"q-26bc662c5bf43b64","options":{"A":"A","B":"C","C":"B","D":"D"}}}};
